  "sections": [
    {
      "cite": "1.1",
      "part": "front",
      "title": "Short Title and Citation",
      "kind": "intro",
      "brief": "This compilation is the Codex of the Mages' Guild, cited C.C.D. State who may cite it in filings. Dry.",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Short Title and Citation",
          "text": "This compilation is the Codex of the Mages' Guild, cited C.C.D. The authority of the Codex is derived from the foundational agreements established within the Autumnwood Accords, serving as the primary regulatory framework for all arcane activities sanctioned by the Guild. Any legal filing, petition for research, or appeal of disciplinary action must reference the specific section of the C.C.D. to be deemed admissible by the Archmage Sovereign or the presiding council of the Accords Desk. The Codex serves as the definitive record of the Guild’s internal governance, distinguishing between the preservationist requirements of the Conservators and the experimental liberties granted to the Innovators.\n\nThe C.C.D. is the sole authoritative text for the interpretation of magical conduct within the Midlands and any territories under Guild jurisdiction. No external decree, local ordinance, or private pact shall supersede the provisions contained herein unless expressly stated in a formal amendment signed by Archmage Veyra. All practitioners, from high-ranking Archmages to the lowliest initiate, are expected to maintain a copy of the Codex or have immediate access to a verified transcription for the purposes of compliance. Failure to cite the correct section during a formal inquiry may result in a procedural dismissal of the petitioner's claims, as the Guild maintains that ignorance of the C.C.D. is no defense against its mandates.\n\nThe citation of the C.C.D. must be precise. When referencing multiple statutes, the petitioner shall list them in ascending numerical order. For example, a violation involving both the unauthorized use of restricted materials and the breach of a sanctuary shall be cited as \"see § 1.6 and § 1.5.\" The Clerk of the Accords Desk reserves the right to strike any filing that utilizes colloquialisms or non-standard shorthand in place of the required C.C.D. designations. The Codex is a living document of the Guild’s history and its future; to cite it is to acknowledge the weight of the Autumnwood Accords and the shared responsibility of the mages to maintain the stability of the weave.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
            "1.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Authority and Validity",
          "text": "§ 102.1 Source of Authority — The Codex derives its force exclusively from the sovereign will of the Archmage Sovereign, currently Archmage Veyra. No other body, whether domestic or foreign, possesses the power to alter this compilation without her express approval. Any contrary provisions in rival codes, such as the Iron Mandate or Edicts of the Flame, are void ab initio within Guild jurisdiction. § 102.2 Binding Effect — The Accords bind all persons subject to their authority, regardless of consent. This includes registered practitioners, licensed artisans utilizing magical services, and any individual benefiting from Guild-regulated magic. Failure to comply constitutes a breach of covenant punishable under the penal provisions herein. § 102.3 Supremacy Clause — In the event of conflict between this Codex and other laws or customs, the provisions hereof shall prevail unless explicitly repealed by the Archmage Sovereign. This supremacy applies to all matters falling within the Guild's purview, including but not limited to magical research, field casting, and commercial licensing. § 102.4 Interpretation — Any ambiguity in these articles shall be construed according to established case law and customary practice of the Mages' Guild. Where no precedent exists, reasonable discretion lies with the Archmage Sovereign or her duly appointed delegates. Such determinations shall be binding on all parties unless overturned by subsequent ruling. § 102.5 Non-Retroactivity — Provisions herein apply prospectively only, except where expressly stated to have retroactive effect. Actions occurring prior to enactment are governed by laws in force at the time, subject to any saving statutes or transitional rules promulgated by the Guild. This ensures fairness and stability within the magical community while allowing for necessary evolution of standards.\n\n\"Thus speaks the Codex itself, binding all who tread under its spell. Beware the subtle traps woven into these words—they may ensnare even the most astute mind.\" — Archmage Theron, *The Conservator's Chronicle*, Vol. XLIX, p. 127.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "102.1",
            "102.2",
            "102.3",
            "102.4",
            "102.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Authority and Validity — Continued",
          "text": "§ 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting — A caster shall not engage in any professional activity that conflicts with their official duties, including but not limited to casting for personal gain or using Guild resources for private ends. Violations may result in disciplinary action up to and including revocation of licensure. This section does not preclude a caster from providing pro bono services outside the scope of their employment.\n\n§ 400.6 Delegation to Clerks — In urgent matters where the presence of a certified caster is required but unavailable, the Desk may authorize a qualified clerk to perform necessary functions under direct supervision. Such delegation shall be limited in duration and scope as dictated by the circumstances. All actions taken pursuant to this provision must be fully documented and subject to review upon conclusion of the emergency situation.\n\n§ 500.6 Specimen Custody — Any magical artifacts, creatures, or materials obtained through lawful means must be properly stored and maintained in accordance with safety protocols established by the Guild. Improper handling or disposal may result in catastrophic consequences for both the custodian and surrounding populations. Regular inspections will be conducted to ensure compliance with these standards at all times.\n\n§ 200.6 Guest Casters — Individuals not currently holding active licensure status may petition the Desk for temporary authorization to practice under specific conditions. Approval is contingent upon demonstration of competency, absence of prior violations, and agreement to abide by all applicable regulations during the term of said permission. Failure to meet these requirements will result in immediate termination of privileges with no right to appeal.\n\nThis page establishes clear guidelines regarding professional conduct, delegation procedures, artifact management, and guest casting arrangements within the Guild framework. Adherence to these provisions is mandatory for maintaining public safety and ensuring orderly operation of magical services across all jurisdictions under our collective oversight. Any deviations require explicit written consent from authorized representatives before implementation.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "100.5",
            "400.6",
            "500.6",
            "200.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Interpretation and Application of the Codex",
          "text": "Where ambiguity arises in the provisions herein, the spirit of the Accords shall govern over their literal text. The Desk interprets this law with an eye toward preserving magical stability while accommodating legitimate scholarly pursuit. Reasonable doubt favors restraint in the application of sanctions, yet tolerance for infractions is not to be mistaken for leniency or indifference.\n\nThe Codex applies universally across all Hall territories and related jurisdictions, regardless of local custom or precedent. No customary usage may contravene explicit terms set forth herein. Where conflict exists between this document and prior arrangements, the latter shall yield unless ratified by subsequent resolution of the Desk. The Accords stand as supreme law within their sphere, binding upon all persons subject to Guild authority.\n\nIn matters of dispute concerning interpretation or enforcement, the exclusive remedy lies with the formal grievance process established under these provisions. Parties are prohibited from seeking extrajudicial recourse or private arbitration that circumvents official channels. Violation of this requirement nullifies any claims arising therefrom and may constitute a separate offense subject to penal action. The integrity of the judicial system must remain paramount in upholding the Rule of Arcane Law.\n\nThis Codex shall be read as one consistent enactment, its parts mutually reinforcing rather than contradictory. Provisions are not to be severed or excised from their context but considered holistically for proper understanding. Technicalities and pedantic distinctions shall not defeat substantial justice where the intent of the Accords is clear despite textual uncertainty. The Desk retains discretion to fill gaps in accordance with fundamental principles of fairness and reasonableness.\n\nThe Mages' Guild codifies its will here, binding all who operate within its domain to these terms. Resistance or evasion invites swift retribution from both institution and individual practitioners alike. Submit yourself gladly to the yoke of lawful magic, lest you find yourself crushed beneath it without recourse. For in this code lies both your salvation and your damnation — take heed accordingly.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "heading": "Authority and Validity — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "The Codex shall remain the supreme law of this Hall, superseding all contrary customs or precedents unless expressly amended by the Desk itself. No external edict may override its provisions without unanimous consent of the Conservators and Innovators. Any clause found void for public policy shall be severed yet leave the remainder intact as if never written. The spirit behind each article governs alongside its letter, lest technicalities swallow the intent whole.\n\nInterpretation and Application of the Codex\nAmbiguities herein shall be resolved in favor of maintaining peace among casters unless doing so violates core principles of justice or fairness. Precedents set by this Desk bind all future adjudications absent compelling reason to depart therefrom. Reasonable reliance on published rules may excuse inadvertent violations committed without malice aforethought. The Codex evolves with society, adapting to new threats and technologies while preserving timeless truths about power and responsibility.\n\nIn short, this text stands as both shield and sword for our craft—a beacon guiding us through darkest trials and brightest triumphs alike. May it serve well the cause of magic within these walls and beyond!",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "heading": "Authority and Validity — Continued — Administration",
          "text": "The Codex derives its binding force solely from the consent of the bound parties, expressed through their participation in Guild activities or acceptance of its benefits. No provision herein shall be construed to impose obligations upon persons outside this scope without explicit agreement. This principle undergirds all subsequent rules and interpretations thereof.\n\nIn matters of doubt regarding the meaning or application of a particular clause, the Desk shall consult established precedent, custom among practitioners, and the overarching purposes of the Accords as articulated herein. Where no guidance exists from these sources, the Desk may issue advisory opinions to inform affected parties of their rights and responsibilities under current law. Such opinions carry persuasive but not binding weight unless later adopted by formal ruling.\n\nThe provisions of this Codex survive any termination or dissolution of the Mages' Guild itself, remaining in full force until expressly repealed or superseded by new legislation enacted pursuant to Article IV thereof. This ensures continuity of legal standards governing magical practice regardless of political upheaval within the organization. Any attempts to circumvent these enduring obligations through clandestine means shall be treated as violations subject to appropriate sanction.\n\nInterpretation of ambiguous terms shall follow standard rules of statutory construction, favoring outcomes consistent with public policy and fairness unless clearly indicated otherwise by context or express language. Technical nuances may arise in specific circumstances requiring careful analysis but ultimately yield to the spirit and intent of each provision when properly understood. The Desk stands ready to provide clarification as needed while maintaining strict neutrality in all deliberations.\n\nThis comprehensive framework seeks to balance innovation with responsibility, fostering an environment where magical arts can flourish safely under wise guidance. By adhering faithfully to these principles, all members contribute to the stability and prosperity of our shared community for generations yet unborn. May this Codex serve as both compass and anchor as we navigate the treacherous waters ahead together.\"\n\n\"See also §§ 100.2–100.3 regarding representation authority; § 400.5 concerning contractual relations with non-magical entities.\"",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "100.2",
            "400.5"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": "lmstudio",
      "fp": "55685283132fea4d",
      "refs": [
        "1.5",
        "1.6",
        "100.2",
        "100.5",
        "200.6",
