    {
      "cite": "100.8",
      "part": "part_i",
      "title": "Emergency Sitting",
      "kind": "section",
      "brief": "Unscheduled weather is not by itself an emergency sitting.",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 100.8 Emergency Sitting",
          "text": "The authority to convene an Emergency Sitting of the Accords Desk, as defined under the overarching governance of the Autumnwood Accords, shall be reserved for matters of immediate and existential threat to the magical stability of the Midlands or the sovereign integrity of Archmage Veyra’s mediation. For the purposes of this Codex, an Emergency Sitting is defined as a formal, high-priority assembly of both the Conservator and Innovator factions, convened outside of the standard lunar cycle to address crises that cannot be deferred without significant risk of arcane collapse, widespread magical fallout, or hostile incursion by recognized adversarial entities. The declaration of such a sitting requires a unanimous vote by the presiding Aegis Magi and a subsequent verification by the Archmage Sovereign.\n\nNotwithstanding the gravity of atmospheric disturbances, it is hereby codified that unscheduled weather shall not, by itself, constitute grounds for an Emergency Sitting. The Guild recognizes that the Midlands is subject to natural fluctuations, seasonal shifts, and the occasional byproduct of independent research; however, the mere occurrence of localized storms, heavy snowfall, frost, or sudden temperature drops does not meet the threshold of a \"crisis\" requiring the immediate suspension of standard administrative procedures. Mages who seek to bypass the standard deliberation process by citing inclement weather as a catalyst for emergency action shall be denied the petition. The Accords Desk maintains that the stability of the Guild is predicated on the deliberate, measured pace of traditionalist oversight, and the preservation of this pace against the pretext of meteorological inconvenience is paramount.\n\nFurthermore, any mage or factional representative who attempts to manufacture a pretext for an Emergency Sitting by intentionally summoning or exacerbating unscheduled weather for the purpose of forcing a legislative outcome shall be subject to immediate investigation by the Aegis Magi. If a weather event is found to be the result of unauthorized field use—such as the unauthorized expansion of titan growth on Markop or other similar violations of the Accords—the resulting atmospheric chaos shall be treated as a matter of disciplinary action rather than a legislative emergency. In such instances, the Desk shall refer the matter to the Paradox Trial for adjudication, as the primary offense is the violation of magical safety protocols, not the weather itself.\n\nMages who find themselves inconvenienced by unscheduled weather during the performance of authorized duties are encouraged to seek refuge in designated Guild halls or utilize standard protective wards as prescribed in the basic training of the Accords. The Guild shall not be held liable for delays in research, transport, or commerce caused by natural weather patterns. If a mage claims that weather conditions have rendered a specific research site inaccessible, they shall file a standard Request for Deferment as per the Innovator guidelines, rather than requesting an Emergency Sitting. The Accords Desk shall not recognize any \"Emergency\" status granted by a mage who fails to provide evidence of an immediate threat to the magical fabric of the Midlands. See § 100.6 for the role of Clerks in verifying the completeness of such petitions. All declarations of emergency must be accompanied by a certified Arcane Impact Report to be considered valid by the Desk.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "100.6",
            "100.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Emergency Sitting Procedures",
          "text": "The authority to convene an Emergency Sitting of the Autumnwood Accords Desk is strictly circumscribed to prevent the trivialization of the Guild’s deliberative processes. An Emergency Sitting shall be defined as a formal assembly of the presiding bodies—the Conservators and the Innovators—convened outside of the standard lunar cycle to address an immediate, existential threat to the magical stability of the Midlands or the sovereign integrity of Archmage Veyra. Such sittings require a verified petition of \"Imminent Arcane Rupture\" or \"Hostile Incursion of Sovereign Scale,\" signed by at least three High Mages of standing or the direct decree of the Archmage Sovereign.\n\nUnder no circumstances shall the occurrence of unscheduled weather, regardless of its meteorological severity or localized atmospheric distortion, constitute sufficient grounds for the invocation of an Emergency Sitting. The Guild recognizes that while atmospheric anomalies may be inconvenient or potentially hazardous to mundane commerce, they do not inherently threaten the foundational Accords unless they are the direct byproduct of a catastrophic magical failure or a deliberate act of hostile sorcery. Mages attempting to bypass the standard quorum requirements by citing \"unprecedented storms\" or \"localized blizzard conditions\" for the purpose of fast-tracking legislative favors or research permits shall be subject to immediate censure.\n\nFurthermore, the Guild explicitly clarifies that weather summoned or manipulated for agricultural advantage, commercial gain, or personal comfort does not qualify as a \"natural\" emergency. Any mage found to be inducing meteorological shifts to create a pretext for an Emergency Sitting shall be held liable for the costs of any administrative disruption and may be referred to the Aegis Magi for summary discipline. If a weather event is indeed caused by a breach of the Forbidden Schools, the matter shall be handled via the standard reporting channels to Archmage Theron and the Conservator faction, rather than through an emergency session, unless the breach poses an immediate threat to the Hall of Autumn Wood.\n\nIn instances where an atmospheric event is caused by a failure of a Heartstone or a rift, the presiding mages must first conduct a full survey of the site before any emergency declarations are issued. If the survey confirms a breach of the Accord’s safety parameters, the Desk may then move to convene. However, the primary burden of proof remains on the petitioner to demonstrate that the threat is not merely a localized phenomenon but a systemic risk to the Midlands. See § 1.6 for definitions regarding \"Systemic Risk\" and \"Arcane Rupture.\" All records of such sittings must be transcribed and filed with the Desk, noting whether the sitting was successfully convened or dismissed for lack of sufficient urgency.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 100.8 Emergency Sitting, Procedures for Declaration and Conduct",
          "text": "An emergency sitting may only be called by the Archmage Sovereign or a full quorum of the Autumnwood Accords Desk convened in extraordinary circumstances where standard legislative processes would jeopardize public safety or the stability of magical research. Under § 100.8(a), such emergencies must arise from events outside the normal scope of Guild operations, including but not limited to uncontrolled arcane breaches, natural catastrophes exacerbated by unauthorized spellcasting, or imminent threats to civilian populations posed by rogue casters. Mere inconvenience, political maneuvering, or disagreements over research priorities do not constitute grounds for an emergency session. Any claim of emergency must be supported by sworn testimony from at least two senior Aegis Magi and reviewed within twenty-four hours by the full Desk acting ex parte. § 100.8(b) further stipulates that during an emergency sitting, all standard rules of debate and deliberation may be suspended to facilitate rapid decision-making. Votes shall be conducted via secret ballot unless a three-quarters majority explicitly requests open voting. Resolutions passed during such sessions carry the force of law immediately upon adoption and cannot be amended for fourteen days following adjournment, after which they become subject to normal review procedures as set forth in § 100.8(c). Any member wishing to challenge the validity of an emergency resolution must file a formal appeal within seven days citing specific grounds under §§ 100.5–100.7 regarding conflict of interest or procedural irregularities. Failure to adhere strictly to these provisions shall render any actions taken during the sitting null and void, subject to reversal by a subsequent regular session. The Desk maintains detailed logs of all emergency proceedings as required by § 100.4, ensuring full transparency once standard operating conditions are restored. This stringent framework balances the necessity for swift response to crises with safeguards against abuse of power, reflecting the delicate equilibrium between effective governance and protection of fundamental rights enshrined throughout the Autumnwood Accords. See also §§ 100.3–100.7 re quorum requirements and conflict avoidance; § 200.4 re suspension of privileges during emergencies.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "100.8",
            "100.5",
            "100.4",
            "100.3",
            "200.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 100.8 Emergency Sitings",
          "text": "An emergency sitting may be convened only upon the affirmative vote of at least two-thirds of the Guild's quorum, present in person and casting legally binding votes. Such a motion requires a formal proposal detailing the nature of the crisis and the proposed resolution, accompanied by supporting testimony from no fewer than three independent witnesses or certified experts. The presiding officer shall then rule whether sufficient cause exists to proceed; absent such determination, any subsequent actions taken may be deemed null and void at the discretion of the full council upon review.\n\nOnce declared in session, emergency proceedings must adhere strictly to expedited timelines outlined herein. Debate is limited to one hour total, divided equally between proponents and opponents of the measure. All motions require a second by another member before being placed before the vote; otherwise, they shall be stricken from record without further consideration. Votes may be conducted via roll call or show of hands at the sole discretion of the chairperson, with results immediately announced aloud for all to hear. Minutes shall be recorded verbatim and distributed within twenty-four hours to all attending members.\n\nShould disagreements arise during an emergency sitting, they must be resolved through binding arbitration by a panel of three senior magisters selected randomly from those present. The arbitrators shall deliberate privately and render a unanimous decision based solely on the merits of the case as presented. Their ruling stands final and conclusive unless overturned by subsequent action of the full council within fourteen days thereof; absent such reversal, it carries the force of law across all jurisdictions subject to Guild authority. Failure to comply with an emergency directive constitutes grounds for immediate disciplinary proceedings up to and including suspension of membership privileges pending further investigation.\n\nIt is hereby mandated that any member found violating these provisions shall face automatic expulsion from current standing within the Guild, forfeiting all rights thereto absent reinstatement by unanimous vote of a newly constituted council called specifically for this purpose. This includes but is not limited to failure to declare an emergency sitting properly, obstruction thereof through malicious intent, or outright refusal to participate when duly summoned under oath. Such penalties shall apply equally regardless of rank held previously within the organization's hierarchy; no one is above the laws established by their collective will expressed freely and fully at this solemn gathering convened for these critical purposes alone.\"\n\n\"See also § 100.7 regarding foreign halls and courtesy, which complements these emergency protocols when dealing with external entities or visitors operating outside traditional Guild boundaries yet still requiring oversight during times of heightened tension or instability.\" \"Under § 200.1 et seq., licensure requirements remain in full force even amidst extraordinary circumstances unless explicitly waived by majority vote of the assembled council after thorough vetting of alternatives.\" \"The provisions outlined herein supersede all prior conflicting rules, resolutions, or informal understandings regarding emergency operations; they represent the culmination of careful deliberation aimed at balancing efficiency with fairness during unprecedented challenges.\" \"Any amendments to these standards shall require identical thresholds for approval as initial passage: two-thirds affirmative vote by qualified quorum members acting in good faith and mutual interest toward preserving peace and prosperity throughout our shared realm.\" \"In witness whereof, I hereby sign my name beneath this seal of truth, pledging allegiance unto those principles herein enshrined forevermore as guiding lights upon which we shall rely henceforth whenever darkness threatens to engulf us all once more...\"",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "100.7",
            "200.1",
            "100.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 100.8 Emergency Sitting — Unscheduled Weather and Related Disruptions",
          "text": "An \"Emergency Sitting\" is declared when conditions arise that make the orderly conduct of a Regular or Special Session impossible, threatening the safety of participants or the integrity of proceedings. Mere inclement weather, without attendant danger to persons or property, does not automatically trigger this status; such matters fall instead under § 500.2 Unscheduled Weather and are addressed through standard adjournment procedures. However, when adverse conditions escalate to include lightning strikes, falling debris, flooding, fire, gas leaks, structural compromise, or any hazard posing imminent threat to life, the Presiding Officer shall immediately convene an Emergency Sitting via remote means if physical assembly is unsafe. During such a Session, all non-essential activities cease and members focus solely on assessing risks and determining necessary protective measures. Decisions made during an Emergency Sitting carry full force unless promptly overturned by subsequent vote of the whole body. The Presiding Officer retains discretion to declare additional emergency measures as conditions warrant, acting in what they deem to be the best interests of all concerned parties. Upon resolution of the crisis or expiration of the declared emergency period, normal business resumes unless further action proves necessary. All members are obligated to comply promptly with directives issued during an Emergency Sitting failure to do so may result in disciplinary proceedings under applicable sections of this Code. The Guild reserves the right to modify these provisions as experience dictates and circumstances require.\n\n\"Emergency Sitings\" may also be convened when a member's conduct becomes sufficiently disruptive or dangerous as to impede the orderly functioning of the Assembly. This threshold is intentionally high, reserved for egregious instances such as physical threats, hate speech inciting violence, unlawful weapons display, or blatant contempt for established procedures. Upon determining that an Emergency Sitting is warranted, the Chair shall immediately adjourn and reconvene via secure telepresence platform to address the matter in closed session absent other affected parties. Such Sessions proceed expeditiously with minimal formality, prioritizing swift resolution over procedural niceties where appropriate given the gravity of circumstances prompting their convening. Any sanctions imposed must nonetheless adhere strictly to the principles laid out in § 100.5 Conflict of Interest and related provisions governing due process. The transcript of an Emergency Sitting is kept confidential except as needed for enforcement purposes, reflecting both the sensitive nature of the issues discussed and the urgent need for prompt action without delay or distraction from extraneous concerns. Should conditions stabilize sufficiently to permit resumption of regular proceedings, the Chair shall announce this formally at the next convening calling members back together with appropriate decorum restored despite whatever tensions may persist following such intense exchanges. All participants bear responsibility for maintaining civility and professionalism even under extreme duress lest they themselves become subject to disciplinary measures for failing to uphold their obligations as responsible stewards of this sacred institution.\n\n\"Emergency Sitings\" represent a necessary mechanism within our framework, enabling rapid response to evolving threats while preserving core values amid crisis. Their proper application requires both bold leadership and unwavering commitment to protecting the well-being of all involved, whether through physical safety measures or safeguarding against moral hazards posed by reckless behavior. By balancing efficiency with accountability, we ensure that even in tumultuous times our collective purpose remains clear: fostering an environment where creativity thrives free from undue constraint yet mindful of shared responsibilities binding us together as one community bound by mutual respect and common ideals. Let these principles guide us always so that no matter what storms may rage without, within ourselves we stand firm against adversity united in strength through knowledge gained hard-won over centuries past carried forward into bright futures ahead.\"\n\n\"Emergency Sitings\" are invoked only when absolutely necessary to ensure the safety of all participants and maintain the integrity of proceedings. Their declaration rests solely with the Presiding Officer who exercises this authority judiciously, weighing risks carefully before acting decisively. Once convened, an Emergency Sitting operates under expedited rules allowing for swift assessment of threats and implementation of appropriate countermeasures as needed. All members must comply fully with directives issued during such Sessions failing to do so may result in disciplinary action consistent with applicable provisions of this Code. Upon conclusion of the emergency or restoration of stable conditions, normal business resumes unless further measures prove warranted given the gravity of circumstances prompting their convening initially. Throughout these challenging moments we remain committed to upholding our highest standards while remaining flexible enough to adapt as situations demand ensuring that even in turmoil our shared vision for a better world remains unshaken.\"",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "500.2",
            "100.5",
            "100.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Emergency Sitting Protocols and Powers",
          "text": "An \"Emergency Sitting\" refers to any session of the Desk convened outside the regular calendar due to unforeseen circumstances that threaten public safety or magical stability. Such situations may arise from natural disasters, outbreaks of illegal magic, acts of war, or other crises requiring immediate intervention by the Guild's highest authorities. The power to declare an Emergency Sitting rests solely with the Archmage Sovereign or her designee, acting in consultation with a majority of the Aegis Magi present.\n\nUpon declaration, all normal procedural requirements may be suspended temporarily, allowing the Desk to act swiftly without the usual delays of debate and deliberation. This includes waiving notice periods for public hearings, streamlining evidence collection, and expediting sentencing proceedings where appropriate. However, these expedited measures must not infringe upon fundamental rights guaranteed under §§ 100.3–100.5 absent compelling justification tied directly to the emergency at hand.\n\nThe scope of an Emergency Sitting is limited strictly to addressing the immediate threat posed by the crisis event. Any actions taken beyond what is necessary to neutralize that specific danger shall be deemed ultra vires and subject to reversal upon review. Furthermore, no permanent changes to the Accords may be enacted via Emergency Sitting; all legislative amendments require full compliance with standard voting procedures outlined in § 100.3 regardless of exigency.\n\nWhen an Emergency Sitting concludes, a detailed report must be filed within seven days outlining the nature of the crisis, actions taken by the Desk and its agents, resources expended, and any lasting impacts on Guild operations or public safety. This record serves both as accountability for those wielding emergency powers and guidance for future similar situations. Failure to comply with these reporting obligations may result in disciplinary action up to and including dismissal from office.\n\nThe authority granted under this section shall be construed narrowly against the interests of individual magi, ensuring that emergency measures remain exceptional rather than routine. Any expansion of Desk powers beyond what is strictly necessary to address the stated emergency constitutes an abuse of discretion subject to challenge before the full Council. This principle applies equally whether invoked by natural disaster or artificial catastrophe wrought by rogue casters.\n\nIn sum, Emergency Sittings represent a vital exception to normal procedure during times of extreme peril, but they must be wielded with restraint and accountability. The Desk holds great power in such moments, yet that power exists only temporarily and for a narrowly defined purpose—to protect the realm from immediate harm while preserving due process wherever feasible under the circumstances.\n\nsee § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; see § 200.6 Constructs That Hold a Quill; see § 300.2 Necromancy; Unsanctioned Arts.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "100.3",
            "100.5",
            "200.6",
            "300.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
