          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 200.5 Guest Casters; Constructs That Hold a Quill — Continued",
          "text": "A \"guest caster\" is defined as an individual who renders magical services to a client without holding a valid Guild License but within the scope of their training and competence. Under § 200.1, all casting activities require licensure; however, guest casters operate under a separate regulatory framework governed by this section. Guest casters must register with the Autumnwood Accords Desk prior to offering services, submitting proof of education and references from licensed mages who vouch for their integrity and skill level. The Desk shall issue a Temporary Practice Certificate valid for no more than ninety days, renewable upon reapplication. Failure to comply with these registration requirements renders any casting performed by an unregistered guest caster void and subject to penalty under § 200.4. Guest casters are prohibited from accepting payment in Wario Coin or any currency not officially recognized by the Guild. All fees must be denominated in standard Guild Credits at prevailing exchange rates established by the Accords Desk on a quarterly basis. Violation of this provision constitutes grounds for immediate revocation of Temporary Practice Certification and referral to the Aegis Magi for investigation into potential fraud or embezzlement.\n\nConstructs That Hold a Quill refer to semi-sentient magical entities created through specialized rituals that possess limited autonomy and cognitive function sufficient to operate simple tools or devices under direction. Such constructs may be employed by licensed mages as assistants in controlled environments where human error poses unacceptable risk, such as during high-stakes ritual preparations or when handling volatile reagents. Construction of a Quill-Holding Construct requires explicit authorization from the Conservators via written permit detailing intended usage parameters and safety protocols. Unauthorized creation or deployment of such constructs violates § 200.2 regarding unauthorized field use and may result in severe sanctions including sealing of magical capabilities under § 1.9. All constructs must bear unique identification markings registered with the Accords Desk to facilitate tracking and accountability. Regular inspections by Guild auditors shall be conducted annually to ensure compliance with established safety standards and operational limitations set forth in this section. Any malfunction or mishap attributable to improper construction or misuse of a Quill-Holding Construct shall be deemed negligence on the part of its creator and may lead to disciplinary action up to and including permanent disbarment from practice under § 200.3.\n\nGuest casters operating outside registered parameters are subject to heightened scrutiny by local law enforcement agencies tasked with monitoring unlicensed magical activity in their jurisdictions. Cooperation between Guild officials and municipal authorities regarding guest caster investigations is mandatory upon request, provided such cooperation does not compromise ongoing legal proceedings or reveal confidential information protected under § 100.4. Refusal to cooperate may result in escalation of charges and invocation of emergency powers granted herein under § 100.8. Furthermore, any allegations of professional misconduct against guest casters must be adjudicated according to procedures outlined for licensed practitioners unless otherwise specified by special ruling from the Accords Desk itself. Appeals from adverse decisions rendered by guest caster review panels may only be pursued through formal channels established in Part III governing appellate review processes applicable to all regulated magic users within Guild jurisdiction. Compliance with these provisions ensures orderly integration of non-traditional magical practitioners into existing regulatory frameworks while maintaining public safety and professional standards paramount to the mission of the Autumnwood Accords as a whole.\n\nsee § 200.1 Licensure Required; see § 1.9 Seals, Stamps, and What Is Not a Seal; under § 300.1 Schedules of Arts regarding prohibited magical practices; pursuant to § 400.1 Research Permits which parallels guest caster authorization requirements.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "200.1",
            "200.4",
            "200.2",
            "1.9",
            "200.3",
            "100.4",
            "100.8",
            "300.1",
            "400.1",
            "200.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Guest Casting and Construct Liability — Continued",
          "text": "A \"guest caster,\" as defined in § 200.5, refers to an individual who provides magical services outside the scope of their primary licensure or employment contract. Such arrangements are permissible only under strict conditions intended to protect both the client and the public from potential harm arising from unregulated magical practice. Failure to adhere to these stipulations may result in disciplinary action against the guest caster by the Autumnwood Accords Desk.\n\nSpecifically, any guest casting must be conducted with full disclosure of risks, limitations, and costs prior to commencing work. The client shall sign an acknowledgment form verifying receipt of this information. Additionally, a detailed written agreement outlining the scope of services rendered must be executed by both parties before any spellwork begins. This contract serves as binding evidence should disputes arise regarding quality or payment later on.\n\nConstructs that function independently under their own power may also qualify for guest casting status if they possess sufficient intelligence and autonomy to negotiate terms directly with clients. Such entities must still comply with all applicable safety regulations and liability limitations set forth herein, regardless of their artificial nature. Failure to do so will be treated as a serious violation subject to appropriate sanctions.\n\nIn all cases involving guest casting or construct-based services, the primary caster remains ultimately responsible for overseeing operations and ensuring compliance with guild standards. They may not delegate this responsibility entirely without violating § 200.3's prohibition against unauthorized subcontracting. Any attempt to circumvent these rules will result in immediate revocation of professional credentials and possible prosecution under existing fraud statutes.\n\nBy engaging a guest caster or construct service provider, clients assume certain obligations alongside their rights. They warrant full cooperation during the engagement period and prompt settlement of outstanding balances upon completion. Furthermore, they agree not to interfere with legitimate investigations into any alleged misconduct connected to said arrangement unless formally subpoenaed by competent authorities having jurisdiction over the matter at hand.\n\nThese provisions are designed to maintain orderly conditions within the magical professions while accommodating necessary flexibility for mutually beneficial collaborations between licensed practitioners and qualified outsiders alike. Strict adherence ensures continued protection of both parties' interests under this comprehensive regulatory framework.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "200.5",
            "200.3"
          ]
        }
      ],
