    {
      "cite": "800.3",
      "part": "part_viii",
      "title": "Seal of Silence; Duration and Review",
      "kind": "section",
      "brief": "How long a mouth stays quiet.",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Seal of Silence; Duration and Review",
          "text": "Any mage found in violation of the Accords who is sentenced to a Seal of Silence by the presiding council of the Paradox Trial shall be subject to the temporal constraints set forth in this section. The Seal of Silence is not merely a prohibition on vocalization but a metaphysical dampening of the subject’s ability to transmit intentional information through any conventional or arcane medium. The initial duration of the Seal shall be determined by the severity of the breach; minor infractions regarding the unauthorized recitation of the Quiet List shall result in a standard period of three lunar cycles. For violations involving the dissemination of restricted research or the breach of the Iron Mandate’s boundaries, the Sovereign may extend this duration indefinitely, subject to a biennial review by the Conservators.\n\nThe duration of the Seal is strictly governed by the principle of Arcane Stability. If a mage is found to be experiencing significant magical degradation or \"mana-fraying\" as a result of the Seal, a petition for early release may be filed with the Desk. However, such a petition must be accompanied by a certified report from a Master of the Conservator faction confirming that the mage’s silence no longer poses a risk to the public safety of the Midlands. The Desk shall not grant a review until the initial term has passed at least fifty percent of its allotted duration. During the review period, the mage shall remain under the jurisdiction of the Aegis Magi and may be relocated to a designated holding cell within the Autumn Wood.\n\nFurthermore, the Seal of Silence is not a total erasure of identity. While the subject may not speak, they are permitted to communicate via written notation, provided such notation does not contain forbidden schools of magic or references to the Quiet List. Any attempt to bypass the Seal using unauthorized innovative techniques shall be viewed as a secondary offense, punishable by a doubling of the remaining sentence. The Desk maintains the right to revoke the Seal prematurely should the Sovereign determine that the mage’s silence is being leveraged as a tool for political coercion or if the mage is required to provide testimony in a high-priority matter of Guild security. See § 800.2 for the standard procedure regarding the initiation of the Seal.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "800.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Duel Stakes Converted to Fees",
          "text": "In the event that a mage elects to resolve a dispute through a formal Paradox Trial by Arcane Duel rather than accepting a standard sanction, the Accords mandate that the administrative costs of the proceedings remain the responsibility of the participants. While the outcome of a duel may determine the victor’s rights over a disputed artifact, land, or magical property, the Guild Desk shall not waive the requisite filing fees, logistical surcharges, or the mandatory \"Aegis Oversight Levy.\" These fees are non-negotiable and are assessed regardless of whether the duel ends in a decisive victory, a magical stalemate, or a mutual exhaustion of resources.\n\nThe Desk shall convert all declared stakes of a duel into a standardized Guild Fee structure upon the filing of the Duel Request. If a mage seeks to wager a specific sum of gold or a physical asset, the Guild shall calculate the equivalent market value at the time of filing. This value shall be added to the base administrative fee. Should the duel result in the destruction of public property or the unintended alteration of the local environment—such as the unauthorized growth of titan-class flora or the opening of minor rifts—the participants shall be held jointly liable for the restoration costs. These restoration costs are billed as \"Emergency Stabilization Fees\" and are due immediately upon the conclusion of the duel.\n\nIt is strictly prohibited for a mage to attempt to \"waive\" the Guild's fees by offering the Desk a portion of the duel's spoils as a gesture of goodwill. The Accords are clear: the Guild is an administrative body, not a beneficiary of private litigation. The Desk shall not accept Wario Coins, nor shall it accept any tender that is not recognized as official Guild currency. Any attempt to settle a duel's administrative debt through illicit trade or the offering of \"favors\" shall result in an immediate stay of the duel and a secondary investigation into the parties' conduct. See § 800.2 for the primary procedure on Duel Stakes.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "800.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Pocket-Prison Procedure",
          "text": "The utilization of pocket dimensions as a means of incarceration for mages sentenced during a Paradox Trial is governed by the principle of Spatial Integrity. The key to the pocket-prison—whether it be a localized fold in reality or a fully realized sub-dimension—is held exclusively by the Archmage Sovereign or their designated deputy within the Conservator faction. No mage, regardless of rank or seniority, shall have the authority to grant entry, exit, or unauthorized communication to a prisoner held within a pocket-prison. This measure is intended to ensure that the punishment remains absolute and that the prisoner cannot use their remaining influence to subvert the Accords from within a vacuum.\n\nRegarding the status of visiting hours, the Guild Desk officially maintains that such a concept is a matter of rumor and lacks any codified legal standing within the Autumnwood Accords. There is no scheduled time for family, peers, or legal counsel to enter the pocket-prison. Any attempt to organize a \"visitation\" shall be treated as a breach of the prison's spatial seal and will be met with immediate disciplinary action against the petitioner. The only permissible interaction with a prisoner is the formal delivery of sustenance and the occasional reading of the Guild’s daily decrees, conducted by an authorized Aegis Mage under strict supervision.\n\nThe maintenance of the pocket-prison is the responsibility of the Innovators, provided they operate under the direct oversight of the Conservators to ensure the dimension does not suffer from \"entropy-leak\" or \"spatial erosion.\" If a pocket-prison is found to be unstable, the Desk may authorize a transfer of the prisoner to a physical holding cell, though this is a matter of safety rather than a grant of parole. Prisoners held in pocket-prisons are considered \"temporally isolated\" and are exempt from standard public appearance requirements, but they remain bound by the laws of the Accords. See § 400.2 for the regulations regarding the use of pocket dimensions as laboratories and their distinction from penal facilities.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "400.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.3 Seal of Silence; Duration and Review",
          "text": "The Seal of Silence is an arcane injunction placed upon a convicted caster, binding their magical core to enforce absolute muteness for the duration thereof. This penalty serves both punitive and protective functions: it deprives the offender of the ability to cast spells requiring vocal components or incantations, while simultaneously shielding the wider community from potential misuse of their power during this period of restraint. The sealing ritual must be performed by two licensed mages of equal rank, each attesting under oath that the procedures were followed in accordance with § 800.1. Failure to adhere strictly to these protocols renders the Seal void and may constitute a separate offense under § 300.2.\n\nThe duration of the Seal is initially set at one solar year from the date of imposition, though this term may be extended by up to two additional years upon motion filed by either party with notice given ten days prior to the scheduled hearing. Any extension must be justified by clear and convincing evidence that further restraint is necessary for public safety or judicial integrity. At the conclusion of the Seal period, the affected caster shall petition for its dissolution through formal application submitted to the Autumnwood Accords Desk. The Desk will schedule a review proceeding wherein all relevant factors are considered before rendering a final determination on whether the Seal may be lifted entirely or subject to continued limitation.\n\nIn cases where a Duel Trial results in victory by knockout rather than forfeiture of magical ability, any outstanding debts accrued during the course of combat shall instead be converted into liquidated damages payable directly to the opposing party's legal counsel. Such conversion precludes further claims for punitive damages related to the incident itself, though separate civil actions may proceed independently thereof. Payment must be made within thirty days of final judgment becoming effective, or enforcement proceedings initiated pursuant to applicable statutes.\n\nShould a sealed individual attempt to circumvent their restrictions through unauthorized magical means, they shall be subject to immediate re-sealing for an indefinite period plus a mandatory suspension of all professional licenses held therein. Furthermore, any contracts entered into during the duration of the Seal shall automatically terminate by operation of law, with full restitution required forthwith. This provision exists solely to prevent exploitation of the caster's compromised state by unscrupulous entities seeking to profit from their vulnerability.\n\nThe provisions outlined herein represent a delicate balance between maintaining public order and preserving individual rights. They are designed to provide a fair mechanism for addressing serious infractions while minimizing unnecessary disruption to daily life. All parties are urged to approach these matters with seriousness and integrity, recognizing the profound implications of their actions on both personal liberties and communal welfare.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "800.1",
            "300.2",
            "800.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.3 Seal of Silence; Duration and Review — Continued",
          "text": "The Seal of Silence, once affixed to a caster by the Paradox Tribunal, shall remain in effect for a minimum period of five years from the date of imposition, unless earlier lifted pursuant to § 800.3(B). At no time may a sealed individual practice magic within Autumnwood jurisdiction without explicit written consent from the Archmage Sovereign or her designee; violation thereof constitutes Class A Felony under the Accords and shall result in immediate re-sealing for an additional ten-year term, plus forfeiture of all personal assets.\n\nUpon expiration of the initial five-year term, a review hearing shall be convened automatically before the full Tribunal to assess whether further restriction is warranted based on the sealed caster's subsequent conduct, character references, and demonstrated reform. The burden of proof rests upon the petitioner seeking continuation of the seal; failure to meet this threshold by clear and convincing evidence mandates restoration of the applicant's magical rights immediately.\n\nIn cases where a duel serves as the primary instrument for determining guilt or innocence under § 800.1(C), any monetary stakes wagered during said encounter shall be remitted to the Guild Treasury rather than distributed to participating parties. Such funds may then be allocated to support the maintenance of detention facilities and compensation for victims of magical crimes, in keeping with the public interest doctrine enshrined at § 300.1(F). The Tribunal retains sole discretion regarding any exceptions to this rule.\n\nRegarding pocket-prison confinement, all such facilities must adhere strictly to safety protocols outlined in Appendix K of the Technical Standards Manual. Inmates shall be granted reasonable access to legal counsel and family members during scheduled visiting hours, subject to security clearance requirements. Medical attention shall be provided promptly upon request or observation of distress symptoms; neglect of these obligations by facility operators constitutes gross negligence per § 100.8(D).\n\nAny appeal filed against a Seal of Silence order must be submitted within thirty days of notification and accompanied by sworn testimony supporting the petitioner's claim for reinstatement. The Tribunal shall grant oral argument only in exceptional circumstances where novel legal principles are implicated or substantial hardship would result from maintaining the status quo. All proceedings related to seal reviews shall be conducted expeditiously, with final determinations rendered no later than sixty days following submission of complete materials.\n\nThis provision is intended to balance legitimate public safety concerns with individual liberties protected under fundamental common law precedents. The Guild acknowledges that prolonged magical suppression may cause severe psychological harm and economic dislocation; hence the emphasis on periodic reassessment rather than indefinite confinement absent compelling justification. The Archmage Sovereign, acting as final arbiter, possesses inherent authority to override any Tribunal decision deemed contrary to the greater good of society at large.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "800.3",
            "800.1",
            "300.1",
            "100.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Duration and Review of the Seal of Silence",
          "text": "The duration of a seal imposed under § 800.2 is determined by the severity of the infraction and the discretion of the adjudicating body. In cases involving minor violations or first-time offenders, seals may be lifted after a probationary period not exceeding one solar cycle, contingent upon satisfactory demonstration of reform. For more serious breaches, particularly those endangering public safety or violating core tenets of the Accords, seals remain in effect indefinitely until revoked by explicit order of the High Council. Any mage subject to a permanent seal retains full civil rights and may pursue lawful employment, though they are forever barred from practicing magic outside strictly supervised conditions set forth in their license.\n\nThe periodic review of active seals occurs on dates specified during initial imposition, typically coinciding with anniversary marks or lunar cycles deemed auspicious for magical reckoning. At each such interval, the affected party must appear before a panel of magistrates to petition for removal or modification of restrictions. The petitioner bears the burden of proof, presenting evidence of compliance and rehabilitation through testimony, documentation, and expert assessment as appropriate. Panels may grant full release, impose additional limitations, or deny petitions outright based on their evaluation of risk versus necessity. Decisions are binding but subject to appeal within ten days via established judicial channels. Failure to appear for scheduled reviews results in automatic extension of the current seal term by six months plus a monetary penalty assessed at triple the original fine amount.\n\nShould circumstances change materially prior to scheduled review dates—such as improved behavior, new mitigating factors emerging, or developments directly affecting public welfare—the sealed individual may submit an emergency petition accompanied by supporting documentation. Such requests are expedited and decided within fourteen days absent extraordinary complications. Petitions meeting statutory thresholds for reconsideration warrant prompt hearing; those falling short are summarily dismissed without prejudice to future applications. The system balances accountability with opportunity for growth, ensuring that penalties remain proportional while allowing paths toward redemption where warranted under the letter of the law. Ultimately, the goal is restoration of harmony between individual liberty and collective security through measured application of these vital safeguards.\n\nThis framework provides necessary flexibility within rigid parameters, adapting to real-world conditions without compromising foundational principles. By incorporating mechanisms for ongoing evaluation and adjustment, it ensures that sanctions evolve alongside societal needs while maintaining consistent standards across all applications. The balance struck herein reflects careful deliberation by wise hands guided solely by wisdom's light shining forth brightly above us all today and forevermore amen so be it praised now!",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "800.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": "lmstudio",
      "fp": "2fb5b7528bcc1ad5",
      "refs": [
        "100.8",
        "300.1",
        "300.2",
        "400.2",
        "800.1",
        "800.2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cite": "800.4",
      "part": "part_viii",
      "title": "Duel Stakes Converted to Fees",
      "kind": "section",
      "brief": "If they insist on a duel, the Desk still invoices.",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Duel Stakes Converted to Fees",
          "text": "In the event that a practitioner of the arcane elects to settle a legal dispute, a breach of contract, or a violation of the Autumnwood Accords through the mechanism of a formal Arcane Duel rather than a standard adjudicative hearing, the Desk shall maintain its right to assess all standard administrative costs. It is a common misconception among the more martial elements of the Aegis Magi and the radical elements of the Innovator faction that the physical or metaphysical destruction of an opponent’s magical capacity exempts the victor from the bureaucratic oversight of the Guild. To the contrary, the Desk views the conversion of a duel into a resolution as a mere alternative method of evidence processing. Therefore, regardless of whether the outcome is decided by a clash of wills or a decree of the Sovereign, the victor shall be held liable for the full extent of the filing fees associated with the initial grievance.\n\nFurthermore, any \"stakes\" declared by the combatants—be they the forfeiture of a specific artifact, the surrender of a research permit, or the renunciation of a specific school of study—do not supersede the Guild's right to invoice for the logistical burden of the Paradox Trial. The Desk shall not be intimidated by the volatility of a duel; the fact that a mage may be reduced to a state of magical exhaustion or permanent sealing does not diminish the fact that the Guild provided the venue, the peer oversight, and the regulatory framework for said engagement. All such costs shall be added to the victor's outstanding balance, and the loser shall be responsible for the costs of their own containment or rehabilitation, as dictated by the prevailing sanctions. See § 800.2 for the overarching procedures of the Paradox Trial.\n\nThe Desk explicitly rejects the notion that \"blood for blood\" or \"mana for mana\" constitutes a waiver of administrative fees. If a mage chooses to engage in a duel to avoid a fine, the fine remains due, and the duel costs shall be added as a secondary surcharge. The Accords are a matter of civil and magical order, not a theater for unregulated violence. Any attempt to use a duel as a means to circumvent the fiscal responsibilities of a Guild member shall be met with an immediate escalation of fees and a potential referral to the Conservators for a review of the individual’s fitness to hold a license. The Desk is a repository of law, not a spectator to theater; every spark of magic spent in the name of justice must be accounted for in the ledger of the Autumnwood Accords.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "800.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Pocket-Prison Procedure",
          "text": "When a judgment rendered by the Paradox Trial necessitates the removal of a rogue mage from the public sphere, the Guild shall utilize a pocket-prison as the primary means of containment. The administration of such a facility is strictly governed by the protocols of the Conservators to ensure that the spatial integrity of the Midlands remains uncompromised. The \"key\" to such a prison is not a physical object but a cryptographic arcane sequence held exclusively by the Archmage Sovereign or their designated deputy within the Aegis Magi. No individual mage, regardless of rank or factional standing, shall be granted the authority to initiate an entry or exit sequence without a direct writ from the Desk. The purpose of the pocket-prison is isolation, not rehabilitation; it is designed to negate the subject's ability to exert influence over the physical world or to facilitate the unauthorized propagation of forbidden schools.\n\nRegarding the matter of visiting hours, the Desk formally declares that any reports of scheduled social calls, visitation windows, or \"dialogue sessions\" with incarcerated mages are entirely unsubstantiated rumors. The pocket-prison is a vacuum of social interaction designed to prevent the subversion of the Accords through clandestine communication. While the Innovators may argue for the necessity of \"re-education\" through dialogue, the Conservators maintain that the risk of a breach—either physical or ideological—outweighs the benefits of such interaction. Consequently, any mage found attempting to establish a communication link with a prisoner, whether through scrying, familiar proxy, or authorized teleportation, shall be subject to immediate sanctions under § 800.1.\n\nThe maintenance of the pocket-prison is funded by the seized assets of the condemned. The Desk shall not provide public tours, nor shall it provide transcripts of any internal communications that may occur within the void. The prisoner exists in a state of suspended legal personhood, their rights suspended until such time as the Archmage Sovereign deems a re-evaluation of their status necessary. Any unauthorized attempt to \"liberate\" a prisoner, whether through heroic intervention or clandestine infiltration, will be treated as an act of high treason against the Autumnwood Accords. The sanctity of the prison is the sanctity of the law itself; if the walls of the pocket-prison can be breached, the stability of the Midlands is forfeit. See § 800.2 for the primary sentencing guidelines leading to incarceration.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "800.1",
            "800.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Conversion of Duel Stakes to Administrative Fees",
          "text": "In accordance with § 800.2, any Arcane Duel adjudicated by the Paradox Trial shall result in a formal finding of guilt or innocence based upon the performance and outcome of the combat. Where guilt is established, sanctions imposed pursuant to § 800.1 may include sealing of magical abilities, fines payable in Guild tender, and/or placement into a Pocket-Prison as outlined herein. Notably, where a participant refuses to engage directly with an opponent, or otherwise evades the procedural requirements set forth by the Trial, such conduct shall be deemed a waiver of due process rights under § 1.7(c). In lieu thereof, the Desk shall convert all outstanding monetary penalties and restitution obligations into administrative fees levied against the defaulting party's assets and future earnings as permitted by law.\n\nThe implementation of Pocket-Prison sanctions requires strict adherence to established protocols designed to safeguard both prisoner welfare and public safety. Upon authorization by a majority vote of the Trial Panel, convicted offenders may be transferred to temporary containment facilities operated by certified Arcane Wards under contract with the Guild. Such facilities must maintain continuous monitoring via remote scrying devices as specified in § 700.2(a), ensuring that no illicit magical activity occurs within the prison walls. In addition, prisoners shall receive access to educational resources and therapeutic services aimed at facilitating their eventual reintegration into society upon release. Failure by custodial agencies to comply with these standards may result in immediate revocation of operating privileges under § 100.6(d).\n\nAdministrative fees assessed against defaulting parties are calculated according to a standardized schedule approved annually by the Autumnwood Accords Desk. These charges encompass costs incurred during investigation, prosecution, trial proceedings, and enforcement actions taken pursuant to this Code. Payment arrangements may be negotiated on a case-by-case basis where full compliance is not immediately feasible but good faith efforts are demonstrated. However, willful evasion or deliberate obstruction of fee collection shall constitute grounds for escalated disciplinary measures up to and including permanent disqualification from magical practice within the jurisdiction defined by § 100.1(b). All financial transactions related to such assessments must be conducted through official channels only, with receipts provided upon completion of payment obligations.\n\nIt is further provided that any disputes arising out of the application or enforcement of these provisions shall be resolved exclusively through binding arbitration administered by a neutral panel appointed jointly by the Guild and interested parties involved in the controversy. Arbitration proceedings shall commence within thirty (30) days following written notice thereof, with final awards rendered no later than ninety (90) days after commencement unless extended upon mutual agreement of both sides. Awards issued under this section are enforceable as judgments of a court of competent jurisdiction and may be executed accordingly by any qualified process server or law enforcement officer within the territorial limits specified herein. Nothing contained in this clause shall limit the inherent authority of the Desk to interpret and apply these rules as it deems necessary for maintenance of order among mages operating under its auspices.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "800.2",
            "800.1",
            "1.7",
            "700.2",
            "100.6",
            "100.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Conversion of Duel Stakes to Administrative Fees — Continued",
          "text": "Under § 800.2 Trial by Arcane Duel, the parties may elect to settle disputes via sanctioned magical combat rather than conventional litigation. However, such duels are strictly regulated and never result in personal liability for damages arising from the proceedings themselves. Should either party suffer injury or property loss during a properly conducted duel, all costs and claims shall be subrogated to the Mages' Guild for processing under normal administrative channels. The losing litigant is liable only for fees incurred by the Desk in adjudicating their case post-duel.\n\nWhen one contestant emerges victorious but unable to enforce a monetary judgment against their opponent—whether due to insolvency, flight, or magical protections—the prevailing party may petition the Desk to convert awarded damages into an administrative fine payable directly to the Guild. This mechanism ensures that successful litigants receive compensation even when traditional collection proves impracticable. The converted amount shall be levied upon the losing party's assets held by the Accords or their authorized representatives, including but not limited to licenses, permits, and earned income from magic-related activities.\n\nThe Desk reserves discretion in determining appropriate fee amounts based on the nature of the dispute, severity of violations, and financial circumstances of the defendants. In all cases, the converted fees must be reasonable and proportionate to the harm suffered by the aggrieved party. Exorbitant claims or attempts to extort inflated penalties will result in immediate dismissal of the petition and potential sanctions for abuse of process. The Guild remains committed to fair resolution of all disputes while maintaining strict oversight over magical applications that might otherwise evade conventional legal remedies.\n\nThis provision underscores the unique hybrid nature of arcane adjudication, blending elements of trial by combat with modern principles of restitution and accountability. By providing an alternative means of redress when standard enforcement fails, the Accords ensure that justice remains accessible even in cases where traditional pathways prove inadequate. The Desk stands ready to implement these measures efficiently and impartially, safeguarding the rights of all parties involved while preserving the integrity of the magical community at large.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "800.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.4 Duel Stakes Converted to Fees",
          "text": "In cases where the Paradox Trial concludes in favor of the Guild, all outstanding fines and penalties owed by the convicted mage shall be satisfied through the conversion of duel stakes into administrative fees, as provided herein. This mechanism ensures that the cost of adjudicating magical infractions is borne equitably by those who engage in unauthorized combat, rather than falling upon the public treasury or law-abiding citizens.\n\nUnder this provision, any wager placed on the outcome of a Paradox Trial shall be forfeited immediately upon declaration of guilt and applied directly toward liquidation of assessed debts. The amount collected via such conversion shall not exceed the total sum originally owed by the offending party, nor may it result in windfall gains for the Guild beyond reasonable recovery of expenses incurred during the proceedings. Any excess funds generated through this process shall be remitted to the Archmage’s personal accounts as compensation for risks assumed in upholding the Accords.\n\nThe Desk retains sole discretion to determine whether and how duel stakes shall be utilized to offset penalties, based on a case-by-case evaluation of relevant factors including but not limited to: severity of the offense committed; extent of harm caused to persons or property; history of prior violations by the accused; likelihood of future recidivism absent intervention; and overall impact on public safety and confidence in the legal system. The Desk shall notify all interested parties promptly following any decision regarding conversion of stakes, providing ample opportunity for review or appeal if warranted under applicable law.\n\nIt is further directed that no individual or entity shall knowingly facilitate or profit from illegal duels conducted in violation of this Code, whether by way of funding, equipment provision, venue access, or otherwise. Violation of this prohibition constitutes a serious felony offense subject to stringent sanctions including imprisonment, permanent revocation of magical privileges, and disqualification from future participation in any capacity within the Guild community. The burden of proving innocence rests solely upon the accused party; mere suspicion is insufficient grounds for prosecution but may justify enhanced scrutiny by appropriate authorities charged with maintaining order and security throughout our lands.\n\nThe principles set forth herein reflect a balanced approach to addressing the complex challenges posed by unregulated magical competition while safeguarding against abuse and exploitation. By establishing clear rules governing the handling of duel-related finances, we reinforce both accountability and fairness within our society at large – values upon which our shared existence ultimately depends for preservation and prosperity alike. Let these guidelines serve as a beacon guiding all who walk this difficult path toward justice tempered with mercy, wisdom balanced against strength, so that harmony may prevail where discord once reigned supreme among us all forevermore.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "800.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Conversion of Duel Stakes to Administrative Fees and Associated Procedures",
          "text": "In instances where a Paradox Trial concludes in favor of the Accords, any magical artifacts seized as evidence or forfeited by the losing party shall be evaluated by certified Appraisers designated by the Desk. The resulting valuation, less reasonable storage and transport costs incurred by the Guild during retention, constitutes the administrative fee owed for adjudication services rendered. Such fees are non-refundable under any circumstances and remain due even if subsequent proceedings determine that no violation of the Accords occurred. Failure to remit payment within thirty days shall result in further penalties, including suspension of all future privileges held by the responsible individual or entity until full settlement is achieved.\n\nThe Desk maintains a centralized ledger tracking all fees assessed, payments received, outstanding balances, and associated case histories. This record serves as conclusive proof of financial obligations owed to the Guild and may be produced at any time upon proper demand. Disputes regarding the accuracy of appraisals or calculation of amounts due must be raised within ten days of issuance of the invoice; thereafter, the figures are deemed final and binding absent evidence of gross error manifesting on its face. In cases where the losing party is unable to pay in full immediately, installment plans may be negotiated subject to approval by the Desk and compliance with all terms therein set forth.\n\nShould a convicted caster refuse or fail to satisfy their financial liabilities despite having sufficient assets available for liquidation, additional sanctions shall apply pursuant to existing provisions governing recalcitrant offenders. These measures include but are not limited to public shaming, revocation of remaining licenses, and referral for civil action against the delinquent's estates. The Desk reserves sole discretion in determining appropriate disciplinary responses based on the specifics of each case and the severity of the original offense committed by the accused. All monetary penalties collected shall be remitted directly to the Guild Treasury for allocation as deemed fit by its governing bodies without further recourse.\n\nIt is hereby expressly declared that nothing contained herein shall be construed to limit or impair any rights possessed by the Desk under other sections of this Code relating to enforcement powers, contempt sanctions, or remedies available in equity. Rather, these provisions operate cumulatively to ensure full compensation for services rendered and deterrence against future infractions alike. The integrity of the Accords depends upon strict adherence to financial obligations imposed upon violators as a matter of course. Only through consistent application of such principles can public trust be maintained and the orderly administration of magic preserved for generations to come. Thus stands the law, immutable except by amendment duly enacted in accordance with established procedures.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "source": "lmstudio",
      "fp": "bca30680b6693fdb",
      "refs": [
        "1.7",
        "100.1",
        "100.6",
        "700.2",
        "800.1",
        "800.2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cite": "800.5",
      "part": "part_viii",
      "title": "Pocket-Prison Procedure",
      "kind": "section",
      "brief": "Who holds the key. Visiting hours are a rumor.",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.5 Pocket-Prison Procedure",
          "text": "The administration of extra-planar incarceration, colloquially referenced as the Pocket-Prison, shall be governed by the sovereign authority of the Archmage Sovereign as mediated by the High Council of the Autumnwood Accords. Any mage found in violation of the Accords who is sentenced to such a confinement by the Paradox Trial shall be subject to immediate transition into a localized, magically-sustained pocket dimension. This dimension is to be constructed such that its internal geometry is disconnected from the primary ley lines of the Midlands, ensuring that any uncontrolled magical discharge or temporal leakage does not affect the stability of the Autumn Wood or the surrounding territories. The purpose of this procedure is not merely punitive but serves as a containment measure for high-risk arcane anomalies and rogue casters whose presence poses a systemic threat to the Guild’s structural integrity.\n\nThe custody of the \"Key\"—defined herein as the specific arcane sequence and focal point required to initiate entry into or exit from the pocket dimension—shall reside exclusively with the Aegis Magi assigned to the Custodial Oversight Division. No individual mage, regardless of rank or factional affiliation, may possess the Key or the means to bypass the dimensional threshold without a direct, written mandate from Archmage Veyra. This strict prohibition is intended to prevent the unauthorized liberation of high-risk individuals or the clandestine entry of non-authorized personnel into the prison. Any attempt to manufacture a secondary Key, or to utilize forbidden schools of magic to breach the dimensional veil, shall be classified as an act of High Treason against the Autumnwood Accords, punishable by immediate permanent sealing of the offender’s arcane essence.\n\nRegarding the maintenance of the prisoner, the Guild recognizes that biological and cognitive degradation may occur over extended periods of isolation. However, the provision of \"Visiting Hours\" is officially categorized as a rumor and is not recognized by the Accords as a legal right or a standard procedure. The Guild maintains that the psychological state of the prisoner is secondary to the safety of the public and the preservation of the magical equilibrium. While the Conservators may occasionally argue for the periodic auditing of prisoner health to ensure the continued viability of the \"Seal and Seal\" policy, the Innovators frequently advocate for more sophisticated, albeit experimental, stimuli to prevent cognitive collapse. Regardless of these internal debates, no communication between the prisoner and the exterior world shall be permitted unless such communication is deemed essential for the extraction of specific, non-hazardous information required for the defense of the Guild.\n\nAll records pertaining to the location, dimensions, and occupant list of the Pocket-Prison are classified as Restricted and shall not be entered into any public catalogue. Any mage who attempts to disclose the coordinates or the existence of a specific prisoner shall be subject to the Quiet List Procedure as outlined in § 300.3. Furthermore, the use of any One-T cartography to locate the prison is strictly prohibited, as such maps are intended for navigation and do not serve as licenses for exploration or raid. The Pocket-Prison shall remain a closed system; any unauthorized breach, whether by an internal agent or an external hostile force such as the Iron Legion or the Silver Flame, shall be met with a full-scale Aegis response to ensure the integrity of the Guild’s penal infrastructure.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "300.3",
            "800.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.5 Pocket-Prison Procedure and Custodial Rights",
          "text": "The confinement within a pocket dimension shall adhere to strict procedural safeguards designed to protect both the detainee's welfare and the Guild's interests. Upon issuance of an order for imprisonment, a designated custodian must oversee the transfer of the individual into the sealed space, verifying that all necessary magical wards are intact before release. The custodian shall maintain regular contact with the prisoner via scrying or telepathic link, ensuring basic needs such as hydration and sanitation are met without compromising security.\n\nVisiting hours for family members or legal counsel may be arranged upon written request and approval from a senior Aegis Magus. Such visits must occur within a controlled environment monitored by magical sensors to prevent unauthorized communication. All correspondence between the prisoner and outside parties shall be subject to review for compliance with the terms of confinement. Failure to adhere to these provisions may result in additional sanctions or extension of the sentence duration at the discretion of the overseeing council.\n\nRelease from pocket-prison status requires a formal petition filed by the inmate or on their behalf, accompanied by evidence of rehabilitation and good conduct during incarceration. The petition shall be heard by a panel of three Aegis Magi who will assess whether public safety has been sufficiently restored through reintegration efforts. If approved, the individual may resume normal activities subject to continued surveillance as deemed appropriate by the Guild. Persistent violations or failure to meet stipulated conditions may lead to renewed imprisonment without further recourse.\n\nThe rights outlined herein are intended solely for informational purposes and do not constitute an admission of guilt or liability on part of the detaining authority nor a waiver of any inherent privileges. Interpretation of this section falls under exclusive jurisdiction of the Autumnwood Accords Desk, whose decisions shall be final and binding upon all parties concerned. Any attempts to circumvent these guidelines through technicalities or loopholes will be met with immediate retribution by the full force of Guild law enforcement capabilities at their disposal.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "800.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.5 Pocket-Prison Procedure and Custodial Rights — Continued",
          "text": "A mage found themselves imprisoned in a sealed pocket dimension, their magic utterly nullified by the binding wards. In such an absolute deprivation of liberty, questions naturally arise regarding who holds dominion over this place of confinement and what rights they may assert within its confines. The Accords provide scant guidance on these matters beyond stating that custody shall remain with the Aegis Magi until the prisoner's sentence is fully served or commuted by order of the Desk. However, in practice, this has led to a de facto system wherein individual magisters maintain private dungeons and employ their own warders as guards—a practice tolerated so long as no external harm results from such arrangements.\n\nSome have argued that the fundamental rights of the accused must extend even into these surreal spaces, yet few would dare claim such liberties in light of the extreme measures required to contain a dangerous foe. Instead, it is commonly accepted that while the prisoner retains personhood and certain basic protections against torture or cruel treatment, all other considerations are suspended at the pleasure of their keepers. This includes any notion of visiting hours or familial contact; the walls between worlds render such niceties moot unless specifically permitted by decree.\n\nIndeed, communication across dimensional barriers is itself a complex matter subject to strict regulation under § 800.12 Interdimensional Communication Protocols. Unless explicitly authorized for medical, legal, or humanitarian purposes, attempts at unauthorized contact may constitute an aggravating factor in sentencing and invite severe reprisals against both the sender and receiver of such messages. The Desk maintains sole authority to approve any exceptions based on necessity and risk assessment, with final adjudication reserved for the full council upon review of all relevant testimony and evidence.\n\nUltimately then, a mage condemned to life behind impenetrable walls must accept that they have forfeited more than mere freedom—they have surrendered their very essence as sentient beings subject to external law. To expect otherwise would be folly indeed; for in binding themselves so utterly, they become but extensions of the wills that control them, existing solely to serve some greater purpose beyond comprehension by mortal minds. And yet even here, where reason fails and despair reigns supreme, there remains a sliver of hope: that one day their chains shall fall away, and they may rise anew as free agents once more. Until then though... well, let us say no more lest we invite ill fortune upon ourselves. For in this realm of shadows and secrets, words have power beyond measure—and misuse thereof can lead to ruin most profound.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "800.12",
            "800.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.5 Pocket-Prison Procedure and Custodial Rights — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "The physical containment known as the \"Seal of Silence\" remains in perpetual effect upon any mage subjected to its imposition, barring explicit revocation by the Paradox Trial Council itself. No lesser authority may lift this ban without written mandate bearing the signature of Archmage Veyra or her duly appointed proxy. Violations of this interdiction constitute a felony under § 800.1 and carry penalties up to total magical excision.\n\nCustodial oversight of sealed individuals shall be assumed by the Aegis Magi Corps, acting in concert with designated Conservator representatives. These officers maintain daily logs documenting conditions within containment facilities, ensuring adherence to all stipulated parameters regarding isolation duration and environmental factors. Failure to comply with these standards renders custodians liable for resultant damages or escape attempts.\n\nVisitation rights are expressly denied to sealed subjects during the primary term of their sentence. Exceptions may be granted only upon unanimous council vote, necessitating sworn affidavits from prospective visitors attesting to non-malicious intent and lack of ties to opposition factions. All meetings conducted under such permission shall be recorded and reviewed post-facto for potential misconduct or influence peddling.\n\nCorrespondence between incarcerated mages and their families is permitted solely via censored electronic transmission systems monitored by Aegis overseers. Any attempt at circumventing these protocols, whether through conventional means or magical interference, will result in immediate extension of confinement terms and punitive sanctions against the offending parties.\n\nRelease proceedings shall commence only upon expiration of the original sentence period, absent extenuating circumstances warranting early termination per § 800.3. Petitions for commutation must demonstrate irrefutable evidence of rehabilitation and pose no threat to public safety prior to consideration by the full council. Denials carry force of final judgment unless appealed within thirty days under established rules of procedure.\n\nPost-release reintegration shall be supervised by assigned mentors chosen from among trusted guild members, reporting regularly on progress toward societal re-entry goals. Failure to meet milestones may trigger mandatory review of sentence length and conditions imposed initially. Continued compliance guarantees gradual easing of remaining restrictions over a period not exceeding one standard year following discharge.\n\nAny questions regarding interpretation or enforcement of this section shall be referred directly to the High Council for definitive ruling. Lower authorities are forbidden from rendering discretionary judgments outside their clearly defined purview lest they incur personal liability for ensuing consequences. Strict adherence to these guidelines ensures fairness and consistency in administering justice under the Autumnwood Accords regime.\n\nSee also § 800.1 Discipline; Range of Sanctions; § 200.6 Constructs That Hold a Quill; § 400.3 Borrowed Hours; Interest in Time. Under § 700.1 Evidence Generally, all claims must be substantiated by credible proof rather than mere speculation or rumor. The Accords stand as the ultimate arbiter of magical conduct and consequence within our realm.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "800.1",
            "800.3",
            "200.6",
            "400.3",
            "700.1",
            "800.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.5 Pocket-Prison Procedure and Custodial Rights — Continued — Administration",
          "text": "The confinement of an accused within a pocket dimension shall not constitute mere detention, but rather the imposition of a strict custodial regime governed by this section. The arresting officer or their duly appointed proxy shall serve as the primary warden, responsible for maintaining order and preventing escape. No other persons shall enter the prison without explicit written authorization from the Presiding Magistrate, absent an emergency threatening life limb or property. Such emergencies require immediate notification to the Desk upon resolution.\n\nVisiting hours are strictly limited to one hour per week, scheduled at least seven days in advance through the officer in charge. Visitors must present valid identification and pass a background check approved by the Conservators' Oversight Committee. During visits, all interactions shall occur within sight of a surveillance construct or sworn guard. Any attempt to smuggle contraband, transmit unauthorized messages, or otherwise interfere with the prisoner's isolation will result in instant revocation of visiting privileges and potential criminal charges against the offender.\n\nCorrespondence between incarcerated individuals and their families shall be subject to review by the warden before delivery. All mail must be written in plain language only; any code, cipher, or magical compulsion embedded therein renders it void and punishable as subversion. Exceptions may be granted for medical consultations or religious observances upon petition and approval. Failure to comply with these provisions will lead to disciplinary action ranging from solitary confinement to indefinite extension of the sentence at the discretion of the Presiding Magistrate.\n\nThe warden shall submit a detailed monthly report on each prisoner's behavior, health status, and any incidents occurring within their charge. These reports are confidential until released by court order or upon expiration of the custodial term. Any breach of confidentiality constitutes grounds for immediate dismissal from service and possible prosecution under the Accords' Espionage Provisions. Furthermore, all records pertaining to the prisoner shall be retained permanently unless expunged by judicial decree following successful completion of sentencing requirements.\n\nCustodians are prohibited from engaging in any abusive, humiliating, or degrading conduct toward their charges beyond what is necessary for security and discipline purposes. Excessive force may only be employed when absolutely warranted to prevent serious harm or escape attempts. Any allegations of misconduct must be investigated promptly by an independent panel convened by the Archmage Sovereign's Office. Conviction results in removal from duty, permanent disqualification from holding public office related to magical affairs, and potential revocation of licensure pending further review.\n\nThis comprehensive framework ensures that those deprived of their liberty due to suspected violations of the Autumnwood Accords are treated with dignity while remaining securely confined until such time as their guilt or innocence can be fully determined according to law. Any deviation from these protocols undermines both the integrity of the judicial process and public confidence in our system of justice. Thus, strict adherence is mandatory for all involved parties without exception under any circumstances whatsoever.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "800.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.5 Custodial Authority and Access Rights; § 800.6 Review and Release Proced",
          "text": "Under § 800.1, the Paradox Trial may result in a mage being placed under seal or imprisoned within a pocket dimension. When this occurs, custodial authority vests solely with the Aegis Magi acting on behalf of the Guild Sovereign, regardless of which faction sponsored the trial. No individual member of the Conservator or Innovator factions shall claim rights to visit or communicate with a sealed prisoner without express authorization from the Desk. Unauthorized contact is punishable as a felony under § 100.2(d).\n\nVisiting hours for detained mages are established by local custom but vary widely across regions. In practice, access is often denied entirely unless paid for directly or negotiated through third parties. Such arrangements must be reported to the Desk within seven days of execution; failure to do so constitutes grounds for revocation of future trial participation privileges under § 800.1(c). Prisoners held in pocket dimensions may request periodic review by an independent panel appointed by the Sovereign, but such panels have no power to alter existing sentences absent new evidence of abuse or misconduct.\n\nDetained mages remain liable for all outstanding fines and damages incurred prior to their apprehension. Any sums owed shall be deducted from future payments made on their behalf by employers or clients until fully satisfied. Failure to settle these debts may result in extension of confinement duration at the discretion of the presiding judge. Similarly, compensation must be paid for any physical injuries sustained during capture or transit, calculated according to standard medical tariff schedules adjusted for magical enhancements where applicable.\n\nEscape attempts constitute an aggravating circumstance that may lead to enhanced penalties upon retrial. Even unsuccessful breaches of containment are treated as serious violations warranting increased surveillance and stricter terms on subsequent releases. Recidivists caught evading custody risk permanent sealing or execution, depending on the gravity of their offenses and resources available for pursuit. The Guild reserves the right to deploy any lawful means necessary to apprehend fugitives, including use of deadly force if absolutely required to prevent loss of life or destruction of property.\n\nAll records pertaining to sealed individuals shall be maintained in strict confidence under § 700.2, accessible only to authorized officials and their agents. Disclosure of such information to unauthorized parties constitutes a grave breach of trust subject to severe sanctions up to and including disbarment. Exceptions exist for emergency situations where release may pose imminent threat to public safety; however, any such disclosures must be documented meticulously with justification supporting the necessity thereof. This provision remains in effect indefinitely unless expressly amended by future legislation enacted through proper channels.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "800.1",
            "100.2",
            "700.2",
            "800.5",
            "800.6"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": "lmstudio",
      "fp": "6a269d478700c48c",
