      ]
    },
    {
      "cite": "1001.2",
      "part": "part_x",
      "title": "Prohibited Spells in Financial Markets",
      "kind": "section",
      "brief": "Named classes. Quiet List stays quiet.",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Spells in Financial Markets",
          "text": "Any mage, Innovator, or Conservator engaged in the facilitation of commerce, the brokering of arcane assets, or the management of guild-sanctioned vaults shall be strictly prohibited from employing specific classes of spells designed to bypass the cognitive faculties of a counterparty. Under the Autumnwood Accords, the use of high-level charms of compulsion, charms of suggestion, or any transmutation intended to alter the perceived weight or value of a physical asset during a transaction is strictly forbidden. Such actions constitute a primary violation of the Accords and shall be subject to immediate referral to the Aegis Magi for investigation. Furthermore, any spell that induces a state of \"magical euphoria\" or \"docile compliance\" in a potential buyer or seller is classified as a predatory arcane act.\n\nThe Guild maintains a strict prohibition on the use of \"Veil-Shifting\" and \"Memory-Softening\" magic within any marketplace, whether physical or ethereal. While the Innovators may argue for the utility of such magic in \"market smoothing,\" the Conservators maintain that the sanctity of the buyer's will is the bedrock of the Midlands' economic stability. Any mage found utilizing these classes of magic in a financial context shall be subject to the Paradox Trial as outlined in § 800.2. The penalties for such violations may range from the permanent sealing of the offending mage's casting ability to a term of service in a pocket-prison, depending on the scale of the financial discrepancy caused.\n\nFurthermore, no mage may use \"True Sight\" or \"Identify\" as a means of coercion to force a sale. While these spells are standard tools of the trade, their use to strip a seller of their \"right to privacy regarding arcane secrets\" is a violation of the Accords. The Guild recognizes the distinction between a professional assay and a predatory search. Any merchant who refuses to allow a standard, non-invasive assay by a licensed clerk may do so, but any mage who attempts to bypass this refusal using invasive scrying or piercing magic shall be fined. See § 1001.1 for the general definition of fraud.\n\nThe Quiet List shall remain strictly confidential and is not to be referenced in any public catalog, ledger, or marketplace declaration. No mage shall recite the names of items or methods contained within the Quiet List in any tavern, public square, or marketplace. Any breach of this secrecy by a mage, even if the breach is not intended for financial gain, shall be considered a felony under the Accords. The secrecy of the Quiet List is paramount to the safety of the Midlands; thus, any mage who discusses \"Quiet items\" in a commercial setting shall face immediate sanctions. See § 300.3 for the procedure of listing such items without public notice.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "800.2",
            "1001.1",
            "300.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Spells in Financial Markets — Continued",
          "text": "§ 1001.2 No Spell May Be Used to Manipulate Market Prices or Asset Values Directly. The use of arcane energies for the purpose of artificially inflating, deflating, or otherwise distorting the value of financial instruments is hereby prohibited. This includes spells designed to induce panic, greed, irrational exuberance, or despair among investors; to manipulate perceived supply and demand curves through magical means; or to directly alter the worth of currencies, commodities, or securities via enchantment. Such practices constitute a grave threat to the integrity of the global economy and are subject to severe penalties under this Code.\n\n§ 1001.3 Exceptions for Legitimate Hedging and Risk Management Strategies Notwithstanding the foregoing prohibition, certain narrowly defined applications of magical theory may be permitted within regulated financial contexts, provided strict safeguards are observed. These include: (a) The deployment of protective wards or counter-curses by authorized risk officers to neutralize hostile magical interference in trading venues; (b) The use of divination techniques for market trend analysis, subject to prior approval by the Oversight Committee and full disclosure of methodology; (c) The employment of enchantments on physical infrastructure (e.g., server farms, data centers) solely to enhance resilience against natural disasters or sabotage attempts. Any such activities must be conducted in accordance with existing licensing requirements and monitored continuously by Guild auditors. Violations will result in immediate revocation of privileges and potential criminal prosecution.\n\n§ 1001.4 Enforcement Powers and Penalties The Autumnwood Accords Desk is empowered to investigate suspected violations of this section, including but not limited to wiretapping communications, inspecting private records, and interviewing witnesses under oath. Upon probable cause being established, the Desk may issue an Emergency Preservation Order mandating cessation of all allegedly prohibited activities pending a full hearing before the Magistrates' Court. Failure to comply with such orders shall be deemed contempt punishable by fine or imprisonment at the discretion of the presiding judge. Convicted offenders face mandatory restitution payments calculated based on actual damages suffered by affected parties, plus punitive sanctions amounting to no less than three times their illicit gains. Repeat offenses will trigger automatic suspension from all licensed activities until further notice.\n\n§ 1001.5 Definitions for Clarity In interpreting this section: \"Market Prices\" refers broadly to any quantifiable measure of value used in commerce, including stock indices, bond yields, exchange rates, commodity futures prices, and even intangible assets like brand reputation or user engagement metrics. \"Direct Manipulation\" encompasses both overt acts (e.g., casting a charm on a trader's brain) and subtle influences (e.g., embedding persuasive subliminal messages in advertising). The burden of proof rests firmly upon the accused party to demonstrate that their actions did not violate this prohibition, regardless of whether they intended harmful outcomes. This strict liability standard reflects the extreme gravity of undermining financial stability through supernatural means.\n\n§ 1001.6 Relation to Other Statutes Nothing herein shall be construed to supersede applicable laws governing insider trading, market manipulation, securities fraud, or other forms of economic misconduct already addressed by civil and criminal codes. Rather, this provision serves as a complementary safeguard specifically tailored to address unique risks posed by magical intervention in financial systems. Where conflicts arise between provisions of this Code and external statutes, the more stringent standard shall prevail unless explicitly overridden by legislation enacted through proper channels. All regulated entities are reminded that adherence to both domestic regulations AND international treaties remains their paramount obligation at all times.\n\n\"See also § 1001.1 regarding general prohibitions on illicit spellcasting; § 600.4 concerning construct labor laws which similarly restrict exploitative practices.\"",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1001.2",
            "1001.3",
            "1001.4",
            "1001.5",
            "1001.6",
            "1001.1",
            "600.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Spells in Financial Markets — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "The use of spells and magical techniques that directly manipulate financial instruments or market conditions is strictly prohibited within any jurisdiction subject to the Accords. This prohibition extends beyond obvious fraud or manipulation to include subtle forms of influence such as divination, charm, and compulsion aimed at swaying investor sentiment. The intent behind these restrictions is to maintain a level playing field for all participants in the financial sector and to prevent the exploitation of arcane advantages that could undermine market integrity.\n\nSpecifically forbidden are spells designed to predict future price movements with certainty, alter public perception of companies or assets, or directly affect the value of securities. Any casting of such prohibited arts within trading floors, exchanges, or related facilities shall be treated as a serious violation subject to immediate investigation and potential sanctions by the Aegis Magi. Penalties may include fines, suspension of licenses, and in severe cases revocation of operating privileges for institutions found guilty of facilitating illegal magical practices.\n\nThe burden of proof rests with the accuser to demonstrate that a prohibited spell was cast with intent to influence financial outcomes. However, any suspicious activity warranting further scrutiny shall be promptly reported to the appropriate authorities by responsible parties. Failure to report known violations may result in disciplinary action against negligent individuals or entities. The ultimate goal is to preserve fair and transparent markets free from the corrupting temptations of unchecked magical power.\n\nThis provision reflects a growing concern among regulators about the potential for arcane interference in economic systems, which could destabilize entire regions if left unaddressed. As magic becomes more integrated into daily life, the need for clear boundaries around its application in sensitive areas grows ever more critical. The Accords stand ready to evolve alongside technological and magical advancements to protect the public interest from emerging threats.\n\nIn sum, the prohibition of spells affecting financial markets underscores a fundamental principle: that power must always be exercised responsibly and within defined limits. Whether wielding swords or wands, all bearers of strength owe a duty to uphold justice and fairness in their dealings with others. By curbing misuse of magic in economic spheres, society safeguards its stability against forces far more unpredictable than any mere mortal could imagine. Let this law serve as both shield and sword against those who would exploit arcane talents for illicit gain at the expense of communal welfare.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1001.2 Prohibited Spells in Financial Markets",
          "text": "The use of forbidden magic within the sphere of financial transactions is strictly prohibited under this section, as such practices threaten both economic stability and public safety. Specifically, spells that manipulate perception, memory, or emotion are deemed unsuitable for commercial application due to their potential for abuse and long-term societal harm. Examples include charm person, mass suggestion, fear, and similar enchantments that may induce irrational decision-making among investors or consumers alike.\n\nFurthermore, the employment of necromantic arts in banking operations is absolutely forbidden, given the inherent risks associated with summoning and binding spirits. The creation of undead servants for labor purposes falls outside acceptable bounds unless explicitly authorized by a special research permit issued by the Conservators. Any attempt to exploit such powers for profit without proper oversight constitutes a serious violation subject to severe penalties under the Accords.\n\nIn addition, the alteration of currency or trade goods via magical means is expressly banned, as it undermines the integrity of regional commerce and facilitates fraud on an unprecedented scale. Spells such as transmute metal to wood or alter self are particularly dangerous in this context, enabling the counterfeiting of precious metals or the degradation of valuable items without detection. Enforcement officers maintain vigilant surveillance over marketplaces to detect and punish offenders swiftly.\n\nThe Desk further mandates that all financial institutions employ licensed mages capable of identifying suspicious magical signatures indicative of illicit activity. Regular audits conducted by Guild investigators ensure compliance with these stringent regulations, with failure resulting in immediate revocation of operating licenses and potential criminal prosecution for responsible parties. Only through such rigorous controls can the Accords safeguard against the corrupting influence of black-market sorcery on the broader economy.\n\nIt is hereby declared that any individual caught utilizing prohibited spells for financial gain shall face summary expulsion from all Guild halls, forfeiture of accumulated credits, and mandatory sealing of their magical aptitudes by authorized Aegis Magi. Repeat offenders risk permanent banishment from the region and prosecution under existing criminal statutes. The collective well-being of society takes precedence over short-term profits derived from unethical practices.\n\nThis provision aligns with the overarching principles enshrined in §§ 1.7(c) and 900.2(a), emphasizing the importance of maintaining ethical standards across all facets of magical endeavor. By prohibiting dangerous applications in sensitive areas like finance, the Accords strive to preserve both individual autonomy and communal security for generations yet unborn. All members are urged to uphold these vital mandates with unwavering dedication and integrity.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1.7",
            "1001.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Spells in Financial Markets — Continued — Administration",
          "text": "The use of certain spells within the context of financial transactions and market manipulation is strictly prohibited under § 1001.2(a). Specifically, any spell that alters the perceived value or scarcity of an asset, regardless of its actual worth, constitutes a violation of these regulations. This includes but is not limited to illusions of abundance, glamours of quality, and enchantments that artificially inflate demand. Such practices undermine the integrity of fair trade and market stability.\n\nFurthermore, any spell designed to influence the behavior or decision-making processes of potential buyers or sellers is forbidden under § 1001.2(b). This encompasses spells of compulsion, suggestion, intimidation, or seduction used solely for commercial gain. The intent behind these prohibitions is to prevent mages from exploiting their supernatural abilities to create an unfair advantage in financial dealings. All transactions must be conducted on a level playing field, free from magical manipulation.\n\nIn addition, the use of divination spells to gain insider information about pending market events is prohibited under § 1001.2(c). Mages may not utilize scrying, precognition, or other forms of foresight to anticipate price fluctuations, regulatory changes, or competitor actions for personal profit. Such practices distort the natural flow of commerce and enable unethical speculation based on privileged knowledge rather than sound economic analysis. The Accords aim to foster transparency and accountability in all financial activities involving magical entities.\n\nViolations of these provisions shall be addressed in accordance with § 800 et seq., which outlines the penalties for breaches of the Autumnwood Accords. Depending on the severity and circumstances, offenders may face sanctions ranging from fines and license suspensions to permanent revocation of their right to practice magic within the Guild's jurisdiction. Repeat offenses will be met with increasingly stringent measures designed to protect the public interest and maintain trust in the financial systems regulated by the Accords.\n\nIt is imperative that all licensed mages familiarize themselves thoroughly with these restrictions and adhere strictly to them in their professional capacities. The integrity of our society depends upon the responsible use of magical powers, especially within sensitive domains like finance where even minor imbalances can have far-reaching consequences. By enforcing these guidelines consistently, the Guild safeguards both its members' livelihoods and the broader community from exploitation by unscrupulous practitioners seeking to bend reality for selfish ends.\n\nsee § 1001.2; see § 800.5; see § 300.1; under § 700.4. This clause serves as a critical safeguard against magical corruption of economic systems, ensuring fair competition and protecting consumers from predatory tactics that exploit supernatural abilities for illicit gain. The Guild remains committed to upholding these principles with unwavering resolve.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1001.2",
            "800.5",
            "300.1",
            "700.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1001.2 Prohibited Spells in Financial Markets - Administrative Oversight and E",
          "text": "The administration and enforcement of the prohibitions outlined herein shall be vested exclusively in the Bureau of Economic Stability under the direct supervision of the Archmage Sovereign. The Bureau is authorized to conduct routine inspections of financial institutions, trading floors, and related facilities to verify compliance with these regulations. Inspectors shall have full access to all records, communications, and physical assets for examination purposes. Any entity found in violation shall face immediate suspension of operations pending a full investigation.\n\nUpon discovery of prohibited spell usage or attempted usage within a regulated financial environment, the Bureau must initiate an ex parte seizure order pursuant to § 1001.4. This order authorizes the immediate confiscation of all materials and devices capable of facilitating such forbidden practices, along with any proceeds derived therefrom. Seized items shall be held in evidence until disposition by a competent tribunal. The burden of proving innocence rests solely upon the accused party, who must demonstrate beyond a reasonable doubt that no violation occurred.\n\nPenalties for violations range from monetary fines to revocation of operating licenses and imprisonment. Fines are calculated based on the severity and duration of the offense, with maximum penalties capped at one hundred thousand gold pieces per incident. License suspensions shall be imposed for repeated or egregious infractions, lasting a minimum of six months. Criminal charges may also be pursued where appropriate under existing penal statutes. The Bureau is empowered to initiate proceedings directly without prior notice when immediate action is warranted to prevent further harm to public safety.\n\nThe provisions of this section are intended to preserve the integrity and stability of the financial markets against magical manipulation. Nothing herein shall be construed to limit the authority of regulatory bodies to enforce additional measures as necessary to maintain order and protect investors. The Archmage Sovereign retains discretion to amend these rules as circumstances dictate, provided such changes do not conflict with higher laws or established rights. All actions taken under this section shall be subject to judicial review upon timely petition by affected parties.\n\nThe Bureau maintains a detailed log of all inspections, seizures, penalties imposed, and related activities for transparency purposes. These records are available for public scrutiny unless classified as sensitive national security matters. Quarterly reports summarizing enforcement efforts shall be submitted to the General Assembly for consideration. The Archmage Sovereign may appoint special task forces with enhanced powers when required to address emerging threats or novel forms of prohibited conduct. Such delegations shall be temporary and subject to strict oversight mechanisms.\n\nUltimately, the goal of these regulations is to ensure that magic remains a force for good within society while preventing its misuse for illicit gain. Through diligent enforcement and fair application of penalties, the Bureau aims to safeguard both the economy and the public trust in financial institutions operating under its jurisdiction. Continued vigilance and adaptability are essential in an ever-changing landscape where new challenges may arise at any moment.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1001.4",
            "1001.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": "lmstudio",
      "fp": "75e70edce15861c9",
