    {
      "cite": "1201.3",
      "part": "part_xii",
      "title": "Extraterritorial Casting into a Diet Chamber",
      "kind": "section",
      "brief": "Do not. File a letter instead.",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Extraterritorial Casting into a Diet Chamber",
          "text": "Any practitioner of the arcane who intends to project, manifest, or otherwise exert magical influence upon a designated Diet Chamber—defined as a consecrated space for the consumption of sustenance by non-magical entities or for the communal nourishment of those under the jurisdiction of the Autumnwood Accords—is strictly prohibited from performing such actions if the target chamber exists outside the immediate terrestrial boundaries of the Midlands. This prohibition is absolute and applies to all schools of magic, including but not limited to transmutation of food, telekinetic delivery of beverages, or any atmospheric manipulation intended to enhance the olfactory profile of a meal. The Guild recognizes that while the logistical needs of travelers and diplomats are significant, the risk of cross-planar contamination, unintended caloric inflation, or the disruption of local culinary sanctity outweighs any perceived convenience of such remote casting.\n\nFurthermore, any mage found in violation of this clause shall be subject to immediate review by the Aegis Magi. The intent of the caster is irrelevant; the mere act of reaching across a jurisdictional boundary to influence a dining environment constitutes a breach of the Accords. This is particularly relevant when dealing with the Regal Empire or the Iron Legion, as their culinary standards are considered sovereign and their reactions to unsolicited magical intervention are often hostile. Mages seeking to provide logistical support to allies, such as the Goodstyle Artisans, must ensure that all such services are performed within the physical vicinity of the recipient. If a request for remote nourishment arises, the mage shall not utilize arcana to bridge the distance.\n\nIn instances where a mage feels compelled to provide sustenance to a party in a remote location, they are hereby commanded to forgo all magical intervention and instead utilize traditional courier methods. See § 1201.1 regarding transit stamps for such couriers. If the distance is prohibitive for physical transit, the mage may instead draft a formal letter of intent and request that the local authorities or the host party arrange for local procurement. This letter must be filed with the Accords Desk and bear the official seal of the caster’s faction, be it Conservator or Innovator. No exceptions shall be granted for \"emergency\" hunger, provided the emergency was not caused by the mage's own failure to plan for sufficient supplies. Failure to comply with this directive will result in a referral to the Paradox Trial for review of the caster's stability.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1201.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Cartography Sold as a License to Raid",
          "text": "The production, sale, and distribution of topographical records, hereafter referred to as Cartography, are governed by the principles of objective observation. It is strictly forbidden for any Cartographer, Merchant, or Mage to represent a map of a geographical feature—specifically the One-T mountain range or any similar landmark—as a license, permit, or authorization to engage in \"raiding,\" \"looting,\" or \"resource extraction.\" A map is a tool of navigation and spatial awareness; it confers no legal right to the contents of the terrain it depicts. Any individual attempting to sell a map with the express intent of implying it grants the bearer permission to bypass local defenses or enter restricted zones is committing a felony of Deception under the Accords.\n\nThe Guild finds that the \"One-T mountain\" has been the subject of frequent confusion regarding its status. While the map of the mountain is a public utility for those seeking to traverse the Midlands, the mountain itself remains subject to the laws of the presiding sovereign or the territorial claims of the dominant faction. The presence of a map in a traveler's possession does not mitigate the penalties associated with trespassing or the unauthorized seizure of materials. If a mage or adventurer intends to conduct a raid, they must secure a formal Raid License from the appropriate regional authority. A map is not a substitute for a license, and the sale of a map as such shall be treated as a fraudulent transaction, subject to the penalties outlined in § 1001.1.\n\nFurthermore, the Cartography Department of the Accords Desk warns that the sale of \"Tactical Maps\" which include notations on \"weak points\" or \"unprotected entrances\" does not exempt the buyer from the consequences of an assault. Such notations are considered descriptive, not permissive. If a mage is caught utilizing a map to conduct an unauthorized raid, the map itself may be seized as evidence of premeditation. Practitioners of the Innovator faction are specifically cautioned against creating \"dynamic maps\" that update in real-time to show the movements of guards or the location of hidden caches, as these may be classified as forbidden surveillance tools. For all matters regarding the legal acquisition of land or the right to harvest resources, mages must consult the proper civic channels rather than relying on the mere possession of a parchment.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1001.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1201.3 Extraterritorial Casting into a Diet Chamber; Cartography Sold as a Lic",
          "text": "No mage shall cast within the confines of an Autumn Wood Diet Chamber unless expressly invited by the presiding Archmage or her duly appointed substitute, nor shall any such casting extend beyond the immediate physical boundaries thereof without prior written consent. Violation of this provision constitutes both a breach of protocol and a potential act of war against the Guild itself, subject to immediate expulsion from the premises and subsequent penal proceedings under § 800 et seq.\n\nIt is further deemed unlawful for any individual or entity to market, distribute, or otherwise disseminate cartographic representations of protected lands, territories, or strategic locations without explicit authorization from the Autumn Wood Council. Such maps, whether drawn by hand or conjured through magical means, shall be treated as contraband upon discovery and subject to seizure under § 1201.5. Unauthorized possession or use of such materials may result in severe penalties, including permanent revocation of licensure and imprisonment for up to one hundred years without benefit of parole.\n\nThe sale or exchange of cartographic data shall be strictly regulated by the Autumn Wood Office of Geospatial Intelligence, which maintains a centralized registry of all approved maps and related documentation. Any entity seeking access to such information must submit a formal application accompanied by proof of need, security clearance, and indemnification against misuse. Failure to comply with these requirements shall constitute grounds for immediate suspension of privileges and possible criminal charges under applicable statutes.\n\nIt is hereby declared null and void any contract or agreement purporting to grant rights of entry, transit, or operation within the exclusive jurisdiction of an Autumn Wood Diet Chamber unless executed in accordance with this section. Such instruments shall be deemed unenforceable at law and subject to invalidation upon application by the Guild or its authorized representatives. Any party found guilty of violating this provision shall forfeit all claims thereto and be liable for damages arising therefrom, including but not limited to legal fees, court costs, and punitive assessments as determined in the sole discretion of the presiding magistrate.\n\nThis section shall take effect immediately upon final approval by the Autumn Wood Council and publication herein. Any existing arrangements inconsistent with these provisions are hereby superseded and void ab initio. All persons having an interest in matters governed thereby are directed to consult this section carefully before proceeding further, lest they incur grievous consequences for their ignorance thereof.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1201.5",
            "1201.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1201.4 Unauthorized Titan Growth and Rift Expansion",
          "text": "It is hereby declared that any deliberate or negligent act resulting in the unauthorized expansion of rifts, portals, or planar anomalies shall constitute a Class A violation under these Accords. This includes but is not limited to: (a) casting spells designed to enlarge existing breaches; (b) neglecting maintenance duties required by one's license agreement; and (c) failing to report suspected instabilities within twenty-four hours of discovery. Such infractions may result in immediate suspension of all magical privileges, revocation of licensure without compensation, and imprisonment for up to five years at the discretion of the Consistory. Furthermore, any individual found guilty of this offense shall be held jointly and severally liable for all damages arising from said expansion, including but not limited to property destruction, loss of life or limb, and environmental contamination by raw arcane energy.\" \"The Conservators argue that unchecked growth poses an existential threat to reality itself, citing the catastrophic events of the Last Conflagration as proof positive. Innovators counter that such fears are unfounded so long as regulations are followed, pointing to decades of safe operation under current statutes. The Archmage Sovereign remains neutral on this matter, deferring judgment until further study can be conducted.\" \"In any event, all parties are reminded that the Accords exist for the protection and ordering of society—not merely the convenience of powerful individuals seeking unfettered access to forbidden arts. Those who would undermine these fundamental principles do so at their own peril, risking not only their freedom but perhaps their very souls in the process.\" \"The undersigned hereby certify that this section was duly read, debated, and approved by a majority vote of the Mages' Guild Consistory on this 17th day of Autumnwood, in the year of our Lord two thousand and twenty-three.\" \"[Seal of Archmage Veyra]\" \"[Signature of Archmage Theron]\" \"[Signature of Janna Brightspark]\" \"[Witnessed by Two Credible Witnesses]\" \"So let it be written, so shall it be done!\" \"For as long as magic shall endure...\"",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1201.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1201.3 Extraterritorial Casting into a Diet Chamber; Cartography Sold as a Lic — Continued",
          "text": "No mage shall cast spells beyond the borders of their Hall without express permission from the Archmage Sovereign and written authorization from the relevant sovereign state or governing body. Violation constitutes unauthorized field use under § 500.1 and subjecting the offender to immediate seizure and trial for breach of contract. The Desk retains sole discretion to approve or deny such requests based on necessity, risk assessment, and diplomatic considerations.\n\nCartographic products depicting magical phenomena, ley lines, rift locations, or other sensitive data shall not be sold, leased, or distributed without a full disclosure of their intended use and explicit consent from the original creator. Any attempt to market maps as \"raid licenses\" or \"exploration permits\" is hereby declared fraudulent misrepresentation under § 1001.2 and punishable by revocation of licensure and permanent disqualification from Guild activities. The sale of such items without proper labeling and warnings shall be deemed a Class A felony offense.\n\nThis section takes precedence over any conflicting provisions in private contracts or local ordinances. Archmage Veyra reserves the right to override her own decisions if new evidence emerges suggesting greater risk to public safety than initially assessed. Failure to comply with these rules constitutes grounds for disciplinary action up to and including permanent expulsion from the Guild and referral to law enforcement authorities.\n\nThe Desk encourages all members to report suspected violations promptly through established channels to ensure swift intervention before harm occurs. Anonymous tip lines are available via encrypted messaging apps and secure mailboxes located at each Hall entrance. Whistleblowers acting in good faith shall receive protection against retaliation under § 1002.3, though false accusations may result in punitive measures including fines and imprisonment.\n\nIt is the collective responsibility of every mage to uphold these standards for the greater good of society. By adhering strictly to the guidelines herein, we safeguard both ourselves and those around us from the dangers inherent in unchecked magical experimentation. Let this serve as a clarion call to renewed vigilance and mutual accountability among all practitioners within our sacred order.\n\nSEE ALSO: § 500.1 Unauthorized Field Use; § 700.2 Diplomatic Immunity Exceptions; § 800.1 Jurisdictional Boundaries; § 900.4 Privacy Clauses in Contracts; § 1001.3 Fraudulent Misrepresentation Standards.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "500.1",
            "1001.2",
            "1002.3",
            "700.2",
            "800.1",
            "900.4",
            "1001.3",
            "1201.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1201.3 Extraterritorial Casting into a Diet Chamber; Cartography Sold as a Lic — Administration",
          "text": "Any act of magical casting, whether for combat or utility purposes, that occurs within the jurisdictional bounds of a Diet Hall is subject to immediate seizure by Aegis Magi unless covered under an active Permit to Work. This includes any spell component, verbal utterance, somatic gesture, or mental projection originating from outside the Chamber but directed inwardly. See § 900.1 Duty to File Before Casting; § 500.1 Field Casting for Value.\n\nCartographic representations of contested territories, including those marked as \"Restricted\" or \"No-Go,\" constitute actionable evidence of intent and preparation for unauthorized operation. Sale, distribution, or possession thereof without explicit written consent from the Archmage Sovereign is prohibited under penalty of confiscation and permanent revocation of licensure. Such maps are deemed integral to the planning of illicit expeditions and thus fall within the scope of § 400.3 Borrowed Hours; Interest in Time.\n\nThe expansion or unauthorized modification of existing rifts, portals, or planar anomalies shall require prior written authorization from the Guild's Planar Oversight Committee. Any such activity discovered without proper documentation will be treated as a Class A violation subject to full investigation and potential prosecution under § 800.1 Penalty for Unauthorized Arcane Operation. See also § 400.2 Pocket Dimensions as Labs; § 500.2 Unscheduled Magic in Public Spaces.\n\nAll mages are reminded that the Autumnwood Accords extend their authority beyond mere physical territory, encompassing all acts of magical expression that may impact public order or safety. Failure to comply with these provisions shall result in escalated sanctions up to and including suspension from practice indefinitely. The Desk retains sole discretion to interpret ambiguities arising under this section without recourse to external bodies. Under § 100.4 Records of Speech; § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse.\n\nThis provision was enacted following the widespread misuse of cartographic data during the recent Titan Incident, wherein several novice casters inadvertently triggered a catastrophic rift collapse by misinterpreting terrain markers on an improperly sourced map. The resulting devastation underscored the need for stricter controls over sensitive information bearing potential tactical value in conflict scenarios. Reference § 400.5 Unauthorized Titan Growth; § 900.2 Reporting of Material Enchantments.\n\nBy signing this Codex, each licensed practitioner acknowledges their full understanding and acceptance of these obligations as binding conditions precedent to continued operation within the Guild framework. Violations shall be addressed swiftly and severely in accordance with established procedure. The Desk reserves absolute authority to enforce compliance through any lawful means necessary to preserve public safety and maintain regulatory integrity. As stated in § 100.7 Foreign Halls and Courtesy: \"No exceptions apply.\"",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "900.1",
            "500.1",
