    {
      "cite": "1301.1",
      "part": "part_xiii",
      "title": "Schedule of Fees",
      "kind": "section",
      "brief": "Named amounts in Guild marks. No Wario Coin.",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Schedule of Fees",
          "text": "The Guild shall maintain a definitive schedule of fees for all administrative, investigative, and regulatory actions performed by the Accords Desk. These fees are established to ensure the continued maintenance of the Autumnwood infrastructure and to compensate the Guild for the oversight of arcane stability. All fees must be rendered in standard Guild marks. The Guild hereby declares that any currency of irregular origin, including but not limited to the Wario Coin, is not a valid tender for the settlement of debts, fines, or administrative costs. Any attempt to utilize non-standard coinage in the settlement of a Guild fee shall result in the immediate rejection of the tender and the assessment of a secondary \"Invalid Tender\" surcharge as dictated by the current fiscal year's guidelines.\n\nFees are categorized by the severity of the violation and the complexity of the requested service. Administrative services, such as the filing of a Provisional Guild Pass or the registration of a new cartographic survey, are subject to a fixed entry fee. Investigative services, including the surveying of a Heartstone or the verification of a rift's boundaries, are billed at a rate commensurate with the risk of planar instability. All fees are non-refundable once the Accords Desk has initiated the requested procedure. See § 1301.1.\n\nThe Guild reserves the right to adjust the Schedule of Fees with a notice period of no less than three lunar cycles. Such adjustments shall be mediated by Archmage Veyra to ensure that the balance between Conservator traditionalism and Innovator expansionism is maintained in the economic health of the Guild. No individual mage, regardless of rank or factional standing, is exempt from these fees unless a formal waiver is granted by the Archmage Sovereign. Failure to pay fees within the allotted timeframe shall result in the suspension of the mage's right to perform authorized research or transit within the Midlands.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1301.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Penalties; Sunrise Accrual",
          "text": "All penalties, fines, and interest accrued on outstanding debts to the Guild shall be calculated based on the temporal flow of the original time zone, specifically the standard time of the Autumnwood region. This provision is enacted to prevent mages from utilizing temporal manipulation, pocket dimensions, or chronal displacement to stall the accumulation of penalties. A mage who is incarcerated within a pocket-prison or a sealed ward does not enjoy a \"temporal reprieve.\" The Accords Desk shall calculate the duration of the penalty based on the time elapsed in the Midlands, regardless of how many years or seconds may pass within the confined space of the sanction.\n\nThe accrual of penalties begins at the moment of the initial violation or the issuance of a formal summons by the Aegis Magi. If a mage remains in a state of non-compliance, the penalty shall increase at a fixed rate per sunrise as observed in the Autumnwood. This ensures that the Guild's interests are protected against the exploitation of \"slow-time\" environments. See § 800.5 for specific procedures regarding the maintenance of pocket-prisons.\n\nAny attempt to argue for a \"subjective time\" calculation based on the experience of the offender is strictly prohibited. The Guild maintains that the preservation of the Accords is a matter of objective reality. Should a mage attempt to use high-level chronomancy to circumvent these accruals, such an act shall be considered a Grade-A violation of the stability protocols, punishable by an immediate and permanent sealing of the offending arcane circuits. The Accords Desk shall provide a weekly statement of accrued penalties to any mage currently under sanction, ensuring transparency in the calculation of the debt.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "800.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Appeals",
          "text": "Any mage who believes a ruling of the Accords Desk to be in error may initiate a formal appeal process. The first stage of appeal resides solely with the Accords Desk. The Clerk shall review the filing for procedural correctness and ensure that all required documentation, including any relevant one-T cartography and proof of identity, has been submitted. If the Clerk finds the appeal has merit, the matter may be elevated for internal review. This stage is intended to resolve clerical errors, misunderstandings of the written word, or minor disputes regarding the interpretation of the Schedule of Fees.\n\nIf the appeal is denied at the Desk level, the mage may request a transition to the Paradox Trial. This is a formal judicial proceeding where the mage's peers shall sit in judgment. The Paradox Trial is the ultimate arbiter of the Guild's internal laws. During this process, the facts of the case are presented to the council, who may choose to uphold, vacate, or modify the original ruling. The Paradox Trial may result in various outcomes, including the sealing of magic, the issuance of a new mandate, or the confirmation of the original penalty. See § 800.4 for the conversion of duel stakes into fees during such proceedings.\n\nOnce a decision is rendered by the Paradox Trial, it is considered final and binding. There is no further mechanism for appeal within the Guild's jurisdiction. The Guild does not provide a secondary court of appeals, and any attempt to seek further adjudication through external means—such as the courts of the Regal Empire or the laws of the Iron Mandate—shall be viewed as an act of secession and a violation of the Autumnwood Accords. Mages are advised to ensure their appeals are well-reasoned and supported by evidence, as the path to \"nowhere useful\" begins once the Paradox Trial concludes.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "800.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Who May Inspect",
          "text": "Access to the internal records of the Accords Desk, the physical archives of the Autumnwood, and the sensitive logs of the Quiet List is strictly restricted. Only authorized Clerks of the Accords Desk and named officers of the Guild may enter these areas for the purpose of official business. This restriction is designed to protect the privacy of the mages, the integrity of the Guild's secrets, and the security of the Midlands from external threats such as the Silver Flame or the Cosmic Jesters.\n\nNo member of the general public, including non-affiliated mages, may request an inspection of the archives without a signed warrant from Archmage Veyra. Furthermore, \"crowd\" inspections are strictly prohibited. Even in the event of a formal inquiry, the inspection shall be conducted by a designated small group of officials rather than a public gathering. This prevents the unauthorized dissemination of information regarding the Quiet List and ensures that the delicate balance of the Guild's internal politics remains undisturbed by outside scrutiny.\n\nMages who are granted \"Provisional Guild Passes\" for political reasons, such as those held by Archie Miser, are not granted automatic inspection rights. Their access is limited to the specific documents required for their current diplomatic engagement and may be revoked at any moment by the Aegis Magi. Any unauthorized individual found attempting to peer into the archives or overhear the deliberations of the Desk shall be subject to immediate detention and a formal review for a Paradox Trial. Security is paramount; the Guild's secrets are the foundation of its power, and their preservation is the primary duty of every Clerk.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.1 Schedule of Fees, Penalties; Sunrise Accrual, Appeals, Who May Inspect",
          "text": "The Desk hereby establishes the following fee schedule applicable to all filings and services rendered under this Codex: (A) Standard Spell Registration – one hundred marks per annum for each registered enchantment; (B) Advanced Rite Certification – five hundred marks plus a two-hundred mark processing surcharge; (C) Paradox Trial Assessment – fifteen hundred marks minimum, payable upfront upon convening of the Tribunal. Penalties for non-compliance shall accrue daily at a rate of one percent per day from the date of default until cured or litigated to finality. No reduction in fees may be granted except by explicit written order of the Desk Chairperson and only after demonstration of undue hardship warranting relief.\n\nAll unfiled magical effects discovered during routine inspection shall trigger immediate retroactive assessment of outstanding fees plus a two-hundred mark late penalty per item, calculated from the date such effect first manifested. Where multiple violations arise from a single incident, penalties shall be aggregated rather than compounded to prevent astronomical liabilities while ensuring full restitution to the Guild for administrative burdens incurred.\n\nAppeals of fee assessments must be lodged within thirty days of notification and submitted in triplicate to the Clerk General for expedited review by an impartial panel comprising representatives from both Conservator and Innovator factions. Such panels shall have authority to uphold, reduce, or vacate original determinations based solely on evidence presented during hearings conducted under sealed conditions outside public view. Final decisions rendered by appeal panels are binding and not subject to further recourse except via writ of certiorari directly to the Arcane Supreme Court upon demonstration of egregious procedural error.\n\nInspection rights granted herein extend exclusively to duly appointed Guild auditors accompanied by a certified scribe. Unlawful intrusion into private quarters or unauthorized attempts to examine magical items shall constitute breach of contract and may result in immediate suspension of filing privileges pending completion of background checks and liability waivers approved by the Desk. All fee payments must be made via secure transfer using recognized tender methods only; receipt of Wario Coin, gold bullion, or other non-standard currencies will not discharge obligations unless pre-arranged with written authorization from a Senior Clerk. Failure to remit fees within thirty days constitutes default under § 1302 and triggers automatic suspension of all privileges until brought fully current plus accrued interest and penalties.\n\nThis Schedule shall remain in effect until superseded by subsequent action of the Desk or revocation pursuant to established procedures set forth elsewhere herein. The Desk retains discretion to adjust fee structures periodically based on inflationary pressures, operational costs, and evolving regulatory needs, provided adequate notice is given to all affected parties through official channels. Any disputes regarding interpretation of this Schedule shall be resolved exclusively by binding arbitration administered under the auspices of the Autumnwood Accords Arbitration Tribunal unless otherwise agreed upon in writing between disputing parties.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1301.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.2 Enforcement and Collection of Fees and Penalties",
          "text": "The Accords Desk shall enforce the collection of all fees, penalties, and restitution ordered pursuant to this Part through lawful means, including but not limited to seizure of assets, liens on property, and garnishment of wages. Any party failing to comply with a final judgment within thirty days shall be subject to contempt proceedings under § 1305. The Desk may appoint a special master or receiver to manage delinquent accounts as necessary to protect the interests of the Guild and its constituents.\n\nAll fees and penalties assessed against individuals, entities, or organizations shall accrue interest at a rate determined by the Board of Archmages from time to time. Such charges shall be added immediately upon assessment and become due without further notice. Failure to pay promptly may result in additional surcharges and escalated enforcement actions. The Desk retains broad discretion regarding payment plans and waivers based on demonstrated hardship or mitigating circumstances.\n\nParties aggrieved by any fee, penalty, or collection action may appeal to the Appeals Tribunal within twenty-one days of service of notice. Such appeals shall be limited to questions of law and not re-litigation of factual determinations already made. The Tribunal shall hear each case expeditiously and issue a written decision within sixty days. Decisions of the Tribunal are final and binding on all parties except where clear error is shown upon rehearing.\n\nThe Accords Desk shall maintain comprehensive records of all fees collected, penalties imposed, and enforcement actions taken pursuant to this Part. These records shall be available for public inspection during normal business hours subject to appropriate redaction protections as outlined in § 1307. Any disputes regarding the accuracy or propriety of recorded entries may be raised through formal objection procedures set forth in the Rules of Practice before the Desk.\n\nNotwithstanding any other provision herein, all fees, penalties, and costs incurred under this Part shall remain fully enforceable against successors-in-interest, assigns, executors, administrators, and representatives of estates. Nothing contained hereunder shall limit or impair the rights and remedies available to the Guild at law or in equity for breach of contract, tortious conduct, or other actionable wrongs arising out of non-compliance with these provisions.\n\nThe Desk may delegate authority to collect minor fees and impose nominal penalties to licensed collectors acting under its supervision. Such agents shall be held liable for any misappropriation or abuse of entrusted funds and subject to strict accountability measures as directed by the Board from time to time. All collections must be remitted immediately to a dedicated trust account maintained in the Guild's name solely for offsetting outstanding obligations and administrative expenses related thereto.\n\nThis Section serves as an essential operational mechanism ensuring timely compliance with the financial requirements of this Code, thereby preserving the integrity and efficacy of the regulatory framework established herein. By providing clear guidelines for assessment, collection, enforcement, and dispute resolution regarding monetary liabilities, it supports the broader goals of promoting responsible magical practice while safeguarding public welfare.\n\nsee § 1305 Contempt Proceedings; § 1307 Access to Records; § 2004 Suspension and Revocation of Licenses; § 900.6 Collection of Unpaid Fees; § 800.7 Enforcement of Judgments Against Non-Compliant Entities\n\n*Note: All amounts specified in this Section shall be denominated exclusively in standard Guild Marks (GM), not Wario Coin or any other form of currency not officially recognized by the Accords Desk.*",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "900.6",
            "800.7",
            "1301.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": "lmstudio",
      "fp": "d4529b53bad61dd1",
      "refs": [
        "800.4",
        "800.5",
        "800.7",
        "900.6",
        "1301.2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cite": "1301.2",
      "part": "part_xiii",
      "title": "Penalties; Sunrise Accrual",
      "kind": "section",
      "brief": "Original time zone, not the pocket's.",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Penalties; Sunrise Accrual",
          "text": "Any punitive measures, fines, or temporal sanctions levied by the Autumnwood Accords Desk against a practitioner found in violation of these statutes shall be calculated based upon the temporal progression of the practitioner’s point of origin. This principle of Sunrise Accrual ensures that the Guild maintains a consistent standard of justice that is not subject to the manipulation of localized chronomancy or the dilation of extra-planar environments. When a mage is detained within a pocket-prison, a localized rift, or any other magically-induced sub-dimension where the flow of time deviates from the standard progression of the Midlands, the duration of the penalty shall be measured by the sunrises occurring in the practitioner’s home jurisdiction at the time of the offense.\n\nThe Guild explicitly rejects the \"subjective duration\" defense. A practitioner who remains in a state of stasis for what they perceive to be a mere hour, but which constitutes a century of elapsed time in the Midlands, shall be held liable for the full century of accrued penalties. Conversely, a practitioner who utilizes a time-dilated pocket-dimension to attempt to \"outlast\" a sentence shall find that the Accords Desk recognizes only the progression of the external world. This provision serves to prevent the evasion of justice through the use of sophisticated chronometric shielding or the exploitation of natural anomalies. See § 1.2 for the enacting authority of these calculations.\n\nFurthermore, the calculation of interest on outstanding magical debts or the duration of \"Seal and Silence\" sanctions shall be reconciled at the moment of the first sunrise following the initial infraction. If a practitioner is currently located in a region where the sun does not rise—such as the deep subterranean vaults or certain high-altitude celestial rifts—the Accords Desk shall defer to the nearest recognized terrestrial municipality that adheres to the Midlands standard. The goal of the Sunrise Accrual is to ensure that the cost of magical delinquency remains proportional to the impact of the crime upon the stability of the Autumnwood Accords, rather than the convenience of the offender's current location.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Appeals",
          "text": "The right to appeal a ruling issued by the Accords Desk is a fundamental prerogative of any licensed practitioner, provided such a request is filed within three lunar cycles of the initial judgment. The primary venue for such appeals is the Desk itself, wherein the presiding Clerk shall review the filing for procedural errors, misinterpretations of the Accords, or evidence of clerical oversight. The Desk maintains the authority to vacate a penalty or issue a stay of execution should it be determined that the original ruling was inconsistent with the prevailing mediation of Archmage Veyra or the established precedents of the Conservators.\n\nShould the Desk uphold its original ruling, the practitioner may petition for a formal Paradox Trial. This is the highest level of judicial review within the Guild’s jurisdiction. A Paradox Trial involves a council of peers—selected from both the Conservator and Innovator factions—who shall determine the validity of the original charge through a process of magical arbitration. During these proceedings, the accused may present a defense, and the council may demand the presentation of artifacts, spell-scrolls, or testimonies. The outcome of a Paradox Trial is final and binding; it represents the ultimate consensus of the Guild’s magical community.\n\nBe it known that there is no further recourse beyond the Paradox Trial. Once the peer council has rendered its verdict, the decision is considered absolute and immutable. No further petitions, grievances, or appeals may be filed with the Accords Desk, the Office of the Archmage, or the Aegis Magi regarding the specific matter at hand. To attempt to seek a higher court of law outside the Guild’s jurisdiction is to forfeit all remaining protections afforded by the Accords. Practitioners are cautioned that seeking \"external\" justice—particularly from the Regal Empire or the Iron Legion—will result in the immediate revocation of their Guild standing and the permanent sealing of their arcane signature. See § 800.5 for the specific procedures regarding the enforcement of these final judgments.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "800.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Who May Inspect",
          "text": "The sanctity of the Archives and the privacy of the practitioner’s registered magical laboratory are upheld by the principle of Restricted Access. Only authorized personnel of the Autumnwood Accords are permitted to conduct formal inspections of any site where restricted research is being conducted or where a magical artifact of significant provenance is being held. These inspectors are strictly limited to active Clerks of the Accords Desk and named Officers of the Aegis Magi. Any individual not holding a verified Guild Seal of Inspection may be barred from entry at the discretion of the site’s primary licensee.\n\nUnder no circumstances shall a public inspection be permitted. The Guild recognizes that the exposure of experimental methodologies—particularly those pursued by the Innovators—could lead to the unintended dissemination of volatile arcana or the compromise of the Quiet List. A crowd, including non-practitioners, journalists, or unauthorized observers, is strictly prohibited from entering any zone designated for inspection. Should a practitioner fail to grant access to a named Officer of the Aegis Magi during a scheduled audit, they shall be subject to immediate summary fines and a potential referral for a Paradox Trial.\n\nIn cases where a practitioner is under active investigation for a violation of the Iron Mandate or other rival laws, the Accords Desk may grant temporary inspection rights to designated mediators, provided these mediators are bound by a non-disclosure oath. However, these rights do not extend to the general populace or to representatives of the Silver Flame or the Cosmic Jesters. Any unauthorized breach of a laboratory or archive by a non-Guild entity shall be treated as an act of hostility against the Accords. See § 900.1 for the requirements regarding the filing of notice before any authorized inspection commences.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "900.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.2 Penalties and Remedies; Sunrise Accrual and Appeals",
          "text": "Any violation of these provisions shall result in immediate cessation of the offending activity, forfeiture of all ill-gotten gains, and imposition of punitive damages as determined by the Archmage Sovereign or their delegate. The prevailing party may recover reasonable attorneys' fees and costs incurred in bringing this action to fruition. In egregious cases involving deliberate malice or repeated offenses, permanent revocation of licensure is mandatory under § 200.4(b).\n\nPenalties shall accrue from sunrise on the first day after the violation occurs (\"sunrise\" meaning actual dawn regardless of local time zone) until such time as full satisfaction has been rendered. Deliberate obstruction of enforcement efforts doubles accrued penalties per § 1301.5. Failure to post adequate security for a judgment renders double daily interest applicable, calculated at twice the standard Guild rate plus an additional ten percent premium.\n\nApplicants dissatisfied with any ruling may file a motion for review within seven days of notification. Such motions must include specific grounds for reversal supported by sworn affidavits and relevant documentary evidence. The reviewing panel consists of three randomly selected Archmages from outside the respondent's home Hall to ensure impartiality. Decisions rendered on appeal are final and binding upon all parties involved.\n\nOnly registered members in good standing with an active license may initiate legal proceedings under this chapter. Unlicensed practitioners forfeit all rights to seek relief through official channels and must instead pursue private remedies at their own peril. This restriction exists to prevent frivolous lawsuits from bogging down the judicial machinery while preserving access for legitimate grievances.\n\nThe Guild retains broad discretion in fashioning appropriate sanctions tailored to the circumstances of each case. These may include monetary fines, community service, mandatory retraining courses, temporary suspension without loss of seniority, or permanent disbarment depending on severity. The goal is always proportional punishment designed to deter future misconduct while maintaining public confidence in magical regulation overall.\n\nAll records relating to investigations and adjudications must be kept confidential unless disclosure is required by law or ordered by a presiding Archmage. This protects the privacy rights of all involved parties while ensuring transparency within the bounds necessary for effective governance. Redacted copies may be inspected upon written request subject to reasonable security clearances as deemed appropriate by the undersigned authority.\n\n§ 1301.2 Penalties and Remedies; Sunrise Accrual and Appeals\nsee § 1.9 Seals, Stamps, and What Is Not a Seal; under § 1.7 Construction: Aggregation of Conduct; cf. § 400.5 Unauthorized Titan Growth for analogous provisions regarding misuse of powers.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "200.4",
            "1301.5",
            "1301.2",
            "1.9",
            "1.7",
            "400.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.2 Penalties and Remedies; Sunrise Accrual and Appeals — Continued",
          "text": "VIOLATIONS OF THIS PART SHALL BE PUNISHABLE AS FOLLOWS: FOR FIRST OFFENSES, THE TYPICALLY INCUR A FINES RANGING FROM ONE TO TEN TIMES THE AMOUNT EVASIVELY AVOIDED, PLUS COSTS OF RECOVERY. SUBSEQUENT VIOLATIONS MAY RESULT IN SUSPENSION OF LICENSURE UP TO ONE YEAR PER COUNT, AT THE DISCRETION OF THE DESK. AGGRAVATING CIRCUMSTANCES SUCH AS WILFUL DECEPTION OR REPEATED OFFENSES WITHIN TWELVE MONTHS MAY LEAD TO REVOCATION OF PRIVILEGES INDEFINITELY.\n\nUNLESS OTHERWISE ORDERED BY THE COURT, ALL PENALTIES AND REMEDIES SHALL ACCRUE FROM SUNRISE ON THE DATE OF VIOLATION, REGARDLESS OF WHEN DISCOVERED OR LITIGATED. THIS \"SUNRISE RULE\" IS DEEMED ESSENTIAL TO MAINTAINING FISCAL STABILITY FOR THE GUILD TREASURY AND ENSURING FAIR TREATMENT OF ALL PARTIES INVOLVED IN UNLAWFUL ACTIVITIES UNDER THESE ACCORDS.\n\nAPPEALS FROM PENALTIES IMPOSED HEREUNDER MUST BE FILED WITHIN THIRTY DAYS OF SERVICE OF NOTICE, STATED IN WRITING AND SUPPORTED BY AFFIDAVITS AS RELEVANT. APPEAL JUDGES SHALL HAVE DISCRETION TO UPHOLD OR SET ASIDE ORIGINAL DECISIONS BASED UPON FACTUAL ERRORS OR ABUSE OF DISCRETION ONLY; PURELY LEGAL QUESTIONS ARE NOT SUBJECT TO REVIEW HEREIN UNLESS RAISED IN THE FIRST INSTANCE.\n\nANY PERSON WHOSE RIGHTS ARE AFFECTED BY THIS PART MAY INSPECT AND COPY ALL RELATED RECORDS DURING NORMAL BUSINESS HOURS, UPON PAYMENT OF FEE PER PAGE AS ESTABLISHED ANNUALLY BY RESOLUTION OF THE DESK. HOWEVER, PROPRIETARY INFORMATION OR TRADE SECRETS CONTAINED THEREIN SHALL REMAIN CONFIDENTIAL UNLESS DISCLOSURE IS REQUIRED BY LAW OR COURT ORDER.\n\nTHE GUILD PRESERVES ITS RIGHT TO SEEK DAMAGES FROM ANY PARTY WHO ACTS IN A MANNER THAT CAUSES FINANCIAL LOSS THROUGH ILLEGAL MEANS, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO CIVIL SUITS FOR COMPENSATION AND RESTITUTION OF UNJUSTLY OBTAINED PROFITS. SUCH CLAIMS SHALL BE ADJUDICATED PURSUANT TO APPROPRIATE PROCEDURES ESTABLISHED FROM TIME TO TIME BY THE DESK.\n\nNO PROVISION HEREIN SHALL BE CONSTRUED TO LIMIT OR EXCLUDE ANY OTHER REMEDY AVAILABLE AT LAW OR IN EQUITY, WHETHER STATUTORY OR COMMON LAW, UNLESS EXPRESSLY SO STATED. INJUNCTIVE RELIEF MAY BE GRANTED UPON ADEQUATE SHOWING OF IRREPARABLE HARM THAT CANNOT BE REDRESSED BY DAMAGES ALONE.\n\nTHIS SECTION SHALL GO INTO EFFECT IMMEDIATELY UPON FILING AND SHALL REMAIN IN FULL FORCE UNTIL SUPERSeded OR REVOKED PURSUANT TO DUE PROCESS PROCEEDINGS BEFORE THE MAGES' GUILD ACCORDS DESK OR ITS AUTHORIZED AGENTS. ANY AMENDMENTS HERETO MUST BE ADOPTED BY UNANIMOUS VOTE OF ALL ACTIVE LICENSURE HOLDERS IN GOOD STANDING AND SHALL BE PUBLISHED FOR THIRTY DAYS PRIOR TO IMPLEMENTATION TO ENSURE PROPER NOTICE AND OPPORTUNITY FOR COMMENT.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1301.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.2 Penalties and Remedies; Sunrise Accrual and Appeals — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "In the event of non-compliance with any provision herein, appropriate sanctions shall be imposed in accordance with established precedent and the gravity of the infraction. For willful violations or persistent disregard of the regulations, the Desk may impose escalating penalties ranging from fines to suspension of privileges, up to and including revocation of licensure under § 200.4. Each sanction must be proportionate, justifiable by evidence, and recorded in perpetuity as a matter of public record.\n\nThe concept of \"sunrise accrual\" applies where violations occur across multiple jurisdictions or timeframes. In such cases, penalties shall compound from the date of initial breach until full remediation is achieved. This principle ensures that transgressors cannot exploit temporal boundaries to evade liability. However, good-faith efforts at correction may mitigate accrued sanctions upon review by the Desk.\n\nParties aggrieved by alleged infractions have a right to due process before any punitive measures are enacted. Affected individuals or entities may petition for a hearing before an impartial tribunal comprising three members of the Desk and one external adjudicator appointed by lot. All proceedings shall be conducted openly, subject only to protective orders where warranted. The burden of proof rests upon the accuser to demonstrate, by clear and convincing evidence, that a violation has occurred and resulted in harm or prejudice.\n\nUpon completion of hearings, written findings and judgments shall be issued within thirty days, detailing the rationale for each decision. These rulings become binding unless successfully appealed within fourteen calendar days on grounds of procedural error or manifest injustice. Appeals shall follow standard appellate review protocols, with de novo consideration reserved solely for cases involving constitutional questions or fundamental rights violations.\n\nThe Desk maintains a publicly accessible log of all penalties imposed under this chapter, including the nature of infractions and sanctions applied. This transparency serves both as a deterrent to would-be violators and as guidance for law-abiding practitioners navigating the complex regulatory landscape. Regular audits ensure consistency in enforcement across regions and sectors.\n\nUltimately, the goal of § 1301.2 is not punishment for its own sake, but rather the cultivation of responsible magical citizenship. Through fair application of consequences and avenues for redress, the Accords strive to balance accountability with opportunity, fostering an environment where innovation may flourish alongside order. As Archmage Veyra once declared: \"Justice delayed is justice denied; yet haste breeds error. Balance must be struck between swift action and thoughtful deliberation.\" Thus stand these provisions, guiding us toward a brighter future illuminated by the twin lights of wisdom and restraint.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "200.4",
            "1301.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": "lmstudio",
      "fp": "16ac8898e62b63b0",
      "refs": [
        "1.2",
        "1.7",
