      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 300.6 Related Requirements; Compliance Obligations",
          "text": "Nothing in this Part shall be construed as limiting or expanding the scope of compliance obligations beyond what is expressly stated herein. Mages and their agents remain subject to all applicable laws, regulations, and ethical standards governing magical practice within the Autumnwood Accords jurisdiction, regardless of whether such matters fall under specific provisions enumerated hereafter. This principle ensures that no loopholes exist for evading accountability through technicalities or narrow readings of statutory language.\n\nFurther, it shall be deemed a continuing obligation upon each licensee to monitor developments in arcane theory and praxis that might impact their licensed activities. When new information emerges which could materially affect compliance status, affected parties must promptly notify the Autumnwood Accords Desk for guidance on appropriate remedial actions. Failure to do so may result in escalated enforcement measures up to and including revocation of privileges without prejudice to further penalties under other laws.\n\nThe requirements set forth herein are intended as minimum standards designed to protect public welfare while enabling lawful magical pursuits. Nothing contained therein shall be interpreted to preclude the adoption by individual practitioners or organizations of more stringent internal controls where deemed prudent in light of their specific circumstances and risks posed. Such voluntary measures may enhance operational efficiency and mitigate liability exposures, but shall not substitute for adherence to mandatory provisions outlined in this section.\n\nFinally, all disputes arising under these related requirements shall be resolved through binding arbitration administered by the Accords Desk, except where jurisdiction resides otherwise by operation of law or mutual agreement between disputants. The arbitrator's decision shall be final and enforceable as a judgment of any court of competent jurisdiction. This comprehensive framework ensures robust oversight while preserving flexibility for legitimate innovation within the bounds of responsible magical stewardship under the Autumnwood Accords regime.\n\nsee § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; see § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse; see § 300.3 Quiet List Procedure; see § 400.2 Pocket Dimensions as Labs\nunder § 1.8 Effective Date; under § 7.2 Continuing Obligations; under § 9.1 Binding Dispute Resolution; under § 10.3 Voluntary Compliance Measures",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "100.5",
            "200.4",
            "300.3",
            "400.2",
            "1.8",
            "7.2",
            "9.1",
            "10.3",
            "300.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 300.7 Compliance Obligations",
          "text": "All persons subject to the provisions of these Accords shall, at all times, maintain full and complete compliance with every term, condition, covenant, and stipulation contained herein, whether express or implied. Any failure to adhere strictly to the mandates set forth in this Code shall constitute a breach of contract and may result in immediate enforcement action by the Autumnwood Accords Desk.\n\nCompliance obligations extend beyond mere possession of required permits or licenses. Licensees must actively engage with regulatory authorities whenever circumstances warrant, providing timely notice of any changes that might affect their standing under these laws. This includes reporting new research findings, modifications to magical apparatus, and alterations in operational procedures that could have implications for public safety or national security.\n\nFailure to fulfill compliance duties shall be deemed willful misconduct, subjecting violators to enhanced penalties including monetary fines, license revocation, and potential criminal prosecution. Repeat offenders may face permanent disqualification from practicing magic within the jurisdiction entirely. The Accords Desk retains sole discretion to determine appropriate sanctions based on the severity of the infraction and any mitigating factors present.\n\nIt is incumbent upon each regulated party to exercise reasonable diligence in monitoring their own activities against the backdrop of evolving statutes and case law interpretations. Regulatory bodies shall provide guidance where necessary, but reliance solely on official communications without independent verification may not excuse subsequent liability for non-compliance. The burden of proof regarding adherence to all applicable provisions rests squarely with those charged with enforcement duties.\n\nViolations discovered through random inspection or whistleblower reports will be addressed expeditiously upon confirmation by competent authorities. Affected entities shall receive written notification detailing the specific breaches identified and afforded an opportunity to respond before any punitive measures are enacted. Due process safeguards remain paramount even as swift action is pursued to protect the broader community from potential harms arising from unlawful magical practices.\n\nUltimately, successful implementation of these standards depends upon collaborative efforts between regulators and industry participants alike. Open dialogue channels must be maintained to facilitate ongoing assessment of regulatory efficacy and adaptability to emerging challenges posed by advances in arcane technology and methodology. Through shared commitment to responsible stewardship of magical resources, we can ensure a prosperous future for all under the enduring shield of these sacred Accords.\n\nsee § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; see § 200.1 Licensure Required; see § 400.3 Borrowed Hours; Interest in Time; see § 500.1 Field Casting for Value.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "100.5",
            "200.1",
            "400.3",
            "500.1",
            "300.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 300.6 Compliance Obligations and Record Retention; § 300.7 Audit Rights and Pe",
          "text": "Every licensee and registered practitioner shall maintain accurate, complete, and up-to-date records of all magical activities conducted under the authority granted herein. Such records must include but are not limited to: a detailed log of all spells cast, transfigurations performed, or planar manipulations executed; copies of all permits obtained and fees paid; documentation of any adverse effects caused by such activities; and an inventory of all materials used in the process. These obligations shall extend to all agents, contractors, and subsidiaries operating on behalf of the licensee, regardless of jurisdictional boundaries.\n\nRecords must be retained for a minimum period of seven (7) years from the date of completion of each magical operation, unless otherwise specified by specific regulations governing particular classes of practice. All records shall be available for inspection upon reasonable notice by designated officials of the Autumnwood Accords Desk or its authorized representatives. Failure to maintain proper documentation in accordance with this section constitutes a material breach of license conditions and may result in immediate suspension of privileges pending review.\n\nIn addition to routine recordkeeping requirements, every licensee must submit an annual compliance report detailing all activities undertaken during the preceding calendar year. Such reports shall be filed electronically through the official portal within thirty (30) days following the close of each fiscal period, accompanied by a sworn affidavit affirming their accuracy and completeness. Late filings will incur a penalty equal to one hundred percent (100%) of applicable licensing fees for that period, plus an additional surcharge of fifty dollars ($50.00).\n\nThe Desk reserves the right to conduct unannounced audits at any time during normal business hours to verify adherence to these obligations. Licensees shall cooperate fully with such examinations and provide requested documentation without delay or resistance. Refusal to comply with audit procedures will be deemed evidence of bad faith intent and may trigger expedited disciplinary proceedings under applicable statutes.\n\nViolations of this section shall be subject to progressive sanctions ranging from monetary fines up to ten thousand guild credits per offense, through revocation of individual practitioner certificates, to outright cancellation of corporate charters. Repeat offenders within a rolling five-year window face automatic disqualification from future applications for at least one full term of office. In egregious cases involving gross negligence or willful misconduct, criminal charges may be pursued concurrently alongside civil penalties under general law.\n\nIt is the further duty of each licensee to promptly notify the Desk in writing of any changes affecting their operational status—including mergers, acquisitions, leadership transitions, or shifts in primary place of business—within ten (10) calendar days of occurrence. Failure to do so shall constitute a separate violation subject to independent sanctioning without prejudice to other ongoing enforcement actions. This proactive disclosure requirement ensures timely recalibration of oversight measures as needed to protect public welfare and maintain regulatory integrity across all sectors governed by the Accords.\n\nBy accepting a license or registration under these provisions, every participant expressly agrees to abide by all terms outlined herein and acknowledges that non-compliance carries serious consequences both legally and professionally. The spirit of cooperation between regulated entities and governing bodies is paramount in fostering an environment where magic may flourish safely for generations to come. Together we build bridges across divides, binding our fates in service of progress while safeguarding against misuse. Thus stands the covenant renewed once more—a testament to our shared commitment toward a brighter tomorrow guided by wisdom earned through trial and error alike. For as long as stars shine above us all, so too shall these laws endure, immutable anchors holding steady amidst shifting tides of change forevermore. Amen and amity unto thee. 🌟⚖️🤝",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "300.6",
            "300.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 300.8 Prohibited Magic and Sanctions",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords explicitly forbid the practice or study of certain magical disciplines deemed inherently dangerous to societal stability or individual safety. These prohibited arts include necromancy, blood magic, summoning entities from outside reality without strict containment protocols, and any form of transmutation that permanently alters matter at a fundamental level without official oversight. Violation of these prohibitions constitutes a serious offense under § 1002.3 and may result in immediate revocation of licensure pursuant to § 200.4(a).\n\nSanctions for unauthorized practice vary based on the severity and consequences of the act. Minor infractions, such as inadvertent exposure during research without malice, may incur fines up to one hundred gold pieces per violation (§ 1301.2(b)). More egregious offenses, including deliberate casting in public spaces or causing harm through reckless experimentation, carry heavier penalties ranging from temporary suspension to permanent expulsion from the Guild ranks. Repeat offenders face additional restrictions on their ability to utilize standard magical services provided by accredited practitioners under § 500.1(c).\n\nThe Accords further mandate that all licensed mages maintain detailed logs of their research activities and experimental procedures as part of ongoing compliance obligations (§ 300.8(d)). Failure to produce these records upon request from the Conservators or Aegis Magi may lead to presumption of guilt and expedited disciplinary proceedings under § 1401.2(b). This rigorous oversight ensures that prohibited magic remains firmly outside the purview of unqualified individuals while allowing responsible scholars access to necessary resources for approved investigations.\n\nIt is hereby declared that any individual found guilty of practicing forbidden arts shall be subject to immediate seizure of all magical implements and materials under § 1001.9(c). Furthermore, such persons may be barred indefinitely from seeking employment with the Guild or related entities unless they can demonstrate complete reform through years of exemplary service (§ 200.5(g)). These stringent measures reflect the profound risks posed by unregulated magic and underscore the collective responsibility of all practitioners to uphold the highest standards of safety and ethics in their work.\n\n\"The Autumnwood Accords\"\nSection 300 - Prohibited Magic and Sanctions\n§ 1002.3 — Offenses Against Magical Order; § 200.4(a) — Suspension for Violations; § 1301.2(b) — Fines for Minor Infractions; § 500.1(c) — Restrictions on Services; § 1001.9(c) — Seizure of Implements; § 1401.2(b) — Presumption of Guilt\n\n\"Magic is a powerful force that must be wielded with wisdom and restraint.\"\n— Archmage Theron, Conservator Leader\n\nUNOFFICIAL COMMENTARY: The prohibition of certain magical disciplines represents one of the most contentious issues within the Guild today. While traditionalists argue for absolute bans on \"dangerous arts,\" innovators contend that responsible research could unlock beneficial applications previously deemed impossible. This tension continues to shape ongoing debates over licensing requirements and oversight mechanisms across all levels of magical practice in the Midlands region.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1002.3",
            "200.4",
            "1301.2",
            "500.1",
            "300.8",
            "1401.2",
            "1001.9",
            "200.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Magic and Sanctions (Continued)",
          "text": "§ 300.8 Prohibited Magic and Sanctions (Expanded)\nIn accordance with § 1.7 Construction; Aggregation of Conduct, any mage found engaging in multiple prohibited magical acts shall face compounded penalties proportional to the severity and frequency of violations. The Desk retains sole authority under § 1.2 Enacting Authority; Autumnwood Accords Desk to determine appropriate sanctions based on individual circumstances. Minor infractions may result in mandatory retraining, fines up to one hundred gold crowns per violation, or temporary suspension of licensure not exceeding thirty days pursuant to § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse. Major offenses warrant imprisonment for a minimum of five years with no possibility of parole, coupled with permanent sealing of magic abilities via ritualistic binding as detailed in Archmage Theron's Codex of Containment Methods. In extreme cases involving threats to public safety or national security, the Sovereign may invoke emergency provisions under § 100.8 Emergency Sitting to impose immediate life imprisonment without trial. All convicted offenders must undergo psychological evaluation and rehabilitation programs overseen by qualified professionals approved by the Guild before being considered for any future leniency. The Desk shall maintain comprehensive records of all violations and sanctions imposed, making them accessible upon request under § 1401.1 Historical Annotations; Form. This clause supersedes all prior agreements or customary practices regarding disciplinary action for magical transgressions within the Midlands jurisdiction. Any dispute concerning interpretation or enforcement shall be resolved exclusively through established legal channels outlined herein, with final adjudication resting solely with the Archmage Sovereign acting in concert with the full Council of Mages. Failure to comply with these mandates renders a mage persona non grata forevermore, subject to extraterritorial prosecution should they ever set foot within Autumnwood's borders again.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "300.8",
            "1.7",
            "1.2",
            "200.4",
            "100.8",
            "1401.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Compliance Obligations and Record Retention",
          "text": "§ 300.6 Compliance Obligations and Record Retention; Every mage bound by these Accords shall maintain accurate records of all magical research, experimentation, and field application as prescribed herein. Such logs must be kept in a secure location accessible to the Aegis Magi upon demand, with a copy filed with the Autumnwood Accords Desk within thirty days of completion. Failure to comply with this provision constitutes grounds for immediate suspension or revocation of licensure under § 200.4.\n\nAll records shall include detailed descriptions of spells cast, materials used, outcomes achieved, and any adverse effects observed. Special attention must be paid to documenting instances where prohibited schools of magic were employed or attempted, regardless of success. These logs serve as the primary evidence for determining violations of the Quiet List and other regulatory provisions. Mages found withholding or falsifying records shall face enhanced penalties pursuant to § 1001.9.\n\nThe Desk reserves the right to audit compliance at any time without prior notice. Refusal to provide requested documentation will be treated as a willful obstruction of justice, subjecting the offending party to criminal prosecution under applicable statutes. Repeated or egregious noncompliance may result in permanent disqualification from practicing magic within the jurisdiction.\n\n§ 300.7 Audit Rights and Penalties; To ensure adherence to these rigorous standards, the Desk shall conduct periodic inspections of registered practitioners' operations. These audits may encompass physical examinations of facilities, review of personal effects, and interviews with associates as deemed necessary by investigating officers. All parties must cooperate fully during such proceedings or risk escalation of sanctions.\n\nViolations uncovered through audit processes will trigger an immediate investigation into potential breaches of the Accords. Depending on severity, consequences may range from retraining mandates to outright expulsion from the Guild. In extreme cases where public safety is jeopardized, authorities shall not hesitate to utilize full force against recalcitrant individuals. The protection of society takes precedence over individual convenience or profit-seeking endeavors.\n\nThis comprehensive framework establishes clear expectations for responsible magical practice while affording appropriate oversight mechanisms. Through diligent enforcement of these rules, the Guild strives to balance innovation with stability in an ever-evolving landscape of arcane possibilities. All members are urged to embrace this shared responsibility and uphold the highest ideals inherent in our noble pursuit of knowledge and mastery over the forces that shape our world.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "300.6",
            "200.4",
            "1001.9",
            "300.7"
          ]
        }
      ],
