    {
      "cite": "400.6",
      "part": "part_iv",
      "title": "Conditions for Valid Research Permits",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.6 Related Requirements and Conditions for Valid Research Permits",
          "text": "Research permits issued under these Accords are subject to ongoing compliance with all applicable provisions herein, including but not limited to §§ 200.1 through 200.5 regarding licensure limits and guest caster protocols, as well as § 300.6 governing the reclassification of sanctioned arts upon discovery of new uses or effects. Any material deviation from permit terms voids authorization immediately and subjects the holder to disciplinary proceedings under Part III herein.\n\nFurthermore, all research activities conducted pursuant to valid permits must maintain full transparency with the Conservator Oversight Committee as established in § 300.4. Quarterly reports detailing experimental parameters, outcomes, and potential societal impacts shall be submitted within fifteen (15) days of each calendar quarter's conclusion. Failure to submit such reports constitutes a substantive violation warranting permit suspension pending investigation.\n\nSpecial provisions apply when research involves the manipulation of temporal constructs or pocket dimensions per §§ 400.2 and 400.3 respectively. Such work requires dual authorization from both the Conservator Oversight Committee AND an independent panel of ethical mages appointed by Archmage Veyra personally. Additional security measures including continuous monitoring via Aegis Magi sensors must be implemented throughout the duration of experiments involving time-dilation effects exceeding three (3) standard hours cumulative per session.\n\nSpecimen custody protocols outlined in § 400.5 remain mandatory even after research conclusion unless otherwise noted in individual permit agreements. Returned materials must undergo full inspection by designated Guild officials before release to researchers, with documented verification of integrity and purity levels meeting established standards. Any discrepancies discovered post-return shall be addressed through formal dispute resolution channels rather than unilateral action by either party.\n\nViolations of these related requirements may result in escalating penalties ranging from fines up to one thousand (1000) gold pieces per incident, suspension of research privileges for periods not exceeding six (6) months, revocation of existing permits with no replacement eligibility during suspension term, or permanent expulsion from the Guild entirely depending on severity and frequency of infractions. Repeat offenders face heightened scrutiny regardless of individual permit status.\n\nThe Conservator Oversight Committee retains sole discretion to modify these requirements as deemed necessary for public safety based on emerging scientific understanding or changing geopolitical circumstances. Such modifications shall be communicated via official bulletin boards posted at all major research facilities within thirty (30) days of adoption, with a minimum two-week notice period prior to implementation unless emergency conditions warrant immediate effectuation.\n\nResearchers are reminded that their obligations under these provisions extend beyond mere contractual compliance and encompass broader ethical considerations regarding the responsible stewardship of magical knowledge for the greater good of society at large. Neglect of this higher duty may invoke additional sanctions independent of technical violation status.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "200.1",
            "300.6",
            "300.4",
            "400.2",
            "400.5",
            "400.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.6 Related Requirements and Conditions for Valid Research Permits — Continued",
          "text": "§ 400.6 Each research permit issued under this Part shall contain specific conditions tailored to the nature of the proposed study, including but not limited to restrictions on magical amplification, mandatory monitoring by Aegis Magi, and limits on temporal displacement. Failure to adhere strictly to these terms constitutes a material breach warranting immediate suspension or revocation of authority granted herein. See § 400.2 regarding spatial containment protocols, and under § 1301.2 for applicable penalties upon violation.\n\nFurthermore, all experiments utilizing borrowed hours must be conducted within officially sanctioned facilities equipped with adequate shielding to prevent collateral temporal instability. Any unauthorized extension beyond allotted timeframes requires supplementary approval from the Innovators' Oversight Committee. Breach of this requirement shall result in forfeiture of future permits and potential criminal charges for endangerment of public safety. Reference § 400.3 for detailed provisions on temporal accounting, and consult § 500.1 regarding liability for field-induced anomalies.\n\nSpecimen acquisition must comply with all import/export regulations set forth by the Autumnwood Customs Bureau, including payment of applicable tariffs and submission of full provenance documentation. Possession of prohibited artifacts without proper clearance exposes the holder to seizure and prosecution under §§ 300.2–300.4. Similarly, replication of protected designs or forbidden techniques without explicit written consent violates intellectual property laws enforced by the Conservators' Guild. See § 100.6 for details on delegation restrictions pertaining to such matters.\n\nIt is hereby declared that no research permit confers ownership rights over discovered phenomena or their applications. All findings remain the exclusive property of the Mages' Guild until formally licensed for commercial exploitation under separate agreement. Unauthorized publication or dissemination of sensitive data constitutes gross misconduct subject to disciplinary action pursuant to § 200.4. For complete terms of assignment and indemnification, refer to §§ 1101.1–1101.5 governing proprietary interests in magical inventions.\n\nThis section shall be construed liberally to promote responsible advancement of arcane knowledge while safeguarding societal welfare. Ambiguities herein shall be resolved in favor of strict adherence to established safety standards and ethical guidelines. Any conflicting provisions elsewhere in this Codex are superseded by these specific operational requirements designed to mitigate inherent risks associated with cutting-edge magical inquiry. Under § 1.7, terms used herein carry their plain meaning unless defined otherwise, ensuring clarity for all parties bound by these regulations.\"",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "400.6",
            "400.2",
            "1301.2",
            "400.3",
            "500.1",
            "300.2",
            "100.6",
            "200.4",
            "1101.1",
            "1.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.6 Related Requirements and Conditions for Valid Research Permits — Administration",
          "text": "The issuance of a research permit under this Part is contingent upon the applicant's full compliance with all stipulated conditions precedent, including but not limited to the completion of requisite safety training, payment of applicable fees in Wario Coin, and submission of detailed experimental protocols for review by the Conservator Council. Failure to satisfy any such requirement shall render the permit void ab initio and may result in immediate revocation of prior authorizations granted to said applicant or their affiliated entities.\n\nFurthermore, all research conducted pursuant to a valid permit must be strictly confined to the parameters outlined therein, with any deviation requiring supplementary approval from the Desk. Unauthorized modification of experimental procedures or scope constitutes gross negligence and shall be punishable as a Class A offense under § 1003.4(a). In cases where the nature of proposed experiments poses unacceptable risks to public safety or ecological stability regardless of containment measures, the Conservators reserve the right to deny issuance outright without further recourse for appeal.\n\nThe permittee bears sole responsibility for maintaining comprehensive records documenting all aspects of their investigations, including raw data, observations, and conclusions derived therefrom. Such documentation must be made available upon reasonable request by Guild officials or qualified third parties acting under authority granted herein. Refusal to provide access to these materials may lead to disciplinary action up to and including expulsion from the profession.\n\nFinally, it is hereby mandated that all findings resulting from permitted research be submitted for archival in accordance with § 1002.9 within thirty (30) days of completion, unless otherwise specified by special directive of the Sovereign Archmage. This ensures preservation of collective knowledge and facilitates future inquiry while preventing duplication of effort or unnecessary risk-taking. Noncompliance with this filing obligation shall be treated as a willful violation of fiduciary duty owed to the Guild community at large.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1003.4",
            "1002.9",
            "400.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.6 Related Requirements and Conditions for Valid Research Permits — Oversight",
          "text": "Under § 400.1, every research permit issued by the Autumnwood Accords Desk is subject to additional conditions precedent that must be satisfied before the grant of authority becomes effective. These ancillary requirements are enumerated herein to ensure that all parties understand their obligations beyond the basic terms set forth in the main body of the statute. Failure to comply with any such condition shall render the permit void ab initio, and may expose the holder to disciplinary action under these Accords or applicable penal provisions.\n\nFirst, every applicant for a research permit must submit a detailed plan of operations outlining the intended scope, methods, and duration of their proposed magical investigations. This operational blueprint must be reviewed and approved by at least two Conservator magi prior to issuance of the permit, in accordance with § 300.2 regarding oversight of unsanctioned arts. The plan shall include risk assessments identifying potential hazards arising from the research activities, along with mitigation strategies designed to minimize collateral damage or injury to third parties. Such documentation serves both as a guide for safe conduct and as evidence of due diligence should adverse events occur during execution of the permitted work.\n\nSecond, each permit holder must maintain comprehensive logs documenting all experimental procedures performed under the authority thereof. These records shall be kept in triplicate: one copy retained by the researcher, one filed with the local Guild Hall where research is conducted, and one submitted quarterly to the central archives at Autumn Wood for audit purposes. Logs must accurately reflect dates, times, locations, materials used, results obtained, and any deviations from the original plan of operations noted above. Tampering with or falsifying such documents constitutes a serious offense punishable under § 1001 regarding fraud in official returns.\n\nThird, researchers operating under valid permits are required to secure written indemnification agreements from all persons or entities potentially affected by their activities. These contracts must expressly hold harmless the Autumnwood Accords Desk and its officers from any claims arising out of negligent or intentional wrongdoing by the permit holder during the course of their research duties. Indemnity shall extend not only to direct losses but also to consequential damages, legal fees, and other costs incurred in defending against such suits. Failure to obtain proper indemnification may result in denial of the initial application or revocation of an existing permit without prejudice to further enforcement actions.\n\nFinally, all research permits automatically expire upon occurrence of any event specified herein that would materially alter the risk profile associated with their continued validity. Such triggering events include but are not limited to: death or incapacitation of the named researcher; cessation of operations at the host facility where work was being conducted; publication of findings contrary to established magical theory; discovery of new hazards related to the subject matter; or lapse of more than one year since date of issuance unless renewed in accordance with § 400.1. Upon expiration, any outstanding permits shall be cancelled forthwith and all associated obligations terminated except where otherwise provided by law or mutual agreement between affected parties.\n\nThese provisions are designed to strike an appropriate balance between fostering innovation within safe boundaries while protecting public welfare from reckless experimentation unchecked by responsible oversight mechanisms inherent in our system of self-governance through the Accords. Compliance with each requirement is mandatory and non-negotiable for all holders of research permits issued under this Code.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "400.1",
            "300.2",
            "400.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.6 Related Requirements and Conditions for Valid Research Permits — Continu",
          "text": "Research permits issued under the authority of this Part are subject to numerous conditions precedent and subsequent, which must be strictly adhered to in order to maintain their validity. First and foremost, permit holders must submit a detailed research proposal outlining the specific magical phenomena to be studied, the methodologies to be employed, and the expected outcomes. This proposal must undergo review by at least two Conservator-approved peers prior to issuance of final approval. Failure to provide adequate justification for proposed experiments may result in denial or revocation of the permit without recourse.\n\nSecondly, all research conducted pursuant to a valid permit must occur within designated facilities under constant supervision by qualified Guild observers. Unauthorized deviations from approved protocols are strictly prohibited and shall constitute grounds for immediate suspension of privileges. Permit holders agreeing to conduct work outside official parameters do so at their own peril and assume full liability for any resulting damages or disruptions. The Guild disclaims all responsibility for accidents or anomalies arising from off-book activities, regardless of prior authorization status.\n\nThirdly, timely reporting of results is mandatory upon completion of each phase of the research project. Final reports must be submitted within thirty days in triplicate, formatted according to standardized templates provided by the Desk. These documents will undergo rigorous vetting before being archived for future reference. Concealment or falsification of data carries severe penalties, including permanent revocation of all licenses and potential criminal prosecution under existing statutes regarding scientific fraud. Transparency remains an absolute requirement throughout the research lifecycle.\n\nFinally, any discoveries deemed significant enough to impact public safety or ethical norms must be promptly communicated to relevant authorities for appropriate action. The Guild reserves discretion to halt ongoing studies at any point if unforeseen risks emerge during execution. Permit holders agree to cooperate fully with such directives and accept binding instructions regarding cessation of work as necessary under the circumstances. This clause does not absolve researchers of their duty to exercise due diligence in monitoring progress and mitigating potential hazards proactively. Compliance with all stipulated obligations is essential for preserving both personal standing and collective security within the magical community at large.\n\nsee § 400.1 Research Permits; § 300.5 Research Copies of Quiet Items; § 500.2 Unscheduled Weather; under § 1.7 Aggregation of Conduct, repeated infractions may lead to escalated sanctions beyond simple permit revocation. Additionally, reference is made to § 1401.3 Savings Against the Iron Mandate regarding potential conflicts with rival legal frameworks. Permit holders should consult with their supervising clerks regularly to ensure continued adherence to all applicable rules and regulations throughout the duration of their assigned projects. Vigilance and accountability are paramount in safeguarding the integrity of magical inquiry while minimizing collateral harm to innocent bystanders.\n\n\"Research permits grant limited authority, not unlimited freedom. Violations will be punished accordingly.\" - Archmage Theron, Conservator Leader",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "400.1",
            "300.5",
            "500.2",
            "1.7",
            "1401.3",
            "400.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.6 Related Requirements and Conditions for Valid Research Permits — Procedure",
          "text": "The issuance of a research permit under these Accords is not merely an administrative act but a solemn contractual obligation laden with conditions precedent, subsequent, and ongoing that must be scrupulously observed to maintain the integrity of the scientific endeavor. Each application submitted by Innovators seeking access to restricted materials or techniques shall include a detailed protocol outlining intended experiments, safety measures, contingency plans for catastrophic failure, and methods for data preservation. Failure to disclose relevant information may result in immediate revocation of approval and potential prosecution under § 300.3 Quiet List Procedure should foul play be suspected.\n\nPermits granted herein are non-transferable and expire upon completion of the stated project or after one calendar year, whichever occurs first, unless renewed by written consent from the Conservators' Council. Any deviation from approved procedures requires prior notification and may necessitate additional oversight measures including unannounced site inspections conducted by Aegis Magi acting in their official capacity under § 200.6 Constructs That Hold a Quill. Researchers found guilty of negligence resulting in loss of life or property shall face disciplinary action ranging from suspension without pay to permanent expulsion from the Guild depending on severity of offense and prior record.\n\nFurthermore, all findings derived from permitted research must be submitted for peer review within ninety days following conclusion of work unless waived by special dispensation. Results deemed controversial or potentially dangerous to public safety may be redacted or classified pending further investigation by independent arbitrators appointed jointly by the Archmage Sovereign and representatives of affected communities. Refusal to comply with post-study reporting mandates constitutes breach of contract and will trigger automatic termination of all future privileges regardless of outstanding debts owed.\n\nIn witness whereof, this Codex is hereunto set forth under the Great Seal of Autumnwood bearing date thereof, serving as binding law throughout the known realms so long as magic itself continues to exist in any form whatsoever! 📜✨🧙‍♀️⚖️",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "300.3",
            "200.6",
            "400.6"
          ]
        }
      ],
