    {
      "cite": "800.6",
      "part": "part_viii",
      "title": "Ancillary Obligations",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.6 Related Requirements and Ancillary Obligations",
          "text": "The provisions contained herein constitute the minimum standards for the administration of disciplinary proceedings within the Autumnwood Accords framework. Nothing in this section shall be construed to limit or restrict the powers vested in the Aegis Magi under existing statutes, nor shall it impair the Guild's inherent right to protect itself from threats to its integrity and safety. Compliance with these requirements is mandatory for all members subject to disciplinary action. Failure to adhere may result in escalated sanctions or revocation of membership privileges entirely.\n\nIn addition to the primary sanctions outlined above, the Desk may impose ancillary obligations deemed necessary to mitigate harm caused by the offending conduct. Such measures might include mandatory counseling sessions, community service projects involving magical safety education, financial restitution for damages incurred, or supervised practice periods under strict oversight. These requirements shall be tailored to the individual circumstances of each case and will remain in effect until such time as the Desk determines that further action is no longer warranted.\n\nAll disciplinary actions taken pursuant to these provisions must be documented thoroughly and stored securely in accordance with applicable privacy laws. Records shall include detailed notes on proceedings, evidence presented, witness statements, expert opinions where relevant, and final determinations along with rationales therefor. Access to such files is restricted to authorized personnel only, except as required by law or court order. This ensures both accountability for the Guild's actions and protection of sensitive information from unauthorized disclosure.\n\nThe Desk retains sole discretion to modify these requirements at any time based on evolving circumstances or new insights regarding the nature and extent of violations committed. Notice of such changes shall be provided promptly via official channels established by the Accords. Members are expected to stay informed about current regulations through regular review of published materials and attendance at mandatory training sessions as scheduled. Ignorance of the law is no excuse for noncompliance under any circumstances whatsoever.\n\nUltimately, these related obligations exist to reinforce the core principles guiding magical practice within society: responsibility, restraint, respect for others' rights and safety, and commitment to continuous self-improvement as a responsible citizen-caster. By accepting them willingly and carrying out their duties diligently, members demonstrate their dedication to maintaining harmony between arcane pursuits and everyday life - a noble goal worthy of our highest aspirations.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "800.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.6 Related Requirements and Ancillary Obligations — Continued",
          "text": "The sanctions imposed under this Part shall extend to any affiliated parties who knowingly aided or abetted the primary transgressor, unless they can demonstrate lack of actual knowledge or participation in the specific illegal act. See § 1001.4 regarding vicarious liability for acts committed within scope of employment or agency relationships. This includes mages who provided training, equipment, or shelter to known violators, as well as those who facilitated concealment or escape from consequences.\n\nIn addition to direct penalties, the Accords mandate restitution payments to victims where feasible, calculated based on actual losses suffered plus reasonable out-of-pocket expenses incurred in mitigating harm. The Guild shall have standing to pursue such claims directly against offending mages and their estates upon default of voluntary repayment arrangements. Recovery priorities are established under § 1001.9, which details the order of satisfaction for competing creditor interests arising from magical misdeeds.\n\nFurthermore, all disciplinary actions taken pursuant to this Part must be accompanied by a formal finding of fact supported by competent evidence, detailing the nature and extent of violations committed. Such findings shall remain on file indefinitely unless expunged through successful review proceedings initiated within two years of final disposition. See § 800.3 regarding appeals processes available to sanctioned individuals seeking reconsideration of adverse determinations.\n\nThe Guild reserves the right to impose additional restrictions or prohibitions on formerly punished mages beyond those explicitly outlined in individual orders, based upon patterns of behavior indicative of continued risk to public safety and magical integrity. These may include limits on practice locations, client lists, transaction volumes, or types of services rendered entirely. Compliance with such conditions is mandatory and subject to random inspection by authorized representatives.\n\nFinally, any attempt to circumvent the spirit of these sanctions through technicalities or minor infractions will be treated as an aggravating circumstance warranting stricter enforcement measures. The ultimate goal remains preservation of magical order and protection of innocent parties from exploitation by rogue practitioners. See § 1001.7 on equitable principles guiding discretionary authority vested in the Desk. Failure to adhere fully to these ancillary obligations may result in escalated penalties, including permanent revocation of licensure and referral for criminal prosecution under applicable statutes.\n\n\"Justice is not merely punishment—it is restoration of balance through comprehensive accountability.\" — Archmage Veyra's Oath as Sovereign of Autumnwood",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1001.4",
            "1001.9",
            "800.3",
            "1001.7",
            "800.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Ancillary Obligations and Related Requirements",
          "text": "§ 800.6 Related Requirements and Ancillary Duties\nBeyond the primary sanctions enumerated in this Part, the Mages' Guild may impose ancillary obligations upon those adjudicated guilty of violations herein. These secondary measures serve both punitive and corrective functions, aimed at mitigating future harm to the arcane community. Such duties shall be deemed integral to any judgment rendered by a competent tribunal under these Accords.\n\nA principal ancillary obligation is the requirement for periodic monitoring of an offender's compliance with court orders. The Guild may assign one or more Aegis Magi to conduct unannounced inspections of the subject's domicile and business premises, ensuring that no prohibited magical activities are undertaken in violation of the ruling. Such monitors shall possess full authority to enter without warrant upon reasonable suspicion of non-compliance. Refusal to permit entry shall constitute a separate offense under § 802.14 Obstruction of Justice, punishable by additional sanctions.\n\nFurthermore, convicted parties may be compelled to submit detailed financial disclosures regarding any income derived from illicit magical practices during the relevant period. These records allow the Guild to assess both the scope and profitability of the violation, informing decisions about restitution amounts and future regulatory oversight levels. Failure to provide accurate information may result in enhanced penalties or revocation of existing licenses.\n\nIn cases involving physical damage caused by unauthorized casting, offenders shall be required to restore affected areas to their prior condition at their own expense, unless impracticality can be demonstrated. This includes repairing structural integrity, cleaning soot and residue from walls and floors, and replacing any destroyed furnishings or equipment. The cost of such remediation may be levied as a civil penalty against the violator's assets upon default judgment.\n\nParties ordered to undergo magical retraining shall attend all mandated sessions conducted by certified instructors approved by the Guild. Attendance records must be submitted weekly for verification. Any missed classes without valid excuse will result in dismissal and reinstatement of original charges, with enhanced penalties applied retroactively. Completion certificates issued by the training facility serve as proof of compliance but do not absolve underlying liability.\n\nFinally, offenders may be required to execute a formal affidavit swearing never again to engage in the specific prohibited activities constituting their offense. This document shall be recorded permanently and produced upon request by any law enforcement agency or interested party. Breach of oath binds the maker to perjury charges under common law, compounding legal consequences.\n\nThese ancillary obligations remain enforceable for a period specified in each individual order, not exceeding five years from entry unless extended by subsequent ruling. All costs associated with monitoring, inspection, and enforcement shall be borne initially by the Guild but may subsequently be recovered through civil action against the defaulting party. Nothing herein precludes additional remedies available at law or equity as appropriate to the circumstances.\n\nsee § 800.1 Discipline; Range of Sanctions for primary penalties; see § 802.14 Obstruction of Justice regarding interference with monitors; under § 1.7 Construction, Aggregation of Conduct allows cumulative sanctions when warranted by severity.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "800.6",
            "802.14",
            "800.1",
            "1.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Ancillary Obligations and Related Requirements — Continued",
          "text": "§ 800.6 Related Requirements and Ancillary Duties in Disciplinary Matters\n\nIn addition to the explicit sanctions outlined herein, mages subject to disciplinary action may be required to fulfill certain ancillary obligations designed to mitigate harm and restore balance. Such duties are imposed at the discretion of the Paradox Trial Panel and shall be commensurate with the severity of the infraction and the resources available to the accused. Failure to comply with these requirements without valid cause shall constitute a continuing violation, subjecting the mage to further penalties up to and including permanent sealing of magical abilities.\n\nOne common ancillary duty involves restitution in kind or value. Where feasible, a convicted mage may be ordered to return stolen materials, undo alterations made to property or persons, or compensate for losses sustained by victims. In cases where direct restoration is impractical, monetary compensation calculated according to established valuation schedules shall suffice. The Panel retains authority to structure payment plans or accept alternative forms of restitution as appropriate under the circumstances.\n\nMages may also be required to undergo mandatory re-education programs aimed at reinforcing adherence to the Accords and correcting flawed thinking patterns that led to their transgressions. Such instruction shall be provided by qualified Guild instructors and completed under supervised conditions. Attendance records and written examinations will constitute part of the official file and shall be reviewed prior to any consideration of sentence reduction or early release from a seal order.\n\nAnother frequent requirement involves community service performed for charitable causes approved by the Guild. These assignments serve both as penance for past misdeeds and as an opportunity for offenders to contribute positively to society during their period of confinement or probation. Work details may range from manual labor at public works sites to providing specialized skills in areas such as tutoring, medical assistance, or technical consulting, always within limits set by safety protocols.\n\nFinally, mages subject to disciplinary measures must submit to periodic evaluation by independent observers appointed by the Panel. These assessments will monitor compliance with all conditions of release and provide recommendations regarding any necessary adjustments to sentencing parameters. Reports generated during this surveillance shall become part of the permanent record and may be referenced in future proceedings involving the same individual or their associates.\n\nIt is imperative that all parties involved recognize these ancillary obligations as integral components of the disciplinary process rather than optional add-ons. Only through comprehensive implementation of both primary sanctions and supplementary duties can the Guild effectively uphold its mandate to preserve order, prevent abuse of magic, and protect the interests of all citizens within its jurisdiction.\n\nsee § 800.2 Paradox Trial Procedure for detailed guidelines on determining appropriate remedies; see also § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting regarding impartial adjudication standards. Under § 300.1 Schedules of Arts, valuations for restitution purposes shall follow established tables unless extraordinary circumstances warrant deviation at the Panel's discretion per § 1401.2 Dead Citations. Ancillary duties imposed hereunder must comply with all provisions set forth in Part III governing fair treatment and due process rights of accused persons.\n\nThis page was last updated on October 3rd, 2024 by Clerk Elara Vane following ratification by the full Autumn Wood Accords Desk via unanimous vote 19-0. Any amendments proposed for future consideration must be submitted in writing at least seven days prior to a scheduled meeting and circulated to all members for review.\"",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "800.6",
            "800.2",
            "100.5",
            "300.1",
            "1401.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.6 Related Requirements and Ancillary Obligations — Administration",
          "text": "The Accords recognize that sanctions imposed under this Part may generate secondary liabilities or duties beyond the primary penalty itself. Such ancillary obligations are deemed related requirements that must be satisfied to complete the remedial process fully. Failure to comply with these derivative mandates may result in additional penalties or escalation of existing sanctions.\n\nUnder § 800.2, a mage found guilty at Paradox Trial faces one of several possible punishments ranging from temporary suspension to permanent sealing of magical abilities. Each sanction carries implicit conditions that extend beyond the initial ruling. For instance, a suspended caster must undergo mandatory retraining under direct supervision before regaining full licensure. This includes periodic testing and written examinations administered by authorized Guild officials.\n\nSimilarly, those subject to § 800.3's Seal of Silence are required to refrain from discussing their conviction outside designated channels. Breach of this confidentiality provision constitutes a separate offense punishable under § 1201.4 for unauthorized disclosure of protected information. Violations may lead to extended confinement or harsher penalties upon review by the Archmage Sovereign.\n\nThe Accords further stipulate that mages sentenced to § 800.5's pocket-prison regime must maintain a specified level of magical discipline while incarcerated. Regular assessments determine whether the offender has sufficiently mastered self-control measures prior to release. Failure to meet these standards may result in indefinite extension of imprisonment without trial.\n\nFinally, § 800.4 mandates that any fines levied against convicted casters be paid directly into the Guild Treasury within thirty days. Late payments accrue interest at a rate of five percent per month until fully resolved. Recalcitrant debtors face further legal action including potential seizure of personal assets held in their name.\n\nIn sum, compliance with sanctions under this Part demands adherence not only to the explicit terms but also to all associated duties arising therefrom. Only through full satisfaction of these combined obligations can a sanctioned mage expect restoration of standing within the Guild community. The Archmage Sovereign retains ultimate authority to interpret and enforce these ancillary requirements as necessary to maintain public safety and order.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "800.2",
            "800.3",
            "1201.4",
            "800.5",
            "800.4",
            "800.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.6 Related Requirements and Ancillary Obligations — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "In addition to the primary obligations enumerated herein, each Licensee shall comply with all ancillary requirements imposed by the Guild or its authorized agents. These may include but are not limited to: submission of periodic progress reports detailing research outcomes; attendance at mandatory safety briefings concerning planar hazards; payment of applicable fees for specialized equipment or consumables; and adherence to any additional protocols deemed necessary to mitigate risk to public welfare. Failure to satisfy such ancillary conditions shall constitute a material breach of the Agreement, entitling the Guild to immediate suspension or revocation of the License at its sole discretion.\n\nThe Licensing Office reserves the right to impose further obligations as circumstances dictate, provided they are reasonably related to the safe and lawful exercise of Licensed Magic. Examples may include the installation of monitoring devices within research facilities, the provision of access logs documenting all spellcastings exceeding certain thresholds, or the requirement to maintain a dedicated emergency fund for rapid remediation of unintended magical side-effects. Licensees agree to promptly notify the Desk of any changes that might impact their ability to fulfill these duties, such as alterations in personnel, financial status, or operational capacity.\n\nMatters not explicitly addressed in this Section shall be governed by custom and practice established through prior rulings of the Autumnwood Accords Desk. In cases of ambiguity, the interpretation most favorable to public safety prevails unless contradicted by express statutory language. Licensees are encouraged to seek clarification from their assigned Clerk whenever uncertainty arises regarding compliance standards or procedural nuances, ensuring continued adherence to the highest ideals of magical stewardship as embodied in this Codex.\n\nThis Section is hereby ratified and incorporated into full force and effect, binding upon all current and future Licensees without exception. Any conflicting provisions shall be deemed null and void to the extent of such inconsistency. The Licensing Office retains ultimate authority over enforcement mechanisms, including but not limited to monetary penalties, suspension of privileges, revocation of certification, and referral for disciplinary action pursuant to applicable laws and regulations. Through diligent observance of these obligations, Licensees affirm their commitment to upholding the integrity and prosperity of the Guild while pursuing their noble quest for knowledge under responsible guidance.\n\nsee § 800.5 Scope of Authority; see § 900.1 Remedies for Breach; see § 200.3 Temporary Mouths — Continued.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "800.5",
            "900.1",
            "200.3",
            "800.6"
          ]
        }
      ],
