    {
      "cite": "500.7",
      "part": "part_v",
      "title": "Public Safety — Additional Protocols",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Public Safety — Additional Protocols",
          "text": "This Part shall be read in conjunction with the following provisions which govern related matters of public safety and ethical conduct: § 1.4 Persons Bound (defining scope of applicability); § 300.2 Necromancy; Unsanctioned Arts (prohibiting forbidden schools without exception); § 500.1 Field Casting for Value (regulating commercial magic work); § 600.1 Contracts with Non-Casters (governing binding agreements involving mundane parties). See also § 400.2 Pocket Dimensions as Labs and § 400.3 Borrowed Hours; Interest in Time regarding temporal manipulation hazards. Under § 700.5 Ethical Boundaries of Professional Practice, all licensed mages must adhere to standards of care even when operating outside formal Guild oversight. The Desk retains discretion under § 100.8 Emergency Sitting to intervene where imminent danger is evident, regardless of jurisdictional limits in § 200.6 Delegation to Clerks. Cross-reference § 300.4 Reclassification for procedures on re-evaluating the risk profile of specific magical applications. All citations herein are binding unless explicitly superseded by newer enactments per § 1.8 Effective Date. The Conservator faction may petition under § 1201.5 Related Requirements to impose additional safeguards deemed necessary for public welfare, subject to review by Archmage Veyra pursuant to § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild. Innovators asserting rights under § 900.6 Related Requirements must submit written justification demonstrating no net increase in societal risk. Failure to comply with any provision of this Part may result in disciplinary action up to and including revocation of licensure per § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse. Mages found guilty of gross negligence or willful misconduct face enhanced penalties under § 1301.2 Penalties; Sunrise Accrual applies where applicable. The Desk shall maintain a register of all complaints filed under this Section, with summaries made available annually in the Official Record per § 100.4 Records of Speech. Any disputes arising from enforcement actions must be resolved through formal grievance procedures outlined in § 1301.3 Appeals before resorting to extralegal measures prohibited by § 900.7 Related Requirements. Violations involving threats to national security fall under exclusive jurisdiction of the Aegis Magi per § 800.6 Related Requirements, with final adjudication authority vested in Archmage Theron subject to appeal to Veyra. This Section remains in full force and effect until explicitly repealed or amended by proper legislative action as defined herein. All provisions shall be construed liberally to promote public safety while preserving legitimate magical pursuits consistent with the spirit of these Accords. See § 1.7 Construction; Aggregation of Conduct for interpretive guidance on cumulative violations. Any ambiguities shall be resolved in favor of the stricter standard applicable under circumstances present, ensuring maximum protection for all citizens within the Guild's purview. The Desk reserves authority to issue binding clarifications where needed without formal amendment per its inherent administrative powers recognized across multiple Sections. Mages operating under temporary permits issued pursuant to § 200.3 Temporary Mouths remain subject to all provisions herein except those explicitly exempted by their terms of authorization. This comprehensive regulatory framework reflects the complex balance between fostering magical innovation and safeguarding against potential abuses inherent in such powerful abilities. Compliance with these standards is not merely optional but imperative for maintaining social order and public trust in the profession as a whole. Violations may trigger cascading consequences affecting licensure status, professional standing, and even criminal liability depending on severity and impact. The ultimate goal remains ensuring magic serves humanity without becoming its undoing through thoughtless exploitation or unchecked ambition. All stakeholders bear responsibility for upholding these vital principles daily through conscientious practice and mutual respect within the community of magical practitioners. By adhering to this code, mages demonstrate their commitment to ethical excellence beyond mere legal compliance alone. Together they uphold values transcending individual gain or factional interests for the greater good embodied by our shared heritage. This Section stands as a testament to our collective resolve to wield power wisely and protect those who cannot defend themselves against its perils. Through vigilance and unity we shall safeguard both ourselves and the wider world from harm caused by magical misuse whether intentional or accidental alike. Such dedication defines us as true stewards of this ancient craft destined to flourish responsibly for generations yet unborn guided always by wisdom tempered with compassion at every turn along our path forward together hand in hand under the banner of these sacred Accords forevermore.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1.4",
            "300.2",
            "500.1",
            "600.1",
            "400.2",
            "400.3",
            "700.5",
            "100.8",
            "200.6",
            "300.4",
            "1.8",
            "1201.5",
