          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Public Safety — Additional Protocols",
          "text": "In the event that a caster is found to have engaged in field casting for value without proper licensure, the Accords dictate a rigorous process for determining liability and remediation. First, an investigation shall be launched by the Aegis Magi to ascertain the full scope of the unauthorized activity. This includes reviewing all records, interviewing witnesses, and analyzing magical residue if applicable. Based on these findings, a preliminary assessment will be made regarding the degree of culpability. If guilt is established beyond reasonable doubt, the caster faces immediate suspension of their license along with substantial fines commensurate to the illicit gains realized. Furthermore, any profits derived from such activities shall be confiscated and donated to the Guild's endowment fund. In cases where repeat offenses are detected or egregious harm was inflicted upon third parties, more severe penalties may be imposed at the discretion of the governing council. This could include permanent revocation of casting privileges and mandatory community service aimed at repairing any damage done to public trust in magical services overall. The ultimate goal remains preserving ethical standards within the profession while ensuring fair recourse for all stakeholders involved. By adhering strictly to these guidelines, we safeguard both individual rights and collective integrity across the realm. It is incumbent upon each mage to uphold this code diligently lest they risk ruinous consequences should they falter in their duties as responsible practitioners of arcane arts bound by solemn oaths sworn before almighty truth itself!\n\nSEE ALSO: § 200.1 Licensure Required; § 500.5 Love Philtre and Undue Influence; § 300.2 Necromancy; Unsanctioned Arts; § 1.4 Persons Bound under the Autumnwood Accords.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "200.1",
            "500.5",
            "300.2",
            "1.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Public Safety — Additional Protocols",
          "text": "§ 500.7 Related Requirements shall encompass all ancillary matters necessary to enforce the prohibitions herein, including but not limited to: (a) monitoring and investigation into suspected violations; (b) temporary seizure of equipment or materials deemed likely to be used in contravention of these rules; (c) administrative hearings to determine liability and appropriate sanctions; and (d) coordination with law enforcement agencies where criminal conduct may have transpired. Nothing herein shall be construed as limiting the authority of the Autumnwood Accords Desk to take any action it deems necessary to uphold the integrity of magical practice within its jurisdiction, including the issuance of cease-and-desist orders, injunctions, or other equitable remedies as appropriate under the circumstances. All actions taken pursuant to this section shall be documented in full and made available for public inspection upon request, subject only to reasonable restrictions on sensitive or proprietary information where warranted by law or the needs of ongoing investigations. This provision serves as a catch-all mechanism ensuring that no loophole remains open for would-be violators to exploit, thereby preserving the sanctity of the Accords and protecting both the Guild and its members from harm arising from unregulated arcane activity. As such, it stands as an essential complement to the more specific directives laid out in preceding sections, working in tandem to create a comprehensive regulatory framework capable of adapting to new challenges and threats as they emerge over time. Only through such vigilant oversight can we hope to maintain balance between freedom of research and public safety, two values equally dear to this body and its constituents alike.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "500.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Public Safety — Additional Protocols",
          "text": "The provisions herein are not merely procedural formalities but substantive safeguards against abuse of power by both casters and non-casters alike. They reflect the Guild's commitment to preserving public trust in magical services while accommodating legitimate economic needs. Failure to comply with these requirements may result in severe penalties, including permanent revocation of licensure and referral for criminal prosecution under applicable statutes.\n\nThe regulations governing field casting fees, weather contingencies, post-explosion etiquette, healing-as-payment arrangements, and philtre-induced relationships serve a dual purpose: protecting clients from exploitation while enabling lawful commerce in magical arts. They establish clear boundaries between acceptable professional conduct and unacceptable misconduct, providing both guidance for practitioners and recourse for aggrieved parties. Enforcement mechanisms are robust and swift, reflecting the Guild's determination to maintain integrity within its ranks regardless of external pressures or temptations.\n\nBy adhering scrupulously to these standards, all licensed casters demonstrate their dedication to serving society responsibly rather than merely advancing personal interests at another's expense. They uphold the sacred covenant between mage and client, fostering an environment where magic can flourish safely and beneficially under wise governance. This collective commitment forms the bedrock upon which the Guild's enduring legacy rests, inspiring confidence in its ability to navigate complex ethical terrain with wisdom and fortitude.\n\n\"Magic is not a commodity to be bartered at will; it is a sacred trust that demands reverence and restraint.\" — Archmage Theron, inaugural address as Conservator Leader",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "heading": "Public Safety — Additional Protocols",
          "text": "The provisions governing field casting and commercial mana services are supplemented by several ancillary obligations designed to ensure both regulatory oversight and public safety. Under § 500.8, all casters engaged in paid magical work must maintain a current log of their transactions and effects, available for inspection upon reasonable notice by Guild auditors or local Conservator officers. This recordkeeping requirement extends beyond mere financial accounting; it necessitates detailed documentation of spell types, durations, outcomes, and any adverse reactions experienced by clients. Such data serves multiple purposes: tracking the scope of commercial magic in the region, identifying potential patterns of abuse or negligence, and providing evidence should disputes arise over service quality or unintended consequences. Failure to comply with these recordkeeping mandates constitutes a Class B infraction subject to fines up to one hundred crowns per violation.\n\nFurthermore, § 500.9 imposes a duty on commercial casters to promptly report any anomalous occurrences arising from their services. This includes but is not limited to spontaneous magical manifestations, unexplained weather shifts, temporal distortions, or appearances of extraplanar entities within reasonable proximity to the site of casting. Such reports must be submitted within forty-eight hours via registered letter to the nearest Guild Hall and copied to relevant local authorities. The rationale behind this provision lies in the recognition that commercial magic carries inherent risks beyond simple backfire effects; large-scale spellwork can disrupt ambient reality, potentially triggering cascading failures or attracting unwanted attention from hostile forces. By mandating early notification, the Accords aim to facilitate rapid response and mitigation efforts before minor issues escalate into major crises affecting public welfare.\n\nIn addition to these operational requirements, § 5010 establishes a system of mandatory liability insurance for all professional casters operating in the public sphere. Each licensed mage must carry at least one hundred thousand crowns worth of coverage protecting against claims stemming from accidental injuries, property damage, or personal losses suffered by clients due to faulty workmanship or negligence. Policies must be issued by carriers approved by the Autumnwood Accords Desk and renewed annually upon expiration. Premium payments are assessed quarterly in advance and factored into overall licensing fees. Non-compliance with this insurance mandate renders a caster's license immediately voidable and subjects them to additional penalties, including suspension of privileges pending resolution of any outstanding claims. The underlying principle is that those profiting from risky magical services must bear the financial burden of potential harms inflicted upon others through no fault of their own.\n\nFinally, § 5011 addresses the issue of post-service follow-up care, requiring casters to provide clients with written instructions regarding proper maintenance and monitoring of any enchanted items or facilities installed as part of their contract. These guidelines must include clear warnings about potential side effects, recommended inspection intervals, and procedures for reporting malfunctions or anomalies. Casters are also obligated to offer reasonable assistance in troubleshooting minor issues arising within thirty days of service completion at no additional cost. Beyond these basic obligations, professional courtesy dictates that experienced mages make themselves available for consultation should clients encounter unforeseen difficulties beyond the scope of standard remediation protocols. By insisting on thorough aftercare, the Accords seek to safeguard both consumer interests and the Guild's reputation for quality craftsmanship in the competitive marketplace of magical services.\n\nsee § 1201.6 Related Requirements; under § 500.4 Healing Offered as Consideration; per § 300.5 Research Copies of Quiet Items; compare § 400.3 Borrowed Hours; refer to § 900.7 Related Requirements for further guidance on commercial magic regulation and liability standards within the Autumnwood Accords framework.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "500.8",
            "500.9",
            "1201.6",
            "500.4",
            "300.5",
            "400.3",
            "900.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Public Safety — Arcane Contingency Zones and Temporary Exclusion Areas",
          "text": "Under the framework established by § 500.7, the Accords Desk maintains absolute authority to designate specific geographic coordinates or dimensional vectors as Arcane Contingency Zones (ACZ), a status that supersedes all other zoning ordinances within the Autumnwood jurisdiction. This designation is not merely administrative but constitutes a proactive measure of public safety, intended to isolate volatile magical signatures before they coalesce into catastrophic events. When an ACZ is declared, any individual found casting spells within those boundaries without explicit clearance from the High Council shall be immediately subject to the provisions of § 500.11 regarding unsanctioned field operations and liability, regardless of their prior licensure or intent. The purpose of such zones is to create a buffer against uncontrolled energy release, ensuring that even minor fluctuations in ambient mana do not trigger the catastrophic containment failures described under § 200.14 Additional Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation. Consequently, any citizen entering an active ACZ must first secure written permission from the nearest Guild Liaison Officer, failing which they shall be deemed to have voluntarily assumed all risks associated with unauthorized exposure to high-grade magical phenomena.\n\nFurthermore, the declaration of an ACZ triggers immediate restrictions on civilian movement and commercial activity within the designated sector, effectively suspending § 500.1 Field Casting for Value and prohibiting any form of artisanal work that might interfere with the stabilization protocols in place. This suspension is critical because the presence of unauthorized casters can disrupt the delicate equilibrium required to seal off a breach or contain a rogue construct, thereby endangering the general populace. The Accords Desk recognizes that the safety of the public relies on a strict separation between licensed professional operations and amateur experimentation, a principle reinforced by § 1.17 Additional Provisions for Mages' Guild Mediation and Peer Review Protocols which mandates that all disputes regarding zone boundaries be resolved through formal mediation before enforcement action is taken against any resident or business operator. It is the duty of every citizen to heed the auditory and visual signals broadcast by the Guild's early warning systems, which serve as the primary indicator of an active ACZ; failure to comply with evacuation orders issued under these protocols shall result in automatic forfeiture of one's standing within the community and potential referral to The Paradox Trial for contempt of safety regulations.\n\nIn instances where an ACZ is established due to a breach in arcane containment, the Accords Desk shall immediately invoke the emergency response mechanisms detailed in § 200.16 Emergency Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation to ensure that the area is secured within the shortest time frame possible. This urgency is compounded by the fact that any attempt to enter an active ACZ without authorization constitutes a felony under the terms of § 500.12 Additional Provisions Regarding Arcane Field Operations and Conduct, which strictly forbids engagement in commercial spellcasting activities outside the bounds of one's licensed practice during times of heightened magical volatility. The law is clear that the safety of the public domain takes precedence over all other considerations, including property rights or personal convenience, and any damage caused to private property located within an active ACZ shall be considered incidental to the greater public good protected by these accords. Moreover, the Accords Desk reserves the right to expand the perimeter of an existing ACZ at its sole discretion if threat assessments indicate that the initial containment radius is insufficient to prevent collateral damage, a power that is exercised in accordance with § 1.15 Additional Provisions for Expedited Remediation and Immediate Response Protocols to address such violations before they escalate into full-scale disasters.\n\nFinally, it shall be noted that the existence of an ACZ does not absolve individuals of their personal liability for any magical activities conducted therein without permission; rather, it serves as a warning that the consequences of such actions will be met with the full weight of the law. The Accords Desk further stipulates that all constructs operating within an ACZ must adhere to the stringent oversight requirements outlined in § 600.15 Catchline Title: Oversight Protocols for Construct Labor and Associated Obligations, ensuring that autonomous agents do not inadvertently destabilize the zone through unregulated energy consumption or malfunction. This comprehensive approach to public safety ensures that the Mages' Guild remains vigilant against the threats posed by both internal negligence and external aggression, thereby preserving the integrity of the realm against the chaotic forces that seek to undo the delicate balance between magic and matter. Any citizen who questions the validity of an ACZ declaration shall be directed to consult § 300.14 Catchline Title: Transmission Protocols and Oversight regarding the official communication channels used to disseminate such critical safety information, thereby maintaining a clear chain of command and accountability throughout the enforcement process.",
          "key": "f",
