    {
      "cite": "600.7",
      "part": "part_vi",
      "title": "Contracts with Non-Casters and Related Obligations",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Contracts with Non-Casters and Related Obligations",
          "text": "§ 600.1 Contracts With Non-Casters\nA binding contract may be executed between a Caster and a non-magical person (\"Non-Caster\"), provided the terms do not violate the Accords or impose impossible conditions upon either party. Such agreements must be reduced to writing, signed by both parties, and witnessed by two licensed Casters who shall verify that neither side is acting under compulsion. The Non-Caster acknowledges receipt of a full copy of the contract within ten days of execution. Failure to adhere to these formalities renders the agreement void ab initio, regardless of any oral assent or performance thereunder.\n\n§ 600.2 Familiars as Agents\nA Familiar may act as an authorized agent for its Caster in matters directly related to the fulfillment of contractual obligations. The Caster remains ultimately liable for all actions and omissions of the Familiar within the scope of representation. No contract shall bind a Familiar independently, nor shall any clause purport to transfer ownership or control of the Familiar to another party except by explicit written consent of both the Caster and the Familiar's owner. Unauthorized disposition of a Familiar constitutes a serious breach of trust and may result in revocation of licensure for all involved parties.\n\n§ 600.3 Geas as an Unconscionable Term\nA contract containing a geas—a magical compulsion forcing compliance with specific instructions—is deemed unconscionable and unenforceable under the Accords. Such clauses violate fundamental principles of free will and bodily autonomy enshrined in § 1.4 Persons Bound. Any attempt to enforce a geas shall be met with immediate legal intervention by the Aegis Magi, who may seize assets and detain responsible parties pending further proceedings. Parties are urged to settle disputes through negotiation rather than resorting to coercive magical measures that threaten public safety and social order.\n\n§ 600.4 Construct Labor: Minimum Wage Standards\nConstructs employed under contract shall be compensated at rates no less than the prevailing minimum wage for comparable human laborers in their locality, adjusted upward by twenty percent to account for the unique skills and risks inherent to magical work. This provision applies regardless of whether compensation is paid directly or indirectly through reduced service fees or other means. Employers violating this standard face penalties ranging from fines up to one hundred gold crowns per offense to permanent suspension of operating privileges. The Conservators maintain strict oversight to ensure fair treatment of all worker-constructions alike.\n\n§ 600.5 Summoned Notary and Witness Requirements\nAll contracts involving Casters must be notarized by a summoned notary with authority delegated directly from the Guild Desk, along with two independent witnesses who shall attest to both parties' identities and capacity to contract. Witnesses must swear under oath that neither party was acting under duress or undue influence at the time of signing. The notary retains original copies of all executed documents for archival purposes, while providing certified duplicates to each signatory within five business days thereafter. Failure to comply with these witnessing protocols invalidates any purported agreement entered into without proper authentication.\n\n§ 600.6 Related Requirements\nSee also §§ 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; § 200.3 Temporary Mouths; § 400.2 Pocket Dimensions as Labs; § 500.1 Field Casting for Value; § 900.7 Foreign Halls and Courtesy; § 1101.6 Related Requirements; § 1201.6 Related Requirements; § 1301.6 Related Requirements; § 1401.6 Related Requirements; § 300.5 Research Copies of Quiet Items; § 400.3 Borrowed Hours; Interest in Time; § 500.4 Healing Offered as Consideration; § 600.2 Familiars as Agents; § 700.6 Related Requirements.\n\n*Note: This section outlines the legal framework governing commercial transactions between magical practitioners and ordinary citizens, balancing innovation with protection of vulnerable parties.*",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "600.1",
            "600.2",
            "600.3",
