    {
      "cite": "700.7",
      "part": "part_vii",
      "title": "Admissibility Standards for Arcane Testimony and",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 700.7 Related Requirements - Admissibility Standards for Arcane Testimony and ",
          "text": "In proceedings before the Autumnwood Accords Desk, all evidence adduced must satisfy the rigorous standards set forth herein to ensure fairness and accuracy in determining matters of magical culpability or entitlement. Under § 700.1, the foundational principles governing admissibility are those established by common law and precedent, adapted for the unique circumstances presented by arcane phenomena. See also § 300.6 regarding the exclusion of hearsay derived from scrying operations absent corroboration under oath.\n\n§ 700.2 specifically addresses testimony obtained through divination or memory charms. Such evidence shall be deemed inadmissible unless the source consents in writing to its use and discloses all methods employed, as required by § 400.1's provisions on informed consent for magical procedures. Unauthorized manipulation of a witness's memories constitutes spoliation under § 700.3 and may result in immediate dismissal of claims predicated upon said altered recollections. See further § 200.5 concerning the limits of permissible psychological interventions during deposition phases.\n\nSimulacra summoned pursuant to § 600.1 may offer testimony subject to cross-examination, provided their origins are fully disclosed and they possess no inherent bias toward either party. Clauses requiring simulation of human emotion or intent shall be scrutinized carefully under § 700.4's safeguards against deceptive practices. The Desk retains discretion to exclude simulative evidence where it risks prejudicing the fact-finding process unduly. Reference is made to § 100.8 regarding emergency exceptions for time-sensitive magical phenomena threatening public safety.\n\nClones created via forbidden arts may assert claims as duplicate entities under specific conditions outlined in § 700.5, but such assertions must be supported by irrefutable proof of lawful origin and continuous chain of custody from point of creation to present moment. Absent such documentation, any attempt to establish standing based solely on clonal duplication shall fail outright. This provision implements the spirit of § 300.4 while maintaining strict adherence to established protocols for verifying magical lineages.\n\nAll evidence introduced must comply with the formal requirements set forth in Part IV, including proper authentication, notarization where applicable, and timely submission prior to hearing dates absent extraordinary circumstances warranting a ruling on late filings under § 500.2's emergency provisions. The Desk shall not be bound by any irregularities or procedural failures attributable solely to the proponent of the evidence unless waived expressly in writing before trial commences. For guidance on calculating applicable deadlines and extensions, consult §§ 1301.1 through 1301.4 inclusive.\n\nViolations of these admissibility standards may result in sanctions ranging from monetary fines up to ten thousand gold pieces per offense to complete forfeiture of rights associated with the disputed matter entirely. Repeat offenders face escalated penalties including suspension or permanent revocation of licensure under §§ 200.3 and 1101.5 respectively. The ultimate authority rests with the presiding Magister whose determinations are final and unappealable except by motion for rehearing granted at their sole discretion pursuant to § 1401.3's savings clause.\n\nSee also §§ 700.8–700.9 concerning expert witness qualifications and standards of care, along with cross-references to foundational provisions on burden of proof (§ 200.4), privilege protections (§ 500.6), and remedies for bad faith litigation tactics (§ 1201.6). Compliance with all stipulations herein is mandatory under pain of severe consequences as outlined in the Preamble to these Accords.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "700.1",
