    {
      "cite": "1301.7",
      "part": "part_xiii",
      "title": "Sunset Provisions",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.7 Related Requirements and Sunset Provisions",
          "text": "§ 1301.7(a) Related Requirements. The fee schedule set forth in Part XIII shall be read in conjunction with the penalties prescribed in § 1301.2, which apply equally to all violations of this Code regardless of whether they are discovered during a scheduled inspection or through other means. Any failure by an inspected party to comply fully and promptly with all directives issued pursuant to these Accords shall constitute grounds for additional sanctions, up to and including revocation of licensure under § 200.4.\n\n§ 1301.7(b) Appeals Procedure. Parties dissatisfied with the results of any inspection or associated penalties may petition the Autumnwood Accords Desk for review in accordance with established appellate procedures. Such petitions must be filed within thirty days of receipt of the initial determination and shall include all relevant evidence supporting the appeal claim. The Desk shall adjudicate appeals expeditiously, utilizing expedited hearing protocols where appropriate to ensure timely resolution of disputes without undue burden on Guild operations.\n\n§ 1301.7(c) Sunset Clause. The fee schedules outlined in this Part are hereby established for a term of five years from the effective date hereof, subject to renewal or modification by the Desk at its sole discretion. Upon expiration of this initial term, the Desk shall conduct a comprehensive review of all operational costs and market conditions before determining whether additional fees are warranted to maintain adequate funding levels. Any proposed changes must be published with sufficient notice to allow for public comment prior to implementation.\n\n§ 1301.7(d) Emergency Provisions. In circumstances where immediate action is required to prevent imminent harm or substantial disruption to Guild functions, the Desk may authorize temporary fee adjustments on an emergency basis without prior notice. Such measures shall remain in effect only until the next regular meeting of the full Council, at which point a final determination regarding long-term policy will be made after due deliberation and consideration of all stakeholder input received during the interim period.\n\n§ 1301.7(e) Transparency Obligations. All fee assessments imposed under this section shall be accompanied by detailed explanations setting forth the specific regulatory services rendered, associated costs incurred, and legal authority supporting each charge itemized therein. The Desk maintains an online portal providing access to historical data regarding past inspections, outcomes achieved, and comparative analyses demonstrating the value proposition offered to licensed practitioners through participation in this framework. Such transparency measures are designed to foster trust between regulators and regulated entities while ensuring accountability throughout the enforcement process.\n\n§ 1301.7(f) Finality of Assessments. Once formally assessed and notified, all fees imposed pursuant to these provisions shall be deemed final and binding upon receipt, absent successful appeal within prescribed timeframes. Failure to pay outstanding balances in full by the deadline specified shall result in automatic suspension of licensure privileges until default is cured in accordance with applicable procedures set forth elsewhere herein. The Desk reserves the right to pursue collection actions as necessary to recover unpaid amounts owed, including but not limited to referral to appropriate authorities for civil litigation or criminal prosecution where warranted under existing law.\"\n\n\"see § 1301.2 Penalties; see § 1401.5 Related Requirements\"",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1301.7",
            "1301.2",
            "200.4",
            "1401.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.7 Related Requirements and Sunset Provisions — Continued",
          "text": "The fees prescribed herein are subject to periodic review by the Mages' Guild Desk, which may adjust rates in response to inflation or shifts in market conditions. Any such adjustments shall be published at least thirty days prior to implementation to afford affected parties adequate notice. Furthermore, all levies imposed under this section shall expire automatically upon the fulfillment of their intended purpose or after a maximum duration of five years unless expressly renewed by resolution of the Desk. Failure to comply with these temporal limitations renders any assessment void ab initio and unenforceable against any person or entity.\n\nIn addition to fee collection, the Guild reserves the right to impose additional charges for services rendered beyond those explicitly enumerated in this schedule. Such ancillary fees must be clearly itemized on all invoices and receipts issued by authorized collectors. Parties disputing the reasonableness of any supplemental assessment bear the burden of demonstrating its necessity and proportionality relative to the scope of work performed. Absent such proof, default judgments entered for excessive amounts shall be overturned upon timely motion.\n\nThe provisions set forth herein operate in conjunction with, but do not supersede, other applicable statutes governing magical commerce within Autumn Wood jurisdiction. In cases of conflict between this section and higher law, the latter shall prevail by virtue of its superior legal force. Conversely, where no specific mandate exists elsewhere, these guidelines serve as the exclusive standard for determining permissible charges and enforcement mechanisms pertaining to the regulation of arcane practices in our region.\n\nNotwithstanding the foregoing, nothing contained herein shall be construed to diminish or impair any pre-existing rights vested in individual casters by virtue of their licensure status under separate provisions of this Code. Such entitlements remain fully intact unless explicitly abrogated through due process proceedings initiated pursuant to applicable rules of administrative law. Similarly, obligations accruing prior to the effective date of these amendments shall continue unabated regardless of subsequent changes to the fee schedule.\n\nFinally, it is hereby declared that all payments made in accordance with this section constitute full and final satisfaction of any outstanding debts owed by payer to payee regarding matters falling within the scope of collection authority granted herein. No further action may be taken on such accounts except as expressly authorized by written instrument executed by both parties hereto or their duly appointed representatives acting under valid power of attorney. This declaration shall remain in effect forever unless modified by mutual consent evidenced in writing signed by all concerned stakeholders.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1301.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.7 Related Requirements and Sunset Provisions — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "The provisions set forth herein shall remain in full force and effect until such time as superseded by subsequent enactments or repealed by the Autumnwood Accords Desk. Nothing contained herein shall be construed to limit the powers of the Desk or its constituent bodies under any other section of this Code, including but not limited to §§ 100.8, 200.4, and 300.5. All rights reserved except as expressly granted herein. No implied license or waiver by conduct shall be inferred from failure to enforce any provision strictly in accordance with its terms. The Desk retains sole discretion to interpret ambiguous language and resolve disputes arising hereunder. Any attempt to circumvent these requirements through subterfuge or evasion shall constitute a violation of this Code and subject the offender to appropriate sanctions under applicable law.\n\n\"Sunset Provisions\": These are temporary clauses that expire after a set period unless renewed by explicit action. They allow flexibility for trying new approaches without permanent commitment. For example, § 1301.7(b) permits emergency licensing procedures only during declared crises, reverting to normal standards once stability is restored. Such provisions must be clearly labeled and their expiration dates prominently displayed. Failure to comply with sunset timelines renders the associated authority void ab initio unless extended pursuant to established amendment protocols outlined in § 1401.3.\"\n\n\"Related Requirements\": Additional obligations beyond those explicitly stated may arise from common law principles, customary practice, or equitable considerations deemed necessary by the Desk in specific cases. These unwritten rules serve to fill gaps and ensure fair treatment absent rigid statutory guidance. While not formally codified, they carry binding force when invoked properly before the Guild's judicial bodies.\"\n\n\"Enforcement Mechanisms\": Violations of this section may trigger automatic penalties per § 1301.2 or require discretionary sanctions at the Desk's discretion. Repeat offenders face escalated consequences including license revocation and permanent expulsion from the Accords community. Civil liabilities may also accrue alongside criminal punishments for egregious breaches.\"\n\n\"Compliance Monitoring\": Ongoing oversight ensures adherence to these evolving standards through periodic audits, random inspections, and whistleblower reporting channels maintained independently of local enforcement agencies. Data gathered feeds into predictive modeling efforts aimed at preemptively identifying potential problem areas requiring proactive intervention rather than reactive punishment alone.\"\n\n*Footnotes omitted for brevity.*",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "100.8",
            "1301.7",
            "1401.3",
            "1301.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.7 Sunset Provisions and Statute Limitations",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords, in their entirety and regardless of individual article, shall expire on the tenth day following the first full lunar cycle after the issuance of this Codex. Upon such expiration, all rights, duties, obligations, and liabilities created thereby shall cease forthwith, unless explicitly renewed by a subsequent resolution of the Mages' Guild Desk. This provision ensures that the Accords remain subject to periodic review and revision in accordance with evolving magical practices and societal needs.\n\nFurthermore, no action arising under this Codex shall be brought more than five (5) years after the date on which such right of action first accrued. For purposes of this limitation, a cause of action accrues when any violation of these provisions occurs or should have been reasonably known by the aggrieved party through the exercise of due diligence. Failure to commence proceedings within the prescribed period shall constitute an absolute bar to recovery, regardless of the merits of the underlying claim.\n\nThe foregoing limitations are applicable uniformly across all articles and sections herein, without exception or qualification. They reflect a deliberate legislative choice to balance the need for legal certainty with recognition of the fluid nature of arcane phenomena. Parties relying on any provision of this Codex must therefore act promptly to preserve their rights under it.\n\nIn the event of any conflict between the terms hereof and prior laws, regulations, or agreements relating to the same subject matter, the provisions of these Accords shall control exclusively during their term of validity. This supremacy clause underscores the intended comprehensive nature of the Autumnwood framework as the governing standard for magical conduct in the Midlands region.\n\nFinally, it is hereby declared that nothing in this Codex shall be construed as creating any new cause of action or liability beyond those expressly set forth herein. All claims must arise directly from the text of these provisions to be cognizable under the law. This restriction serves to maintain clarity and predictability in legal relations involving magic users and practitioners alike.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1301.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.7 Sunset Provisions and Statute Limitations — Continued",
          "text": "The temporal efficacy of penal sanctions imposed under these Accords is subject to specific limitations, both in terms of duration and applicability to subsequent infractions. Any seal or magical restraint affixed pursuant to a Paradox Trial shall remain active for no longer than three standard solar years from the date of imposition, absent renewal by majority vote of the Aegis Magi Council. Upon expiration, all binding effects automatically dissolve unless extended. This limitation reflects the fundamental principle that punitive measures against individuals must be proportionate and time-bound, preventing indefinite subjugation under threat of further sanction for past conduct.\n\nFurthermore, no penal order issued hereunder shall serve as a bar to prosecution or adjudication for any new violation of the Accords committed during its term of validity. Each infraction constitutes an independent wrong demanding separate consideration by the proper authorities. Thus, while active seals may temporarily curtail the application of certain magical arts, they do not confer immunity from future liability should the restrained individual again transgress guild law. This preserves the integrity of the regulatory framework and ensures that repeated offenders face escalating consequences commensurate with their ongoing disregard for established norms.\n\nIn cases where a sanctioned seal is intentionally circumvented or deliberately nullified by the subject, the original penalty shall be deemed void ab initio, and any resulting harm attributable to such evasion shall be fully actionable against the offending party. Conversely, accidental breach of a magical restraint does not automatically trigger additional sanctions; rather, it necessitates review by the adjudicating body to determine appropriate remedial action based on the circumstances surrounding the incident. This safeguard prevents disproportionate punishment for inadvertent failures and maintains fairness in enforcement.\n\nUltimately, these sunset provisions embody the balance between retribution and rehabilitation inherent to civilized society. By limiting the scope of punitive authority over time, they acknowledge that individuals retain an inherent dignity even under duress, while simultaneously preserving the Guild's right to address ongoing threats posed by recidivists. Such measured application of power serves both justice and the greater good of maintaining order within the magical community at large.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1301.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.7 Related Requirements and Sunset Provisions — Administration",
          "text": "The Accords recognize that certain provisions may require periodic review to ensure their continued relevance and efficacy in the face of evolving magical landscapes. Under this authority, the Desk shall establish a mechanism for assessing the necessity and impact of each regulation on an ongoing basis. Such assessments must be conducted with transparency and input from all affected parties, including practitioners, researchers, and members of the public.\n\nWhen a provision is deemed obsolete or redundant, it may be subject to repeal or modification through the standard legislative process. In such instances, appropriate notice shall be given to allow for meaningful comment and participation. The Desk retains discretion to implement interim measures where necessary to maintain stability during the transition period.\n\nConversely, emerging trends in magical theory or practice may warrant the adoption of new rules to address previously unforeseen challenges. These additions must align with the overarching principles of safety and fairness enshrined in the Accords. Proposed amendments shall undergo rigorous scrutiny prior to enactment, ensuring they serve the public interest without imposing undue burdens on legitimate pursuits.\n\nThe Desk is further empowered to delegate limited authority to subcommittees or appointed panels for expedited handling of routine matters. Such delegations must be clearly defined and time-limited, with regular reporting back to the full body. Decisions made by these proxies shall carry equal weight as those rendered directly by the Accords' representatives.\n\nIn all instances involving the revision or interpretation of existing statutes, the Desk shall strive for clarity and consistency in its rulings. Ambiguities should be resolved favorably toward open inquiry rather than restrictive enforcement, fostering an environment conducive to advancement without compromising core values. Through diligent stewardship and adaptive governance, the Accords remain a living document capable of meeting the changing needs of society while safeguarding against potential harms.\n\nsee § 1301.5 Related Requirements for additional context on administrative procedures; see § 1201.6 Related Requirements regarding delegation protocols; see § 900.7 Related Requirements concerning public engagement standards.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1301.5",
            "1201.6",
            "900.7",
            "1301.7"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "§ 1301",
      "source": "lmstudio",
