    {
      "cite": "1401.7",
      "part": "part_xiv",
      "title": "Authority and Validity",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 1401.7 Related Requirements - Authority and Validity",
          "text": "The provisions contained herein shall be deemed valid only when enacted in conformity with the procedural mandates set forth under §§ 100.1–100.8 of this Codex, including but not limited to proper quorum, notice periods, and formal recordation of all deliberations. Any resolution adopted in contravention of these foundational rules shall be considered void ab initio and unenforceable under any circumstance. See § 100.3 Quorum; § 100.4 Records of Speech.\n\nThis Codex supersedes all prior statutes, charters, customary practices, or oral agreements inconsistent with its express terms as of the Effective Date specified herein. However, nothing contained in this document shall be construed to diminish any vested rights acquired by bona fide parties under previously existing laws unless explicitly abrogated by subsequent legislation. Under § 1401.3 Savings Against the Iron Mandate, no provision hereof may conflict with superior imperial directives or national security imperatives declared by duly constituted authorities.\n\nThe Governing Body retains inherent authority to interpret ambiguous clauses and fill gaps in this regulation as necessary to effectuate its purposes. Such interpretations shall be published promptly in official gazettes along with rationales for any significant departures from prior precedent. Failure to comply with binding rulings issued pursuant to this power may result in disciplinary sanctions up to and including revocation of licensure privileges. Refer to § 200.1 Licensure Required; § 500.1 Field Casting for Value regarding applicable penalties.\n\nAll members of the Guild shall actively participate in maintaining the integrity and efficacy of these statutes through diligent adherence, timely reporting of violations, and constructive engagement with oversight mechanisms established under this framework. Collective accountability is paramount to safeguarding both public welfare and professional standards within our esteemed community. See § 1401.2 Dead Citations; § 300.1 Schedules of Arts for compliance obligations.\n\nAny questions concerning the meaning or application of specific articles should be directed in writing to the Office of Legal Counsel no later than seven (7) business days after publication. Responses will be rendered within fourteen (14) calendar days unless extended due to extraordinary circumstances beyond reasonable control. Parties dissatisfied with official answers may petition for review by a three-member panel appointed jointly by the Archmage Sovereign and the Desk Chairperson. Consult § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting for recusals procedures.\n\nThe full text of this enactment is available online at [redacted URL] or upon request from any registered practitioner paying applicable copying fees. Updated versions will be posted immediately following final ratification without further notice deemed adequate compliance with public disclosure mandates. All persons subject to these regulations are hereby put on formal notice thereof. Under § 1401.5 Related Requirements, failure to acknowledge receipt of this document shall not excuse subsequent liability for noncompliance.\n\nIt is expressly declared that the intent behind each section herein was carefully considered by the drafting committee responsible for its preparation prior to submission for approval. Nothing contained in these provisions should be interpreted restrictively or expansively absent clear textual evidence supporting such reading. Plain language governs unless specialized terminology necessitates otherwise pursuant to established canons of statutory construction. See § 1.7 Construction; Aggregation of Conduct regarding interpretive principles applicable throughout this Code.\n\nThe Great Seal of the Mages' Guild shall be affixed to all certified copies issued under this authority as conclusive proof of authenticity and official status until proven otherwise by competent judicial proceeding or administrative appeal filed within one hundred eighty (180) days of issuance date stamping thereof. Copies lacking proper authentication may be rejected outright by receiving agencies exercising enforcement powers delegated herein. Refer to § 1.9 Seals, Stamps, and What Is Not a Seal for detailed requirements governing acceptable forms of verification.\n\nNothing in this regulation shall be construed to impair existing contractual obligations undertaken prior to the Effective Date unless expressly prohibited thereby. Nor shall it impose retroactive liability absent affirmative waiver by affected parties exercising their full rights under applicable law. Privity of contract remains inviolate except where explicitly modified or superseded by mandatory provisions herein. See § 1.5 Relation to Other Law; § 600.1 Contracts with Non-Casters for limitations on implied terms.\n\nAll disputes arising out of or related to the interpretation, enforcement, or alleged violation of these statutes shall first be submitted to binding arbitration administered under rules promulgated by the Guild Dispute Resolution Committee unless otherwise agreed in writing between disputing parties. Arbitral awards rendered pursuant thereto shall have full force and effect as final judgments entered by courts of competent jurisdiction without further review except upon grounds specifically enumerated in relevant procedural orders. Consult § 1301.6 Related Requirements regarding enforcement mechanisms available to aggrieved litigants seeking relief beyond the scope of initial remedial measures granted herein.\n\nThis enactment shall remain in full force and effect until expressly repealed, amended, or superseded by subsequent action duly taken pursuant to established legislative processes outlined above. Continual vigilance remains essential to preserve both literal fidelity and spirit of original purpose motivating adoption thereof by consensus of responsible stewards invested with fiduciary duties toward all stakeholders impacted thereby. See § 1401.1 Historical Annotations; Form for guidance regarding preservation of legislative history relevant to ongoing debates concerning scope and application of individual provisions contained within this comprehensive regulatory scheme governing conduct subject to oversight jurisdiction vested herein.\n\n[End of section]",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "100.1",
            "100.3",
            "100.4",
            "1401.3",
            "200.1",
            "500.1",
            "1401.2",
            "300.1",
