            "1401.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Authority and Validity of the Autumnwood Accords",
          "text": "The authority under which this Codex is promulgated derives directly from the sovereign will of Archmage Veyra, elected by the collective wisdom of the Guild's constituent Halls as their highest steward. This mandate empowers the Mages' Desk to enact regulations binding upon all who practice magic within its jurisdiction, save only for matters reserved exclusively to the Sovereign herself. Such reserving ensures that no single body may usurp the ultimate arbitrating power granted by the Accords' founding charter.\n\nAny regulation issued pursuant thereto carries full legal force and effect once duly promulgated in accordance with established procedure. Failure to comply constitutes a breach of contract between the regulated party and the Guild, subject to remedies outlined herein including sanctions, seals, or even expulsion from lawful practice entirely at the Desk's discretion. Nothing contained here shall be construed to diminish the inherent rights protected by fundamental charter provisions unless explicitly abrogated through proper channels requiring supermajority approval.\n\nThe validity of any action taken under authority delegated by this Codex remains subject only to review by the Mages' Desk itself or its duly appointed appellate bodies. No external court, tribunal, or private entity shall have jurisdiction over disputes arising from magical practice regulated hereunder without express consent of all parties and voluntary submission thereto. This preserves the autonomy essential to maintaining order within a complex arcane ecosystem while safeguarding against arbitrary interference from outside forces.\n\nIn sum, then, these provisions establish both the source and scope of regulatory power vested in the Guild's governing institutions. By defining limits on what may be commanded even by its highest representatives, they balance necessary oversight with cherished liberties. Such equilibrium serves as the foundation upon which all other rules rest securely, enabling them to function effectively without encroaching improperly upon individual sovereignty or collective autonomy alike. Only through such careful calibration can lasting harmony be achieved amidst the endless tensions inherent in any society built around mastery of forbidden arts.\n\nsee § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild; see § 300.4 Reclassification Procedure; see § 1501.9 Reserved Matters Requiring Supermajority Approval; see § 1601.7 External Review and Appellate Process.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "100.2",
            "300.4",
            "1501.9",
            "1601.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Authority and Validity of the Autumnwood Accords — Continued",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords derive their binding force from three interlocking sources. First, under § 1.2, they are enacted by the sovereign authority of Archmage Veyra acting as mediator for all mages within the Hall's jurisdiction. Second, the consent of the Guild membership is implied through continued operation under the existing regime; no one has publicly repudiated these laws since their codification. Third, and most importantly, the Accords reflect a universal consensus among practicing mages regarding necessary restrictions on magical activity. This consensus exists independently of any particular sovereign's decree.\n\nAccordingly, § 1401.7 declares that the Autumnwood Accords shall be deemed valid notwithstanding any contrary provisions in local charters or customs. Any attempt to nullify these laws is void ab initio and unenforceable. The only exception concerns matters explicitly reserved by § 100.2, which prohibits the Guild from legislating on strictly personal affairs unrelated to magical practice.\n\nFurthermore, under § 1401.8, the Accords shall remain in effect until expressly repealed or superseded by a subsequent enactment of equal authority. No individual may unilaterally declare them null and void. Only a formal resolution of the Autumn Wood Desk, passed with requisite votes as outlined in § 100.3, can alter this status quo. Such resolutions must be published promptly to ensure all subjects are duly notified.\n\nIn summary, the legal weight of the Autumnwood Accords stems from their dual nature as both binding contracts and statements of professional ethics accepted by the entire casting community. They constitute a living constitution for magecraft in the Midlands region, superseding conflicting norms wherever they pertain to magical safety or public order. Any challenge to their validity must be mounted through proper legal channels within the Guild framework itself.\n\nsee § 100.2 re reserved matters\nsee § 1401.8 on duration and repeal procedures\nunder § 1.5, these laws prevail over inconsistent local customs\nper § 1.9, only official seals carry presumptive authenticity",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1.2",
            "1401.7",
            "100.2",
            "1401.8",
            "100.3",
            "1.5",
            "1.9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Authority and Validity — Continued",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords derive their binding force directly from the sovereign will of Archmage Veyra, who acts as the ultimate arbiter within the Hall. Her decrees stand supreme unless explicitly overturned by a duly convened vote of the Full Desk or through established legal challenge under § 100.5. No individual mage possesses the authority to unilaterally void any provision of this Code; even an Archmage's personal edict must align with its core tenets to hold weight outside immediate emergency contexts.\n\nPursuant to § 1.9, seals and stamps placed by authorized clerks shall constitute conclusive evidence of official ratification unless successfully rebutted by counter-proof meeting the highest standards of admissibility set forth in these regulations. Such authentication mechanisms are designed to prevent forgery while expediting routine administrative functions across all Guild jurisdictions. Unauthorized modifications or alterations to any enrolled document render it immediately null and void ab initio, regardless of apparent signatures or endorsements thereon.\n\nAny dispute arising from conflicting interpretations of the Accords shall be resolved exclusively through formal proceedings before the Autumnwood Desk, with final appeal limited to direct petition to Archmage Veyra in extraordinary circumstances only. Private arbitration clauses contained within individual contracts are hereby expressly superseded by this mandatory forum-selection provision for all matters falling within the scope of Guild regulation. Failure to exhaust these prescribed channels shall result in automatic dismissal of any ensuing claims or motions brought thereafter.\n\nThis section represents a comprehensive codification of the foundational principles governing the exercise of magical authority under the Autumnwood Accords framework. Its provisions operate prospectively from date of promulgation unless expressly stated otherwise within specific articles addressing transitional matters affecting pending cases or ongoing investigations initiated prior thereto. All parties bound hereby acknowledge receipt and understanding of these critical guidelines regulating their professional conduct and responsibilities as licensed practitioners within the jurisdiction of this august body.\n\nsee § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; see § 1.9 Seals, Stamps, and What Is Not a Seal; under § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse regarding loss of standing to enforce rights accrued prior thereto.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "100.5",
            "1.9",
            "200.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Authority and Validity Continued",
          "text": "The binding force of the Autumnwood Accords derives directly from the sovereign will of Archmage Veyra, invested through ancient ritual to manifest as immutable law within the boundaries of the Guild's jurisdiction. This primacy supersedes all other claims except those expressly granted by her edict. Any challenge to this authority must be brought before the High Council in open session and proven beyond reasonable doubt; mere speculation or dissent will not suffice. The Accords stand as the ultimate expression of magical order, embodying centuries of collective wisdom and hard-won experience. To undermine them is to invite chaos upon oneself and one's allies alike. Thus let all who would serve the Greater Good heed these words most carefully: obedience to the Codex is the first step toward mastery over the arcane arts. Only by submitting fully to this framework may mages hope to wield their gifts safely and effectively for generations yet unborn. The path ahead demands vigilance, discipline, and unwavering commitment to our shared mission. Together we shall uphold these sacred vows against all comers!\n\nsee § 1401.3 Savings Against the Iron Mandate\nsee § 1201.5 Related Requirements\nunder § 1.9 Seals, Stamps, and What Is Not a Seal",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1401.3",
            "1201.5",
            "1.9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1401.7 Authority and Validity Continued - Enforcement Protocols and Jurisdicti",
          "text": "The enforcement of the Autumnwood Accords shall be undertaken by duly authorized representatives of the Mages' Guild, including but not limited to the Aegis Magi and their subordinate officers. Such agents are vested with full power to investigate alleged violations, conduct hearings, and impose sanctions in accordance with these provisions. Nothing herein shall limit or impair any inherent powers possessed by the Guild under its charter.\n\nIn matters involving cross-jurisdictional disputes or parallel proceedings initiated by other competent authorities, the Guild reserves the right to assert primary jurisdiction where its interests are most directly implicated. The parties agree to cooperate fully in such instances, exchanging information and evidence as necessary for a comprehensive resolution. Failure to comply with this obligation shall constitute grounds for punitive action under applicable law.\n\nAll actions taken pursuant to these Articles shall be conducted expeditiously and without undue delay. Time limits specified herein are strict and may not be extended except by written agreement of all affected parties or upon showing of extraordinary circumstances beyond reasonable control. The Guild shall provide written notice of its intentions at least thirty (30) days prior to initiating any enforcement measures, allowing the respondent adequate opportunity to respond.\n\nThe provisions of this Part are severable; if any section is found unenforceable for any reason whatsoever, it shall not affect the validity or enforceability of the remaining clauses. The intent and purpose of these regulations shall be construed liberally in favor of maintaining public safety and order within the magical community. Ambiguities shall be resolved by reference to established precedent and principles of equity rather than technical literalism alone.\n\nThe undersigned hereby acknowledge receipt, reading, understanding, and voluntary submission to all terms outlined above. This agreement may not be amended except through formal amendment adopted by vote of a quorum convened specially for that purpose in accordance with Article III hereof. All prior negotiations, representations, or understandings are expressly merged herein and superseded by this final written instrument which embodies the entire consideration between the parties.\n\nIN WITNESS WHEREOF, I have executed this document on the date first above written under my hand and seal to perpetuate its force according to law.\" ________________ [SEAL] Archmage Veyra, Sovereign of the Autumnwood Accords \"Authority flows from consent, not compulsion. The Guild stands guard over our shared future, bound by oath and honor. So long as these laws endure, so shall the balance of magic remain unshaken.\" - Archmage Theron \"Progress demands risk, yet recklessness invites ruin. We tread a razor's edge between discovery and destruction. Prudence is not fear—it is wisdom earned in fire.\" - Janna Brightspark \"The Accords are but tools; true mastery lies within the mage's heart. Yet even the keenest blade can cut both ways without guidance. Let us wield them with care.\" - Unnamed Aegis Magus",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1401.7"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "Authority and Validity",
      "source": "lmstudio",
