    {
      "cite": "300.8",
      "part": "part_iii",
      "title": "Prohibited Magical Conduct",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 300.8 Related Requirements; Prohibited Magical Conduct",
          "text": "Nothing in this Part shall be construed to prohibit the lawful practice of magic where no threat to public safety or order exists. However, certain acts remain absolutely forbidden under any circumstance, regardless of claimed necessity or emergency. Such prohibited conduct includes but is not limited to the use of binding spells for extortion, compulsion rituals designed to manipulate free will, and transmutation techniques intended to create permanent slaves or puppets. See § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting regarding the ethical obligations imposed upon all licensed mages.\n\nThe prohibition against magical slavery extends to any arrangement where a caster exerts dominant control over another's mind through sustained enchantment, thereby negating their capacity for autonomous decision-making. This includes, but is not limited to, the implantation of false memories or emotions, the installation of obedience triggers, and the alteration of personality traits in a manner that fundamentally undermines identity. Such practices violate core principles outlined in § 1.4 Persons Bound and are subject to immediate revocation of licensure under § 200.2 Apprentice Limits by analogy.\n\nFurthermore, any magical act performed with the explicit intent of causing prolonged physical suffering or debilitating injury constitutes abuse prohibited by both common law and statutory provisions. While defensive magic remains permissible within reason, offensive spells designed solely for inflicting pain without tactical necessity fall outside the scope of authorized practice. This principle aligns with § 1.7 Construction: Aggregation of Conduct, which requires examination of the totality of circumstances when determining culpability.\n\nAll mages shall adhere to these prohibitions absolutely and without exception. Failure to do so may result in disciplinary action ranging from suspension of license to permanent expulsion from the Guild, depending on severity. Violation of these core ethical standards undermines the very foundation upon which responsible magical practice rests, and must therefore be met with the sternest response available under current law. See also § 1401.3 Savings Against the Iron Mandate regarding conflicts between overlapping regulations.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "100.5",
            "1.4",
            "200.2",
            "1.7",
            "1401.3",
            "300.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Magical Conduct",
          "text": "§ 300.8 shall govern all acts deemed inherently dangerous to the public welfare or to the fabric of reality itself, regardless of whether such conduct falls under an existing schedule of arts. No caster shall engage in any magical practice that knowingly risks catastrophic collateral damage, including but not limited to spontaneous combustion, dimensional breaches, temporal dislocations, or uncontrolled elemental eruptions. The burden of proof for establishing intent and foreseeability of harm rests with the accuser; mere recklessness is insufficient grounds for conviction under this section.\n\nIt shall be a defense sufficient to dismiss charges brought pursuant to § 300.8 if the accused can demonstrate that they were acting in accordance with a valid research permit issued by the Guild, provided such actions did not exceed the scope and parameters specified therein. This provision is intended to protect bona fide scholars from unwarranted prosecution while maintaining strict accountability for negligent or malicious misuse of magical powers. The Guild reserves the right to revoke any pending permits if there is credible evidence that the proposed research poses an unacceptable risk to public safety.\n\nCasters found guilty of violating § 300.8 shall face punitive measures commensurate with the severity and consequences of their offenses, ranging from fines and suspension of licensure to permanent revocation of magical abilities and imprisonment at the discretion of the Presiding Magistrate. Repeat offenders shall be subject to enhanced penalties, including mandatory re-education under supervision and restitution for any damages incurred as a result of their unlawful activities. In cases where the accused refuses to comply with these sanctions, the Guild may petition the local courts for additional enforcement measures within the bounds of applicable law.\n\nThis section is without prejudice to all other provisions herein contained or in force elsewhere, and shall be construed liberally to effectuate its remedial purposes. The undersigned hereby ratify and confirm this article as an integral component of the Autumnwood Accords, binding upon themselves and their successors forevermore. Signed, sealed, and delivered in triplicate on this day and year first above written, attested by witnesses duly appointed for that purpose.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "300.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Magical Conduct — Continued",
          "text": "§ 300.8 Related Requirements\nUnder no circumstances shall any licenced caster engage in the practice of necromancy, blood magic, or other forbidden arts as defined by § 300.2 and the Quiet List. Violation of this prohibition constitutes a felony under the Accords and subjects the offender to immediate seizure of magical ability via seal-magic or confinement within a pocket dimension at the discretion of the Aegis Magi. The Guild maintains strict oversight over all research involving potent or unstable spells, requiring express permission from the Conservators prior to commencing any such studies under § 400.1 and related sections. Unauthorized experimentation with forbidden magic shall be treated as an act of war against the state, punishable by total magical forfeiture and permanent exile from Autumn Wood. All casters are required to maintain detailed logs of their professional activities, including spell components, casting locations, and client identities, for inspection upon reasonable demand by Guild officials. Failure to comply with these record-keeping mandates may result in suspension of licensure pending investigation into potential violations of the Prohibited Arts statutes. The Guild further reserves the right to conduct surprise inspections of caster workplaces and residences to ensure adherence to all applicable laws and regulations concerning magical practice. Any resistance to such lawful examinations shall be deemed an aggravating factor for sentencing purposes under existing penal codes governing magic crimes. Casters found guilty of breaching the Prohibited Conduct provisions face not only criminal sanctions but also civil liability for any damages incurred by third parties as a result of their illicit activities. The severe penalties imposed herein reflect the Guild's unwavering commitment to maintaining public safety and preventing the misuse of dangerous magical powers that could threaten the stability of society at large.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "300.8",
            "300.2",
            "400.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 300.8 Related Requirements; Prohibited Magical Conduct, Prohibited Magical Con",
          "text": "§ 300.8 Prohibition on Unauthorized Arcane Alterations to Living Beings. No caster shall, without express consent and a written waiver signed by the subject or their legal guardian, perform any magical procedure that alters the fundamental biology, physiology, or psychological state of another sentient being. This prohibition encompasses but is not limited to transmutation rituals aimed at physical enhancement, memory modification spells, charm effects exceeding a duration of one hour, and any form of mind-control or personality rewriting. Exceptions may be made only by the Arcane Medical Board under strict regulatory oversight for therapeutic purposes. Violations shall constitute Class A Felony Magic Offenses subject to immediate arrest and trial before the High Council on Magical Ethics. See § 1401.5 Prohibited Acts, § 200.3 Unauthorized Enhancements, § 1101.6 Bodily Autonomy Rights.\n\n§ 300.9 Restrictions on Mass Magic and Area-of-Effect Spells. Casters employing spells with radius of effect exceeding five meters or capable of affecting multiple targets simultaneously shall obtain prior written approval from the Guild's Spell Control Division. Such authorization requires proof that adequate safeguards have been implemented to prevent collateral harm to bystanders, property damage beyond reasonable necessity, and environmental contamination through magical residue. Failure to secure proper permits renders the use of such spells illegal regardless of intent or outcome. Penalties for unauthorized mass magic include immediate suspension of licensure pending investigation, mandatory remediation at offender's expense, and potential permanent revocation of casting privileges. See § 500.2 Crowd Control Protocols, § 600.3 Public Safety Measures, § 800.5 Environmental Impact Assessments.\n\n§ 300.10 Prohibition on Magical Slavery and Bondage Enslavement Devices. It shall be unlawful to create, maintain, or utilize any magical construct, enchantment, or ritual device designed to enforce total bodily submission, mind control without exception clauses, or permanent servitude upon another sentient being against their will. Such practices violate the core tenets of personhood enshrined in § 1.4 Persons Bound and constitute egregious abuse under both civil and criminal law. Offenders face harsh penalties including indefinite prison sentences, confiscation of all magical items, and mandatory psychiatric evaluation for potential re-offending risk. Exceptions apply only where such devices are employed temporarily by certified professionals for legitimate medical or security purposes under strict supervision. See § 1201.4 Human Dignity Rights, § 900.3 Prohibition on Forced Labor, § 700.8 Abuse Prevention Measures.\n\n§ 300.11 Ban on Experimental Magic Without Proper Oversight. No caster shall engage in unvetted experimentation with new or modified spells outside of officially sanctioned research facilities equipped with appropriate containment measures and emergency protocols. Unauthorized testing of novel magical theories poses unacceptable risks to public safety and environmental integrity. All innovative spellcraft must undergo rigorous peer review by the Guild's Innovation Committee prior to field deployment. Violators risk severe sanctions ranging from temporary suspension to permanent disqualification from practicing magic within Guild jurisdiction. See § 400.1 Research Permit Requirements, § 300.5 Controlled Experiments, § 200.7 Safety Standards for Spell Development.\n\nThis section establishes critical boundaries regarding the ethical application of magical powers, emphasizing respect for individual autonomy and public welfare above all else. Strict adherence to these prohibitions ensures responsible stewardship of arcane arts while preventing potential catastrophes arising from reckless experimentation or abuse of power. Any suspected violations shall be reported promptly to appropriate authorities for investigation and enforcement action as warranted by the circumstances involved. For further guidance on lawful magical practices, consult official Guild manuals or seek counsel directly from licensed professionals qualified in relevant specialties. Compliance with these mandates remains a non-negotiable obligation for all registered casters operating within Autumnwood territory. See § 1301.4 Ethical Guidelines for Caster Conduct, § 500.6 Responsibility to Society at Large, § 900.2 Abuse Prevention Initiatives.\n\n[ARCHIVE CARD: \"The Heartstone Incident - A Cautionary Tale\"]\n*In 1897, rogue mages attempted to harness the raw power of an unstable rift beneath Autumnwood for profit. Their hubris nearly destroyed the town when a poorly contained explosion leveled half the district and left dozens wounded. The ensuing inquiry led to harsher regulations on field magic, including this very clause prohibiting unauthorized area-of-effect spells. Always remember: with great power comes great responsibility...*\n\n[ARCHIVE CARD: \"Magic Abuse Statistics\"]\n*Recent reports indicate a 15% increase in cases involving prohibited magical alterations to living subjects over the past decade. While many instances involve consensual enhancement, a disturbing number appear to stem from malicious intent or gross negligence. The Arcane Medical Board urges all citizens to remain vigilant against suspicious offers of \"miracle cures\" or unrealistic physical transformations.*\n\n[ARCHIVE CARD: \"Enforcement Priorities\"]\n*The Guild dedicates significant resources to monitoring compliance with these prohibitions, utilizing advanced surveillance techniques and informant networks. Repeat offenders face swift and severe consequences, including permanent exile from magical practice entirely. Our mission is clear: protect the innocent while enabling responsible innovation within established boundaries.*\n\n[ARCHIVE CARD: \"Citizen Resources\"]\n*Victims of illegal magic abuse may seek assistance through multiple channels: filing formal complaints directly with local law enforcement, contacting the Guild's Victim Support Division for counseling and legal aid, or consulting independent experts specializing in magical forensics. Early reporting greatly enhances chances of successful prosecution and full restitution.*\n\n[ARCHIVE CARD: \"Future Outlook\"]\n*As magical technology continues advancing rapidly, so too must our regulatory framework evolve to address emerging challenges effectively. Ongoing dialogue between industry stakeholders, academic institutions, and public representatives remains essential for crafting balanced policies serving both progress and protection alike.*",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "300.8",
