        {
          "heading": "§ 300.8 Prohibited Magical Conduct — Continued",
          "text": "§ 300.9 The Ban on Blood Magic\nUnder no circumstances shall any practitioner engage in the ritualistic use of blood magic or vivisection for magical effect, a prohibition codified at § 1250 et seq. Such practices are deemed inherently barbaric and antithetical to civilized society. Violators face immediate suspension of licensure and referral to disciplinary panels for potential permanent revocation. See also § 300.6 Related Requirements; § 400.1 Research Permits.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "300.9",
            "300.6",
            "400.1",
            "300.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 300.9 Unsanctioned Divination Practices",
          "text": "Divination arts, including scrying and fortune-telling, remain strictly regulated under the auspices of the Divination Council established by Resolution 87-B. Unauthorized practice constitutes a Class D infraction subject to fines up to one thousand gold crowns per offense. Exceptions may be granted for academic research purposes upon approval from the Ethics Committee, which shall evaluate each proposed study on a case-by-case basis in accordance with established guidelines set forth in § 2105 et seq. For further details regarding permitted divination activities, consult § 300.7 Related Requirements; § 1401.4 Related Requirements.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "300.7",
            "1401.4",
            "300.9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 300.9 Alchemical Safety Standards",
          "text": "All alchemical laboratories must adhere to rigorous safety protocols outlined in the National Laboratory Code of Practice (NLCOP), including proper ventilation systems, blast-resistant containment units, and emergency shutdown mechanisms capable of neutralizing runaway reactions within milliseconds. Failure to comply with these mandates may result in immediate closure of offending facilities until rectification is completed to satisfaction of the Bureau of Hazardous Materials Control. Regular inspections shall be conducted quarterly by certified inspectors appointed by the Guildmaster's office. Detailed provisions regarding alchemical safety are contained herein at § 1502 et seq.; see also § 400.3 Borrowed Hours; § 600.1 Contracts with Non-Casters.",
          "key": "g",
          "refs": [
            "400.3",
            "600.1",
            "300.9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 300.9 Magical Weaponry Restrictions",
          "text": "The manufacture, sale, and possession of enchanted weapons remain subject to strict oversight by the Bureau of Controlled Substances and Dangerous Goods. Any individual wishing to acquire a magical firearm or edged instrument must first obtain a Special Possession Permit (SPP) from the appropriate regional authority, demonstrating both financial solvency and moral character through background checks and references. Violation of these regulations may lead to revocation of said permit and subsequent criminal charges under applicable state laws governing dangerous items. For complete guidance on acquiring lawful magical arms, refer to § 1605 et seq.; consult additionally § 300.4 Reclassification; § 700.2 Taxation of Magical Goods.",
          "key": "h",
          "refs": [
            "300.4",
            "700.2",
            "300.9"
          ]
        }
      ],
