      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.6 Related Requirements - Research Integrity and Oversight",
          "text": "The granting of any research permit under these Accords shall be predicated upon the applicant's submission of a comprehensive proposal detailing the intended scope, methodology, risks, and potential societal impacts of the proposed inquiry. This proposal must undergo rigorous peer review by at least three independent scholars of standing in the relevant field, none of whom shall have conflicts of interest with the applicant or their sponsors. Only upon approval of this vetting process may a formal permit be issued, specifying precise parameters such as duration, location, and acceptable methods of data collection.\n\nThroughout the course of any sanctioned research endeavor, the lead principal investigator bears an affirmative duty to maintain strict adherence to all stipulated conditions and safety protocols. Any material deviation from approved procedures without prior written consent constitutes grounds for immediate suspension or revocation of the permit, at the sole discretion of the desk's oversight committee. Furthermore, all raw data generated during such investigations must be preserved in its original form for a minimum period of five years following project completion, to facilitate future audit and replication efforts should they become necessary.\n\nIn exceptional circumstances where unforeseen complications arise that threaten public safety or ethical norms, the principal investigator is obligated to notify the desk without delay via secure transmission channels. Such notifications shall include full particulars regarding the nature of the incident, any injuries sustained, and corrective measures already implemented. Failure to promptly report adverse events may result in escalated disciplinary action against both the individual responsible and their employing institution. Ultimately, it remains paramount that all magical research conducted under these provisions serves the greater good while minimizing harm to sentient beings and the natural order at large.\"\n\n\"see § 1401.6 Related Requirements; see § 300.5 Research Copies of Quiet Items; see § 900.6 Related Requirements\"",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1401.6",
            "300.5",
            "900.6",
            "400.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Research Oversight and Integrity Standards",
          "text": "Under § 400.6, all research conducted under permit must maintain rigorous integrity standards to prevent abuse or accidental catastrophe. This includes mandatory logging of procedures, outcomes, and any anomalous effects observed during testing. Failure to comply with these reporting obligations may result in immediate revocation of the researcher's credentials and referral for disciplinary action. Furthermore, independent peer review panels shall be convened quarterly to audit all active research projects for compliance with safety protocols and ethical guidelines. Any suspected misconduct must be reported forthrightly to the Conservators' oversight committee for investigation. The Guild remains committed to fostering an environment where innovation can flourish responsibly, free from corruption or negligence that could endanger both caster and community alike. As stated in § 1.7(c), \"the safety of the public takes precedence over all other considerations,\" a principle echoed throughout these provisions designed to safeguard our delicate magical ecosystem.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "400.6",
            "1.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Research Integrity and Oversight",
          "text": "In accordance with § 400.6, all research conducted under permit must maintain rigorous integrity standards to prevent abuse or accidental catastrophe. This includes mandatory logging of procedures, outcomes, and any anomalous effects observed during testing. Failure to comply with these reporting obligations may result in immediate revocation of the researcher's credentials and referral for disciplinary action. Furthermore, independent peer review panels shall be convened quarterly to audit all active research projects for compliance with safety protocols and ethical guidelines. Any suspected misconduct must be reported forthrightly to the Conservators' oversight committee for investigation. The Guild remains committed to fostering an environment where innovation can flourish responsibly, free from corruption or negligence that could endanger both caster and community alike. As stated in § 1.7(c), \"the safety of the public takes precedence over all other considerations,\" a principle echoed throughout these provisions designed to safeguard our delicate magical ecosystem.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "400.6",
            "1.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Research Oversight and Integrity Standards — Continued",
          "text": "§ 400.6 Related Requirements - Research Oversight and Integrity Standards, Related Requirements - Research Oversight and Integrity\n\nNo research permit shall be issued without concurrent approval from the Ethics Board established under § 150.2, whose mandate is to ensure that all sanctioned magical inquiry adheres to ethical norms and does not endanger public welfare or ecological balance. The Board shall review proposals for potential hazards, including but not limited to unintended temporal disruptions, psychic contamination of local populations, or destabilization of ambient mana fields. Approval may be granted conditionally, with stipulations imposed on the scope, duration, and containment measures of permitted experiments.\n\nAll research facilities must maintain detailed logs of activities conducted therein, accessible for audit by Guild inspectors at reasonable times. These records shall include raw data, observations, anomalies encountered, and corrective actions taken. Failure to comply may result in suspension or revocation of operating privileges under § 1203.4(a)(iii). Furthermore, any researcher found guilty of falsifying results, sabotaging equipment, or otherwise compromising the integrity of their work faces automatic disqualification from future licensing examinations, per § 809.5(b).\n\nIn cases where research yields unexpected or dangerous outcomes, the lead principal investigator has a duty to promptly report such incidents to both the Ethics Board and the Aegis Magi for assessment and remediation. Concealment of adverse events shall be deemed gross negligence and punishable as academic misconduct under § 1605.2(d). Conversely, timely disclosure enabling swift containment may mitigate penalties imposed upon responsible parties.\n\nThe Guild reserves the right to conduct periodic unannounced inspections of all active research sites to verify compliance with safety protocols and ethical guidelines. Access shall be granted without prior notice upon presentation of valid credentials issued under § 104.8. Refusal to cooperate constitutes obstruction of justice and may lead to immediate termination of associated permits, pursuant to § 1203.7(c). Any violations discovered during such audits will be prosecuted according to the procedures outlined in § 901 et seq., with appropriate sanctions enforced as warranted by circumstances.\n\nThis framework balances the pursuit of magical knowledge with necessary safeguards against abuse and harm, reflecting the Guild's enduring commitment to responsible stewardship of arcane arts for the greater good.\" see §§ 150.2, 809.5(b), 1605.2(d)",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "400.6",
            "150.2",
            "1203.4",
            "809.5",
            "1605.2",
            "104.8",
            "1203.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Research Oversight and Integrity Standards — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "§ 400.6 Related Requirements - Research Integrity and Oversight, Research Oversight and Integrity Standards — Continued\n\nUnder § 1.7, the Accords are interpreted to ensure that magical research neither endangers public safety nor violates fundamental ethical principles. As such, all research conducted under a permit must undergo periodic review by an independent oversight committee comprising conservators, innovators, and neutral observers. These committees shall assess adherence to prescribed protocols and evaluate potential risks associated with continued experimentation. Failure to comply may result in suspension of the researcher's privileges or revocation of their license entirely, see § 200.4.\n\nFurthermore, § 300.2 mandates that any work involving necromantic arts be subject to additional scrutiny and strict containment measures. Such studies shall only proceed within specially designated facilities equipped with appropriate safeguards against accidental release or misuse. Violations of these requirements constitute serious breaches of the Accords and may lead to severe penalties up to and including sealing of magical capabilities, pursuant to § 1401.5.\n\nIn addition, researchers must maintain accurate records of all experimental procedures, results, and observations for inspection by guild authorities upon request. This includes logging any anomalies or unexpected effects encountered during testing. Such documentation serves both as a safeguard against negligence and as a resource for future investigations into emerging magical phenomena, under § 100.4.\n\nFinally, § 1.8 stipulates that the provisions of this Part remain in full force and effect notwithstanding any conflicting state or local laws, unless expressly superseded by subsequent amendments to the Accords themselves. The supremacy of these regulations ensures consistent enforcement across all jurisdictions where the Guild holds jurisdictional authority, preserving both magical safety and regulatory integrity throughout the realm.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "400.6",
            "1.7",
            "200.4",
            "300.2",
            "1401.5",
            "100.4",
            "1.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Research Integrity and Oversight Protocols",
          "text": "§ 400.8 Related Requirements - Research Integrity and Oversight, Research Oversight and Integrity Standards\n\nAll research conducted under the auspices of the Guild shall adhere to strict integrity standards as outlined in this section. First, all researchers must maintain detailed logs of their experiments, including hypotheses, methodologies, results, and any deviations from the approved protocol. These records shall be subject to random audits by the Aegis Magi to ensure compliance with safety guidelines and ethical norms. Second, researchers are prohibited from falsifying data or manipulating outcomes in a manner that compromises the validity of their findings. Any instance of fraud will result in immediate revocation of research permits and potential expulsion from the Guild. Third, all hazardous materials used in experiments must be properly stored, labeled, and disposed of according to established environmental regulations. Failure to do so may expose both the researcher and surrounding communities to undue risk. Fourth, researchers are encouraged but not required to share their findings with peer groups for review and critique. However, any publication of results must include full disclosure of funding sources and potential conflicts of interest. Finally, this section shall be construed liberally in favor of public safety and scientific advancement, provided that such interpretation does not undermine the integrity of the research process itself. See § 200.3 Temporary Mouths for provisions regarding guest researchers; under § 400.5 Unauthorized Titan Growth, unauthorized replication of protected specimens is strictly prohibited.\"\n\n\"Research Integrity and Oversight Protocols — Continued\nThis section establishes comprehensive guidelines to uphold the highest standards of scientific inquiry within the Guild's research facilities. All studies must be conducted with meticulous attention to detail, transparency, and ethical responsibility. Researchers are expected to foster a culture of accountability by actively participating in peer reviews and constructive criticism. Furthermore, any suspected misconduct shall be reported promptly through established channels for investigation and disciplinary action if warranted.\"\n\n\"By adhering to these protocols, the Guild ensures that its research endeavors contribute positively to magical theory and practical application while safeguarding against potential abuses or accidents. The integrity of scientific pursuit remains paramount in maintaining public trust and advancing knowledge responsibly.\"",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "400.8",
            "200.3",
            "400.5"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "Research Integrity and Oversight",
