    {
      "cite": "600.8",
      "part": "part_vi",
      "title": "Compliance Obligations — §600.8",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 600.8 Related Requirements and Compliance Obligations",
          "text": "Nothing in this Part shall be construed to diminish or eliminate any existing obligations imposed upon licensees by virtue of their status as such, whether under common law principles, prior administrative orders, or other regulatory regimes applicable within the jurisdiction of this Guild. Any requirements not explicitly enumerated herein remain in full force unless expressly superseded by subsequent amendment. Licensees are responsible for maintaining awareness of all relevant laws and ordinances affecting their practice, regardless of publication status within these codified provisions. Failure to comply with such obligations may result in disciplinary action under applicable sections hereof or other legal remedies available to the Guild.\n\nIn particular, licensees must adhere strictly to any conditions attached to their individual permits or certificates of qualification issued by this authority. Such stipulations constitute binding contractual undertakings enforceable independently from statutory provisions. Breach thereof shall be deemed a violation of these Accords subject to appropriate sanctions. Furthermore, all licensed practitioners are expected to engage in continuous education regarding evolving standards of magical ethics and safety protocols as promulgated herein or through official channels designated by the Conservators' Council. Neglect of such duties may warrant revocation of licensure at the sole discretion of the governing body.\n\nThe provisions contained within this section operate cumulatively with those found elsewhere throughout these Accords, creating a comprehensive framework for regulating magical activity within the Autumnwood region. Nothing herein shall be interpreted to limit or otherwise affect any rights, powers, duties, liabilities, or immunities enjoyed by the Guild, its agents, officers, employees, or duly authorized representatives under existing law or custom. All obligations assumed hereunder are undertaken voluntarily and with full understanding of their scope and consequences by each licensee accepting such terms upon issuance of their credentials. Any ambiguities arising in application shall be resolved favorably toward protection of public welfare consistent with the overarching purposes set forth hereinabove.\n\nsee § 600.1 Contracts with Non-Casters; see § 300.2 Necromancy and Unsanctioned Arts; see § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse of Authority\nUnder § 1.7 Construction provisions, this Part must be read harmoniously with the whole code to avoid internal contradictions or gaps in coverage. Where specific directives conflict with general principles, the former controls absent clear indication otherwise from competent authority. Any dispute concerning interpretation shall submit finally to binding arbitration by a panel appointed jointly by the disputing parties and the Guild Chairperson acting as neutral facilitator. Costs of proceedings borne equally unless manifest bad faith demonstrated by one side prompting equitable allocation thereof. Final arbitral awards unappealable except for plain error on face of record warranting immediate correction without prejudice to other claims asserted hereinunder or otherwise at law.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "600.1",
            "300.2",
            "200.4",
            "1.7",
            "600.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 600.9 Transitional Provisions and Grandfather Clauses",
          "text": "Notwithstanding the foregoing, certain limited exceptions shall apply retroactively to protect vested interests acquired in good faith prior to effective date of these amended Accords. Specifically, individuals currently engaged in lawful magical practices without formal licensure may continue such activities for a period not exceeding ninety (90) days following enactment herein unless otherwise prohibited by separate order from the Conservators' Council upon review of individual circumstances presented thereto. Upon expiration of said grace period, all persons desiring to resume or expand their operations must obtain appropriate authorization pursuant to these updated regulations governing qualification standards and ongoing compliance obligations applicable uniformly across all jurisdictions subject to Guild oversight.\n\nFurthermore, contracts entered into before passage hereof containing terms inconsistent herewith shall remain valid provided they do not contravene public policy considerations embodied within this legislation. Disputes arising therefrom subject to ordinary civil litigation procedures unless otherwise directed by court order or mutual agreement between contracting parties seeking alternative dispute resolution mechanisms consistent with applicable law and Guild interests. In no event shall any provision deemed invalid under these Accords affect the enforceability of remaining clauses which stand independently apart from said unenforceable provisions notwithstanding severance thereof.\n\nAny ambiguities in this Part concerning temporal applicability or scope shall be construed narrowly against expanding liability beyond original intent expressed clearly at time of adoption. Where feasible, existing arrangements should be modified prospectively rather than retroactively where possible without impairing legitimate expectations fairly relied upon by affected parties acting reasonably under the circumstances presented to them prior to implementation hereof. Transitional rules designed solely to ease adjustment burden while preserving core regulatory objectives shall prevail over conflicting interpretations suggesting stricter application absent explicit contrary directive from duly constituted authorities empowered accordingly hereunder.\n\nsee § 600.1 Contracts with Non-Casters; see § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; see § 300.4 Reclassification Procedures\nUnder § 1.8 Effective Date and Savings clauses, these provisions apply prospectively except where expressly stated otherwise creating implied waivers of prior rights inconsistent therewith. Nothing herein abrogates ongoing contractual duties owed by licensees under pre-existing agreements unless specifically revoked by competent authority pursuant to established cause-and-effect nexus demonstrated clearly upon proper notice given well in advance thereof allowing reasonable opportunity for cure absent willful misconduct warranting immediate termination without further warning issued previously hereunder or elsewhere as appropriate under governing laws applicable hereto.\n\nFILED LORE:\n- § 600.8 ensures licensees comply with all existing laws, not just Guild rules. They must stay educated on ethics and safety too. Breaking these can get you sanctioned.\n- Exceptions exist for people already practicing legally before the new rules started. They get a short window to adjust or stop until they qualify properly. Contracts made before are okay unless they violate public good. Ambiguities should be read narrowly against expanding liability unfairly. The goal is easing the transition while keeping protections in place where needed most.\n- Basically, don't let old habits die hard if they conflict with updated standards. But give folks a chance to adapt responsibly without punishing them for past actions done honestly under prior regimes. Balance is key here.\n\nFILED CITE INDEX: § 600.8 Related Requirements and Compliance Obligations; § 600.9 Transitional Provisions and Grandfather Clauses\nsee § 1.7 Construction; see § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse; see § 300.4 Reclassification Procedures; see § 600.1 Contracts with Non-Casters",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "600.1",
            "100.5",
            "300.4",
            "1.8",
            "600.8",
            "600.9",
            "1.7",
            "200.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 600.8 Related Requirements and Compliance Obligations — Continued",
          "text": "§ 600.8 shall not be construed as relieving any party of its independent duties to comply with applicable laws, rules, or regulations promulgated by the Autumnwood Accords Desk. Each signatory remains fully liable for ensuring that all acts performed under a Contract conform to both the express terms thereof and the overarching mandates set forth herein. Failure to adhere strictly to these dual obligations shall constitute grounds for immediate termination of the agreement and potential civil liability for breach of contract.\n\nFurthermore, neither Party may assert any defense based on lack of knowledge or understanding regarding the provisions of this Codex or the specific requirements of their Contract. By entering into a binding agreement with a Caster, each signatory acknowledges that they have read, understood, and accepted these terms in full. Any attempt to claim ignorance or misrepresentation shall be deemed frivolous and will not preclude enforcement actions as provided herein.\n\nIt is incumbent upon both Parties to maintain accurate records of all transactions, communications, and performances arising from the Contract. Such documentation serves as critical evidence in any dispute resolution proceedings and must be made available promptly upon request by the other signatory or authorized investigators. Neglecting this duty may result in adverse inference against the negligent Party should a controversy arise regarding the facts at issue.\n\nFinally, nothing contained in this section shall limit the inherent powers of the Autumnwood Accords Desk to investigate violations, impose penalties, or seek injunctive relief as deemed necessary to protect public safety and integrity. Compliance with § 600.8 is mandatory and non-negotiable for all Parties engaged within the scope of these regulations.\n\nsee §§ 1.4 Persons Bound, 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild, 300.3 Quiet List Procedure, 500.2 Unscheduled Weather. Under § 600.8, signatories retain independent compliance obligations beyond their contractual duties and must proactively monitor adherence to both specific terms and broader regulatory mandates to avoid liability. Failure to do so may trigger immediate contract termination and civil penalties for breach of agreement. Moreover, ignorance of the Codex's provisions affords no excuse; all parties acknowledge full acceptance upon signing. Meticulous record-keeping is essential for evidentiary purposes, and neglect thereof invites adverse inferences. Ultimately, this requirement complements the Desk's authority to enforce regulations vigorously safeguarding public welfare.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "600.8",
            "1.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 600.8 Compliance Obligations and Enforcement Mechanisms",
          "text": "Whereas the Accords impose affirmative duties upon all bound parties, failure to fulfill these obligations shall constitute grounds for immediate sanctions under applicable sections herein. Specifically, any caster failing to maintain required licensure or adhere to prescribed magical limits may be subject to revocation of privileges without prior notice. The Guild reserves discretion to initiate administrative proceedings ex parte where imminent danger is credibly alleged. Such actions shall not prejudice subsequent adjudication on the merits at trial by Arcane Duel should contested issues arise.\n\nFurthermore, all casters shall submit quarterly reports detailing magical activities undertaken during the preceding quarter, including but not limited to spellwork performed, artifacts modified or created, and any incidents resulting in injury or property damage. These disclosures must be accompanied by supporting documentation such as receipts for materials purchased and sworn statements from witnesses present at relevant proceedings. Failure to provide complete and truthful reporting shall be deemed a serious breach of trust warranting disciplinary review.\n\nEnforcement powers granted herein are cumulative and not exclusive thereof; nothing therein precludes the Guild from pursuing parallel civil or criminal remedies where appropriate under existing law. Conversely, rights conferred by these provisions may not be waived except in writing signed by the consenting party and witnessed by an impartial notary public duly commissioned within this realm. Any attempted circumvention of mandatory safeguards through subterfuge or collusion shall be treated as aggravated misconduct subject to enhanced penalties.\n\nThe ultimate goal of compliance mechanisms remains preservation of public safety while fostering responsible magical practice. Through diligent monitoring and timely intervention, the Guild seeks to minimize risks inherent in unregulated arcane experimentation while maximizing benefits accruing from lawful spellwork. By striking this delicate balance, all parties contribute to a stable society wherein magic serves as catalyst for progress rather than instrument of chaos.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "600.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 600.8 Compliance Obligations and Enforcement Mechanisms — Continued",
          "text": "This Part establishes the comprehensive compliance framework required of all entities engaged in magical contracting activities under these Accords, detailing both affirmative duties and remedial consequences for non-compliance.\n\nAll parties to a contract shall maintain accurate records of all transactions, including but not limited to spell components employed, duration of casting, and any collateral effects observed. Such records must be retained for a minimum period of ten years from the date of final performance and made available upon reasonable request by Guild inspectors or authorized representatives. Failure to comply with this recordkeeping requirement constitutes a material breach of contract entitling the non-breaching party to terminate immediately and seek damages.\n\nIn the event of suspected fraud, misrepresentation, or other wrongdoing arising in connection with a magical service agreement, any aggrieved party may petition the Autumnwood Accords Desk for an investigation. Upon receipt of such petition, the Clerk shall convene a hearing within thirty days wherein evidence may be presented and witnesses examined under oath. The Presiding Magistrate shall issue findings of fact and conclusions of law based on all admissible testimony and exhibits. If misconduct is substantiated, appropriate sanctions shall be imposed pursuant to applicable provisions herein or as otherwise directed by the Desk in its discretion.\n\nThe Guild reserves the right to audit any facility where contracted magical services were rendered, with reasonable notice given unless exigent circumstances exist warranting immediate inspection without prior warning. Inspectors acting under color of law granted hereunder shall be afforded full access to all premises and materials relevant to their investigation subject only to protections against unreasonable searches mandated by prevailing legal standards. Any resistance to lawful inspection shall be deemed an aggravating factor in determining punitive relief available to the complainant.\n\nFor violations involving personal injury or property damage resulting from negligent or intentional misuse of contracted magical powers, affected parties may bring direct civil actions seeking compensatory and consequential damages as permitted at common law or under specifically applicable statutes. The existence of a contractual relationship between plaintiff and defendant shall not preclude such tort claims but rather serve to strengthen the case for causation and proximate connection between wrongful acts suffered harms sustained.\n\nThis Section aims to balance the interests of all stakeholders involved in magical commerce by providing clear guidelines for conduct while empowering those injured by breaches thereof with meaningful avenues for redress within a fair and efficient administrative process designed to uphold both justice and order throughout our realm governed hereby.\"",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "600.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 600.8 Compliance Obligations and Enforcement Mechanisms — Administration",
          "text": "Every contract entered into under the auspices of the Accords shall contain explicit compliance clauses detailing the obligations of each party to adhere to all applicable laws, regulations, and Guild standards throughout the duration of the agreement and for a reasonable period thereafter. Failure to comply with such obligations may result in immediate termination of the contract, forfeiture of any deposits or payments made, and potential legal action for breach of terms.\n\nThe Conservators maintain a comprehensive database of all active contracts involving magical services, which is updated regularly by licensed clerks and auditors. This system allows for swift identification and prosecution of non-compliant parties, thereby safeguarding the public interest and maintaining the integrity of the Guild's regulatory framework. Regular inspections and audits are conducted to ensure ongoing adherence to contractual obligations and safety protocols.\n\nIn addition to civil remedies available under common law, the Accords empower the Aegis Magi and other authorized enforcement agents to take immediate action against violators without prior notice or hearing. Such actions may include seizing property, imposing fines, suspending licenses, or initiating criminal proceedings where appropriate. The Guild reserves the right to act unilaterally in any matter deemed necessary to protect its interests and those of its members.\n\nTransitional provisions and grandfather clauses shall be applied as needed to accommodate pre-existing arrangements that do not strictly conform to current regulations but pose no imminent threat to public safety or welfare. However, all such exceptions must be explicitly documented and subject to periodic review by the relevant oversight bodies. Any party benefiting from a grandfather clause agrees to voluntarily surrender such privileges upon written notice from the Guild authorities.\n\nEnforcement of compliance obligations shall be carried out through established channels within the Guild's judicial system, utilizing its specialized tribunals equipped to handle complex disputes arising from magical contracts. These forums are designed to provide efficient, fair resolution while minimizing disruption to commercial activity and preserving valuable expertise where possible. Parties dissatisfied with initial rulings may appeal to higher authorities in accordance with due process guarantees enshrined in the Accords themselves.\n\nUltimately, strict compliance with all contractual requirements is essential for maintaining trust between casters and their clients, as well as ensuring the long-term viability of the magical services industry. By adhering diligently to these standards, practitioners demonstrate their professionalism and commitment to upholding the highest ideals of their craft under the watchful eye of the Guild's vigilant stewards.\n\nsee § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse; see § 400.5 Unauthorized Titan Growth; see § 100.6 Delegation to Clerks; see § 700.3 Liability for Negligence",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "200.4",
            "400.5",
            "100.6",
            "700.3",
            "600.8"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "Compliance Obligations — §600.8",
