    {
      "cite": "1201.8",
      "part": "part_xii",
      "title": "Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty",
          "text": "The provisions of this Part do not supplant any applicable laws governing the transport of hazardous materials through planar space or the taxation thereof at designated transit points. See §§ 300.2, 500.4; cf. § 700.6. All magical items bearing a Guild seal must be inspected upon entry into an Autumwood jurisdiction by a duly appointed Aegis Magi or their designate. Failure to comply may result in seizure and destruction of the item at the owner's expense, under §§ 800.3, 1401.2; see also § 900.7. Any dispute arising from the interpretation of this section shall be resolved by a panel consisting of two Conservators and one Innovator appointed by Archmage Veyra, pursuant to § 100.5. Panels may issue binding orders subject only to appeal within thirty days on grounds of manifest error or abuse of discretion; such appeals are governed by Part VI hereof and shall be expedited where the public safety is implicated. Nothing herein prohibits private citizens from forming voluntary associations for the purpose of studying magic under qualified supervision, provided that no such organization engages in unsanctioned research or field casting without prior written consent from the Guild Desk. Violations shall be prosecuted as violations of this Code and punished accordingly; double jeopardy does not apply given the distinct nature of administrative sanctions versus criminal penalties. This section takes effect immediately upon adoption by a majority vote of the Accords Desk, superseding all conflicting local ordinances to the extent necessary for full implementation. See §§ 100.2, 300.5. [End of Section]",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "300.2",
            "700.6",
            "800.3",
            "900.7",
            "100.5",
            "100.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty",
          "text": "The authority of the Autumnwood Accords extends beyond terrestrial boundaries into adjacent planes of existence where Guild operations are conducted or consequences thereof manifest upon arrival. Under § 1201.3, casting spells within a Diet Chamber grants immunity from local jurisdiction but subjects the caster to full Accords enforcement upon re-entry into normal space unless exempted by special dispensation. This principle applies equally to travel between planes via pocket dimensions or natural portals where the Guild maintains oversight through stationed Aegis Magi or contracted enforcers.\n\nPlanar tolls and transit fees assessed under § 1201.2 are not mere administrative charges but represent sovereign rights of the Guild over specific extraterritorial zones. Failure to pay may result in immediate expulsion from the plane, imprisonment within a seal-bound stasis field until compliance is achieved, or both at the discretion of the presiding Arcane Councilor. Such penalties apply regardless of whether the violation occurred directly under Accords authority or was merely consequential upon entry into Guild-controlled territory.\n\nThe Desk retains inherent power to designate entire regions—including cities, wilderness tracts, and pocket realms—as zones subject exclusively to Accords law without regard for conventional geopolitical borders. Any entity operating within these areas does so by explicit permission of the Guild and must submit unconditionally to its rulings on all matters arising from such operation. Refusal to comply constitutes grounds for immediate revocation of operating privileges and potential prosecution under § 1201.6 for willful defiance of lawful authority.\n\nIn cases involving cross-jurisdictional disputes between multiple planes or realms, the original place of offense retains primary claim unless otherwise determined by mutual agreement among affected parties or arbitration by an independent panel convened specifically for such matters. The Accords recognize that magical phenomena often transcend traditional boundaries and thus require flexible approaches to enforcement tailored to unique circumstances encountered during investigation or adjudication proceedings.\n\nUltimately, the Guild asserts paramount authority over all spaces it controls whether physically present or virtually accessed through digital interfaces linked directly to its central servers anywhere in existence. Any attempt to circumvent this jurisdiction by operating covertly or utilizing unauthorized proxy services will be met with swift and severe consequences aimed at preserving the integrity of the entire magical regulatory framework established herein. Compliance is not optional but mandatory for all registered practitioners seeking continued lawful operation within any capacity recognized under these laws.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1201.3",
            "1201.2",
            "1201.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Extraterritorial Application and Planar Sovereignty",
          "text": "§ 1201.8 Related Requirements, Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty\nUnder § 1201.3, the Accords extend beyond physical borders to encompass all planes of existence where Guild-regulated magic occurs. This principle ensures that no caster may evade liability by simply stepping onto another realm's soil. The Desk retains authority wherever its laws touch, whether through direct action or mere presence.\n\nSee § 1201.6 for the definition of \"presence,\" which includes any spell component cast across dimensional boundaries. A fireball ignited in a tavern may still violate Accords if its smoke drifts into an adjacent dimension. Similarly, a research copy left on a shelf constitutes possession under § 300.5, regardless of location. The Desk interprets these provisions liberally to prevent circumvention.\n\nPlanar sovereignty remains intact unless explicitly waived by the local power. The Guild does not claim dominion over foreign lands, only regulatory oversight within its jurisdictional reach. However, when a caster's actions affect multiple realms, the Accords supersede conflicting laws. This avoids paradoxes where incompatible rules apply to the same event.\n\nIn practice, this means casters must comply with all applicable codes simultaneously. A duel in an alternate dimension follows both local custom and Guild penalties for violations. The latter may include seizure of equipment or sealing of magic, even if such sanctions seem harsh under foreign law. Equity dictates that no one escapes accountability simply because they operate beyond conventional space-time constraints.\n\nThe Desk issues advisory opinions on complex cross-planar cases as needed. These non-binding guidelines help resolve ambiguities without requiring formal litigation. Caster's Guild members are encouraged to consult these interpretations before acting in uncertain situations. Prudence minimizes risk and preserves harmony across the multiverse.\n\nUltimately, § 1201.8 affirms that magic knows no borders when it comes to responsibility. Whether cast from a bedroom or another plane entirely, every act falls under ultimate review by the Autumnwood Accords. This ensures consistent enforcement regardless of where transgressions occur. The Desk stands ready to uphold this mandate with impartial vigor.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1201.8",
            "1201.3",
            "1201.6",
            "300.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Extraterritorial Application and Planar Sovereignty — Continued",
          "text": "§ 1201.8 Related Requirements, Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty\n\nThe Autumnwood Accords shall extend their full force and effect to all casters operating within the sphere of influence of the Mages' Guild, regardless of physical location or planar state. This includes activities conducted in pocket dimensions, astral planes, demiplanes, and other non-Earthly realms that are subject to Guild oversight under § 100.7 Foreign Halls and Courtesy. Any casting performed outside Earth's native bounds shall be deemed equivalent to a sanctioned operation within the Midlands for all legal purposes, subject only to such additional requirements as may be prescribed by this Part or its successors.\n\nThe sovereign authority of the Mages' Guild over extraterritorial activities stems from its status as a universal body transcending mere geographic boundaries. As stated in § 100.6 Delegation to Clerks, the Desk possesses plenary power to regulate all matters within its purview, including those that occur beyond physical space. This jurisdiction is not limited by national borders or planar barriers but exists wherever the Guild's writ may reach. Casters who violate Accords in any locale remain fully liable under this Code, and penalties shall be enforced accordingly without regard for location.\n\nPlanar sovereignty over non-Earthly realms falls primarily to the Mages' Guild, subject to such exceptions as may arise from specific treaties or arrangements with other entities. While local powers may assert nominal oversight within their territories, ultimate control remains vested in the Desk pursuant to § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting and related provisions. Any disputes concerning jurisdiction shall be resolved by reference to this Part and applicable international accords governing cross-planar relations. The Guild reserves the right to act unilaterally where necessary to protect its interests or maintain stability across all planes.\n\nThe Accords explicitly recognize that magical phenomena often transcend conventional spatial limitations, necessitating a broad interpretation of territorial scope. As articulated in § 100.4 Records of Speech, all actions undertaken by licensed casters are subject to review and potential sanction irrespective of location. This principle extends fully to extraterritorial operations, ensuring consistent enforcement across all domains where Guild authority may apply. Casters must therefore comply with Accords even when operating beyond Earth's physical confines, aware that their conduct will be evaluated under the same rigorous standards as domestic casting.\n\nIn conclusion, § 1201.8 establishes the foundational principle that the Mages' Guild maintains comprehensive jurisdiction over all its members wherever they may find themselves, whether within traditional borders or across the vast expanse of known space and beyond. This expansive reach reflects the unique nature of magical practice as an activity unbound by conventional limitations, requiring correspondingly flexible yet firm governance to ensure safety and order throughout all realms under Guild oversight. Casters must therefore exercise due caution at all times, mindful that their actions carry legal consequences regardless of proximity to physical space or familiar laws.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1201.8",
            "100.7",
            "100.6",
            "100.5",
            "100.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty — Continued",
          "text": "§ 1201.8 Related Requirements, Extraterritorial Application and Planar Sovereignty — Continued\n\nThe Autumnwood Accords shall extend their full force and effect beyond the physical boundaries of the Midlands and the immediate plane of existence upon which they were originally promulgated. This includes all accessible pocket dimensions, alternate realities, and metaphysical spaces wherein authorized casting may occur in pursuit of lawful ends. Under § 100.4 Records of Speech, all acts governed by these provisions shall be subject to scrutiny regardless of location or dimensional displacement.\n\nPlanar sovereignty remains with the native governing authorities of each realm entered upon by a Guild licensee under a valid permit issued pursuant to Part II hereof. However, no local edict shall supersede the fundamental rights and protections accorded to casters by this Codex, including those enumerated in §§ 200–900 inclusive. Any attempt to abrogate these guarantees shall be deemed void ab initio under § 1.5 Relation to Other Law.\n\nCasters operating outside their home territory must comply with both the Accords and applicable planar statutes unless explicitly exempted by special provision contained herein or granted via written waiver from a Conservator of equal standing. In cases of conflict between competing legal regimes, priority shall be given first to safety protocols outlined in Part III, then to the greater good as interpreted by an impartial tribunal convened under § 100.8 Emergency Sitting procedures.\n\nExtraterritorial jurisdiction shall not apply where enforcement would violate core tenets of human dignity or contravene universally recognized principles of natural justice. Such exceptions are reserved exclusively for matters involving egregious misconduct warranting immediate containment rather than conventional prosecution. Determination thereof lies solely with the Aegis Magi acting under direct orders from Archmage Veyra or her duly appointed proxy.\n\nThis section incorporates by reference all existing precedents established prior to the effective date of this revision, including those set forth in §§ 1–800 inclusive. Any ambiguities arising from divergent interpretations shall be resolved favorably toward preserving the integrity and efficacy of the Guild's regulatory framework as a whole. Nothing herein shall be construed to limit inherent powers reserved by the Sovereign or her successors pursuant to § 1.2 Enacting Authority.\n\nThe provisions set forth in this article shall remain operative until expressly repealed or superseded by subsequent legislation enacted through proper channels under Articles I and II of these Accords. Until such time as formal amendment occurs, all parties bound hereby are deemed to have accepted binding adherence thereto regardless of personal knowledge thereof. Failure to comply may result in sanctions ranging from temporary suspension up to permanent revocation of licensure depending on severity of infraction.\n\nIn witness whereof, the undersigned hereby attest their solemn commitment to uphold these sacred vows amidst all trials and tribulations that may befall them on this journey through space and time together as one unified whole under the banner of truth and righteousness forevermore! Thus concluded at Autumn Wood Hall in the Year of Our Lord [REDACTED] during the reign of His Majesty King [REDACTED], by authority vested in me by virtue of office held without limitation or reservation whatsoever except as expressly limited herein. Signed this ____ day of ____________, AD ________.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1201.8",
            "100.4",
            "1.5",
            "100.8",
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty — Administration",
          "text": "§ 1201.8 Related Requirements. The Autumnwood Accords apply fully to all acts committed by licensed casters, whether within the physical bounds of Autumn Wood or in any extradimensional space under their control. No caster may invoke planar travel as a shield against lawful oversight; they remain subject to Guild authority wherever their magic manifests. See § 100.7 Foreign Halls and Courtesy for provisions on reciprocal recognition between Member Halls operating under this Code. Under § 400.2 Pocket Dimensions as Labs, all private realms created by authorized casters constitute extensions of the caster's domicile and are subject to routine inspection by Aegis Magi upon reasonable notice. Any unauthorized pocket dimension discovered in active use shall be deemed a prima facie violation of §§ 300.1 Schedules of Arts and 400.5 Unauthorized Titan Growth, punishable as a Class B felony under § 800.6 Related Penalties. Planar sovereignty is not absolute; the Guild retains inherent authority to regulate all magical activity originating from its licensed members, regardless of location. This includes monitoring for prohibited schools listed in the Quiet List (§ 300.1) and ensuring compliance with research permits (§ 400.1). Violations occurring outside traditional jurisdiction shall be adjudicated by a special tribunal convened under § 900.8 Emergency Sitting procedures. The Aegis Magi are empowered to seize any equipment or materials facilitating unlawful magic, subject to due process safeguards outlined in §§ 200.5 Guest Casters and 700.6 Related Rights. Caster's personal realms remain private sanctuaries unless specifically implicated in ongoing investigations; however, all such spaces must maintain an open channel for Guild oversight at the discretion of local Archmages. See also § 1401.9 Seals and Marks regarding identification protocols applicable to planar casters. This provision ensures comprehensive coverage of magical conduct across all domains, preventing jurisdictional loopholes that could undermine the Accords' integrity. Any attempt to evade this reach shall be treated as evidence of malicious intent under § 600.4 Presumptions of Guilt in Flagrante Cases. The Guild stands ready to assert its full authority, both domestically and abroad, to protect the public from rogue magical practices wherever they may occur.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1201.8",
            "100.7",
            "400.2",
            "300.1",
