        "700.6"
      ],
      "unresolved_refs": [
        "1200.5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cite": "200.9",
      "part": "part_ii",
      "title": "Prohibited Practices and Disciplinary Measures",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 200.9 Related Requirements - Prohibited Practices and Disciplinary Measures",
          "text": "No caster shall engage in any practice expressly forbidden by the Accords or deemed injurious to public safety, including but not limited to unauthorized ritual magic, blood offerings, necromantic summoning, or the creation of sentient constructs through forbidden transmutation. Such acts constitute a grave violation warranting immediate investigation by the Aegis Magi and potential revocation of licensure. The burden of proof shall rest upon the accuser in all disciplinary proceedings involving alleged violations of § 200.9.\n\nViolations of this section may result in sanctions ranging from fines up to one thousand gold pieces, suspension of casting privileges for periods not exceeding six months, mandatory retraining under direct supervision of an Aegis Magi, or permanent expulsion from the Guild and all associated benefits. Repeat offenders shall face escalated penalties including confiscation of magical items, public shaming via posting on the Quiet List, and in egregious cases, imprisonment without bail pending trial by peers under § 2010.\n\nCasters found guilty of violating § 2009 shall additionally be required to pay a restitution fee calculated at three times the estimated value of any damage caused or magical services rendered improperly. Failure to comply with these financial obligations within thirty days may lead to seizure of assets and further legal action under applicable laws. The Guild reserves the right to adjust penalty amounts as necessary based on circumstances surrounding each specific infraction.\n\nNothing in this section shall be construed to limit the authority of local law enforcement or civil courts to pursue separate actions against casters for crimes committed outside the scope of professional practice, provided such charges do not duplicate penalties already imposed under these Accords. Concurrent proceedings remain permissible unless expressly prohibited by statute or judicial order. Casters are reminded that dual liability carries significant personal and financial risks requiring prudent legal counsel before engaging in any potentially problematic activity.\n\nAll casters must acknowledge receipt of this section upon licensure renewal annually, confirming understanding of their obligations regarding prohibited practices. Refusal to sign shall result in denial of license until compliance is verified through alternative means acceptable to the Desk. The Guild maintains strict confidentiality around disciplinary records except as required by law or for internal review purposes only. Breach of privacy protections may subject violators to additional sanctions under § 2015 regarding data handling protocols.\n\nThis provision serves as a critical safeguard against abuse of magical powers and protection of societal interests, reflecting the consensus wisdom of countless generations of practitioners who have shaped these rules through hard experience. Casters are urged to internalize its teachings fully rather than treating them as mere bureaucratic formalities devoid of substance. Only thus can we preserve both our profession's integrity and our own safety in an increasingly complex world where magic shapes reality itself.\n\nsee § 1.4 Persons Bound; see § 300.2 Necromancy; Unsanctioned Arts; see § 900.7 Related Requirements for additional context on disciplinary procedures.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "200.9",
            "1.4",
            "300.2",
            "900.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Practices and Disciplinary Measures",
          "text": "Mages who violate the core tenets of the Accords face immediate disciplinary action, regardless of their rank or standing within the Guild. The Aegis Magi are empowered to arrest any individual suspected of practicing forbidden arts without warrant, provided there is reasonable cause for such belief. Suspects shall be brought before a tribunal composed of three Conservators and two Innovators, with the Archmage Sovereign presiding in cases involving high-ranking officials or members of her immediate family.\n\nUpon conviction of a serious offense, the accused mage may face one or more of the following sanctions: permanent revocation of licensure, sealing of magical abilities via riturgical suppression, exile from Autumn Wood and its environs for an indefinite period, or confinement within a magically stabilized pocket dimension until such time as they demonstrate genuine remorse and rehabilitation. In particularly egregious cases where the threat to public safety is deemed existential, execution by means consistent with the laws of magic may be authorized as a last resort.\n\nThe Guild maintains strict oversight over all magical research conducted under its auspices, requiring detailed reporting on experimental procedures and results. Any attempt to conceal findings or falsify data shall result in immediate expulsion from the relevant study group and potential revocation of all privileges held by the offender. Violations involving the misuse of classified materials will be treated as high treason against the Guild itself, punishable by severe measures short of death if deemed necessary for the greater good.\n\nDisciplinary hearings shall be conducted with due process, affording suspects ample opportunity to present their defense and call witnesses in their favor. However, appeals are limited to cases where procedural errors materially affected the outcome, lest endless litigation paralyze enforcement efforts. Final decisions rest solely with the tribunal, whose judgments are binding on all parties except in instances of blatant corruption or malice.\n\nThe Accords remain steadfast in their commitment to maintaining order within the magical community while protecting the wider population from potential harm caused by rogue practitioners. This balance between liberty and security shall be preserved at all costs, even when it requires harsh measures against those who threaten the delicate equilibrium upon which civilization itself depends. Only thus can the light of reason shine forth unclouded by the darkness of unchecked ambition.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Practices and Disciplinary Measures — Continued",
          "text": "§ 200.9 No Caster Shall Engage in Forbidden Rituals or Black-Market Dealing\n\nIt is hereby enacted that no holder of this License shall practice any forbidden school of magic, nor engage in the sale or purchase of prohibited artifacts, under penalty of immediate revocation and permanent disbarment. This prohibition extends to all forms of illicit magical commerce, including but not limited to the trafficking of sentient constructs, unholy relics, and cursed items of unknown provenance. The Guild maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy regarding such activities, which threaten both public safety and the integrity of the arcane community. Violators shall be subject to swift disciplinary action at the sole discretion of the Desk, without prejudice to any further legal proceedings that may arise.\n\nIn addition to these prohibitions, holders are reminded of their ongoing obligation to comply with all applicable laws and regulations governing magical practice within the jurisdiction of this Hall. This includes adherence to local zoning ordinances, environmental statutes, and consumer protection measures as they pertain to magical services. Failure to abide by these external mandates shall constitute grounds for disciplinary review under this License, regardless of any prior approvals obtained from the Guild. The Desk reserves the right to audit compliance with such laws at its discretion, utilizing reasonable means including but not limited to inspections, subpoenas, and sworn testimony. Holders are advised to maintain thorough records of all business activities, as these may be requested in connection with any disciplinary investigation.\n\nThe penalties for violating this section are severe and cumulative. Upon finding a holder guilty of engaging in forbidden practices or black-market dealings, the Desk shall first suspend their License effective immediately, pending completion of an inquiry into the extent and nature of the violations. If sufficient evidence is produced to justify permanent revocation, such action shall be taken forthwith, leaving no opportunity for appeal. In cases where criminal charges are warranted, the Guild shall cooperate fully with law enforcement authorities in bringing perpetrators to justice. This includes providing access to relevant records, testimony from witnesses, and any other materials deemed necessary for a thorough investigation. Holders are warned that repeated offenses will be treated as aggravating factors in determining appropriate sanctions.\n\nFinally, holders should note that this prohibition is not limited solely to their individual conduct, but extends to all business associates and representatives acting on their behalf within the scope of authorized activities. Any person found complicit in facilitating a holder's prohibited actions shall be deemed jointly liable for any resulting penalties imposed upon said holder. This joint liability provision underscores the collective responsibility inherent in maintaining a lawful and orderly magical marketplace. All parties are urged to exercise due diligence in vetting potential partners and suppliers before entering into agreements that could implicate them under this section. Failure to do so may result in shared culpability and consequent punishment, regardless of direct involvement in any specific violation.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "200.9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Magical Activities and Sanctions for Violation",
          "text": "Section 200.9 establishes the prohibitions governing all licensed casters within the Autumnwood jurisdiction, alongside the disciplinary measures applicable to those who breach these mandates. No licensor shall employ magic that directly contravenes the fundamental tenets of the Accords: the preservation of life and the maintenance of societal stability. Specifically, it is forbidden for any caster to use their art to manipulate biological processes in a manner intended to cause bodily harm or permanent disability to another sentient being, regardless of consent given under duress or ignorance. Such actions constitute an egregious violation of the sacred bond between magic and morality enshrined in Clause 3012 of the original Accords.\n\nFurthermore, casters are strictly prohibited from engaging in any magical practices that threaten the structural integrity of buildings, bridges, infrastructure, or natural formations without explicit authorization from a Conservator Councilor. Unauthorized alteration of terrain through spellwork may result in catastrophic failure and loss of life, for which the responsible caster shall bear full liability under common law principles of negligence and strict tort. This prohibition extends to any ritualistic activities involving the summoning or binding of extra-planar entities deemed dangerous or unpredictable by the Guild's arcane research division. Such practices require a minimum clearance level of 40 plus ten percent of the entity's power rating, subject to prior approval by at least two independent mages of equal standing.\n\nDisciplinary measures for violation of these prohibitions are enumerated in Appendix C, and include immediate suspension of license privileges pending investigation, revocation of certification status upon substantiation of guilt, and mandatory retraining courses focused on ethical conduct and responsible spellcasting techniques. Repeat offenders may face permanent expulsion from the Guild rolls and disqualification from holding any future licensure within the Autumnwood territory. In cases where violations involve criminal activity such as assault or theft facilitated by magic, authorities shall be promptly notified to initiate appropriate legal proceedings concurrent with internal disciplinary actions. The Guild reserves the right to seek restitution for damages incurred due to prohibited magical operations performed by its members, regardless of whether those operations were conducted in a professional capacity.\n\nThe spirit and intent of Section 200.9 shall govern all determinations made hereunder, ensuring that magic remains a force for good within our community rather than a tool for personal gain or malevolent ends. All licensed casters are charged with upholding these standards diligently and reporting any suspicious activities observed during their professional engagements to the nearest Conservator Station without delay. Failure to comply may result in severe consequences both personally and professionally, underscoring the gravity of one's obligations under this comprehensive code of conduct binding upon all practitioners of the arcane arts within our realm. By accepting licensure into the Autumnwood Guild, each caster pledges allegiance not only to the letter but also to the noble ideals embodied therein, striving always to serve their clients faithfully while safeguarding the welfare of society at large.\n\nsee § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; see § 300.2 Necromancy: Unsanctioned Arts; see § 400.3 Borrowed Hours and Interest in Time\nunder § 1.8 Effective Date and Savings Provisions, these prohibitions take immediate effect upon enactment of this revised code.\nsee § 500.1 Field Casting for Value Regarding compensation issues arising from prohibited practices.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "100.5",
            "300.2",
            "400.3",
            "1.8",
            "500.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Magical Activities and Sanctions for Violation — Continued",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords strictly prohibit the practice of certain magical arts, regardless of licensure status or intended purpose. These forbidden practices include necromancy, blood magic, hexcraft, shapeshifting, divination beyond permitted scrying, and any spellwork involving sentient beings without explicit consent. The violation of these prohibitions constitutes a felony under § 200.1 and subjects the offender to immediate arrest and trial before the Aegis Magi, who have sole jurisdiction over such cases per § 100.5.\n\nSanctions for prohibited magical activities range from confiscation of illegal equipment and permanent sealing of illicit magic circuits (§ 400.3) to imprisonment in specialized containment facilities designed for high-risk casters. Repeat offenders face escalating penalties including exile from the Midlands, revocation of all future licensure rights under § 200.4, and potential criminal charges under Imperial Law if applicable. In egregious cases involving harm to persons or property, the offender may be subject to capital punishment as authorized by § 1301.6.\n\nThe Conservators maintain that these prohibitions are necessary to preserve public safety and prevent the destabilizing effects of rogue magical practices upon society at large. They argue that even seemingly benign forms of forbidden magic can have unforeseen consequences that threaten both individual welfare and the broader political order. The Innovators, by contrast, contend that such restrictions stifle legitimate research and hinder progress in understanding the full scope of arcane potential. Despite these philosophical differences, all parties agree that certain lines must not be crossed under any circumstances.\n\nEnforcement of these prohibitions falls primarily to the Aegis Magi, who operate with broad discretion to investigate suspected violations as they see fit. The Desk may issue warrants for immediate seizure of illegal materials and apprehension of offenders without prior notice or judicial review in urgent situations (§ 100.8). However, all subsequent proceedings must adhere strictly to due process requirements outlined herein and under general criminal procedure statutes. Failure to follow proper channels can result in dismissal of charges and potential liability for wrongful detention.\n\nThe Accords further mandate that licensed casters report any suspected illegal magical activity observed during the course of their professional duties pursuant to § 300.5. While anonymous tips are not actionable, credible evidence submitted by sworn witnesses may trigger an investigation at the discretion of the Aegis Magi. Refusal to cooperate with lawful inquiries may constitute contempt and invite disciplinary action against the recalcitrant party under § 1201.7.\n\nUltimately, the goal of these prohibitions is to maintain a delicate balance between fostering beneficial magical innovation while preventing abuse that could endanger lives or undermine social stability. The Desk remains committed to upholding this equilibrium through vigilant oversight and unwavering adherence to established standards of conduct for all practitioners operating within its purview.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "200.1",
            "100.5",
            "400.3",
            "200.4",
            "1301.6",
            "100.8",
            "300.5",
            "1201.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Magical Activities and Sanctions for Violation — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "Any licentiate who knowingly engages in prohibited magical activities shall be subject to immediate suspension of their license pending investigation by the Aegis Magi. Upon completion of such inquiry, if guilt is established beyond a reasonable doubt, further disciplinary measures may be imposed at the discretion of the Guild. These sanctions include but are not limited to revocation of licensure, permanent expulsion from the ranks of authorized casters, and referral for criminal prosecution where applicable under secular law.\n\nIt shall be deemed an act of gross misconduct for any licentiate to utilize their professional standing or credentials to facilitate illegal arcane practices by third parties. Such complicity will result in severe penalties mirroring those applied to direct violators, including imprisonment without bail pending trial. The burden of proof rests solely upon the accuser to demonstrate clear evidence of guilt before any punitive action may be taken against a named individual.\n\nIn cases where prohibited activities are discovered during routine inspections or audits conducted by Guild officials, all materials and equipment involved shall be seized and held in secure storage until disposition can be determined by the appropriate adjudicatory body. Ownership claims must be substantiated with verifiable documentation prior to release of any items. Failure to comply with these provisions may constitute a separate offense punishable independently of the original violation.\n\nThe Guild reserves the right to impose additional restrictions or limitations on specific licentiates deemed high-risk based on their past behavior patterns and potential for future misconduct. Such measures shall be implemented without notice unless otherwise required by due process protections outlined herein. Affected parties remain entitled to appeal adverse determinations through established grievance procedures within a reasonable timeframe after notification of action taken.\n\nAll provisions contained in this section regarding prohibited magical activities and corresponding sanctions are hereby reaffirmed as essential components of the overarching regulatory framework governing licensed casting services throughout the jurisdiction. Compliance with these rules is mandatory for all holders of valid practice permits issued under authority of these Accords, regardless of individual circumstances or extenuating factors alleged to exist outside the scope of official review proceedings.\n\nNon-compliance with this subsection may lead to escalation of enforcement actions including but not limited to administrative citations, monetary fines levied against responsible entities and/or individuals, civil liability claims brought by aggrieved third parties suffering harm as a result of unlawful operations carried out under color of law, and potential indictment for related felonies if applicable under prevailing statutes. The Guild acts swiftly and decisively in matters concerning public safety implications arising from illegal magic use to maintain order and protect citizen welfare interests paramount to its mission mandate set forth hereinabove with full force and effect.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
