    {
      "cite": "1201.9",
      "part": "part_xii",
      "title": "Waiver and Modification",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Waiver and Modification",
          "text": "The provisions herein are intended to supplement rather than supplant the core obligations established in earlier sections. A caster licensed under these Accords must maintain at all times an active membership in good standing with one of the recognized Guild Halls as defined by § 100.1, and shall promptly notify their Hall of any material change in circumstances that might affect their licensure status pursuant to § 200.4. Failure to comply with these maintenance requirements constitutes a breach of contract under § 600.7 and may result in suspension or revocation of the license without prejudice to further action for damages. Nothing in this section shall be construed to limit the applicability of any other provisions herein, including but not limited to those governing permissible acts, prohibited conduct, and disciplinary proceedings. The Desk retains full discretion to interpret these requirements as necessary to preserve the integrity of the licensure system and protect the public interest. Any ambiguities shall be resolved in favor of a strict construction against the licensee, consistent with established principles of statutory interpretation applicable to professional certifications. This section operates as an independent covenant, enforceable even upon termination or expiration of the original license agreement.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "100.1",
            "200.4",
            "600.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1201.10 Waiver and Modification",
          "text": "No waiver of any provision herein shall be implied by failure to act or enforce rights diligently; express written consent from all affected parties is required for any modification. The Guild reserves the right to amend these requirements at its sole discretion with thirty days' written notice, subject to approval by a majority vote of the Desk under § 100.3. All changes shall be published in an official bulletin and posted prominently at each Hall entrance. Licensees are deemed to have constructive knowledge of amendments upon publication regardless of actual receipt. Any dispute regarding the validity or scope of modifications must be brought before the Desk within ten days of notice; failure to do so constitutes acceptance of the new terms. This clause is designed to ensure flexibility in addressing evolving challenges while maintaining clear standards for accountability and oversight. No oral representations or informal understandings shall override these written provisions except through formal amendment procedures as outlined above.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "100.3",
            "1201.10"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1201.9 Related Requirements — Continued",
          "text": "§ 1201.9 Related Requirements governs the procedural prerequisites for initiating and sustaining an Accords Trial under § 1201.3, ensuring that due process is afforded to all accused casters regardless of their status or affiliations. The Desk shall not commence proceedings until such time as a formal Indictment has been filed with sufficient particularity to inform the defendant of the specific allegations against them; mere suspicion or circumstantial evidence shall not suffice for this purpose. Furthermore, any person facing charges must be afforded a reasonable period to marshal their defenses and consult with legal counsel prior to appearing before a Magistrate or Trial Panel, unless waived in writing by the accused. Failure to adhere to these foundational mandates renders any subsequent actions void ab initio, subject only to remedy by the aggrieved party through proper channels as outlined herein.\n\nIn addition to the foregoing requirements, all evidence presented during an Accords Trial must be submitted in a format deemed admissible under the Rules of Arcane Evidence set forth at § 1201.5. This includes transcripts of testimonies, certified copies of relevant documents, and any physical or digital artifacts pertinent to the case at hand. The presiding Magistrate shall review such materials ex parte prior to opening sessions for public deliberation, redacting any sensitive information as necessary to protect privacy interests while preserving the integrity of the evidentiary record. Parties may object on procedural grounds if they believe that improper evidence has been introduced or excluded, provided said objections are raised promptly and accompanied by a detailed statement of reasons therefor.\n\nIt is further mandated that all proceedings conducted under § 1201 shall be recorded verbatim via both audio-visual means and written transcripts prepared by official court reporters appointed by the Desk. These records constitute the sole official account of events transpiring before the Tribunal and may be accessed upon request by any interested party subject to applicable privacy restrictions. Copies thereof shall be made available free of charge unless redaction is warranted for security or confidential reasons, in which case a nominal fee may be assessed to cover administrative costs associated with processing such requests. Through these meticulous safeguards, the Accords ensure that justice remains blind and impartial, administered fairly according to the highest standards of magical jurisprudence recognized throughout the Realm.\n\n\"Under § 1201.9 Related Requirements, every step must be followed precisely—from filing the Indictment to submitting admissible evidence—to guarantee a fair trial for all accused casters.\"",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1201.9",
            "1201.3",
            "1201.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1201.9 Related Requirements — Administration",
          "text": "The regulation of interplanar transit remains a contentious issue within the Autumnwood Accords, with disputes frequently arising between the Mages' Guild and other powerful entities. To address this growing complexity, new provisions have been enacted to govern the movement of goods, people, and magical phenomena across dimensional boundaries. These requirements are designed to ensure that such crossings do not disrupt the delicate balance of power in the multiverse.\n\nFirstly, all items transiting between planes must bear an official transit stamp from a licensed Arcane Customs Office. This seal serves as proof that the contents have been inspected and deemed safe for passage through unstable thresholds. Failure to affix this mark may result in confiscation of goods or fines imposed upon the responsible party. Exceptions apply only in cases of urgent necessity, where prior approval may be granted by an Archmage.\n\nSecondly, tolls must be paid in advance whenever traversing a plane under the jurisdiction of another faction's Hall. These fees compensate for wear and tear on dimensional gateways as well as administrative oversight costs. Payment is typically made via Wario Coin or equivalent currency accepted by the receiving authority. Refusal to settle debts may lead to denial of further passage privileges until resolution occurs.\n\nThirdly, extraterritorial casting into a Diet Chamber requires explicit permission from both local authorities and any involved foreign Halls. Such activities are heavily regulated due to potential risks posed by uncontrolled magical reactions occurring outside established parameters. Violators face severe penalties including imprisonment or exile depending on severity of infractions committed during unauthorized experiments conducted abroad without consent.\n\nFinally, cartographic materials depicting sensitive locations must not be marketed as licenses to raid enemy territories indiscriminately. While maps serve useful navigational purposes within legal frameworks, they cannot justify aggressive actions against sovereign powers lacking mutual defense agreements in place beforehand. Misuse of such resources will result in immediate revocation of privileges held by offending individuals or organizations until corrective measures are taken satisfactorily.\n\nThese provisions reflect the evolving nature of interplanar commerce and diplomacy under current conditions dictated by rapid expansion of magical capabilities across myriad realms simultaneously experiencing unprecedented growth spurts fueled largely by innovation-driven breakthroughs achieved through collaborative efforts among diverse stakeholders worldwide seeking shared prosperity amidst rising tensions threatening peace stability globally at large scale levels requiring urgent attention from all concerned parties alike if catastrophic consequences are to be avoided entirely henceforth moving forward permanently without delay whatsoever ever again!!\"\n\nsee § 1201.3 Extraterritorial Casting into a Diet Chamber; see § 1201.4 Cartography Sold as a License to Raid; see § 1201.5 Related Requirements; under § 1.7 Construction, Aggregation of Conduct applies here too.\"",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1201.3",
            "1201.4",
            "1201.5",
            "1.7",
            "1201.9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1201.9 Related Requirements — Transit and Jurisdictional Boundaries",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords recognize that magical practice often transcends conventional political borders, whether through interdimensional travel or the casting of spells with area-of-effect consequences. To address these complexities, § 1201 establishes a framework for determining jurisdiction when disputes arise across regional lines. Under § 1201.9, any mage operating outside their Hall's territorial limits shall be subject to the laws and regulations of that locale, provided those rules do not conflict with core Accords provisions. This principle ensures consistent standards while respecting local autonomy.\n\nThe Desk may issue special permits allowing conservative casting in restricted zones, such as near sensitive infrastructure or civilian populations (§ 1201.9(a)). Such permissions require rigorous risk assessment and compensation for potential damages, outlined in § 1201.10. Conversely, § 1201.11 prohibits any casting that could destabilize planar barriers without explicit authorization from the Conservators. Violations trigger immediate seizure of equipment and fines proportional to harm caused (§ 1201.12).\n\nIn cases where multiple jurisdictions claim authority over a single incident, seniority among Halls determines precedence (§ 1201.13(a)). The presiding Desk shall mediate disagreements using established protocols in § 1201.14. All rulings must be documented and published promptly for transparency (§ 1201.15). Appeals lie only to the Arcane Tribunal, whose decision is final under § 1201.16.\n\nThis structure balances flexibility with accountability, acknowledging that magic defies geographical constraints while safeguarding public welfare. By clarifying jurisdictional boundaries and enforcement mechanisms, the Accords aim to minimize conflicts between neighboring regions and maintain overall stability in an increasingly interconnected magical society.\"\n\n\"see § 1201.7 Related Requirements; see § 1201.8 Related Requirements; under § 1201.9(a) transit permits;\"",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1201.9",
            "1201.10",
            "1201.11",
            "1201.12",
            "1201.13",
            "1201.14",
            "1201.15",
            "1201.16",
            "1201.7",
            "1201.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1201.9 Jurisdictional Boundaries and Transit Stamps",
          "text": "The Accords shall not apply within the borders of any sovereign nation, unless expressly extended by treaty or special permit. This limitation ensures that local laws remain paramount in matters of public order and civil rights. Any attempt to enforce Guild authority outside its designated halls shall be deemed null and void under § 1.5 Relation to Other Law. Exceptions exist for minor infractions committed by members during transit between licensed locations, provided such acts do not disrupt the peace or endanger the innocent. In these instances, the member may invoke § 1201.3 Extraterritorial Casting into a Diet Chamber as a mitigating circumstance at their discretion. Transit stamps issued by authorized officials serve as proof of lawful passage through restricted zones and must be presented upon request by law enforcement or Guild inspectors. Failure to produce such documentation may result in temporary detention for verification purposes under § 1201.6 Related Requirements. The Desk retains the ultimate authority to interpret and apply these provisions according to the spirit of the Accords, not merely their literal text, as outlined in § 1.7 Construction Aggregation of Conduct. Any ambiguities shall be resolved through established precedents set by prior rulings of the Archmage Sovereign or delegated panels thereof. It is hereby declared that nothing herein shall be construed to undermine the sovereignty and dignity of any nation-state whose laws may conflict with those contained in this Code. Should a dispute arise regarding the extent of Guild jurisdiction, it shall be adjudicated solely by the full Council assembled under emergency protocols defined elsewhere. Members are reminded that their actions abroad remain subject to scrutiny even when beyond physical presence within Autumn Wood grounds. This clarification aims to prevent misunderstandings and potential conflicts stemming from unclear territorial mandates inherent in cross-planar commerce and study pursuits. Let no one mistake these boundaries for mere formalities—they represent the very foundation upon which lawful magical practice rests securely amidst a world fraught with peril and uncertainty alike.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1.5",
            "1201.3",
            "1201.6",
            "1.7",
            "1201.9"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "Waiver and Modification",
