    {
      "cite": "1301.9",
      "part": "part_xiii",
      "title": "Sunrise Accrual and Default Penalties",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Sunrise Accrual and Default Penalties",
          "text": "The enforcement of these Accords extends beyond mere punitive measures to encompass the holistic rehabilitation and reintegration of those who have violated them. Under § 1301.2 Penalties; Sunrise Accrual, sanctions are designed not only to punish but also to restore balance to the magical equilibrium disrupted by transgressions. This philosophy underpins the various mechanisms employed by the Guild for post-sanction oversight and community reintegration.\n\n§ 1301.5 Related Requirements mandates that all individuals subject to sanction must undergo a mandatory period of supervised probation, during which their conduct is closely monitored by assigned mentors or guardians. These mentors shall be drawn from reputable members of the Guild community committed to guiding the mentee toward lawful behavior and ethical magical practice. Failure to comply with the terms of one's probationary agreement may result in the imposition of additional sanctions under § 1301.2 Penalties; Sunrise Accrual, including extended periods of confinement or sealing of magical faculties.\n\nFurthermore, § 1301.5 Related Requirements stipulates that all sanctioned individuals must contribute a portion of their earnings to the Guild's Reintegration Fund during their period of probation. These funds shall be used to support educational programs, community outreach initiatives, and other efforts aimed at fostering understanding of the Accords among those most susceptible to temptation. Through such means, the Guild seeks to address the root causes of magical misconduct while empowering former offenders to become positive contributors to society once more.\n\nFinally, § 1301.6 Related Requirements grants any member of the public the right to petition for revocation or modification of a sanction if they can demonstrate substantial compliance with its terms and a genuine commitment to lawful behavior. Such petitions shall be reviewed by an independent panel comprising Guild officials, community leaders, and representatives of affected parties. Decisions regarding revocation shall be made solely on the merits of each individual case, ensuring fairness and equity in all enforcement actions undertaken under these Accords.\n\nSee also § 1301.4 Who May Inspect for provisions pertaining to oversight and monitoring of sanctioned individuals; § 200.5 Guest Casters regarding temporary permissions for non-members; and § 700.9 Related Requirements on appeals procedures applicable across all Guild sanctions. Under § 400.3 Borrowed Hours; Interest in Time, timely compliance with probationary obligations may yield favorable outcomes in future sanction reviews. Finally, per § 500.1 Field Casting for Value, sanctioned individuals retain certain rights to engage in lawful magical commerce subject to ongoing supervision.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1301.2",
            "1301.5",
            "1301.6",
            "1301.4",
            "200.5",
            "700.9",
            "400.3",
            "500.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Sunrise Accrual and Default Penalties",
          "text": "In accordance with § 1301.2, failure to remit the full amount due by midnight on the first business day following notification shall constitute an immediate default event, triggering accrual of additional fees under Section III(C) unless cured within four hours. Such prompt payment is a condition precedent to continued licensure privileges and must be maintained at all times during the term of each permit granted under these Accords. § 1301.4 empowers any Guild officer or authorized agent to inspect books, records, and physical premises without prior notice where reasonable suspicion exists that fees remain unpaid or have been improperly collected. Upon discovery of such violations, immediate suspension of all casting activities shall ensue until compliance is verified through satisfactory proof of payment rendered directly to the Desk Treasury in Wario Coin. The burden of establishing timely remittance rests solely upon the licensed caster and their agents; mere assertion of force majeure or external hardship shall not excuse default absent prior written waiver by the Archmage Sovereign or her duly appointed representatives. This strict liability standard reflects the Guild's fundamental interest in preserving public trust and maintaining fiscal integrity across all jurisdictions bound hereby. Any attempt to evade assessment through artificial inflation of costs, falsification of receipts, or collusion with fraudulent vendors shall be deemed willful misconduct warranting revocation of licensure without prejudice to further action under applicable penal statutes. § 1301.5 mandates that all disputes regarding fee calculations or collection procedures be resolved exclusively through established administrative channels rather than private negotiation or litigation outside the Guild's purview. The Desk Clerk retains sole authority to interpret ambiguous terms within this Code and render final determinations binding upon all parties involved, subject only to review by the full Council of Archmages at their next scheduled session. Violation of these provisions shall result in progressive sanctions ranging from monetary penalties up to threefold the original amount owed, through indefinite suspension of privileges, culminating in permanent expulsion from the Guild rolls and immediate referral for criminal prosecution where warranted. Compliance with this section is non-negotiable as it forms the bedrock upon which the entire regulatory framework rests, ensuring equitable treatment of all members while safeguarding against abuse or exploitation of the system designed to govern magical practice throughout our realm.\"",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1301.2",
            "1301.4",
            "1301.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Sunrise Accrual and Default Penalties — Continued",
          "text": "§ 1301.9 Related Requirements, Sunrise Accrual and Default Penalties. Under this section, the Desk establishes the temporal framework for fee accrual and default proceedings. All fees prescribed herein shall begin to accrue at \"sunrise,\" meaning the first moment of daylight on the day a permit is issued or an obligation becomes enforceable. This rule ensures equitable treatment across all jurisdictions within the Guild's dominion, preventing disputes over time zones or local customs from affecting financial liability.\n\nShould any party fail to meet their payment obligations by the due date, default penalties shall automatically apply in accordance with § 1301.2. These penalties serve both punitive and compensatory functions, offsetting losses incurred by the Guild for administrative overhead and potential revenue loss. The Desk retains discretion to waive or mitigate penalties based on demonstrated hardship or exceptional circumstances, but such relief must be formally requested and approved prior to default occurring.\n\nFor purposes of enforcement, a \"default\" is deemed to exist when fees remain unpaid thirty days after the expiration date specified in any applicable permit or contract. At this juncture, the Desk may initiate collection proceedings without further notice to the delinquent party. Such actions shall be conducted with due process and fairness, affording affected individuals an opportunity to contest charges before any punitive measures are implemented.\n\nThe provisions of this section are designed to maintain fiscal integrity within the Guild's operations while balancing the practical realities faced by licensed casters. By standardizing accrual times and penalties across all regions, the Desk aims to streamline administration and minimize friction between regulators and practitioners alike. It is imperative that all parties familiarize themselves with these requirements promptly upon receiving any official communications regarding fees or compliance obligations. Failure to do so may result in unnecessary complications during audits or inspections later on.\n\nIn sum, § 1301.9 serves as a foundational element of the Guild's financial regulatory scheme, underpinning both routine operations and extraordinary enforcement actions alike. Its careful calibration reflects decades of experience managing complex economic relationships between diverse stakeholders. As such, it demands rigorous adherence by all concerned to preserve the integrity and efficacy of this vital system.\"",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1301.9",
            "1301.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Sunrise Accrual and Default Penalties — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "Under § 1301.9, the Guild may elect to accrue interest on any overdue fees or penalties at the rate specified in the applicable Schedule of Fees. Such interest shall begin accruing automatically upon expiration of the grace period set forth herein and shall continue until full payment is received. The accrued amount shall be added to the principal balance for purposes of calculating further penalties, thereby compounding the financial burden imposed on late payers. This provision reflects the Guild's commitment to maintaining fiscal integrity and ensuring equitable treatment of all members who comply with their obligations in a timely manner.\n\nDefault Penalties — Continued\nIn addition to accruing interest, failure to remit fees within the prescribed timeframe may result in the imposition of additional default penalties as outlined below: (a) A flat fee assessment equal to ten percent (10%) of the outstanding balance shall be levied upon expiration of the grace period; and (b) For each subsequent month or fraction thereof during which payment remains delinquent, an additional penalty of five percent (5%) shall apply. These penalties are designed to incentivize prompt compliance and offset administrative costs associated with tracking overdue accounts. The Guild reserves the right to escalate collection efforts, including legal action where warranted, should a member persistently neglect their financial responsibilities. It is incumbent upon all casters registered under the Accords to adhere strictly to payment deadlines to avoid escalating consequences that could jeopardize their licensure status or standing within the organization at large.\"\n\n\"see § 1301.2 Penalties for detailed breakdown of applicable fines; under § 1301.5 Related Requirements regarding enforcement mechanisms available to the Guild.\"",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1301.9",
            "1301.2",
            "1301.5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "1301.9 Related Requirements, Sunrise Accrual and Default Penalties — Continued —",
          "text": "The default penalties enumerated herein are not intended to be exhaustive nor do they supersede applicable criminal statutes where more stringent sanctions may be warranted under the circumstances. Rather, these provisions establish a baseline framework for administrative enforcement within the Guild's jurisdictional sphere. Nothing in this section shall preclude the Desk from imposing additional civil remedies or equitable relief as deemed necessary to redress violations of the Accords and protect public interest. The accrual of penalties commences at sunrise on the day following any breach, regardless of whether formal notice has been served upon the offending party. This temporal rule exists solely to prevent dilatory tactics that would undermine the efficacy of enforcement mechanisms. Failure to remit outstanding obligations within the prescribed period constitutes a continuing default, thereby triggering cumulative sanctions proportionate to the duration and severity of noncompliance. The Guild reserves discretion to adjust penalty rates upward or downward based on factors including but not limited to the offender's financial status, history of violations, demonstrated remorse, and potential for rehabilitation through corrective measures. All assessments shall be calculated prospectively from the date of first default unless evidence proves otherwise. Parties contesting the validity or amount of levied penalties must petition the Desk within thirty (30) days of receipt thereof, providing substantiation supporting their claim in accordance with § 1301.3 Appeals. Untimely challenges shall be summarily denied without prejudice to subsequent proceedings. The provisions herein apply mutatis mutandis to all forms of monetary liability arising from Accords infractions, whether predicated on contract law principles or strict statutory mandates. Nothing contained herein limits the right of aggrieved individuals or entities to pursue separate legal action against defaulters for damages exceeding those recoverable through administrative channels alone. The Desk shall maintain a comprehensive ledger documenting all defaults, payments made, penalties accrued, and resolutions reached in connection with each case number assigned thereto. Such records are subject to inspection by interested parties pursuant to § 1301.4 Who May Inspect, provided reasonable notice is given and relevant privacy concerns addressed accordingly. The ultimate objective of these rules remains preservation of order through predictable consequences for wrongful conduct while affording fair opportunity for correction where appropriate under the law. Compliance with this section shall be deemed a continuing condition precedent to maintenance of licensure privileges granted hereinby. Any deliberate evasion or obstruction thereof may result in immediate revocation of said privileges along with initiation of further disciplinary measures as warranted by the facts and applicable policy directives issued by the Archmage Sovereign.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1301.3",
            "1301.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1301.9 Related Requirements — Delayed Assessment and Compound Interest",
          "text": "Where fees are assessed under these Accords, the default shall accrue at a rate not to exceed five percent per month or sixty percent annually, whichever is less. This interest compounds monthly and attaches immediately upon breach of any obligation, whether by omission or commission. The Guild reserves discretion to adjust rates periodically based on inflationary trends or administrative costs, provided such changes are publicly posted with thirty days' notice.\n\nNo caster may claim ignorance of the fee schedule as a defense against collection efforts. Publication in this Codex and posting at each Hall constitutes sufficient notice to all bound parties. Attempts to evade payment through shell companies, proxies, or magical concealment will result in double penalties plus confiscation of any illicit gains derived from the prohibited practice.\n\nPayment must be made within ten days of assessment unless otherwise specified. Late submissions incur a flat surcharge equivalent to one month's accrued interest regardless of the underlying debt amount. Failure to settle within fourteen days triggers immediate suspension of all privileges held by the debtor and their associates, subject to restoration upon full remittance plus outstanding charges.\n\nThe Guild may pursue collection through any legal means at its disposal, including liens on property, garnishment of wages, or referral to civil authorities for contempt proceedings. Recalcitrant casters face potential revocation of licensure entirely, barring reapplication for a period not less than one year following full compliance with all outstanding obligations.\n\nNothing herein shall be construed as waiving any rights the Guild may possess under applicable laws or customs. All fees collected are irrevocably assigned to the Guild and may be applied against any past, present, or future debts owed by the same individual or entity. Disputes over calculation methodology must be raised within seven days of receipt of notice; thereafter they are deemed waived unless formally contested through established channels.\n\nThis Section supersedes all prior fee schedules, oral agreements, or informal understandings between parties and the Guild. Ambiguities in interpretation shall always be resolved in favor of clear written terms contained herein, absent evidence to the contrary presented under oath. The integrity of these financial provisions is paramount to maintaining order within the magical community at large.\n\n\"Interest mounts like a tide against those who linger too long in debt; swift resolution ensures all may cast their spells without fear.\" — Archmage Theron's Final Exhortation, Autumnwood Hall, Year 324 of the Accords.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1301.9"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "Sunrise Accrual and Default Penalties",
