    {
      "cite": "1.11",
      "part": "front",
      "title": "Jurisdictional Authority",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Jurisdictional Authority",
          "text": "The provisions contained herein shall be construed in conjunction with the other articles and sections of this Codex, as well as any applicable federal statutes, regulations, treaties, or international agreements that may bear upon the subject matter at hand. Nothing herein shall be deemed to supersede or conflict with such external legal authorities unless expressly stated otherwise within these pages.\n\nFurthermore, it is hereby clarified that all terms and concepts employed throughout this instrument are intended to have their ordinary meanings unless specifically defined elsewhere in this document. In cases of ambiguity or dispute regarding interpretation, recourse shall first be made to the official commentary appended hereto, followed by consultation with the presiding magistrate or their duly appointed delegate. Should such measures fail to resolve the matter satisfactorily, binding arbitration shall commence forthwith before a panel composed of three impartial experts selected jointly by the disputing parties.\n\nIn addition, it is imperative that all signatories thereto carefully review and understand the full scope of their obligations under this agreement prior to affixing their signatures or seals thereto. By doing so, they acknowledge acceptance of both the rights and responsibilities enumerated herein without qualification or reservation. Failure to comply fully with these stipulations may result in immediate breach of contract proceedings being initiated against the offending party by the aggrieved counterpart(s).\n\nFinally, any amendments or modifications sought after execution must be effected through mutual written consent executed by all affected individuals/entities involved therein. Oral agreements or informal understandings shall hold no weight whatsoever vis-à-vis this formal instrument unless subsequently ratified in proper form by relevant authorities charged with enforcement duties pursuant to these provisions.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1.12 Jurisdictional Authority",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords Desk asserts exclusive jurisdiction over all matters pertaining to the regulation, licensure, and enforcement of magical arts within its sovereign domain as defined by the Archmage Sovereign. This authority extends to any individual, entity, or organization operating under a Guild license regardless of their origin or residency status. The Desk further claims inherent power to investigate alleged violations occurring beyond territorial boundaries when such acts impact Guild interests or threaten public safety. No external court, tribunal, or quasi-judicial body shall entertain cases arising from Accords violations without prior consultation with the Desk's Chief Clerk. The Desk retains sole discretion to determine admissibility of evidence and applicability of mitigating circumstances in all disciplinary proceedings. Enforcement actions initiated by the Desk are binding upon all parties subject to its jurisdiction and may be executed through authorized agents without further notice or hearing. Objections to the Desk's authority must be raised within thirty (30) days of service of process or deemed waived. Failure to contest jurisdiction timely shall constitute a waiver thereof and acceptance of the Desk's ruling as final and conclusive. The Desk's determinations regarding its own scope of power are conclusive upon all persons bound by these Accords unless overturned by unanimous vote of the full Council in extraordinary session convened specifically for that purpose. This clause stands as an expression of the Accord's supremacy over all other laws, customs, or usages inconsistent with its provisions.\n\nsee § 1.4 Persons Bound; see § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild; see § 300.1 Schedules of Arts; see § 500.1 Field Casting for Value\"",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1.4",
            "100.2",
            "300.1",
            "500.1",
            "1.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1.12 Jurisdictional Authority and Venue Provisions — Continued",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords Desk exercises plenary jurisdiction over all matters arising under this Code, whether within the territorial bounds of the Hall or beyond. No other body shall assume authority to adjudicate disputes involving magical practice without explicit delegation from the Desk itself, lest it invite chaos upon the lands. This plenary power extends to both civil and criminal proceedings, encompassing investigation, trial, sentencing, and post-judgment enforcement.\n\nVenue for any action brought under this Code lies within the immediate precincts of the Autumn Wood Hall, regardless of where the underlying conduct occurred or where the parties reside. The Desk maintains strict control over scheduling and procedural posture to ensure orderly resolution of all claims. Petitioners seeking redress must file their complaints at the main entrance during regular business hours and await assignment by a clerk. Failure to comply with these minimal requirements may result in dismissal without prejudice, leaving the aggrieved party to pursue alternative remedies at their own peril.\n\nThe jurisdiction of the Accords Desk is exclusive and non-waivable under any circumstances. No court, tribunal, or other authority shall entertain claims pertaining to magical arts except by leave granted in writing by the Archmage Sovereign acting on behalf of the Guild. This exclusivity is paramount to preserving the integrity of the judicial process and preventing conflicting rulings that could undermine the stability of the entire system. Any attempt to circumvent these provisions will be met with swift and severe sanctions, including immediate revocation of all privileges and immunities enjoyed by the violator.\n\nIt shall be lawful for the Desk to convene special sessions outside normal operating hours or locations when deemed necessary for the efficient administration of justice. Such emergency gatherings may be called at the discretion of the Archmage Sovereign upon presentation of compelling cause by counsel or interested parties. Minutes of these extraordinary meetings shall constitute prima facie evidence of all actions taken and remain binding on all concerned until superseded by subsequent orders from higher authorities within the Guild hierarchy.\n\nThis comprehensive grant of jurisdiction serves to consolidate power in a single, accountable entity capable of adapting swiftly to evolving threats posed by rogue casters and their ilk. By centralizing authority in this manner, the Accords ensure consistent application of the law across time and space, thereby safeguarding both public safety and private rights alike. Let none presume to challenge this mandate without facing the full weight of the Guild's wrath. The Desk shall stand unchallenged as the ultimate arbiter of all magical affairs within our realm.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1.12 Jurisdictional Authority and Venue Provisions — Administration",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords Desk exercises plenary jurisdiction over all matters arising under the Accords, regardless of where such matters originate or where their effects are felt. This broad authority is necessary to ensure uniform enforcement across the diverse regions served by the Guild's network of Halls and stations. No other body shall preside over disputes between mages licensed under this Code; any attempt to seize such jurisdiction is void ab initio and subject to immediate revocation of offending licenses.\n\nVenue for proceedings brought pursuant to these provisions lies within the Autumnwood itself, at such time and place as the Desk may designate in its sole discretion. This centralized approach facilitates consistent application of the law while minimizing disruption to daily operations across multiple jurisdictions. The Desk may convene special sessions when required by emergency circumstances or expedient necessity; notice thereof shall be provided via standard channels at least seven days prior, unless waived by mutual agreement of the parties concerned.\n\nParties aggrieved by any ruling rendered under this Code have a right to appeal within fourteen days to an expanded panel comprising three additional magisters selected at random from the full roster of active practitioners. The expanded panel shall reconsider de novo all issues presented and issue its own decision, which shall be final unless overturned on direct review by the Desk itself upon application for extraordinary relief. Applications for such review are granted only in rare cases involving fundamental errors of law or fact that would substantially undermine public confidence in the administration of justice under these Accords.\n\nThe Desk retains inherent authority to prescribe rules and procedures governing all aspects of proceedings brought hereunder, including but not limited to discovery protocols, evidentiary standards, default judgments, summary disposition motions, and post-judgment enforcement mechanisms. Such procedural regulations shall be promulgated through formal rulemaking processes ensuring adequate public notice and opportunity for comment prior to adoption. Failure to comply with prescribed procedures may result in dismissal of claims or defenses at any stage, without prejudice to resubmission upon proper re-filing where applicable.\n\nNothing contained herein shall be construed to limit the authority of local magistrates and law enforcement officers acting under appropriate warrants issued by duly constituted courts having cognizance over criminal matters arising from magical activity within their respective territories. Coordination between the Desk and municipal authorities is encouraged where feasible to promote efficient resolution of overlapping concerns while respecting distinct spheres of responsibility delineated herein and elsewhere in applicable statutes.\n\nThe foregoing provisions shall remain in full force and effect until expressly amended or repealed by action of the Autumnwood Accords Desk following notice and public hearing as required under § 100 et seq. Any ambiguities regarding scope or application hereof shall be resolved liberally to advance the purposes and policies embodied throughout this comprehensive regulatory framework designed to govern magical practice responsibly and effectively within our society.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1.12 Jurisdictional Authority and Venue Provisions — Oversight",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords shall have full force and effect within the sovereign boundaries of the Midlands, as delineated in the Official Cartographic Survey approved by the Sovereign Council on this date. This jurisdiction extends to all persons, magical constructs, and entities operating within said territory, regardless of origin or citizenship status. However, no provision herein shall bind those expressly exempted by prior Royal Charter or international treaty obligations binding upon the Crown. In matters involving cross-border disputes or extraterritorial conduct with sufficient nexus to the Midlands, concurrent jurisdiction may be invoked under § 205 \"Concurrent Jurisdiction and Choice of Law.\" Venue for any proceeding arising under these Accords shall lie in the nearest District Court having territorial competence over the locus delicti. Absent specific agreement otherwise by all parties, motions to change venue shall only be granted upon a showing of grave inconvenience or prejudice unremediable by other means. The Sovereign retains ultimate authority to assign cases directly to specialized tribunals when circumstances warrant expedited resolution or heightened security measures. Nothing in this Section precludes the application of customary international law principles regarding territorial sovereignty and flag-state rights where relevant to the substantive issues presented.\"\n\n\"§ 1.12 Jurisdictional Authority and Venue Provisions: The Autumnwood Accords shall have full force and effect within the sovereign boundaries of the Midlands, as delineated in the Official Cartographic Survey approved by the Sovereign Council on this date. This jurisdiction extends to all persons, magical constructs, and entities operating within said territory, regardless of origin or citizenship status. However, no provision herein shall bind those expressly exempted by prior Royal Charter or international treaty obligations binding upon the Crown. In matters involving cross-border disputes or extraterritorial conduct with sufficient nexus to the Midlands, concurrent jurisdiction may be invoked under § 205 'Concurrent Jurisdiction and Choice of Law.' Venue for any proceeding arising under these Accords shall lie in the nearest District Court having territorial competence over the locus delicti. Absent specific agreement otherwise by all parties, motions to change venue shall only be granted upon a showing of grave inconvenience or prejudice unremediable by other means. The Sovereign retains ultimate authority to assign cases directly to specialized tribunals when circumstances warrant expedited resolution or heightened security measures. Nothing in this Section precludes the application of customary international law principles regarding territorial sovereignty and flag-state rights where relevant to the substantive issues presented.\"",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1.12 Jurisdictional Authority and Venue Determination",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords establish exclusive jurisdiction over all disputes arising from the practice, regulation, or enforcement thereof within the bounds of the Hall's domain and any territories under its de facto control. This principle, known as \"Arcane Primacy,\" supersedes conflicting claims by other bodies unless explicitly modified by mutual treaty. See § 1.5 Relation to Other Law; § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse.\n\nVenue for all proceedings shall be fixed at the Autumnwood Hall or such alternative location designated by a majority vote of the Accords Desk, taking into account factors including convenience to parties, security requirements, and potential influence on witnesses or evidence. The presiding officer possesses discretionary power to alter venue mid-trial upon sufficient cause being shown. Under § 1201.9 Waiver and Modification; see also § 700.6 Competent Witnesses and Expert Testimony.\n\nNo court outside the Autumnwood jurisdiction shall entertain any action directly challenging the validity or enforcement of Accords provisions, absent leave granted by the Desk. Violations of this prohibition constitute contempt punishable under § 1301.8 Penalties and Enforcement; sanctions may include sealing of magical abilities, monetary fines, or imprisonment at discretion of the presiding judge. Refer to § 200.20 Contempt Powers for additional details on remedial measures available to the bench in egregious cases.\n\nIn matters involving cross-border elements or multi-jurisdictional complexity, the Accords Desk may appoint a special master with full authority to investigate facts and make binding recommendations regarding appropriate venue allocation and applicable law. Such masters serve at pleasure of the Desk and enjoy all powers necessary to fulfill their assigned duties effectively. See § 900.5 Special Masters and Their Powers for further elaboration on this procedural mechanism designed to ensure fair resolution of intricate disputes.\n\nThe foundational doctrine of \"One Hall, One Law\" remains paramount in preserving the integrity of the Accords system. Attempts to circumvent established jurisdictional rules through forum shopping or parallel litigation shall be summarily dismissed and may result in additional penalties imposed upon offending parties for wasting scarce judicial resources. This stance aligns with broader principles articulated in § 100.7 Foreign Halls and Courtesy regarding proper channels for inter-organizational communication and dispute resolution.\n\nUltimately, the determination of which body holds authority to adjudicate any given matter rests solely within the discretion of the Accords Desk, guided by criteria including nexus between parties and forum, complexity of issues presented, and potential impact on wider magical communities. Such determinations are subject only to appeal via established review procedures outlined in subsequent articles of this Codex. For comprehensive guidance on navigating these critical jurisdictional questions, consult §§ 1301.7 Motion Practice and § 800.5 Procedural Economy provisions addressing efficient case management practices employed by modern tribunals alike.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1.5",
            "200.4",
            "1201.9",
            "700.6",
            "1301.8",
            "200.20",
            "900.5",
            "100.7",
            "1301.7",
            "800.5",
            "1.12"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "Jurisdictional Authority",
      "source": "lmstudio",
