    {
      "cite": "400.11",
      "part": "part_iv",
      "title": "Research Permits and Supervised Experiments; Unauthorized Field Casting",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.11 Research Permits and Supervised Experiments; Unauthorized Field Casting",
          "text": "§ 400.12 Related Requirements; Specimen Custody Protocols and Chain of Evidence Procedures; Unauthorized Titan Growth Penalties and Remedies; Field Casting Compensation Schedules and Dispute Resolution Mechanisms; Unscheduled Weather Event Notification and Mitigation Guidelines; Corridor Courtesy Standards Post-Explosion Cleanup and Decontamination Duties; Healing Services Quotas and Priority Allocation Under Emergency Conditions; Love Philtre Manufacturing Licenses and Usage Restrictions; Undue Influence Determinations in Consent Cases Involving Magical Substances; Contractual Obligations Imposed on Non-Casters Through Proxy Agreements\n\nUnder § 400.12, all research permits issued pursuant to this Part shall include explicit conditions regarding specimen custody protocols, chain of evidence maintenance requirements, and penalties for unauthorized growth or modification. Any field casting conducted for value without a valid permit shall be subject to immediate revocation and financial restitution as outlined in the applicable compensation schedule. Unscheduled weather events resulting from magical activity must be reported within twenty-four hours via standard channels for proper mitigation measures. Following any explosion or significant magical incident, all parties involved must adhere strictly to corridor courtesy standards during cleanup and decontamination operations. Healing services rendered in exchange for payment shall not constitute a binding contract unless explicitly stated in writing with full disclosure of risks and limitations. Love philtre manufacturing requires separate licensing beyond standard research permits, and usage restrictions apply regardless of intended purpose. Determinations of undue influence in consent cases involving magical substances shall be made on a case-by-case basis considering all relevant factors including power dynamics and prior conduct. Contracts imposing obligations on non-casters through proxy agreements are void unless they meet specific statutory criteria and receive independent legal counsel review before execution. See also § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; § 200.6 Constructs That Hold a Quill; § 300.4 Reclassification Procedures; § 900.7 Related Requirements; § 500.8 Field Casting Ethics and Oversight.\"",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "400.12",
            "100.5",
            "200.6",
            "300.4",
            "900.7",
            "500.8",
            "400.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.12 Unauthorized Field Casting and Specimen Contamination",
          "text": "No research permit issued under § 400.1 shall authorize the casting of spells outside approved facilities unless explicitly stated in the grantee's license, which may be granted only for exceptional circumstances deemed necessary by a majority vote of the Conservators. Any unauthorized field casting constitutes gross misconduct punishable by immediate revocation of licensure and permanent disqualification from Guild service, pursuant to § 100.6(b). Furthermore, all specimens collected during research must remain in secure containment at all times; failure to maintain proper custody resulting in loss or contamination of evidence shall be treated as willful destruction of property under common law principles and may result in criminal charges against the responsible caster and their employer. Research permits are non-transferable and strictly personal to the named researcher, who bears sole responsibility for maintaining compliance with all stipulated conditions throughout the duration of the project. Violation of any term herein shall render void not only the specific permit but also any associated contracts or agreements entered into in reliance thereon. The Guild reserves the right to audit facilities at any time without notice and to seize suspected contraband materials subject to legal proceedings thereafter. Grantees agree to indemnify and hold harmless the Autumnwood Accords Desk from any claims arising out of negligent research practices or failure to adhere to safety protocols outlined in their license. This provision applies equally to individual practitioners operating outside formal employment relationships, who shall be held personally liable for all violations committed within their sphere of influence regardless of corporate affiliation status at time of infraction. Any disputes regarding interpretation of permit terms shall be resolved exclusively through binding arbitration administered by the Aegis Magi under rules mutually agreed upon prior to commencement of work; failure to arbitrate promptly may result in suspension of funding until resolution achieved. The integrity and sanctity of research environments must never be compromised, for carelessness here risks not only scientific progress but also public safety itself. All casters are reminded that their actions bear consequences far beyond mere academic inquiry, and they accept full responsibility for upholding the highest standards of ethical conduct in pursuit of magical knowledge. See § 100.6(b) regarding disciplinary measures; § 400.5 concerning specimen integrity obligations; and general principles laid forth in Part I relating to fiduciary duties owed by professionals to their clients and communities alike.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "400.1",
            "100.6",
            "400.5",
            "400.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.13 Unauthorized Field Casting and Specimen Contamination",
          "text": "§ 400.13 Unauthorized Field Casting and Specimen Contamination\n\nNo caster shall engage in field casting outside the confines of an authorized laboratory or research facility without prior written permission from the Conservators' Oversight Committee. Such unauthorized activity is strictly prohibited under § 200.1(a)(iv) and constitutes a Class A violation subject to immediate revocation of licensure pursuant to § 400.5(c).\n\nAny specimens brought into contact with unauthorized magical effects shall be deemed contaminated for research purposes. Contaminated materials must be immediately segregated from the main collection and disposed of in accordance with hazardous waste protocols outlined under § 300.8(b)(ii). Failure to comply may result in additional fines and potential imprisonment up to five years per § 400.5(d).\n\nThe Guild reserves the right to inspect any premises suspected of unauthorized magical experimentation without warrant under Article IX, Section 2 of the Autumnwood Accords. Inspectors shall be granted full access to records, equipment, and personnel involved in such activities for a period not exceeding fourteen days unless extended by majority vote of the Oversight Committee.\n\nViolations of § 400.13 may also trigger civil liability for damages caused to third parties through negligent or reckless magical practices outside controlled environments. Plaintiffs need only prove causation between the unauthorized casting and resulting harm, placing the burden of proof on the accused caster to demonstrate due diligence in containing effects.\n\nThe Conservators maintain a list of approved field sites where limited experimental work may be conducted under strict supervision by licensed researchers. These locations undergo regular safety audits to ensure compliance with all applicable regulations regarding containment, shielding, and emergency response procedures as detailed in Appendix C of these Accords.\n\nUnauthorized casting in public spaces or near residential areas is particularly egregious and subject to enhanced penalties including permanent revocation of licensure and lifetime ban from the Guild's jurisdiction. Such actions threaten both public safety and the integrity of magical research as a whole.\n\nIt is the responsibility of every licensed caster to familiarize themselves fully with these provisions before commencing any experimental work outside established facilities. The consequences for noncompliance are severe and may have lasting impacts on one's career within the arcane community at large.\n\nThis section shall be read in conjunction with §§ 200.1, 300.8(b)(ii), 400.5(c)-(d), and Articles IX-Section 2 of the Autumnwood Accords governing inspection rights and civil liability standards. Any ambiguities shall be resolved in favor of public safety and containment of magical effects wherever possible.\n\nThe undersigned hereby acknowledge receipt and understanding of § 400.13 as enacted by the Mages' Guild General Assembly on this day, year 2987, during their forty-second annual session held within the sacred halls of Autumn Wood.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "400.13",
            "200.1",
            "400.5",
            "300.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.6 Research Permits and Supervised Experiments",
          "text": "§ 400.7 Unauthorized Field Casting, Specimen Contamination, and Ecological Harm\n\nNo researcher shall engage in field casting outside the bounds of their licensed premises without explicit consent from the local Conservator's Office. Violations constitute a Class C infraction punishable by immediate suspension of all privileges. Furthermore, researchers must maintain meticulous logs of any specimens collected during experiments, noting species designation, quantity harvested, and method of acquisition. Failure to comply with these record-keeping requirements shall be deemed gross negligence and subject to severe penalties including permanent revocation of licensure. The Guild reserves the right to audit such records at its sole discretion upon reasonable notice. Researchers found guilty of knowingly contaminating local ecosystems through reckless experimentation may face criminal charges under applicable environmental statutes in addition to Guild sanctions. It is incumbent upon every caster to exercise due diligence in minimizing their environmental footprint, recognizing that unchecked magical activity poses an existential threat to the delicate balance of nature. The Archmages stand ready to intervene decisively should any individual prove unwilling to abide by these fundamental tenets of responsible practice.\n\nFILED CITE INDEX (use these exact cites, e.g. 'see § 1.6'): § 400.1 Research Permits; § 400.2 Pocket Dimensions as Labs; § 400.3 Borrowed Hours: Interest in Time; § 400.4 Specimen Custody; § 400.5 Unauthorized Titan Growth; § 400.6 Related Requirements; § 100.4 Records of Speech; § 200.2 Apprentice Limits; § 300.4 Reclassification; see also § 1.7 Construction: Aggregation of Conduct; under § 1.9 Seals, Stamps, and What Is Not a Seal; pursuant to § 1.5 Relation to Other Law; cf. § 1.8 Effective Date; Savings.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "400.7",
            "1.6",
            "400.1",
            "400.2",
            "400.3",
            "400.4",
            "400.5",
            "400.6",
            "100.4",
            "200.2",
            "300.4",
            "1.7",
            "1.9",
