            "1.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 400.6 Unauthorized Field Casting and Specimen Contamination",
          "text": "§ 400.6 No caster shall engage in unscheduled field operations within the Guild's jurisdiction without prior authorization from the Archmage Sovereign or her delegate. Violation of this provision constitutes a Class A felony under the Accords, subject to immediate arrest and trial by Paradox Trial (§ 100.5). Furthermore, any unauthorized magical activity that results in contamination or degradation of specimens held in safekeeping shall be treated as gross negligence warranting disbarment without recourse. See § 200.9 for penalties applicable to unlicensed practitioners.\n\nThe prohibition against unscheduled field casting arises from the inherent unpredictability and potential hazards associated with such operations outside controlled environments. The Guild's primary mandate is the preservation of magical knowledge and public safety, both of which are compromised when mages engage in risky experiments without proper oversight. As stated in § 300.2, \"the study of magic demands rigorous discipline and meticulous recordkeeping,\" principles that cannot be adequately maintained during impromptu fieldwork.\n\nSpecimen contamination poses an additional threat to the integrity of the Guild's research efforts. Specimens are invaluable resources for advancing magical understanding, and their loss or degradation due to careless handling undermines years of painstaking collection and preservation work. Under § 400.5, all casters must exercise extreme caution when working near specimen storage areas, ensuring that no stray spells or effects interfere with the delicate balance maintained by the Conservators.\n\nIn cases where emergency field casting becomes absolutely necessary—for instance, to neutralize an imminent threat—the caster bears sole responsibility for obtaining retroactive approval from senior magi within twenty-four hours of the incident's resolution. Failure to comply with this reporting requirement will result in automatic suspension of licensure pending investigation into the circumstances surrounding the unauthorized operation. See § 600.1 regarding contractual obligations between casters and clients, which must not supersede public safety concerns outlined herein.\n\nThe penalties for violating § 400.6 are severe and designed to deter reckless behavior by all practitioners operating under Guild protection. Disbarment serves as the ultimate sanction, effectively ending a caster's career in accordance with § 300.8 (\"the privilege of casting is earned, not given freely\"). Lesser offenses may incur monetary fines or temporary suspension proportional to the gravity of the infraction and any resulting harm caused. Ultimately, adherence to these provisions ensures that magic remains a force for good rather than chaos unchecked by reason.\n\nThis section supplements existing regulations governing professional conduct and public safety without duplicating material already codified elsewhere in the Accords. By clarifying the scope of permissible field activities, § 400.6 strikes an appropriate balance between facilitating legitimate research endeavors and protecting against abuse of powers entrusted to those licensed by the Guild's authority.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "400.6",
            "100.5",
            "200.9",
            "300.2",
            "400.5",
            "600.1",
            "300.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "400.6 Research Permits and Supervised Experiments; Unauthorized Field Casting",
          "text": "§ 400.13 Related Requirements — Conducting Experiments Outside the Guild\n\nA research permit issued under § 200.9 shall not authorize a caster to conduct experiments beyond the limits prescribed therein, nor does it relieve the holder of any obligations imposed by law or custom. Any attempt to exceed these boundaries renders the experiment void and subject to immediate revocation of the permit. The Guild retains sole discretion over where, when, and how research may be performed, with no exceptions for emergency situations unless expressly stated in the original grant. Unauthorized experiments constitute a serious breach of trust and may result in permanent disqualification from future licensure.\n\nFurthermore, all experiments must be conducted under direct supervision by a licensed supervisor appointed by the Guild. This individual shall verify that safety protocols are followed at all times and intervene immediately if any irregularities arise. Failure to comply with these oversight measures will nullify the validity of the experiment's results and may lead to disciplinary action against both the principal investigator and their supervisor. The Guild reserves the right to audit research facilities, review logs, and interview personnel as part of its quality assurance process. Any resistance to such audits shall be deemed a violation of the Accords.\n\nIn addition, casters are reminded that unauthorized field casting remains strictly prohibited outside of approved settings. This prohibition extends to all forms of experimental magic, whether performed for personal gain or curiosity. Violations will be prosecuted under applicable statutes and may result in criminal charges beyond mere civil penalties. The Guild takes such matters extremely seriously, as they pose significant risks to public safety and the integrity of magical practice. All casters are urged to adhere scrupulously to these guidelines at all times.\n\nFinally, this section serves notice that no private arrangements or side deals shall circumvent the terms set forth herein. Any attempt to do so will be treated as a deliberate act of sabotage against the Guild's interests and may warrant severe consequences under existing law. The Accords stand firm on this point: there are no exceptions for those who choose to ignore them. All parties concerned are expected to abide by these rules without deviation, now and forevermore. Only then can we ensure that magic continues to flourish safely within our borders.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "400.13",
            "200.9"
          ]
        }
      ],
