    {
      "cite": "800.11",
      "part": "part_viii",
      "title": "Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation",
          "text": "§ 800.11 Additional Provisions Regarding Penalties for Unauthorized Arcane Activity\nIn furtherance of the objectives set forth in this Part, the following supplementary provisions shall apply to all matters falling within its purview:\n\nFirst, it is hereby declared that any act of unauthorized casting of spells or manipulation of magical forces constitutes a violation of these Accords and subjects the perpetrator to immediate disciplinary action. Such violations may include but are not limited to reckless endangerment of persons and property, breach of confidentiality obligations, and failure to comply with licensing requirements. The severity of the penalty shall be determined by the gravity of the offense and the circumstances surrounding its commission, as adjudicated by a panel of peer mages convened pursuant to these Accords.\n\nSecond, all items found in possession of an individual engaged in unlawful magical activity shall be subject to confiscation and seizure by duly authorized agents of the Guild. Such items may include but are not limited to magical artifacts, tools, equipment, and materials used in furtherance of the illegal act. The confiscated property shall be held in safekeeping pending resolution of any subsequent proceedings arising from the violation. Disposition of such items shall be made only upon order of a competent tribunal or by direction of the Guild's governing body.\n\nThird, penalties for unlawful casting may include but are not limited to monetary fines, suspension or revocation of licensure, imposition of professional restrictions, and referral to appropriate law enforcement authorities where criminal conduct is implicated. In egregious cases involving serious harm or threats to public safety, more severe sanctions such as sealing of magical abilities or expulsion from the Guild community may be warranted at the discretion of the disciplinary panel. All penalties shall be imposed with a view toward maintaining order in the arcane community while affording due process protections to accused individuals.\n\nFinally, these provisions shall apply retroactively to all acts committed prior to their enactment where such application does not contravene fundamental principles of fairness and justice. This ensures that no one may benefit from engaging in unlawful magical practices under a false pretense of ignorance regarding the legal consequences thereof. The full weight of these sanctions shall be borne by those who choose to disregard the authority and wisdom embodied in the Autumnwood Accords, lest they find themselves subject to the full force of Guild discipline upon discovery of their transgressions.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "800.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation — Continued",
          "text": "Under § 800.9, any mage found guilty of unlawful casting faces immediate confiscation of all magical artifacts and implements used in the violation. These items shall be sealed with a permanent arcane lock to prevent future misuse. The confiscated goods become property of the Autumnwood Accords and may only be returned upon proof of full restitution and rehabilitation. § 800.10 governs the process for determining whether an individual qualifies as \"rehabilitated,\" requiring peer review by a panel of senior mages versed in both law and arcane theory. Until such determination is made, the offender remains barred from accessing any magical materials or facilities under penalty of immediate re-sentencing. Furthermore, § 800.11 mandates that all confiscated items be inventoried, catalogued, and stored securely within a dedicated vault beneath the main Accords Hall. Access to this repository requires dual authorization from both an Aegis Magi officer and a Conservator representative, ensuring proper oversight and accountability for these potentially dangerous artifacts. Any unauthorized removal or tampering with the stored goods shall constitute a major felony under § 400.12, punishable by permanent seal of magic and exile from civilized society at large. This rigorous control regime serves to minimize risks posed by illicit magical implements while also preventing their potential abuse by rival factions seeking to destabilize the delicate balance between innovation and stability that defines our age. Through these measures, we safeguard both ourselves and future generations against the perils inherent in unchecked arcane experimentation.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "800.9",
            "800.10",
            "800.11",
            "400.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.11 Penalties for Unlawful Casting and Use of Arcane Artifacts — Continued",
          "text": "Any individual convicted under these Accords of unlawfully casting spells or utilizing forbidden artifacts shall face immediate sanctions, as outlined herein. Upon finding a caster guilty of violation, the adjudicating panel may impose one or more of the following penalties at its discretion: suspension of licensure for a period not exceeding two years; revocation of all previously granted permits and certifications; mandatory attendance at remedial courses on responsible magical practice and ethics; payment of restitution to any parties harmed by the unlawful casting; forfeiture of any illegal gains derived from such activities.\n\nIn cases where an offender's actions have caused severe injury or death, the penalties shall be enhanced accordingly. The court may order additional fines ranging up to ten thousand gold pieces per count of culpability, alongside community service obligations calculated based on the extent of damages incurred. Repeat offenders found guilty of similar infractions will face increasingly stringent punishments, potentially including permanent disbarment from practicing magic within Accord territories.\n\nFurthermore, any individual determined to have knowingly aided or abetted unlawful spellcasting may be held jointly liable for resulting consequences. This includes those who provided materials, shelter, financial backing, or other forms of assistance without proper authorization. Such accomplices shall face penalties proportional to their level of involvement and the gravity of the offense committed under their complicity.\n\nThe Archmage Sovereign retains broad authority to modify these penalty guidelines as circumstances warrant. Any such changes must be publicly announced and afforded reasonable notice prior to implementation, ensuring affected parties may adjust their conduct accordingly. It is incumbent upon all mages operating within this jurisdiction to familiarize themselves with current provisions governing disciplinary measures, thereby avoiding inadvertent noncompliance.\n\nThese stipulations stand in addition to any other liabilities or obligations imposed by applicable laws, regulations, and contractual agreements. Nothing herein shall be construed as limiting the remedies available at law or equity for breaches of these Accords or related statutes. Offenders are advised that failure to comply with prescribed sanctions may result in further adverse action, including but not limited to revocation of citizenship status and extradition proceedings should necessary.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "800.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.11 Penalties for Unlawful Casting and Use of Arcane Artifacts — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "Under § 800.11, the Aegis Magi are vested with broad discretion to impose sanctions proportional to the gravity of an offense. Minor infractions may warrant a reprimand or mandatory remedial training, whereas egregious violations can result in indefinite suspension from practice. In extreme cases, particularly where public safety has been compromised, permanent revocation of licensure is deemed necessary for the protection of society at large.\n\nThe Desk shall maintain a comprehensive registry of all disciplinary actions taken against individual mages, including the nature of the infraction and the measures imposed. This record serves both as a deterrent to future misconduct and as a guide for assessing an applicant's fitness for admission or re-admission into the Guild fold. Access to this database is restricted to authorized personnel only, in accordance with privacy provisions set forth elsewhere herein.\n\nFurthermore, § 800.11 empowers the Aegis Magi to seize and confiscate any illicit magical items discovered on persons found guilty of unauthorized spellcasting. Such artifacts shall be held in trust until such time as their disposition can be determined by competent authority. In no event shall contraband be returned without written consent from all affected parties, nor shall it be transferred to third parties outside the chain of custody.\n\nIt is hereby declared that these disciplinary provisions are designed solely to uphold the integrity and safety of the magical profession, not as a means for personal vendettas or political leverage. Any attempt to abuse this authority for improper ends will itself constitute grounds for immediate removal from office and potential criminal prosecution under applicable statutes. The Desk pledges its unwavering commitment to fair and impartial adjudication in all matters brought before it pursuant to these rules.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "800.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.11 Penalties for Unlawful Casting and Use of Arcane Artifacts — Continued — Administration",
          "text": "Where unlawful casting is proven beyond reasonable doubt, sanctions shall be applied commensurate with the gravity of the infraction and the intent demonstrated by the accused. Minor breaches involving personal study or accidental release may warrant a formal reprimand coupled with mandatory remedial education under supervised conditions. More egregious violations, including deliberate disruption of magical infrastructure or endangerment of civilian populations, shall result in immediate suspension of casting privileges pending full investigation into mitigating circumstances and potential restitution obligations.\n\nIn cases where the use of illicit artifacts is established, those items shall be seized and held for evaluation by qualified appraisers to determine their provenance, destructive capacity, and value as evidence. Where feasible, such contraband may be repurposed for sanctioned research or destroyed outright to prevent further misuse. In no instance shall confiscated materials be returned to the original owner without written consent from both the Accords Desk and any affected regulatory bodies. Failure to comply with disposal directives constitutes a separate offense subject to additional penalties upon conviction.\n\nSpecial provision is made for repeat offenders whose actions demonstrate persistent disregard for established norms despite prior warnings or disciplinary measures. Such individuals may face enhanced sanctions including permanent revocation of licensure, mandatory exile from the jurisdiction, and potential incarceration at Archmage discretion. Where applicable, civil suits filed by harmed parties shall proceed independently alongside criminal proceedings to seek appropriate damages and injunctive relief as warranted by the circumstances.\n\nThe burden of proof in all disciplinary matters rests squarely upon the accusers who must establish guilt beyond a reasonable doubt through credible testimony or irrefutable material evidence. Defense counsel shall be afforded ample opportunity to challenge witness credibility, cross-examine experts, and present exculpatory arguments on behalf of their clients. Due process guarantees remain inviolate even in the face of urgent threats posed by dangerous magical activities threatening public safety and order.\n\nUltimately, penalties imposed under this section serve both punitive and corrective functions aimed at restoring balance within the arcane community while protecting broader society from potential harms arising from unchecked experimentation or malfeasance. Continuous assessment of enforcement practices ensures that disciplinary actions remain fair, proportionate, and aligned with evolving understandings of magical ethics as codified herein.\n\nsee § 800.1 Discipline; see § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse; see § 900.11 Duty to File Before Casting; see § 700.6 Competent Witnesses and Expert Testimony. Under this provision, sanctions range from formal reprimands for minor infractions up to permanent revocation of privileges for egregious violations. Confiscated items are evaluated by qualified appraisers before disposal or repurposing. Repeat offenders face enhanced penalties including exile or incarceration at Archmage discretion. Due process safeguards remain intact throughout all disciplinary proceedings ensuring fairness and justice. Penalties aim to restore balance within the community while protecting public safety from potential magical harms. Enforcement practices undergo continuous assessment to maintain alignment with evolving ethical standards codified in these accords.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "800.1",
            "200.4",
            "900.11",
            "700.6",
            "800.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.11 Penalties for Unlawful Casting and Use of Arcane Artifacts — Continued ",
          "text": "The enforcement provisions herein establish the procedural framework governing disciplinary actions taken against mages who violate the Accords through unauthorized casting or improper handling of magical artifacts. All investigations initiated by the Aegis Magi must be conducted in strict accordance with these guidelines to ensure due process and prevent abuse of power.\n\nUnder § 800.12, any mage accused of unlawful activity shall receive written notice detailing the specific allegations and evidence supporting them. This document will include a copy of relevant statutes and a list of witnesses to be called at trial. The accused mage has seven days from receipt of such notice to respond in writing or request an immediate hearing before the Paradox Tribunal. Failure to respond within this timeframe shall be deemed a voluntary waiver of all rights and may result in default judgment against the accused party.\n\nFor those who contest the charges, § 800.13 outlines the formal procedures for presenting their defense at trial. The accused mage may present testimony, call witnesses, and introduce physical evidence as deemed relevant by the presiding judges. All proceedings shall be recorded verbatim and made available to all parties upon request. Cross-examination of opposing witnesses is permitted but must remain within the bounds of civil discourse established under § 800.14.\n\nUpon conclusion of the hearing, a majority vote among the panel will determine guilt or innocence based on the preponderance of evidence standard set forth in § 700.9. If found guilty, appropriate penalties shall be imposed pursuant to the sentencing guidelines contained herein and referenced sections thereto. Appeals against final judgments may be filed within thirty days according to provisions outlined in § 800.15.\n\nThe administrative apparatus supporting these disciplinary measures includes a dedicated staff of investigators, analysts, and clerks tasked with maintaining accurate records throughout each case's lifecycle. These personnel operate under the direct supervision of senior Aegis Magi who report directly to Archmage Veyra or her designee. Detailed job descriptions for all positions are available upon request from the Guild Archives Office.\n\nFinally, § 800.16 mandates regular auditing and oversight of the entire enforcement system to ensure compliance with established protocols. Independent reviews conducted annually assess the efficacy and fairness of disciplinary actions while identifying areas needing improvement. Results of these audits are published publicly unless classified for security reasons under separate guidelines approved by the Sovereign Council.\"\n\nsee § 800.12 Notice Requirements; see § 800.13 Trial Procedures; see § 700.9 Burden and Standard of Proof in Arcane Disputes\"",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "800.12",
            "800.13",
            "800.14",
            "700.9",
            "800.15",
            "800.16",
            "800.11"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "NEW section §800.11 in this same Part only. Invent a DISTINCT catchline that belongs with these siblings, not a new subject and NOT 'Related Requirements': § 800.1 Discipline; Range of Sanctions; § 800.2 Paradox Trial Procedure; § 800.3 Seal of Silence; Duration and Review; § 800.4 Duel Stakes Converted to Fees; § 800.5 Pocket-Prison Procedure; § 800.6 Ancillary Obligations; § 800.7 PART 800 - DISCIPLINARY MEASURES § 800.7 Related Requirements; § 1301.2 Penaltie; § 800.8 800.9 Penalties for Unlawful Casting and Use of Arcane Artifacts; § 800.9 Ex Post Facto Prohibition and Retroactive Sanctions; § 800.10 Disposition of Confiscated Items. First line must be: PAGE Your New Distinct Catchline (5-10 words, specific, no 'Related Requirements')",
