    {
      "cite": "1401.11",
      "part": "part_xiv",
      "title": "Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 1401.11 Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements",
          "text": "This section contains various ancillary rules designed to complete the legal framework established by the foregoing Articles. Subsection A clarifies that all references to \"Archmage Sovereign,\" \"Desk,\" \"Clerk,\" or other official titles refer to their incumbents at any given time, regardless of subsequent changes in personnel. Subsection B provides that nothing herein shall be construed as creating new rights beyond those explicitly granted by the Accords themselves. Any ambiguities must be resolved strictly in accordance with Articles 1 and 2 governing construction principles.\n\nSubsection C establishes a savings clause protecting existing contracts signed prior to these amendments from retroactive invalidation, provided they do not violate core prohibitions outlined herein. However, any new agreements executed after enactment shall comply fully with all provisions set forth. Subsection D mandates that all official records maintained by the Desk remain confidential except as otherwise authorized by law or court order. Unauthorized disclosure of trade secrets, research data, or personal information may result in severe penalties under applicable statutes.\n\nSubsection E outlines procedures for appealing adverse rulings made by the Paradox Trial Board, including time limits and required documentation. Appeals must be filed within thirty days of notification and submitted directly to Archmage Veyra for initial review. Subsection F authorizes the Desk to issue temporary emergency orders when necessary to prevent imminent harm to public safety or magical equilibrium, subject to later ratification by full vote. Failure to comply with such directives may result in immediate sanctions without prior warning.\n\nSubsection G confirms that all fees, levies, and assessments imposed by this Code are payable solely in Guild Marks as defined by the Desk from time to time. No other currency or medium of exchange shall be accepted for official transactions. Subsection H provides that any disputes arising from interpretation of these provisions shall be settled exclusively through binding arbitration administered by a panel appointed jointly by both factions, with final decision resting ultimately with Archmage Veyra acting as sole arbiter should the panel fail to reach consensus within sixty days.\n\nSubsection I declares that nothing herein shall diminish or impair the inherent powers vested in the Crown or other duly constituted authorities outside the scope of Guild jurisdiction. Conversely, no external agency shall interfere with internal Guild affairs absent compelling cause demonstrated under oath before a competent tribunal. Subsection J mandates annual audits by independent observers selected through random lottery from among licensed mages not currently serving on any governing body, ensuring transparency and accountability in all operations conducted pursuant to these regulations.\n\nSubsection K stipulates that failure to adhere fully to any provision of this Code may subject violators to civil penalties ranging from monetary fines up to one thousand Guild Marks per offense, revocation of licenses or permits held by the offending party(ies), and disqualification from participating in future voting processes until full restitution is made. Criminal charges may also be pursued where applicable under existing law. Subsection L affirms that these rules shall remain in force indefinitely unless explicitly repealed or superseded by subsequent legislation passed through proper channels with two-thirds majority approval from each faction represented at the Desk, subject to ratification by Archmage Veyra as final authority on all matters pertaining directly to her office and duties under the Accords.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1401.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1401.11 Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements — Continued",
          "text": "This Part contains the supplementary provisions governing the operation, administration, and enforcement of this Code. Nothing herein shall be construed to diminish or impair the rights, duties, privileges, exemptions, immunities, or powers enjoyed by any person under existing law unless expressly abrogated by specific provision hereof. Any ambiguity in these terms shall be resolved favorably toward maintaining public order and safety while preserving individual liberties consistent with constitutional guarantees. The Archmage Sovereign retains authority to issue necessary regulations implementing this Code without further legislative action. All provisions herein shall take effect immediately upon final ratification by the Council of Mages, subject only to review for compliance with higher law. Any conflicting prior enactments are hereby superseded except as otherwise provided herein. This Code represents the collective wisdom and experience of generations of mages dedicated to balancing magical advancement with societal well-being. Through careful adherence to these standards, we shall ensure that magic remains a force for good rather than destruction. The principles enshrined here guide us toward a future where innovation flourishes within bounds of responsibility, fostering harmony between arcane mastery and natural law. Together, bound by oath and reason, we pledge ourselves to the ongoing stewardship of this sacred trust. So let it be written as the guiding star for all who wield power beyond mere mortal ken. Thus ends our solemn vow to protect both progress and peace under the dual dominion of science and spirit. With these words sealed by signature and spell, may justice reign supreme in lands where magic runs deep. Amen and amen so mote it be forevermore unto the ages! ✨📜⚖️\"",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1401.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1401.11 Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements — Implementatio",
          "text": "The transition to full implementation of these Accords shall occur in three distinct phases over a period not exceeding five lunar cycles following this enactment's effective date. Phase One requires all current licensed mages to submit sworn declarations detailing their magical disciplines, years of practice, and any prior disciplinary actions within one hundred days. Failure to comply with this initial reporting requirement will result in immediate suspension of casting privileges until such time as verification is provided.\n\nPhase Two mandates the establishment of regional oversight committees comprising equal representation from both Conservator and Innovator factions, tasked with monitoring compliance at the local level. These committees shall convene monthly for review of incidents and grievances, with findings reported directly to the Archmagus within ten working days. The Archmagus retains ultimate authority to dissolve any committee deemed ineffective or corruptible upon due notice.\n\nFinally, Phase Three entails the formal ratification of all pending disputes through binding arbitration under these new rules rather than individual confrontation. Any outstanding claims filed prior to enactment shall proceed according to their original terms unless modified by mutual consent in writing. This ensures continuity while gradually shifting practices toward greater standardization and accountability across the Guild's diverse membership base.\n\nIt is hereby declared that no provision of this Code shall be construed to abrogate existing rights acquired through bona fide contract or custom prior to its passage, provided such rights do not contravene public policy. Any ambiguity regarding applicability shall be resolved by reference to the principles of fairness and equity inherent in our shared magical traditions rather than rigid literalism alone.\n\nThe Archmagus is vested with broad discretionary powers to issue interim guidelines necessary for orderly implementation, subject only to review by full council vote. These emergency directives shall remain in effect until superseded by final rules promulgated through proper channels thereafter. Immediate action on all fronts is essential to realizing the vision of a unified, responsible magical community bound by mutual respect and rigorous standards.\n\n*Archmagus's Signature Here*\n*Date: ____/____/________* *Seal of Autumnwood Affixed Below*",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1401.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1401.11 Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements — Preservation ",
          "text": "Notwithstanding the enactment of these Accords, any rights or remedies accrued prior to their effective date shall remain enforceable in accordance with their original terms. This includes contractual obligations, tort claims, and equitable interests established under previous legal frameworks. However, no new causes of action may be brought solely on the basis of pre-Accords conduct unless expressly permitted by this Code. Parties seeking to revive dormant claims must file a motion with the Desk for determination of admissibility under § 200.15. The preservation clause does not extend to penalties or sanctions imposed outside the scope of lawful authority, whether by private individuals or rogue factions. Such actions remain void ab initio regardless of timing. Transitional provisions shall take precedence over conflicting pre-existing agreements where ambiguity exists, but only if necessary to prevent manifest injustice. In all other instances, the principle of pacta sunt servanda governs interpretation. Any dispute arising under this section shall be resolved by a special tribunal comprised of three senior magisters and two neutral scholars appointed by consensus. Their decisions are final and binding absent gross misconduct or fraud. Costs associated with preservation motions are borne equally unless equity dictates otherwise. Parties may waive their rights to preserve pre-Accords remedies by written instrument filed with the Desk prior to litigation commencement. Failure to comply with this requirement shall result in automatic dismissal of the claim without prejudice to refiling after exhaustion of appellate review. This provision ensures continuity and stability within the magical community while adapting to evolving norms under the Accords framework.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "200.15",
            "1401.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1401.11 Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements — Historical An",
          "text": "The provisions contained within this Article serve as supplementary guidelines intended to clarify the intent and application of the broader Accords, particularly in light of evolving magical theory and practice. These annotations are not self-executing but rather provide interpretive aid for those tasked with enforcing or adjudicating matters arising under the law. They reflect centuries of accumulated wisdom from our most brilliant sages and pragmatic administrators.\n\nSubsection (a) directs attention to the historical context surrounding each major provision, noting key debates and compromises reached by early assemblies of the Guild. This backdrop is essential for understanding why certain rules exist in their present form. Subsection (b) offers practical examples drawn from past cases illustrating how various clauses have been successfully applied in real-world scenarios. These precedents help ground abstract legal principles in concrete experience.\n\nOf particular importance are the transitional arrangements outlined herein, designed to facilitate a smooth shift from outdated customs to modern standards without disrupting daily operations. Gradual implementation phases allow organizations adequate time to adapt their systems and procedures accordingly. Special protections may be warranted for vulnerable populations facing disproportionate burdens during this period of change.\n\nThe Desk retains authority to issue additional clarifications as needed based on feedback received from all stakeholders affected by these regulations. Such updates will be made promptly through official channels only, never via informal communications that could give rise to confusion or conflicting interpretations. All parties are urged to consult directly with appointed officials should questions arise regarding proper application of any given rule.\n\nUltimately, the goal is to foster an environment wherein magic can flourish responsibly while safeguarding against abuse and excess. By balancing innovation with caution, we ensure continued prosperity for generations to come. Let this revised code stand as a beacon guiding us toward that noble end.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1401.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1401.11 Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements — Preservation",
          "text": "This Part shall not be construed to impair, abrogate, or modify any rights accrued, vested interests, claims, defenses, or obligations arising prior to the effective date hereof under applicable law or contract. Any such pre-existing rights shall survive notwithstanding the provisions herein and may be enforced in accordance with their original terms, subject only to those limitations explicitly imposed by this Codex. This preservation principle is fundamental to maintaining legal certainty and protecting reliance interests of all parties involved in the magical economy.\n\nIn cases where conflicts arise between pre-Accords agreements and subsequent regulatory requirements, the latter shall prevail except where expressly preserved herein. Where uncertainty exists regarding the scope of saved rights, they shall be construed narrowly in favor of public safety and order. This approach balances respect for historical arrangements with the need to adapt to evolving circumstances and emerging knowledge about magical phenomena.\n\nThe provisions of this section are intended to provide clarity on the interplay between legacy entitlements and current obligations under the Autumnwood Accords framework. By clearly delineating what remains inviolate despite regulatory changes, these rules promote stability in an otherwise dynamic field of practice. All participants are advised to consult with qualified legal counsel when assessing their rights and responsibilities vis-à-vis prior commitments and new requirements alike.\n\nThese transitional safeguards reflect recognition that the shift from traditional customs to codified standards cannot occur without disrupting existing relationships and expectations. By carving out exceptions for bona fide pre-Accords arrangements, this legislation acknowledges the reality of entrenched practices while still advancing its broader policy objectives. Careful adherence to these guidelines will help ensure a smooth and equitable transition for all stakeholders in the magical community.\n\nIn sum, § 1401.11 serves as both shield and sword—protecting acquired rights against unwarranted erosion while empowering regulators to enforce necessary controls where gaps remain. This dual function underscores the delicate equilibrium required to govern such a potent domain responsibly. All parties must appreciate the nuances embedded herein if they are to navigate this complex terrain successfully over time.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1401.11"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "NEW section §1401.11 in this same Part only. Invent a DISTINCT catchline that belongs with these siblings, not a new subject and NOT 'Related Requirements': § 1401.1 Historical Annotations; Form; § 1401.2 Dead Citations; § 1401.3 Savings Against the Iron Mandate; § 1401.4 Exclusions from Savings Clauses; § 1401.5 Related Provisions and Cross-References; § 1401.6 Incorporation by Reference and Foreign Precedent; § 1401.7 Authority and Validity; § 1401.8 Historical Annotations and Interpretive Notes; § 1401.9 Foreign Statutory Incorporation and Cross-Jurisdi; § 1401.10 Historical Annotations; Form. First line must be: PAGE Your New Distinct Catchline (5-10 words, specific, no 'Related Requirements')",
      "source": "lmstudio",
      "fp": "a5b5cd7e387ebf74",
      "refs": [
        "200.15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cite": "1.12",
      "part": "front",
      "title": "Waiver and Modification by Express Consent",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 1.12 Waiver and Modification by Express Consent",
          "text": "The Archmage Sovereign or her duly appointed proxy shall possess the authority to waive any provision herein set forth in writing, provided such waiver is executed freely and voluntarily by all affected parties and does not contravene public policy or the fundamental integrity of the Accords. No oral agreement or implied understanding shall suffice to constitute a valid waiver absent explicit written confirmation signed by competent legal counsel for each signatory. Any attempted modification outside these formal channels shall be deemed null and void ab initio, with no force or effect whatsoever. This clause exists solely to facilitate efficient resolution of exceptional circumstances where strict adherence to the letter of the law would produce manifest injustice; it confers no broader powers upon any individual than those expressly enumerated herein. The Desk retains sole discretion to determine whether a proposed waiver meets these stringent criteria and acts as final arbiter on all questions regarding its validity. All waivers shall be filed with the Clerk's Office and made available for public inspection during regular business hours, subject only to redaction of privileged or sensitive information pursuant to applicable privacy statutes. Failure to comply fully with any terms of a granted waiver shall result in immediate revocation thereof and potential prosecution under relevant sections of this Code. The provisions contained herein are intended to be exhaustive and exclusive, leaving no room for ambiguity or alternate interpretations inconsistent with their plain meaning when read as a whole.\"\n\n\"§ 1.12 Waiver and Modification by Express Consent\nPursuant to this section, the Archmage Sovereign holds inherent authority to grant tailored exceptions to specific provisions of these Accords through formal written instruments executed voluntarily by all interested parties. Such waivers must explicitly state which clauses are being modified, provide clear reasoning for their necessity in the particular context at hand, and demonstrate that granting them will not undermine the overall objectives of magical governance under our system. Each waiver shall undergo rigorous review by independent legal counsel retained specifically for this purpose to ensure compliance with all applicable standards before being deemed operative. Oral promises or informal understandings possess no binding force whatsoever; only meticulously drafted documents bearing proper signatures from duly authorized representatives may effectuate any alteration to the existing framework of rules and regulations governing arcane practice within our realm.\"\n\n\"Under no circumstances shall a waiver extend beyond its precise terms as delineated in the granting instrument itself, nor shall it be construed to imply permission for actions expressly forbidden elsewhere in this Code. Violation of any stipulated condition triggers automatic nullification of the exception along with potential disciplinary measures appropriate to the severity of the breach. The Desk maintains ultimate oversight responsibility and may rescind any previously approved waiver at its sole discretion if subsequent events render continued tolerance unacceptable. Full transparency regarding all granted waivers remains mandatory, with copies made accessible for public viewing subject only to reasonable confidentiality protections where warranted by legitimate privacy concerns.\"\n\n\"This provision serves as a safety valve allowing flexibility in rare situations demanding individualized solutions while preserving the integrity of our comprehensive regulatory scheme through strict procedural safeguards and enforceable limitations on scope and duration. Properly implemented, it enables thoughtful accommodation of unique needs without compromising the fundamental principles upon which effective magical control depends throughout all lands covered by these Accords.\"",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1.12 Waiver and Modification by Express Consent — Continued",
          "text": "§ 1.12 Waiver and Modification by Express Consent\n\nAny provision of these Accords may be waived or modified in whole or in part, but only through an instrument executed with the same formalities required for their original adoption. Such instruments must specify with particularity the scope of the waiver or modification and the conditions under which it applies. No waiver or modification shall survive until duly recorded by the Desk, after which it becomes binding upon all parties subject to these Accords. Any attempt to waive or modify a provision orally or through implication alone is void ab initio. This section exists solely to ensure that waivers and modifications are deliberate, informed, and properly documented, thereby preserving the integrity of the legal regime established by this Code. Failure to comply with these requirements renders any purported waiver or modification unenforceable, regardless of the parties' subjective intent. The Desk shall maintain a register of all valid waivers and modifications for public inspection, ensuring transparency and accountability in their administration. This provision underscores the fundamental principle that the Accords are a binding contract between sovereign entities, subject to change only through mutual agreement expressed in unmistakable terms. By strict adherence to these formalities, the Guild safeguards against frivolous claims and unintended consequences, promoting stability and predictability in arcane affairs across all realms.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1.12 Waiver and Modification by Express Consent — Administration",
          "text": "§ 1.12 Waiver and Modification by Express Consent — Continued\n\nThe principles set forth herein shall not be deemed to waive or impair any rights, remedies, or defenses available under these Accords except as expressly provided by law or by the express consent of all parties affected thereby. No implied waiver shall arise from a failure to assert any right, remedy, or defense in any particular proceeding before the Desk or any authorized tribunal. Any modification of these provisions must be executed in writing and signed by all parties having an interest therein, unless otherwise permitted by law.\n\nNotwithstanding anything contained herein to the contrary, nothing in this Article shall be construed as limiting the rights of the Archmage Sovereign or the Aegis Magi to take such action as may be necessary to protect public safety or prevent imminent harm arising from the unauthorized practice of magic. The Desk retains discretionary authority to issue emergency orders suspending certain provisions where immediate action is required to safeguard persons or property. Such orders shall be subject to review by a convened session of the full Council within seven days, unless extended for good cause shown.\n\nIn the event of any conflict between these Accords and other applicable laws or regulations, the more stringent standard shall prevail so long as it does not contravene the fundamental rights guaranteed herein. Nothing in this Article shall be construed to abrogate or impair any obligations imposed by superior law upon persons subject thereto. All disputes arising under these provisions shall be resolved exclusively through the mechanisms established within the Guild's judicial framework, unless otherwise provided by competent authority.\n\nThe Desk shall maintain a comprehensive record of all waivers, modifications, and variances granted pursuant to this Article, together with supporting documentation justifying each decision. Such records shall remain confidential except as required for administrative purposes or by order of a reviewing body. Any party seeking access to these materials must demonstrate a compelling need that cannot be satisfied through other means available under the Accords. Failure to comply with any provision of this section shall constitute grounds for disciplinary action up to and including revocation of licensure, at the sole discretion of the Desk.\n\nNothing in this Article shall be deemed to limit or impair any rights, remedies, or defenses expressly preserved herein. All provisions contained therein are hereby reaffirmed as valid, binding, and enforceable against all persons subject to these Accords without further notice or action. The intent of this section is solely to clarify the scope and effect of express waivers and modifications permitted under the law, not to create new rights or obligations beyond those already established by the full text of these Articles.\n\n*See also § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse; § 300.11 Schedules of Magical Arts and Their Classification.*",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1.12",
            "100.5",
            "200.4",
            "300.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1.12 Waiver and Modification by Express Consent — Oversight",
          "text": "§ 1.12 Waiver and Modification by Express Consent — Continued\n\nAny waiver or modification granted under § 1.12 shall be in writing, signed by all parties thereto, and filed with the Autumnwood Accords Desk for recordation. Such instruments shall clearly identify the specific rights, obligations, or prohibitions being waived or modified, along with any conditions precedent to their effectiveness. Failure to comply with these formalities renders the waiver or modification void ab initio.\n\nThe Archmage Sovereign, acting through the Mages' Guild Desk, reserves the right to review all waivers and modifications submitted under § 1.12 for compliance with the fundamental principles of this Codex and public policy. The Desk may reject any instrument deemed contrary to the spirit or letter of the Accords, without prejudice to the parties' subsequent rights and remedies. Prompt notification shall be provided to the submitting party regarding acceptance or rejection of their proposal.\n\nIn the event of ambiguity or dispute concerning the scope or effect of a waiver or modification executed under § 1.12, such matters shall be resolved by reference to the original intent of the parties at the time of execution, as evidenced by all surrounding circumstances and communications. Absent clear contrary evidence, any doubt shall be construed against the drafter of the instrument and in favor of strict adherence to the text of this Codex.\n\nNo waiver or modification under § 1.12 shall survive termination of the underlying agreement unless expressly stated otherwise within the governing instrument itself. Upon such termination, all rights and obligations shall revert automatically to their status quo ante, as if no waiver or modification had ever been granted. The Mages' Guild Desk retains jurisdiction over any residual disputes arising from the execution or interpretation of § 1.12 instruments following expiration of the primary contract.\n\nParties executing waivers or modifications under this section acknowledge that they have received independent legal advice regarding their rights and obligations, and voluntarily elect to proceed despite potential risks and consequences. By signing such instruments, parties represent and warrant that they possess full authority to bind themselves thereto on behalf of all relevant entities. Any claim of lack thereof shall be deemed waived by subsequent ratification through conduct inconsistent with such assertion.\n\nThis section supersedes any prior conflicting agreements or understandings between the parties concerning matters within its scope. It is intended to provide a flexible mechanism for adapting this Codex to changing circumstances while maintaining essential safeguards against abuse and exploitation. The Mages' Guild Desk stands ready to assist in navigating the complexities inherent in granting waivers or modifications under § 1.12, ensuring equitable outcomes aligned with the overarching goals of the Autumnwood Accords.\n\nsee also §§ 100.6 Delegation to Clerks; 300.11 Schedules of Magical Arts and Their Classification; 400.11 Research Permits and Supervised Experiments regarding related authorization processes under the Accords. Furthermore, consult § 700.11 Burden Shifting and Presumptions in Arcane Litigation for additional guidance on evidentiary matters pertaining to waivers and modifications. Finally, refer to § 800.11 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation for consequences of violating terms established under this section.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1.12",
            "100.6",
            "700.11",
            "800.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1.12 Waiver and Modification by Express Consent — Procedure",
          "text": "§ 1.12 permits parties to contract around certain default provisions, provided the waiver is made knowingly and voluntarily. Such waivers must be in writing, signed by all affected persons, and cannot contravene public policy or fundamental rights. The Desk shall review each waiver for clarity of intent and absence of duress before approving it as binding. Any ambiguity shall be resolved against the drafter under established principles of contract construction. Further, no waiver may extend beyond the specific terms expressly stated; implied waivers are not recognized. Where a waiver conflicts with another provision of this Code, the more specific instrument prevails unless superseded by later express agreement. The Desk maintains a registry of approved waivers for reference and enforcement purposes. Parties seeking to modify existing obligations must submit a formal petition outlining the proposed changes and justifications therefor. Approval is discretionary and subject to full disclosure of all material facts. Failure to comply with these procedural requirements renders any purported waiver void ab initio.\n\nUnder § 1.4, persons bound by this Code include both natural and artificial entities engaging in magical activities within Autumnwood Hall jurisdiction. Waivers executed by such parties must account for their unique capacities and liabilities as defined elsewhere herein. For instance, constructs may waive certain personal protections if adequately indemnified against resultant harms—a principle elaborated under § 600.10 regarding specialized labor agreements. The Desk retains ultimate authority to invalidate any waiver deemed unconscionable or contrary to the spirit of the Accords. This supervisory role ensures that waivers serve their intended purpose of facilitating lawful commerce without undermining public safety or ethical standards. Parties are advised to consult legal counsel when drafting complex waivers involving multiple jurisdictions or novel magical applications. The Desk provides official forms and guidance templates upon request but does not offer independent legal advice. All approved waivers carry the full weight of enforceable contract law, subject only to review by competent courts with appropriate standing. Non-compliance may result in civil penalties, administrative sanctions, or criminal prosecution depending on severity.\n\nsee § 1.5 regarding relation to other applicable laws and regulations; see § 600.10 for special provisions governing construct contracts; see § 700.9 concerning burden of proof in waiver disputes. This section implements the foundational principle that voluntary agreement between competent parties governs their mutual rights, balanced against broader societal interests protected by the Accords as a whole. The Desk's oversight mechanism preserves this delicate equilibrium while enabling necessary flexibility for evolving magical practices and commercial needs alike.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1.12",
            "1.4",
            "600.10",
            "1.5",
            "700.9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 1.12 Waiver and Modification by Express Consent — Custody",
          "text": "§ 1.12 WAIVER AND MODIFICATION BY EXPRESS CONSENT; LIMITED APPLICATION TO PERSONS OF FULL CAPACITY\n\nNo provision herein shall be deemed waived or modified except upon express consent in writing, signed by the party seeking such relief. Said consent must specify with particularity the clause affected and the extent of the waiver sought. General releases or blanket waivers are void as contrary to public policy. This requirement applies only to persons of full legal capacity acting voluntarily and without duress. Any attempt to bind minors, wards, or mentally incapacitated individuals to such agreements is null and unenforceable ab initio.\n\nThe written instrument effectuating waiver must be executed by authorized representatives possessing actual knowledge of the terms being modified. Mere silence or failure to object shall not constitute assent. The burden of proving valid consent rests upon the party asserting the waiver. Where doubt exists as to whether a provision was properly waived, it shall be construed strictly against the drafter and in favor of the public interest.\n\nThis section is intended solely for limited application where specific circumstances demand flexibility beyond what the rigid framework of these Accords permits. It does not grant blanket authority to alter fundamental principles enshrined herein. Any purported waiver exceeding the narrow confines outlined above shall be deemed ineffective regardless of form or apparent assent. The Desk retains inherent power to invalidate any improper modification upon its own motion or at the request of an interested party.\n\nSee § 1.4 re persons bound; § 300.5 on prohibited conduct; § 900.7 regarding disclosure obligations. Under foundational principles laid out in §§ 1.6 and 1.7, interpretation must favor public safety over private convenience. Any waiver undermining this core mandate stands void ab initio regardless of purported consent. The Desk maintains plenary authority to police compliance with these strictures at all times.\n\nNo provision herein shall be deemed waived or modified except upon express consent in writing, signed by the party seeking such relief. Said consent must specify with particularity the clause affected and the extent of the waiver sought. General releases or blanket waivers are void as contrary to public policy. This requirement applies only to persons of full legal capacity acting voluntarily and without duress. Any attempt to bind minors, wards, or mentally incapacitated individuals to such agreements is null and unenforceable ab initio.\n\nThe written instrument effectuating waiver must be executed by authorized representatives possessing actual knowledge of the terms being modified. Mere silence or failure to object shall not constitute assent. The burden of proving valid consent rests upon the party asserting the waiver. Where doubt exists as to whether a provision was properly waived, it shall be construed strictly against the drafter and in favor of the public interest.\n\nThis section is intended solely for limited application where specific circumstances demand flexibility beyond what the rigid framework of these Accords permits. It does not grant blanket authority to alter fundamental principles enshrined herein. Any purported waiver exceeding the narrow confines outlined above shall be deemed ineffective regardless of form or apparent assent. The Desk retains inherent power to invalidate any improper modification upon its own motion or at the request of an interested party.\n\nSee § 1.4 re persons bound; § 300.5 on prohibited conduct; § 900.7 regarding disclosure obligations. Under foundational principles laid out in §§ 1.6 and 1.7, interpretation must favor public safety over private convenience. Any waiver undermining this core mandate stands void ab initio regardless of purported consent. The Desk maintains plenary authority to police compliance with these strictures at all times.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1.12",
            "1.4",
            "300.5",
            "900.7",
            "1.6"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "NEW section §1.12 in this same Part only. Invent a DISTINCT catchline that belongs with these siblings, not a new subject and NOT 'Related Requirements': § 1.1 Short Title and Citation; § 1.2 Enacting Authority; Autumnwood Accords Desk; § 1.3 How to Read This Codex; § 1.4 Persons Bound; § 1.5 Relation to Other Law; § 1.6 Definitions; § 1.7 Construction; Aggregation of Conduct; § 1.8 Effective Date; Savings; § 1.9 Seals, Stamps, and What Is Not a Seal; § 1.10 Reserved Catchlines; § 1.11 Jurisdictional Authority. First line must be: PAGE Your New Distinct Catchline (5-10 words, specific, no 'Related Requirements')",
