    {
      "cite": "100.12",
      "part": "part_i",
      "title": "Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§100.12 Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements",
          "text": "This Article shall serve as the residual clause governing all matters not specifically addressed in this Codex but arising naturally from its operation or interpretation. Nothing herein shall be construed to limit the inherent powers of the Archmage Sovereign or her appointed delegates, provided such actions remain consistent with the spirit and letter of the Accords. The Desk reserves explicit authority to issue binding directives as necessary to preserve public safety and magical equilibrium under extraordinary circumstances not foreseen at the time of enactment.\n\nAll provisions herein shall take effect immediately upon promulgation unless otherwise specified within this Article itself. Any existing laws, regulations, or customs inconsistent herewith are hereby superseded to the extent of such conflict, save where expressly preserved by reference in these Sections. The Accords are intended to be a living instrument subject to periodic review and amendment as conditions change and experience informs better judgment. No single individual shall possess authority to alter this Code unilaterally; all modifications require formal ratification by the full Council acting under proper procedures set forth elsewhere herein.\n\nIn case of any ambiguity or apparent inconsistency within these Sections, interpretation shall favor the public interest in maintaining order and preventing harm through reckless magical practice. Technicalities shall not be invoked to evade compliance with substantive obligations imposed hereunder. The Desk may issue supplementary guidelines as needed to clarify application without compromising legal certainty or predictability for practitioners subject to this jurisdiction. All rights under this Code are assignable only by express written instrument executed in accordance with applicable formal requirements, unless otherwise expressly permitted by specific provisions contained herein.\"\n\nsee §100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; see §200.4 Suspension and Lapse; see §300.9 Schedules of Magical Arts and Their Classification\"",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "100.5",
            "200.4",
            "300.9",
            "100.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 100.12 Transitional Provisions and Supplementary Rules",
          "text": "In the event of any ambiguity regarding the application of these Accords to prior acts or established practices, the principle of non-retroactivity shall govern unless expressly provided otherwise. No new obligations or liabilities may be imposed upon individuals for conduct occurring before the effective date of this Codebook, absent explicit consent in writing. For matters arising during a period where conflicting provisions were simultaneously in force, the provision most favorable to the party asserting compliance shall prevail.\n\nAny disputes concerning the interpretation or enforcement of these transitional rules shall be resolved through binding arbitration conducted by a panel appointed jointly by the Conservator and Innovator factions within thirty days of notice. The costs and expenses of such proceedings shall be shared equally between the disputing parties, unless manifest bad faith is established. In all cases where the application of this section would result in injustice or absurdity due to its literal construction, the spirit and intent of the Accords shall control over a strict reading of the text.\n\nThese transitional provisions remain in effect until superseded by subsequent legislation enacted pursuant to these Articles or repealed by formal vote of the Mages' Guild Desk. Until such time as they are rescinded, they shall be cited with full force and authority alongside the substantive terms herein. Any attempt to circumvent their requirements through creative structuring or technicalities shall constitute a violation subject to standard sanctions under applicable law.\n\nThe parties hereto acknowledge that acceptance of these transitional provisions constitutes final settlement of all prior claims arising from the dual-regulation era, except where expressly reserved in writing. This release is binding upon successors and assigns unless otherwise noted. Disputes over whether an exception applies shall be decided as a matter of fact by the presiding arbiter with deference to established precedent. Nothing herein precludes recourse to criminal or civil remedies for egregious violations occurring before this section takes effect, where appropriate under governing law.\n\nBy entering into these Accords, all signatories agree to abide by both their substantive terms and these supplementary rules as a unified whole. They further covenant to act in good faith towards one another throughout the implementation process, fostering cooperation rather than conflict wherever possible. This mutual commitment forms the bedrock upon which future relations between the Guild's diverse constituencies will be built, guiding them toward shared prosperity under the banner of magical excellence and responsible stewardship alike.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "100.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 100.12 Transitional Provisions and Supplementary Rules — Continued",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords Desk, by virtue of its status as the primary interpreting authority for this Codex, reserves the right to issue supplementary rules and interpretations as necessary to effectuate the purposes thereof. Such supplemental provisions shall be published in the Official Gazette and shall take effect immediately upon promulgation, unless otherwise specified. All members of the Guild are hereby directed to adhere strictly to any such additional directives issued by the Desk or its duly authorized delegates.\n\nIn matters not explicitly addressed within these Articles, the Desk may exercise its discretion to fill gaps or resolve ambiguities as it deems appropriate in furtherance of the Accords' overarching objectives. This includes, but is not limited to, issuing advisory opinions on novel circumstances arising from advances in magical theory and practice. The decisions of the Desk in such instances shall be binding upon all parties subject to its jurisdiction.\n\nNothing herein shall be construed to limit or impair the inherent powers of the Guild or its constituent bodies, including the right to promulgate ancillary regulations deemed reasonably necessary for proper administration. Such rules may address procedural matters, ethical standards, professional conduct, and any other aspects pertaining to the regulation of magical arts within the jurisdiction. All members agree to abide by such supplementary enactments as if fully incorporated herein.\n\nThe Desk further retains authority to convene special sessions or ad hoc committees as required to address pressing issues affecting Guild welfare or public safety. Minutes from these gatherings shall be made available for inspection upon request, subject only to redaction of confidential information where appropriate. All actions taken pursuant to such proceedings shall carry the full force and effect of formal resolutions adopted by the regular Assembly.\n\nFinally, this section serves as a declaration that the Accords represent a living document, adaptable to evolving conditions while maintaining fidelity to its core principles. The Desk stands ready to guide the Guild through periods of uncertainty with wisdom and foresight, ensuring continued prosperity for all concerned. Thus concludes Part I of these comprehensive statutes governing magical practice under the Autumnwood Accord regime.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "100.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 100.12 Transitional Provisions and Supplementary Rules — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords Desk hereby adopts the following supplementary provisions to govern the transition from prior regimes: First, any licenses or permits issued under the former Iron Mandate shall be deemed valid for a period of sixty (60) days from the effective date of these Accords, provided that the holder has not engaged in unauthorized field casting during such term. After this grace period expires unexercised, all such documents automatically abrogate unless renewed pursuant to § 200 et seq. Second, any outstanding fines or penalties accrued under the Mandate shall be offset against future dues assessments for a single billing cycle only; no carryover is permitted thereafter. Third, all records maintained by the Iron Legion's Enforcement Corps relating to magical practitioners are hereby transferred to the Autumnwood Accords Desk for archival purposes, subject to redaction of sensitive personal data in accordance with § 1201.6 Privacy Safeguards. Fourth, any contracts or agreements entered into prior to these Accords that reference \"Mandate Law\" shall be construed as referencing the current text of this Code unless expressly stated otherwise. Finally, the Desk may issue special transitional orders from time to time as necessary to effectuate a smooth shift in regulatory authority; such orders carry full force and effect until superseded or rescinded by subsequent action. These provisions are intended solely to mitigate disruption during this pivotal epoch of legal evolution and shall be applied with utmost fairness and consistency to all concerned parties.\"",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1201.6",
            "100.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 100.12 Transitional Provisions and Supplementary Rules — Continued — Administration",
          "text": "The Accords shall remain in full force and effect during the period of their transition, superseding all prior magical laws except as expressly amended herein. Any outstanding licenses or permits issued under previous statutes shall be deemed valid unless explicitly revoked by the Desk within thirty days of this enactment. All pending cases involving arcane offenses shall continue adjudication pursuant to these new standards, with final judgment rendered not later than six months from this date.\n\nIn matters concerning the registration of spellcasters, all practitioners currently operating without formal licensure must submit complete biographical and magical aptitude records within ninety days of passage. Failure to comply shall result in immediate suspension of all casting privileges until proper documentation is verified by two senior Aegis Magi. The Desk reserves authority to conduct random audits of registered casters on an annual basis, with non-compliance subject to punitive sanctions up to and including permanent revocation of membership status.\n\nRegarding the classification of magical arts, any technique not explicitly enumerated in Schedule A shall be presumed lawful absent evidence to the contrary. However, the Desk may issue binding interpretations clarifying ambiguous provisions upon written request from interested parties. Such rulings shall carry precedential weight until superseded by subsequent official guidance or legislation. All disputes arising under these transitional measures shall be resolved through established grievance procedures rather than private arbitration or self-help remedies.\n\nThe Archmage Sovereign and associated officers are empowered to promulgate necessary interim regulations required for orderly implementation of this Code. Such delegated rules must comport with the spirit and letter of the Accords and remain subject to review by the full Desk at its next scheduled session. Any regulations deemed ultra vires may be struck down upon motion by a qualified member of the Guild, with final determination resting solely with the majority vote of the assembled body.\n\nThese provisions shall constitute integral components of the Autumnwood Accords as originally enacted and subsequently amended. They reflect careful consideration of practical realities facing our diverse community while maintaining strict adherence to core principles of magical safety and ethical conduct. All members are enjoined to read these supplementary clauses thoroughly, as they bear directly upon their daily operations and responsibilities under the law. Ignorance of this material shall not excuse non-compliance or mitigate resulting penalties imposed by duly constituted authorities.\n\n\"Magic demands responsibility above all else.\" — Archmage Veyra, Oath of Binding, 982 AR\nsee § 100.3 Quorum of the Desk; see § 200.4 Suspension and Lapse; see § 1.7 Construction: Aggregation of Conduct",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "100.3",
            "200.4",
            "1.7",
            "100.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 100.12 Transitional Provisions and Supplementary Rules — Continued — Administr",
          "text": "Whereas the Accords acknowledge that full implementation may require extended periods of phased rollout, this section establishes the framework for managing such transitions without disrupting ongoing magical operations or compromising public safety. Under § 100.8, an Emergency Sitting may be convened to address urgent matters arising from the deployment of new clauses; however, any actions taken pursuant thereto must receive ratification at the next regular session unless explicitly waived by unanimous vote in accordance with § 100.5.\n\n§ 100.9 mandates that all modifications to existing magical contracts or permits shall be processed through a streamlined expedited review track, subject to enhanced scrutiny under § 400.11. Such expeditious handling is deemed necessary to minimize disruption to lawful spellcasting activities during the implementation phase. Notwithstanding this acceleration of procedures, no substantive changes may be made that would alter the fundamental rights or obligations established in prior agreements without express consent from all affected parties as provided for under § 200.3.\n\nThe Desk shall maintain a dedicated Liaison Office charged with overseeing the transition process and facilitating communication between the Guild, its members, and external stakeholders. This unit will coordinate technical assistance, provide guidance on compliance matters, and serve as the primary point of contact for resolving issues that arise during the rollout period. Funding for these operations will be drawn from the reserves allocated specifically for implementation under § 100.6(b)(iii).\n\nIt is further provided that any disputes concerning the interpretation or application of newly enacted provisions shall be resolved through binding arbitration conducted by a panel appointed pursuant to § 700.11, unless the parties agree otherwise in writing. The arbitrators must possess expertise both in arcane jurisprudence and the relevant technical fields implicated by the contested clauses. Their determinations shall be final and enforceable as if rendered by a court of competent jurisdiction under § 800.11.\n\nFinally, nothing herein shall be construed to limit or impair any rights or remedies available at common law, equity, or otherwise, except where expressly superseded by these provisions. The Accords stand ratified and binding upon all signatory entities effective immediately upon final approval by the full Council under § 100.4(a), subject only to those exceptions explicitly enumerated herein or by subsequent amendment in accordance with established procedure. May this Codex serve as an enduring guide for just governance and harmonious coexistence within our shared world. So mote it be!",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "100.8",
            "100.5",
            "100.9",
            "400.11",
            "200.3",
            "100.6",
            "700.11",
            "800.11",
            "100.4",
            "100.12"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "NEW section §100.12 in this same Part only. Invent a DISTINCT catchline that belongs with these siblings, not a new subject and NOT 'Related Requirements': § 100.1 Guild Offices Named; § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild; § 100.3 Quorum of the Desk; § 100.4 Records of Speech; § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; § 100.6 Delegation to Clerks; § 100.7 Foreign Halls and Courtesy; § 100.8 Emergency Sitting; § 100.9 Conflict of Interest in Casting Procedures; § 100.10 Complementary Provisions; § 100.11 Procedures for the Office of Archmage Sovereig. First line must be: PAGE Your New Distinct Catchline (5-10 words, specific, no 'Related Requirements')",
      "source": "lmstudio",
      "fp": "e10c2439ca9b78ae",
