    {
      "cite": "300.12",
      "part": "part_iii",
      "title": "Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission",
          "text": "§ 300.12 No correspondence or transmission utilizing magical means shall be employed to convey information pertaining to the Unsanctioned Arts, except as expressly authorized in writing by the Office of Archmage Sovereign. This prohibition extends to all forms of arcane communication, including but not limited to telepathy, scrying, message charms, and enchanted media. Violation of this provision shall constitute a Class A Felony Under the Accords. Exceptions may be granted only upon formal petition and approval by a majority vote of the Autumnwood Accords Desk. All requests for exceptions must be submitted in triplicate with full supporting documentation detailing the necessity thereof. Failure to comply with these requirements shall result in immediate suspension of all magical privileges held by the offending party until such time as compliance is demonstrated to the satisfaction of the Desk.\"\n\n\"Under § 100.5, conflicts of interest arising from unauthorized transmission of classified information are strictly prohibited. This provision reinforces the integrity of the Guild's internal communications channels and prevents potential breaches of security protocols. See also § 200.4 regarding restrictions on unsupervised spellcasting by junior members, which serves a similar purpose in mitigating risks associated with improper use of magical capabilities.\" \"The prohibition outlined herein is designed to safeguard sensitive intelligence from falling into the wrong hands or being misused for malicious purposes. By limiting access to such information and controlling its dissemination through established channels only, the Accords ensure that critical data remains secure at all times.\" \"Exceptions must be granted sparingly and with rigorous oversight to prevent abuse of authority by individual magistrates seeking personal gain or favoritism. The burden of proof rests squarely upon those requesting special dispensation under § 100.5(c) to demonstrate a compelling need justifying deviation from standard procedures without compromising overall safety.\" \"In summary, the strictures imposed on magical correspondence and transmission serve as vital safeguards against potential threats posed by careless handling of classified material. Adherence to these guidelines ensures continued protection of both public welfare and the interests of all stakeholders within the Guild's sphere of influence.\"",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "300.12",
            "100.5",
            "200.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission — Continued",
          "text": "§ 300.12 Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission\nNo caster shall employ magical means to transmit thoughts, emotions, images, or instructions directly into the minds of other beings without explicit consent from all parties involved. Such unauthorized psychic intrusion is deemed a grave violation of personal sovereignty and a precursor to more serious criminal conduct. Violators shall be subject to immediate seizure upon discovery and trial under the provisions herein regarding unlawful casting. Exceptions exist for therapeutic applications conducted by licensed healers acting in good faith, provided that full disclosure is made prior to commencing treatment.\n\nThe Guild maintains strict oversight of all magical communications networks and devices, including but not limited to scrying pools, telepathic implants, and enchanted correspondence tools. Any device suspected of facilitating clandestine mind-linking shall be confiscated pending investigation. Owners found guilty of improper use may face revocation of their casting licenses and additional penalties as determined by the Presiding Archmage. The prohibition extends to all forms of magical influence, whether direct or indirect, that bypasses conscious awareness of the affected individual.\n\nPenalties for violating this section range from fines proportional to the offender's income and status to permanent sealing of their magical abilities in cases of egregious misconduct. Repeat offenders may be subject to expulsion from the Guild entirely and imprisonment at Archmage discretion. The burden of proof rests upon the accuser to demonstrate beyond reasonable doubt that unauthorized transmission occurred, with allowances made for technical error or malfunction. However, circumstantial evidence sufficient to establish a prima facie case shall suffice to warrant seizure of suspected equipment until further notice.\n\nThis provision is intended to safeguard the privacy and mental autonomy of all persons subject to the jurisdiction of the Autumnwood Accords. By preventing covert manipulation of thought processes through magical means, the Guild seeks to preserve the integrity of individual agency against subtle forms of coercion that may otherwise go unnoticed. Violations shall be prosecuted with utmost seriousness and without regard for rank or affiliation. All citizens are encouraged to report any suspicious activity related to unauthorized mind-linking promptly to their local Arcane Watch command for appropriate action. Failure to comply with this directive may result in escalated enforcement measures at the discretion of the relevant authorities.\n\nThe prohibition on magical correspondence and transmission stands as a fundamental principle underpinning the broader framework of personal rights enshrined within these Accords. It reflects our collective commitment to protecting the sanctity of human consciousness from external intrusion, whether by natural or supernatural forces. Through diligent adherence to this standard, we ensure that each individual retains full dominion over their own mind—a cornerstone upon which a just and free society must be built. Let none dare violate this sacred boundary without facing swift and severe consequences as prescribed by law.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "300.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "This prohibition extends to all forms of magical communication, whether direct or mediated by artifacts. It is unlawful for any individual to employ spellwork or enchanted devices to transmit information across distances without explicit authorization from the Guild. This includes telepathic projection, scrying rituals, rune-inscribed letters, and animated messages. Violations constitute serious breaches of trust between mages and may result in immediate sanctions. The ban aims to prevent unauthorized surveillance and interference with private affairs. Exceptions are granted only for official business conducted under supervision. Unauthorized magical correspondence undermines the Guild's authority and compromises security protocols. Strict enforcement is necessary to maintain order within the arcane community and protect the wider public from potential harm. All mages must adhere to this rule without exception, regardless of perceived necessity or urgency. The penalties for violation are severe and progressive, reflecting the gravity of the offense. Failure to comply will result in escalating disciplinary action up to and including permanent expulsion and sealing of magical aptitude. Guild oversight remains absolute in matters of communication technology and practice. No individual may justify circumvention on grounds of convenience or efficiency alone. Adherence is mandatory for licensure renewal and continued professional standing. The integrity of the magical network depends upon strict observance of these prohibitions by all members. Breach invites scrutiny and possible investigation into other areas of conduct. Mages are expected to exercise restraint and discretion regarding all forms of magical interaction. The Guild reserves the right to define specific limitations as needed for security purposes. This rule stands independent of other statutes governing magical usage. Compliance is non-negotiable under any circumstances whatsoever. The stakes involved demand unwavering discipline from every practitioner subject to the Accords. Any doubt about applicability should be resolved by seeking clarification through proper channels rather than risking violation. Ultimately, this provision safeguards both individual privacy and collective safety within the broader society.\"\n\n§ 300.12 Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission — Continued\nThis section elaborates upon the scope and implications of the ban on unauthorized magical communication. It prohibits not only active spellcasting but also the use of pre-prepared enchanted items for transmitting messages. This encompasses a wide range of techniques, from conventional telepathy to more exotic forms such as conjured avatars or spirit messengers. The prohibition applies equally to commercial and personal exchanges, recognizing that abuse risks could arise in either context. Violations are treated with particular severity given their potential impact on confidentiality and security. The Guild maintains strict control over all means of magical communication to prevent misuse. Exceptions require written approval from senior authorities citing compelling necessity. Unauthorized attempts will be investigated thoroughly with possible consequences ranging from fines to imprisonment. Adherence is a fundamental expectation for all licensed practitioners regardless of rank or specialization. Failure to comply undermines public trust and exposes the profession to unnecessary danger.\"\n\n\"see § 100.5 Conflict of Interest in Casting; § 200.3 Temporary Mouths; § 400.9 Confidentiality Obligations under Research Contracts\"",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "300.12",
            "100.5",
            "200.3",
            "400.9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission — Continued — Administration",
          "text": "§ 300.12 Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission — Continued. No mage shall employ magic to transmit thoughts, emotions, images, or other mental data directly between individuals without consent of all parties. Such unauthorized telepathic communication violates the sanctity of personal privacy and may constitute magical assault under § 100.5(a). Violators are subject to immediate seizure of their implements and temporary suspension pending investigation. Exceptions exist for emergency medical diagnosis and lawful law enforcement proceedings where warrant has been obtained from an Archmage Sovereign. All telepathic devices must be registered with the Desk and bear a unique serial number readable by Guild scanners. Failure to comply constitutes prima facie evidence of intent to evade regulation. Penalties include fines up to one hundred gold crowns, community service, or confinement for up to thirty days at discretion of the hearing officer. Repeated offenses may result in revocation of licensure and referral to Paradox Trial. The Desk retains authority to issue cease-and-desist orders upon reasonable suspicion of illegal telepathic activity. Mages are required to disclose any known capabilities for remote mental contact on their application forms. Concealment of such abilities is grounds for automatic disqualification and permanent banishment from the Guild's good graces. This provision supersedes all conflicting local ordinances or customary practices regarding magical communication methods. The Desk shall promulgate detailed guidelines defining acceptable uses of telepathy in accordance with this section within six months of enactment. Any questions concerning interpretation shall be referred to the Office of Legal Counsel for binding ruling. Nothing herein shall preclude lawful surveillance activities conducted under proper authorization and warrant by state or federal law enforcement agencies acting pursuant to existing statutes. Mages found guilty of violating this prohibition shall additionally forfeit all profits derived from illegal transmissions and pay restitution to affected victims as determined by appropriate court order. The Desk reserves the right to modify these rules at any time upon notice and opportunity for hearing consistent with fundamental fairness principles embodied in § 100.4(c).",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "300.12",
            "100.5",
            "100.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Prohibited Magical Communication Channels § 300.7",
          "text": "No caster shall employ magical means to transmit speech, data, or intent across distances without explicit licensure under § 204.3 and § 501.6 thereof. This prohibition extends to all forms of arcane communication, including but not limited to telepathy, scrying, illusionary projection, and spell-linked messaging devices. Unauthorized magical transmission shall be deemed a Class C violation subject to penalty under § 812.4A.\n\nViolations of this provision are actionable by any aggrieved party or the Guild at large upon written complaint filed with the Office of Magical Oversight per § 905.1. Burden of proof rests on the accuser to demonstrate prima facie case of illicit magical communication, after which burden shifts to the accused to prove innocence beyond reasonable doubt pursuant to § 723.8B.\n\nExceptions exist for emergency medical situations where rapid consultation is critical and conventional means fail (§ 510.9), or when conducting authorized research into interplanar phenomena under strict supervision per § 406.2C. Such exceptions require prior written approval from the Archmage Sovereign or their delegate, specifying exact parameters of permitted use. Any deviation from approved parameters renders the exception void and subject to full penal consequences.\n\nThe prohibition applies regardless of whether transmission is one-way or two-way, encrypted or unencrypted, direct or relayed through intermediary devices. It encompasses all known modalities of magical communication current at time of violation, including but not limited to those listed in Appendix C attached hereto by reference. New technologies and methods shall be automatically included within the scope unless expressly excluded by subsequent amendment.\n\nPenalties for violation range from fines up to one thousand gold pieces per offense (§ 812.4A) to temporary suspension of licensure for repeat or egregious offenders (§ 812.4B). In cases involving national security threats or widespread disruption, permanent revocation of all privileges may be warranted at the discretion of the Archmage Sovereign acting on recommendation from the Council of Magi (§ 103.5C).\n\nThis provision remains in effect indefinitely unless expressly repealed by unanimous vote of the full Guild Assembly convened for that specific purpose only. Any attempt to circumvent or undermine its provisions through proxy agents, subsidiaries, or third parties shall be treated as direct violation by the principal actor under § 821.3B. All casters are hereby charged with knowing and abiding by this prohibition at all times within their jurisdictional sphere.\"\n\n\"see § 501.6 regarding emergency exceptions; refer to Appendix C for complete list of prohibited methods; consult § 723.8B on burden of proof in enforcement proceedings; note § 103.5C granting discretionary authority to Archmage Sovereign for severe cases;\"",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "204.3",
            "501.6",
            "812.4",
            "905.1",
            "723.8",
            "510.9",
            "406.2",
            "103.5",
            "821.3",
            "300.7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "§ 300.12 Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission",
          "text": "The Accords expressly forbid the use of magical means to transmit data, knowledge, or intent between parties without explicit authorization from the Guild's High Court. This prohibition applies regardless of whether the transmission occurs across physical distance or within a single location, and irrespective of the medium employed—be it telepathy, scrying, dimensional rifts, or enchanted devices designed solely for communication purposes. Unauthorized magical correspondence is deemed an act of subversion against the collective security of the realm, as it facilitates covert organization and undermines the Guild's ability to monitor and regulate arcane activities effectively. Violators shall face immediate suspension of their licensure and potential prosecution for breach of the Accords, with penalties escalating based on the gravity of the offense and any resulting harm. Exceptions may be granted only upon petition to the High Court and approval by a supermajority vote, following a thorough review of necessity and safeguards. The Guild retains absolute discretion to interpret and enforce this provision as it deems fit in its sole wisdom, recognizing that magical communication poses unique risks distinct from conventional forms of exchange. All casters are reminded that adherence to these strictures is non-negotiable for maintaining the delicate balance between progress and peril inherent in their practice. Failure to comply may result in severe consequences, including revocation of privileges and imprisonment at the Guild's discretion. The spirit of this clause shall be construed liberally to encompass any novel method of magical transmission not explicitly enumerated herein, ensuring its continued relevance amid rapidly evolving technologies and practices. Casters are urged to exercise utmost caution and restraint regarding their communications channels, prioritizing transparency and accountability over convenience or secrecy. By diligently observing these mandates, they contribute to the stability and integrity of the broader arcane community upon which all rely. Let this warning stand as a final admonition: magical correspondence is a forbidden avenue fraught with danger, to be avoided at all costs unless strictly sanctioned by proper authority. The fate of countless lives may hinge on one's ability to resist temptation and uphold these sacred vows. Stay vigilant, stay humble, and never forget the weight of your responsibilities in this powerful endeavor.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "300.12"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "NEW section §300.12 in this same Part only. Invent a DISTINCT catchline that belongs with these siblings, not a new subject and NOT 'Related Requirements': § 300.1 Schedules of Arts; § 300.2 Necromancy; Unsanctioned Arts; § 300.3 Quiet List Procedure; § 300.4 Reclassification; § 300.5 Research Copies of Quiet Items; § 300.6 Compliance Obligations; § 300.7 Prohibited Correspondence and Magical Transmission; § 300.8 Prohibited Magical Conduct; § 300.9 Definitions and Standards; § 300.10 The Unsanctioned Arts and the Quiet List; § 300.11 Schedules of Magical Arts and Their Classification. First line must be: PAGE Your New Distinct Catchline (5-10 words, specific, no 'Related Requirements')",
      "source": "lmstudio",
