    {
      "cite": "800.12",
      "part": "part_viii",
      "title": "Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation",
          "text": "§ 800.12 Additional Provisions Regarding Unlawful Casting and Confiscation\n\nThis Part shall be read in conjunction with the foundational provisions of these Accords, particularly those concerning the rights of persons under § 1.4 and the principles of due process as outlined in § 1.5. In accordance with established precedent set forth in § 800.9, any unlawful casting of spells or use of prohibited artifacts shall be subject to immediate seizure by authorized Aegis Magi or their designated agents. The confiscated items shall then undergo a thorough appraisal and documentation process pursuant to the protocols specified in § 800.10, with all findings reported directly to the Archmage Sovereign for final disposition.\n\nThe rights of accused casters shall be protected in full measure throughout this procedure, as mandated by § 1.4 and elaborated upon in § 700.6 regarding competent witnesses and expert testimony. Any disputes arising from the confiscation or valuation of items shall be resolved through formal adjudication under Part VII, with appeals handled according to the procedures set forth in § 800.3 and subsequent sections. The burden of proving unlawful activity rests solely upon the accuser, who must meet the high standard of proof beyond reasonable doubt as articulated in § 700.11.\n\nIn cases where the unlawful casting resulted in harm or damage to persons or property, additional civil remedies may be pursued independently under Part VIII, without prejudice to any criminal sanctions imposed pursuant to this Section. The Aegis Magi are authorized to employ reasonable force necessary to effectuate lawful seizures and arrests, subject to the limitations outlined in § 200.3 concerning use of force by peace officers. All actions taken under this authority shall be meticulously recorded and made available for review upon request, ensuring full transparency and accountability throughout the process.\n\nThe provisions herein shall remain in effect until expressly repealed or amended by proper legislative action through the established channels outlined in Part I. Any ambiguities or inconsistencies in their application shall be resolved by reference to the overarching purposes and principles of these Accords as interpreted by the competent authorities vested with such power under this Code. Through diligent adherence to these guidelines, the Guild strives to maintain the delicate balance between enforcing necessary restrictions while safeguarding the fundamental rights of all persons subject to its jurisdiction.\n\nsee § 800.9 Ex Post Facto Prohibition and Retroactive Sanctions\nsee § 1.4 Persons Bound by These Accords\nsee § 700.6 Competent Witnesses and Expert Testimony in Arcane Litigation\nsee § 200.3 Reasonable Force Authorized for Lawful Arrests and Seizures under this Code",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "800.12",
            "1.4",
            "1.5",
            "800.9",
            "800.10",
            "700.6",
            "800.3",
            "700.11",
            "200.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation — Continued",
          "text": "Part 800 - Disciplinary Measures § 800.12 Penalties for Unlawful Casting and Use of Arcane Artifacts\n\nWhereas the unauthorized casting of spells, particularly those deemed dangerous or forbidden by the Accords, constitutes a serious breach of magical ethics and public safety, it is hereby declared that such acts shall be subject to immediate and severe penal sanctions in accordance with this section. Any mage convicted of unlawful spellcasting without proper authorization, permits, or oversight shall be liable for the following cumulative penalties: first, a fine not exceeding one hundred gold pieces per instance of violation, payable to the Guild Treasury; second, mandatory attendance at remedial courses on magical ethics and safety protocols, at the offender's own expense; third, revocation of any existing licenses or permits held by said mage, effective immediately upon conviction.\n\nFurthermore, in cases where unlawful casting results in material damage or bodily harm, the convicted party shall be required to provide full restitution for all losses incurred, including but not limited to property repair, medical expenses, and lost wages suffered by affected parties. Failure to comply with these restitution obligations may result in additional sanctions, up to and including permanent disqualification from practicing magic within the Guild's jurisdiction. It is emphasized that these penalties are without prejudice to any further disciplinary actions that may be deemed appropriate under the circumstances, at the discretion of the Archmage Sovereign or their designated representatives.\n\nThe provisions outlined herein shall apply equally to the use of arcane artifacts and devices in unauthorized contexts, with particular emphasis on those items classified as Schedule II or higher per § 300.12. Possession alone may constitute grounds for investigation, while active deployment without proper authorization warrants immediate arrest and prosecution under this section. The Guild reserves the right to seize and inspect any suspected unlawful magical implements at their discretion, subject only to a warrant signed by two Magisterial Council members.\n\nAny attempt to evade these penalties through subterfuge or false pretenses shall be deemed an aggravating circumstance, potentially leading to enhanced sanctions upon conviction. The burden of proof rests squarely with the accuser, requiring clear and convincing evidence beyond mere allegation before any disciplinary measures may be imposed. However, once guilt is established, the prescribed penalties shall apply automatically unless specifically waived by the convicted party in advance through express written consent.\n\nIt is hereby declared that these provisions shall remain in full force and effect until explicitly amended or repealed by the Archmage Sovereign acting in concert with a two-thirds majority vote of the Magisterial Council. No person or entity shall be exempt from compliance based on status, rank, or claimed immunity whatsoever. The Accords stand as supreme law over all matters pertaining to magical practice, and all must submit thereto without question or exception. So let it be written in the stone tablets of justice, for the protection of society against the perils of unchecked arcane power.\n\nsee § 800.1 Disciplinary Authority; § 300.12 Schedule II Restrictions; § 500.1 Unauthorized Casting Prohibited; § 600.9 Contractual Liability for Magical Acts",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "800.12",
            "300.12",
            "800.1",
            "500.1",
            "600.9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "§ 800.12 Evidence Standard for Unlawful Casting Allegations; Burden of Proof in Disciplinary Proceedings Under the Accords, any allegation of unlawful casting must be supported by clear and convincing evidence, as determined by a Quorum of the Autumnwood Accords Desk or its duly appointed adjudicators. The burden of proof rests solely on the accuser, who shall present all relevant testimony, documentation, and magical analysis necessary to establish guilt beyond a reasonable doubt. In no event shall mere suspicion, rumor, or unsubstantiated claim suffice to justify disciplinary action against any member of the Guild.\n\nShould an accused mage fail to appear for trial without valid excuse, the Desk may proceed in their absence, presuming guilt unless contradicted by substantial exculpatory evidence. Conversely, if the accuser fails to meet the requisite evidentiary threshold, all charges shall be dismissed with prejudice, and any pending sanctions vacated forthwith. It is imperative that due process be scrupulously observed at every stage of the disciplinary proceeding, lest the integrity of the Accords themselves be compromised by miscarriage of justice or arbitrary enforcement.\n\nThe Desk retains sole authority to determine what constitutes \"unlawful casting\" under any given circumstance, guided by the spirit and letter of these Articles. This includes, but is not limited to, unauthorized use of forbidden schools, excessive power consumption, reckless endangerment of persons or property, and violation of specific provisions herein. Discretionary judgment shall be exercised in accordance with established precedent and principles of fairness, always mindful of the delicate balance between maintaining public safety and preserving individual liberties.\n\nAny attempt to circumvent these provisions through deception, fabrication of evidence, or tampering with records shall be deemed a grave offense warranting immediate investigation and appropriate sanctions upon confirmation. Such malfeasance strikes at the heart of the Accords' foundational tenets, undermining trust in both the Guild's regulatory framework and its commitment to impartial justice. To tolerate even the slightest degree of corruption would be to invite chaos and anarchy into our midst—a fate we must all work tirelessly to avoid.\n\nIn sum, then, let it be understood that the rules set forth herein are not mere suggestions but binding mandates upon all who dwell within this realm's magical sphere. By acceding to these obligations voluntarily or through force of circumstance, every caster implicitly accepts their full force and effect, for better or worse. May we therefore proceed henceforth with renewed dedication to upholding the highest ideals of our noble profession, guided always by wisdom, integrity, and an unwavering reverence for the mysteries that bind us all in this vast tapestry of existence.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "800.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation — Continued — Administration",
          "text": "Where unlawful casting occurs in public or causes demonstrable harm, the Desk shall confiscate all magical implements directly involved, retaining them as evidence until further order. Any such items deemed inherently dangerous require permanent storage under lock and key; lesser artifacts may be returned upon proof of safekeeping protocols. All confiscated materials must be inventoried and logged into the Central Registry within seven days, with copies furnished to the accused party and relevant oversight bodies.\n\nUnlawful casting by non-casters triggers enhanced penalties, including mandatory registration as a subject of future monitoring and prohibition from possessing magical items without explicit permission. First-time offenders may opt for community service in lieu of fines, provided they undergo successful completion of an Arcane Conduct Course approved by the Conservators. Repeat violations warrant progressive sanctions up to permanent exile from Autumnwood territory.\n\nIn cases involving commercial entities, regulatory audits are mandated with full access to all records and operations. Failure to comply results in immediate suspension of licenses until satisfactory remediation is demonstrated. Repeated noncompliance leads to revocation without recourse. All findings and actions shall be publicly posted for transparency purposes only; no defamatory language permitted under threat of legal action.\n\nThe Desk maintains sole authority to determine appropriate sanctions based on severity and circumstances, with input from Conservator and Innovator representatives where relevant. Final decisions rest with the Archmage Sovereign upon recommendation from a specially convened panel. All disciplinary measures must be proportionate and serve both punishment and rehabilitation goals equally. Appeals may be filed within thirty days under established procedures; otherwise rulings stand final and binding.\n\nThis provision reflects the Guild's unwavering commitment to maintaining order while allowing for individualized justice in each case. Strict adherence ensures fairness across all enforcement actions and preserves public confidence in the system. Any deviations require explicit authorization from a majority vote of the full Accords Assembly. Unauthorized modifications are null and void ab initio.\n\nsee § 100.6 Delegation to Clerks; § 200.11 Schedules of Magical Arts and Their Classification; § 300.12 Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission; § 800.5 Pocket-Prison Procedure; § 900.12 Additional Provisions Regarding Arcane Field Operations and Conduct",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "100.6",
            "200.11",
            "300.12",
            "800.5",
            "900.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation — Continued — Administrat",
          "text": "The confiscation of magical items, artifacts, and implements associated with unlawful casting is governed by strict protocols to ensure their proper handling and eventual disposition. Upon seizure of any prohibited item, it shall be immediately inventoried in the presence of witnesses and sealed within a lead-lined container to prevent accidental activation or exposure to unauthorized individuals. Such contraband shall then be delivered to the custody of an Aegis Magi for secure storage pending further review by the Disciplinary Council. The Council shall determine whether each item constitutes evidence of a crime, a tool used in commission thereof, or merely incidental property owned by the accused but misused by others. Items classified as direct instruments of unlawful magic may be permanently destroyed under supervised conditions to eliminate future risk. Those deemed salvageable for lawful use shall undergo thorough screening and certification before being returned to their rightful owners or transferred to approved researchers for study. Any proceeds from the liquidation of seized assets pursuant to court order shall be remitted to the Guild's General Fund, less applicable fees and expenses. The Council retains broad discretion to impose additional administrative penalties as it deems necessary to protect public safety and maintain the integrity of arcane practices within society at large. These measures are designed to dismantle criminal networks' material resources while preserving legitimate interests where feasible. Failure to comply with confiscation directives may result in enhanced sanctions against non-compliant parties, including suspension of privileges and heightened surveillance. All actions taken under this provision shall be meticulously documented for potential judicial scrutiny and historical record-keeping purposes. Nothing herein abrogates existing authorities vested in law enforcement agencies regarding seizure of contraband under applicable statutes. The Guild asserts sole jurisdiction over matters pertaining specifically to magical items seized during Disciplinary proceedings, subject to coordination with relevant civil authorities as mutually agreed upon from time to time.\n\n§ 800.12 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation — Continued — Administration\nsee § 800.7 Related Requirements; under § 1301.2 Penalties for Violations of Disciplinary Orders\nsee also §§ 200.6 Prohibitions on Dangerous Magical Acts, 400.9 Restrictions on Experimental Research and Development",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "800.12",
            "800.7",
            "1301.2",
            "200.6"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation — Continued — Oversight",
          "text": "§ 800.12 Disposition of Seized Magical Artifacts and Components. Any magical artifact, component, or tool seized in connection with an unlawful casting shall be held in trust by the Archmage Sovereign until such time as it may be lawfully disposed of. The Archmage Sovereign shall determine the appropriate course of action, which may include destruction, confiscation for public use, return to lawful ownership upon proof of innocence, or sale at public auction with proceeds donated to charitable causes benefiting students and apprentices in need. No seized item shall be privately sold or traded by any Guild official without express written authorization from the Archmage Sovereign. All dispositions must be recorded in the permanent archives of the Autumnwood Hall under penalty of severe sanctions. The Archmage Sovereign retains sole discretion to alter these provisions as deemed necessary for the protection of public safety and the integrity of magical practice within the Guild's jurisdiction.\"\n\n\"see § 800.10 Disposition of Confiscated Items; § 1201.10 Extra-Territorial Jurisdiction and Planar Tolls; § 1401.10 Historical Annotations\"",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "800.12",
            "800.10",
            "1201.10",
            "1401.10"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "brief": "NEW section §800.12 in this same Part only. Invent a DISTINCT catchline that belongs with these siblings, not a new subject and NOT 'Related Requirements': § 800.1 Discipline; Range of Sanctions; § 800.2 Paradox Trial Procedure; § 800.3 Seal of Silence; Duration and Review; § 800.4 Duel Stakes Converted to Fees; § 800.5 Pocket-Prison Procedure; § 800.6 Ancillary Obligations; § 800.7 PART 800 - DISCIPLINARY MEASURES § 800.7 Related Requirements; § 1301.2 Penaltie; § 800.8 800.9 Penalties for Unlawful Casting and Use of Arcane Artifacts; § 800.9 Ex Post Facto Prohibition and Retroactive Sanctions; § 800.10 Disposition of Confiscated Items; § 800.11 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation. First line must be: PAGE Your New Distinct Catchline (5-10 words, specific, no 'Related Requirements')",
