    {
      "cite": "1401.12",
      "part": "part_xiv",
      "title": "Preservation of Canonical Continuity and Scriptural Integrity",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Preservation of Canonical Continuity and Scriptural Integrity",
          "text": "The preservation of the primary texts of the Autumnwood Accords shall be maintained as the foundational cornerstone of all internal adjudication within the Guild. These provisions ensure that despite the fluctuating tensions between the Conservators and the Innovators, the core tenets regarding stable magic remain immutable. All archival entries must reflect the original intent of the High Council as established during the founding era in the Midlands. Any modification to the core text requires a unanimous consensus from both Archmage Theron’s faction and Janna Brightspark’s faction, mediated by the Office of Archmage Veyra. Under § 1.2, the Sovereign holds the ultimate authority to interpret these nuances when internal disputes arise regarding the definition of \"stability\" versus \"innovation.\"\n\nThe Clerk of the Accords Desk shall maintain a strict separation between historical commentary and active law. While the Innovators may advocate for the expansion of research parameters, such requests must be filed as petitions for new permits under § 400.11 rather than attempts to rewrite existing statutes. No scholar or practitioner shall attempt to bypass established restrictions by citing \"experimental\" status unless they possess a valid permit from the Office of Archmage Veyra. Furthermore, any documentation pertaining to the Quiet List must be handled with extreme discretion; the disclosure of such contents in public forums, including common taverns or marketplace squares, is strictly prohibited and shall result in an immediate referral to the Paradox Trial as outlined under § 1301.12.\n\nFurthermore, all notations regarding external entities, specifically those associated with the Iron Mandate or the Regal Empire, must be clearly demarcated from internal Guild law. The Accords do not recognize the jurisdiction of the Iron Legion within the Autumn Wood boundaries, and any attempt to conflate these legal systems shall be deemed a violation of § 1.5. Any material received from external allies, such as the Goodstyle Artisans, regarding trade or shared resources must be vetted through the appropriate petition process before being integrated into the internal archives. Such materials are not considered \"official\" until they have been stamped by the Office of Archmage Veyra to ensure compliance with § 1.9.\n\nFinally, any research involving the Heartstone or associated rifts shall be governed by specialized protocols for high-risk zones. These areas are strictly monitored; unauthorized exploration or mapping without a specific charter is prohibited. A \"One-T\" cartography certificate is a mere map of geographical features and does not constitute a license to enter restricted arcane zones. Any practitioner found attempting to breach these boundaries shall be subject to the penalties for unlicensed activity as defined in § 200.11. All such incidents must be reported immediately to the Aegis Magi for containment, ensuring that no \"contagion\" of uncontrolled magic spreads beyond the designated survey perimeters under § 1101.11.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1.2",
            "400.11",
            "1301.12",
            "1.5",
