        },
        {
          "heading": "Records of Forbidden Knowledge and the Quiet List",
          "text": "The preservation of arcane stability within the Autumnwood Accords necessitates a rigorous distinction between public academic inquiry and the clandestine maintenance of restricted truths. Under § 1.6, certain arcane phenomena are deemed inherently volatile; therefore, any knowledge pertaining to such instabilities is subject to the protocols of the Quiet List. It is strictly forbidden for any member of the Guild, including those within the Innovator faction, to recite or broadcast contents of the Quiet List in public forums, taverns, or common gathering spaces. Such acts are considered a breach of scriptural integrity and may result in immediate disciplinary review under § 1301.12 regarding the assessment of penalties for unauthorized disclosure.\n\nThe sanctity of these records is maintained to prevent the accidental destabilization of local reality. While the Innovators may seek to expand the boundaries of permissible research, such endeavors must remain within the confines of supervised laboratories as outlined in § 400.11. Any information deemed \"volatile\" by the Conservators shall be moved into the Quiet List archives. These records are not intended for public consumption nor are they part of the standard curriculum; rather, they serve as a protective barrier against the erosion of canonical continuity. Unauthorized dissemination of these secrets constitutes a direct violation of the Accord's intent to stabilize the Midlands region.\n\nFurthermore, any individual found in possession of materials from the Quiet List without the express authorization of Archmage Veyra shall be subject to the scrutiny of the Aegis Magi. Under § 100.2, only designated officials may speak for the Guild regarding these specific matters. Any attempt to commodify or trade information contained within the Quiet List is strictly prohibited and shall be treated as a felony of the highest order. Such actions are viewed not merely as a breach of internal policy but as an affront to the foundational safety of the realm, potentially necessitating a Paradox Trial under § 1301.12 if the disclosure leads to a localized arcane rupture or significant ontological shift.\n\nIn the event that a member of the Innovator faction believes a piece of information currently held on the Quiet List should be reclassified for study, they must petition the Conservators through the proper channels established in § 400.12. No independent determination of \"safety\" is permitted by individual mages. The integrity of the script is paramount; therefore, any unauthorized modification or publication of restricted scripts shall result in the immediate revocation of research permits and potential seizure of materials under § 800.12. All members are reminded that the Quiet List remains a non-public catalogue to ensure that the boundaries between safe practice and existential risk remain clearly defined for all practitioners within the Autumnwood Accord.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
