        {
          "heading": "Protocol for the Maintenance of Restricted Archives",
          "text": "The preservation of arcane continuity within the Autumnwood Accords requires that all records pertaining to forbidden methodologies remain strictly sequestered from public and non-sanctioned inquiry. This protocol establishes the boundaries between academic exploration and the preservation of institutional stability. Under § 1.6, any material deemed \"forbidden\" specifically refers to schools of magic—such as necromancy or blood-binding—that have been formally struck from the permitted curriculum by the Conservators. The records of these specific practices are not merely suppressed; they are archived under high-security seals to ensure that their existence does not contaminate the public consciousness or the safety of the Midlands.\n\nAny mage seeking information regarding these sequestered archives must first establish a standing for restricted research as defined under § 400.11. Such inquiries are subject to the oversight of the Innovator faction, who may grant access only if the request is deemed to have a practical application that does not threaten the primary stability of the Accord. However, even with such authorization, the seeker must adhere to the restrictions regarding the dissemination of these findings. The disclosure of forbidden knowledge in common spaces—including but not limited to taverns, marketplaces, or public forums—is strictly prohibited and may result in immediate disciplinary action under § 1301.12.\n\nFurthermore, all internal records pertaining to the Quiet List are exempt from general transparency requirements. The Quiet List is a non-public catalog of specific arcane anomalies and historical incidents that must never be recited or transcribed in an unofficial capacity. Access to this list is restricted to high-ranking members of the Accord and the Aegis Magi. Any individual found reciting entries from the Quiet List in a public setting shall be deemed to have willfully breached the sanctity of the records, potentially triggering a mandatory review by the Office of the Archmage Sovereign as outlined under § 100.11.\n\nThe integrity of these archives is maintained through physical and metaphysical seals. Any attempt to bypass these seals without proper authorization from the Archive Custodians constitutes an act of unauthorized field operation. Such actions are subject to prosecution under § 500.12, where the intruder may face immediate seizure of equipment and potential summary judgment by their peers. The distinction between a legitimate scholarly inquiry and a breach of security is governed by the principles of construction found in § 1.7; any action that compromises the containment of forbidden knowledge shall be viewed as an intentional violation of the Accord's core tenets regarding safety and stability.\n\nAll personnel involved in the handling of these documents must ensure that their work does not inadvertently lead to a breach of the prohibition on magical correspondence and transmission. Under § 300.12, any digital or magically-transmitted data containing fragments of forbidden lore is subject to immediate interception and neutralization by the Aegis Magi. The continuity of the Accord relies upon the isolation of these elements from the common sphere; therefore, the preservation of scriptural integrity is not merely a matter of archiving history, but a vital defense against the erosion of current magical stability as mandated under § 1.5.",
          "key": "c",
