        {
          "heading": "Sanctity of the Quiet List and Restricted Archive Protocols",
          "text": "The integrity of the Autumnwood Accords relies upon the strict sequestration of certain arcane truths from the public consciousness. Under § 1.6, those specific matters deemed hazardous to the stability of the Midlands or the safety of the common populace are codified within the \"Quiet List.\" It is strictly forbidden for any member of the guild, including those of the Innovator faction, to recite, transcribe, or broadcast the contents of the Quiet List in public venues. This prohibition extends to all non-magical settings, such as taverns, marketplaces, or common thoroughfares. Any breach of this silence constitutes a primary offense against the sanctity of the Order, and shall be subject to immediate investigation by the Aegis Magi under § 800.12.\n\nThe maintenance of these records is governed by specific protocols for the Restricted Archives. Only those individuals holding a high-level clearance, as defined under § 400.12, may access the physical repositories where forbidden knowledge is housed. Access to such materials does not grant the holder the right to disseminate the information; rather, it imposes an additional burden of secrecy upon the practitioner. Any scholar seeking to explore \"Restricted Research\" must obtain express permission from both the Conservators and the Innovators as mandated under § 400.11. Failure to adhere to these internal oversight protocols may result in the immediate revocation of research permits and the initiation of a Paradox Trial, as outlined in the penal procedures of § 1301.12.\n\nFurthermore, any material identified as \"forbidden\" by Archmage Theron’s conservative mandate must be physically sealed using official guild stamps as defined under § 1.9. These seals are not merely symbolic; they represent a legal barrier against the unauthorized flow of volatile information. Should a seal be broken without a notarized warrant from the Office of the Sovereign, the perpetrator shall be deemed to have committed an act of intentional breach. Such actions may result in the offender being cast into a pocket-prison for the duration of their sentence. All inquiries regarding the contents of these archives must be directed through official channels; no private inquiry or informal request shall be entertained by the guards of the archive, as per the standards of § 100.2.\n\nThe preservation of canonical continuity ensures that the laws governing magic remain stable and consistent over time. This means that while the Innovators may push for new experiments, they may not do so in a manner that undermines the foundational protections established in the earlier Accords. Any proposed change to the \"Quiet List\" or the status of forbidden schools must be submitted to Archmage Veyra for mediation before it can be codified. The use of unauthorized symbols or the inclusion of non-sanctioned artifacts within the archives is strictly prohibited under § 1.7. All records must remain consistent with the established definitions provided in § 1.6, ensuring that the law remains a coherent body rather than a collection of contradictory mandates.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
