      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Interpretative Nuance and Lexicographical Consistency",
          "text": "The provisions set forth within this Codex shall be interpreted by the Autumnwood Accords Desk with strict adherence to the definitions established in § 1.6. Any ambiguity arising from the linguistic construction of a specific mandate shall be resolved by applying the principles of Aggregation of Conduct as defined under § 1.7, ensuring that no single act is viewed in isolation but rather as part of a continuous pattern of arcane behavior. The Clerk’s Office maintains that the intent of the Accord is the preservation of stability; therefore, where a literal interpretation would lead to an absurdity that threatens the equilibrium of the Midlands, the more restrictive interpretation favored by the Conservators shall prevail unless specifically waived under § 1.12.\n\nFurthermore, all references to \"Official Conduct\" within these pages are governed by the standards of those identified as Persons Bound under § 1.4. No individual may claim immunity from the Accord's scrutiny based on personal reputation or external accolades; every mage, whether a high-ranking Innovator or a novice practitioner, is bound by the literal text of the law. In instances where a legal conflict arises between a local ordinance and an Autumnwood mandate, the hierarchy of authority established in § 1.11 shall be invoked to determine the prevailing jurisdiction. The Clerk’s Office does not recognize external treaties as valid unless they have been formally incorporated into this Codex through a registered amendment.\n\nIn matters concerning the physical manifestation of magic, any occurrence that results in a tangible alteration of local reality must be reported to the Office of Archmage Veyra for assessment. Such alterations are subject to the scrutiny of the Aegis Magi to ensure no breach of the prohibited schools has occurred. Should an act be deemed potentially hazardous, it shall fall under the purview of standard safety protocols; however, any intentional deviation from these protocols constitutes a violation of the primary intent of § 1.7. The Clerk’s role is to maintain the integrity of the text, and thus, no oral testimony or \"common understanding\" may supersede the written word as codified in § 1.1.\n\nFinally, all technical terms regarding the physical containment of magical energy are governed by the specifications found in § 1.9. Any device, sigil, or ward used to contain a rift or stabilize a breach must meet the criteria for a recognized Seal. If a seal is deemed insufficient or intentionally bypassed, the practitioner shall be subject to immediate investigation under the protocols for unlicensed behavior. The Clerk’s Desk maintains that linguistic clarity is the primary defense against arcane instability; thus, any colloquialism used in public discourse regarding these laws is not considered a valid defense during an inquiry. All legal proceedings must rely solely on the codified language found within this volume and its linked sections.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
            "1.7",
