    {
      "cite": "100.13",
      "part": "part_i",
      "title": "Protocols for Mediation and Inter-Factional Arbitration",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Protocols for Mediation and Inter-Factional Arbitration",
          "text": "The Office of the Archmage Sovereign shall serve as the primary adjudicatory body in matters concerning internal disputes between the Conservator and Innovator factions. Under § 100.11, the Sovereign maintains the ultimate authority to mediate conflicts regarding the definition of \"Restricted Research\" versus \"Forbidden Schools.\" When a dispute arises from the interpretation of the Autumnwood Accords regarding new magical methodologies, the matter shall be brought before the Archmage Veyra for a definitive ruling. The presence of the Archmage’s seal signifies that a mediation has been concluded and the resulting decree is binding upon all members of the Guild, regardless of their primary affiliation or factional allegiance.\n\nIn instances where the Innovator leadership, under Janna Brightspark, seeks to expand the boundaries of permissible research, the petition must be submitted in writing to the Office of the Archmage Sovereign. Such petitions shall undergo a period of review wherein the Conservator leadership, under Archmage Theron, may submit counter-arguments regarding the stability of existing arcane foundations. During this period, all contested magical practices shall remain under the supervision of the Aegis Magi. Pursuant to § 1.6, any terms involving \"stability\" shall be interpreted in favor of the preservation of the current status quo unless a formal variance is granted by the Sovereign.\n\nThe role of the Aegis Magi remains strictly enforcement-oriented; they possess no deliberative power and shall not participate in the debate of new research methodologies. Their duty is to ensure that while a dispute is pending, no unauthorized field usage occurs. Any mage found conducting experiments outside of the established parameters during an active mediation period shall be subject to immediate seizure under § 800.11. The Aegis Magi are tasked with maintaining the physical and metaphysical integrity of the Autumn Wood until a final decree is issued by the Archmage Sovereign.\n\nFurthermore, any diplomatic outreach involving external entities, such as the Goodstyle Artisans or other non-aligned parties, must be conducted through the proper channels established in § 100.7. The Office of the Archmage Sovereign shall not recognize agreements made with outside parties that bypass the internal arbitration process. All negotiations regarding shared resources or collaborative research projects must be codified within the Autumnwood Accords to ensure consistency. Any breach of these protocols may result in a formal review of the offending party's credentials and standing under § 1.4, ensuring that only those who respect the hierarchy of the Accord remain in good standing with the Guild.\n\nShould an arbitration reach a stalemate, the Office of the Archmage Sovereign shall invoke the emergency sitting provisions as outlined in § 100.8 to resolve the deadlock. In such cases, the High Council of Peers may be convened to provide a binding vote on the matter of research eligibility. Any resulting decisions shall be recorded in the official logs of the Desk under § 100.4. All participants are reminded that while the internal debate between the Conservators and Innovators is vigorous, the final word rests with the Sovereign as defined by the core tenets of the Accord.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "100.11",
            "1.6",
            "800.11",
            "100.7",
            "1.4",
            "100.8",
            "100.4"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Resolution of Internal Schisms and Factional Deadlock",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords recognize the inherent friction between the traditionalist Conservators, led by Archmage Theron, and the radical Innovators, under the leadership of Janna Brightspark. To maintain the stability of the Midlands and ensure that the flow of magic remains regulated rather than volatile, certain protocols are established for the resolution of internal schisms. When a dispute regarding the classification of arcane arts or the permission of restricted research arises between these two primary factions, it shall be moved to the Office of the Archmage Sovereign for formal mediation. During such proceedings, the conflicting parties must submit their grievances in writing, ensuring that all technical specifications of the magic in question are clearly delineated as defined under § 1.6.\n\nIn instances where a deadlock persists between the Conservators and the Innovators regarding the boundaries of \"acceptable\" research, the Archmage Sovereign shall act as the ultimate arbiter. The sovereign's role is to weigh the necessity of innovation against the imperative of stability. If a proposed project falls under the purview of restricted research but lacks a specific prohibition from the established list of forbidden schools, the matter may be granted provisional status under § 1.12, provided that the Innovators can prove sufficient containment measures are in place. Any dispute regarding the physical safety of the Autumn Wood during such experiments shall be referred to the Aegis Magi for immediate oversight and enforcement of containment perimeters.\n\nShould a deadlock occur specifically concerning the inclusion of new arcane techniques into the official records of the Guild, the matter shall be subjected to an internal review by the Council of Peers. This process is distinct from external arbitration; it is a technical evaluation of whether the new magic poses a threat to the structural integrity of current wards or if it constitutes a breach of the sacred pacts. All participants in such a debate must adhere to the standards of professional conduct and are prohibited from utilizing aggressive magical discharge during deliberation, as such actions would constitute a violation of the protocols for peaceful mediation.\n\nFurthermore, when an external entity—such as the Goodstyle Artisans or any other recognized affiliate—is involved in a contract that requires both Innovator techniques and Conservator safety standards, the Archmage Sovereign shall issue a binding decree to resolve conflicting requirements. The intent of this arbitration is to ensure that the Guild remains unified in its outward presentation while managing internal ideological differences. Any failure by a faction leader to submit to the mediation of the Archmage Sovereign may result in a formal inquiry into their standing within the Guild, and potential referral for a Paradox Trial as outlined under § 1301.12. All arbitration records shall be filed with the Autumnwood Accords Desk and remain confidential from public dissemination, consistent with the protections afforded to internal governance.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
            "1.12",
            "1301.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Resolution of Internal Schisms and Factional Deadlock — Continued",
          "text": "The arbitration of internal disputes between the Conservator and Innovator factions shall be governed by the primary mandate of stability as defined under § 1.6. When the divergent philosophies regarding \"Forbidden Schools\" and \"Restricted Research\" result in a procedural impasse, the Office of Archmage Sovereignty shall invoke mediation protocols to prevent the degradation of the Autumnwood Accords. Such deadlocks are specifically addressed when the Innovator faction seeks expansion of research boundaries that would otherwise jeopardize the established safety protocols of the Conservators. In these instances, the dispute shall be moved to a closed chamber for deliberation by the Archmage Sovereign, whose role is to ensure that neither radical experimentation nor extreme traditionalism compromises the integrity of the realm’s magical weave.\n\nDuring periods of active deadlock, the Aegis Magi are mandated to maintain a neutral stance and may only enforce those measures explicitly codified in § 100.1. Any attempt by the Aegis Magi to favor one faction over another during an arbitration phase shall be grounds for immediate disciplinary review. If the Archmage Sovereign cannot reach a consensus between the Innovators, led by Janna Brightspark, and the Conservators, led by Archmage Theron, the matter shall be referred to a secondary council of peers for a formal determination. This process ensures that the internal friction of the Guild does not leak into public-facing operations or compromise the safety of the Midlands.\n\nIn cases where an Innovator’s proposed research is deemed \"high-risk\" under § 400.11, but the Conservators refuse to grant a prohibition, the Archmage Sovereign may issue a Temporary Stay of Action. This stay allows for continued study only within a localized, magically-shielded environment, thereby satisfying the Innovator’s requirement for advancement while upholding the Conservator’s demand for containment. All such stays must be documented in the official records as per § 100.4. Furthermore, any arbitration resulting from an unauthorized field use—such as those involving the growth of entities on Markop or other non-sanctioned sites—shall be subject to the penalties outlined in § 500.11.\n\nShould a deadlock persist for more than three lunar cycles, the matter may be escalated to a formal inquiry. During this period, all related research permits are suspended under § 400.12 until a definitive ruling is issued. The parties involved must adhere to the standards of professional conduct and shall not engage in public disputes or \"spirited\" debates in common areas, as such behavior violates the protocols for internal governance. All arbitration proceedings are confidential; any leak of these discussions to external entities, including members of the Silver Flame or the Iron Legion, will result in a violation of the confidentiality clauses found in § 1.5.\n\nThe ultimate goal of these mediation protocols is to preserve the unity of the Autumnwood Accords against external pressures from rival powers like the Regal Empire. By internalizing the friction between the Conservators and Innovators through structured arbitration, the Guild ensures that its primary mission—the stewardship of magic—remains uninterrupted by internal discord. Any breach of these mediation procedures shall be handled as a violation of administrative law rather than an act of magical misconduct, unless the breach involves the direct use of unauthorized spells during the deliberation process, in which case § 800.11 shall apply.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
            "100.1",
            "400.11",
            "100.4",
            "500.11",
            "400.12",
            "1.5",
            "800.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Resolution of Internal Schisms and Factional Deadlock — Continued — Continued",
          "text": "The resolution of internal schisms between the Conservative and Innovator factions shall be governed by the primary mandate of stability as defined under § 1.6. In instances where a deadlock occurs regarding the classification of a new arcane methodology, the Office of the Archmage Sovereign serves as the ultimate arbiter. During such periods of deadlock, all research activities involving contested methodologies are subject to immediate stay of execution until a formal arbitration hearing is convened. Such hearings shall be conducted within the Autumn Wood and may include testimony from representatives of both the Conservators and the Innovators, ensuring that the dual perspectives on safety versus advancement are weighed by the Sovereign.\n\nWhere a deadlock persists despite mediation, the Aegis Magi are authorized to implement a temporary containment protocol. Under § 1.9, any magical artifacts or ritual sites involved in the disputed research shall be sealed until the arbitration is concluded. This ensures that the physical integrity of the Midlands remains uncompromised by the internal ideological friction of the Guild's leadership. The Aegis Magi do not possess the authority to decide the merits of the magic itself, but rather to ensure that the process of deliberation does not result in a breach of safety standards or public hazard.\n\nIn cases where the Innovators seek to bypass standard oversight under § 400.11 through claims of \"urgent necessity,\" the Sovereign may grant a Provisional Research Permit. Such permits are strictly limited in scope and duration, and any deviation from the granted parameters shall result in immediate disciplinary review under § 800.12. The issuance of such permits is intended to balance the radical ambitions of Janna Brightspark’s faction with the cautionary requirements of Archmage Theron’s stance on forbidden schools.\n\nFurthermore, if a dispute arises concerning the inclusion of a new school into the \"Quiet List,\" the matter shall be moved to a closed-door session of the Accord's Council. During these proceedings, members are prohibited from disclosing the contents of the list in any public forum or tavern, as mandated by § 1.6. Any mage found to have leaked information regarding the internal deliberations of the Accord during a period of deadlock shall face immediate referral for a Paradox Trial under § 100.3.\n\nFinal determinations made by the Sovereign are binding upon all members of both factions. Once a resolution is reached, the resulting decree must be recorded in the official logs to ensure that the decision serves as a precedent for future disputes regarding internal schisms. No scholar or practitioner may contest the validity of an arbitration ruling once it has been sealed and entered into the archives. Failure to comply with these mediation protocols shall result in the revocation of specialized research privileges and potential referral for seal magic application under § 1.9.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
            "1.9",
            "400.11",
            "800.12",
            "100.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Resolution of Internal Schisms and Factional Deadlock — Finalized Procedures",
          "text": "In the event that the ideological divergence between the Conservators and the Innovators results in a functional impasse regarding the interpretation of the Autumnwood Accords, the Office of Archmage Sovereignty shall invoke the protocols for mediation. Such a deadlock is defined as any situation wherein the internal factions are unable to reach a consensus on the legality of research parameters or the classification of arcane arts under § 300.11. When such a stalemate occurs, the matter shall be elevated from the respective factional leadership—specifically Archmage Theron and Janna Brightspark—to the mediation desk for binding arbitration. Under these circumstances, the Sovereign’s role as defined in § 100.1 is to provide a neutral adjudicative ground where the conflicting priorities of stability and advancement may be weighed against the core tenets of the Accord.\n\nDuring a declared state of deadlock, all immediate operations regarding the disputed magic must be suspended until a resolution is reached. The Aegis Magi are tasked with maintaining the status quo of the local area during this period, ensuring that no unauthorized field casting occurs as prohibited by § 200.11. If the dispute involves the expansion of \"Restricted Research\" boundaries, the mediation shall focus on whether the proposed innovation poses a risk to the structural integrity of the current magical weave. In cases where the Innovators seek permission for high-risk experiments that the Conservators deem hazardous, the mediator may impose a condition of oversight as outlined in § 400.12. The intent is to ensure that safety protocols are never sacrificed for speed, nor innovation stifled by excessive caution.\n\nShould the mediation fail to produce a consensus within three lunar cycles, the dispute shall be moved to a formal hearing before a council of peers. This process may culminate in a Paradox Trial if the deadlock was caused by an individual's willful defiance of established safety protocols or unauthorized experimentation. Under § 1.4, all participants in such a trial are bound by the conduct of the Accord, and any violation of these procedures during arbitration may result in the immediate sealing of magic for the offending party as per § 800.11. The mediation desk shall maintain an official record of all arguments presented by both factions to ensure that historical precedents are preserved for future arbitration.\n\nFurthermore, no external influences or pressures from outside entities—specifically those associated with the Iron Mandate or other rival organizations—may influence the internal arbitration process. Any attempt to introduce foreign political interests into a deadlock regarding the Autumnwood Accords shall be viewed as an act of subversion and may lead to the revocation of special permissions. All final decisions made during mediation are binding on both the Conservators and the Innovators, and any subsequent deviation from these settled points will be prosecuted under § 700.11. The goal of these procedures is to preserve the unity of the Guild by ensuring that internal friction does not compromise the safety of the realm or the sanctity of the Accord.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "300.11",
            "100.1",
            "200.11",
            "400.12",
            "1.4",
            "800.11",
            "700.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Mandated Procedures for Resolving Internal Schisms and Factional Deadlock",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords recognize that the internal stability of the Guild is paramount to the preservation of arcane order within the Midlands. Given the inherent ideological friction between the Conservators, who prioritize the containment of volatile magic under Archmage Theron’s direction, and the Innovators, who seek expansion under Janna Brightspark’s leadership, a formal mechanism for arbitration is required when such disputes reach an impasse. When a disagreement regarding the classification of new research or the enforcement of safety protocols results in a legislative standstill, the matter shall be elevated to a Formal Arbitration. During such periods of deadlock, the primary objective is to ensure that neither faction can unilaterally bypass established restrictions under § 300.11.\n\nIn cases where the Innovators propose research that the Conservators deem hazardous, but which falls within the scope of potentially beneficial advancement, the Archmage Veyra shall act as the primary mediator. Under § 100.2, only authorized voices may speak for the Guild; however, during a declared deadlock, the Sovereign’s mediation serves to balance the competing interests of both factions before they escalate into open internal conflict. If a compromise cannot be reached through direct negotiation between Archmage Theron and Janna Brightspark, the matter is subjected to a Review of Intent. This review examines whether the proposed magic violates the fundamental prohibitions outlined in § 200.11. If the research remains within permissible bounds but merely challenges traditional methodology, it may proceed under strictly monitored conditions as defined by the oversight protocols in § 400.12.\n\nShould a deadlock persist regarding the interpretation of safety margins or the scope of \"Restricted Research,\" the Aegis Magi shall be deployed to maintain neutrality and physical security during the deliberation. The Aegis are tasked with ensuring that no magical surge resulting from heated debate compromises the sanctity of the Autumn Wood. Furthermore, any action taken by an individual mage during a period of deadlock that deviates from the established status quo may be subject to investigation under § 700.11. A failure to reach a consensus on high-risk projects will result in a mandatory cooling-off period, wherein all research activities on the disputed topic are suspended until a joint committee can draft a revised proposal for submission to the Archmage's desk.\n\nFinally, if internal arbitration fails to resolve a dispute regarding the \"Unsanctioned Arts,\" the matter shall be immediately moved to the disciplinary phase. Any mage found attempting to circumvent the mediation process through unauthorized experimentation or by pressuring the Aegis Magi may be subjected to the legal determinations of § 800.11. Such actions are viewed as a breach of the internal trust of the Accords and may lead to an immediate referral for a Paradox Trial under the penalties established in § 1301.12. All documentation regarding these proceedings shall be recorded by the Desk, ensuring that no private agreement between the Innovators and Conservators supersedes the overarching requirements of the Accord.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "300.11",
            "100.2",
            "200.11",
            "400.12",
            "700.11",
            "800.11",
            "1301.12"
          ]
        }
