          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Remediation of Spontaneous Weave-Fractures",
          "text": "Upon the occurrence of a spontaneous weave-fracture, any mage present within the immediate vicinity is mandated to initiate containment procedures as outlined under § 500.12 regarding arcane field operations. A fracture shall be defined as an uncontrolled rupture in the local magical fabric, often resulting from unauthorized experimentation or the failure of a ritualistic seal. In such instances, the primary objective of the responding mage is the stabilization of the breach to prevent the migration of external energies into the terrestrial plane. Any practitioner identified under § 1.4 who encounters such an event must immediately broadcast a distress signal to the nearest Aegis station; however, they shall not attempt to \"mop up\" or fully seal the fracture without explicit authorization from the Office of Archmage Veyra as described in § 100.11.\n\nFailure to contain a known fracture within three minutes of its manifestation may result in the imposition of a Paradox Trial under § 900.12, particularly if the breach is caused by negligence or willful disregard for the safety of non-casters. When a breach is confirmed as \"volatile,\" the responding party must establish a perimeter and apply stabilizing wards to prevent the growth of arcane bleed-through. If these measures fail, the area shall be declared a \"Zone of Contagion\" under § 1101.12, necessitating a full evacuation of civilians and the sealing of the site by specialized containment teams. The presence of any unauthorized artifacts or experimental components at the site of the fracture shall be confiscated as evidence for subsequent litigation regarding research integrity, see § 400.12.\n\nIn cases where the breach is caused by an entity not recognized by the Autumnwood Accords, such as those associated with the Silver Flame or other rival entities, the responding mage may invoke emergency protocols to seal the rift using standard containment matrices. However, any lingering magical residue must be documented and submitted for review by the Conservators of the Guild. The Innovator faction may request a variance under § 1.12 to study the \"decaying\" edge of a fracture, but such requests are strictly prohibited if the site is still actively leaking mana. All containment materials used during these operations must bear the official seal of the Autumnwood Accords; any substance or sigil lacking such identification shall be deemed an illegal arcane tool under § 1.9 and may result in the immediate seizure of the mage’s license.\n\nFurthermore, if a fracture leads to a localized spatial distortion, the surveyor must consult the protocols for planar transit as defined in § 1201.12 to ensure no cross-planar leakage occurs. Any material gathered from a stabilized breach must be quarantined and handled according to the standards of safe storage. If a mage fails to report a fracture that they were aware of but did not report, they shall face penalties for non-compliance with mandatory reporting duties under § 900.11. The ultimate goal of these protocols is the preservation of the Weave's stability and the prevention of uncontrolled magical growth within the Midlands, ensuring that all arcane activity remains within the boundaries established by the Accord_Council.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "500.12",
            "1.4",
            "100.11",
            "900.12",
            "1101.12",
            "400.12",
