          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Emergency Response to Spontaneous Weave-Fractures",
          "text": "In the event that an arcane surge results in a localized instability or \"fracture\" within the weave, immediate containment protocols shall be enacted by the nearest certified practitioner. Such fractures are defined as involuntary ruptures in the local magical fabric, often caused by experimental failures or unauthorized high-level casting. Under § 1.6, these events are classified as \"Critical Anomalies.\" Upon detection of a fracture, the responding mage is mandated to establish a physical and mystical perimeter to prevent the seepage of raw energy into civilian zones. This containment must be performed in accordance with standard safety measures; however, if the breach exceeds a Grade III severity, the responder shall immediately signal for assistance from the Aegis Magi to ensure the integrity of the local weave.\n\nStabilization efforts for such fractures require specialized techniques designed to \"stitch\" the fraying strands of reality back into a cohesive state. During this process, practitioners must exercise extreme caution to avoid secondary ruptures caused by over-correction. All stabilization actions are subject to the oversight of the Conservators to ensure that traditional methods of weave-weaving are preserved. If an Innovator seeks to employ non-traditional stabilization techniques, such an action is permitted only under § 400.11, provided a temporary waiver has been granted by Archmage Veyra. Any practitioner attempting to stabilize a fracture without the proper credentials or during a period of high atmospheric instability may be subject to the disciplinary measures outlined in § 800.12 regarding the consequences of unauthorized and hazardous arcane activities.\n\nIn cases where a weave-fracture is deemed \"volatile\" due to its proximity to populated centers or sacred sites, the primary objective shifts from stabilization to containment through sequestration. If a fracture cannot be stabilized within a sixty-minute window, the responding mage shall initiate a sealing ritual to isolate the affected area. This isolation must be documented as a formal event and reported to the Autumnwood Accords Desk for subsequent review. Any evidence of negligence or failure to follow containment protocols during such an event will result in a mandatory referral to the Paradox Trial under § 100.13, where the peer council shall determine if the mage acted with due diligence or reckless abandon.\n\nRemediation of the aftermath is required once the fracture has been successfully sealed or stabilized. This includes the purging of lingering arcane \"residue\" which may cause long-term degradation of local reality. Failure to perform these remediation steps may result in a permanent blight upon the land, for which the original caster shall be held liable under § 1101.11 regarding collateral contamination. All materials used during the containment and stabilization process must be cataloged and submitted to the Office of Archmage Veyra as part of the post-incident report. Furthermore, any unauthorized use of high-level sealing magic for the purpose of hiding a breach from the authorities is strictly prohibited and shall be prosecuted under § 200.11 as an act of deliberate concealment of magical hazards.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
            "400.11",
            "800.12",
