        {
          "heading": "AUTHORIZATION FOR EXPERIMENTAL ARCANE BRANCHES",
          "text": "The pursuit of novel arcane methodologies, while inherently volatile, is recognized under the Autumnwood Accords as a necessary component of magical evolution. However, such exploration must be governed by strict oversight to ensure that \"innovation\" does not devolve into \"instability.\" Any mage seeking to deviate from the established schools of magic—as defined in § 300.11—must submit a formal petition for an Experimental Arcane Branch (EAB). This process is primarily overseen by the Innovator faction, led by Janna Brightspark, yet it remains subject to the mediation of Archmage Veyra. No researcher may engage in methodologies that bypass established safety protocols without explicit written consent from both the High Council and the designated oversight officer.\n\nUnder § 400.12, all research must maintain integrity; thus, any methodology deemed \"deviant\" by the Conservators under the leadership of Archmage Theron shall be subject to immediate review. A deviation is defined as any casting technique that utilizes unstable mana-channels or interacts with prohibited elements without a pre-approved containment field. If such an inquiry is flagged by the Aegis Magi, the practitioner must immediately cease operations and submit their findings to the Office of Innovation Oversight for a determination of risk. Failure to do so may result in the immediate revocation of research permits as outlined in § 400.11.\n\nFurthermore, any deviation that results in an uncontrolled magical discharge or a breach of local reality shall be prosecuted under § 200.13 regarding containment and breach mitigation. The presence of an \"unstable\" methodology does not grant immunity from the consequences of negligence. If a practitioner is found to be intentionally bypassing the standard protocols for the purpose of rapid experimentation without seeking a variance, they shall be subject to the disciplinary measures defined in § 1301.12. All experimental logs must be filed with the Guild within three lunar cycles of the initial casting to ensure that no \"shadow research\" is conducted outside the purview of the Accord's oversight.\n\nThe interaction between the Innovator and Conservator factions regarding these deviations remains a point of significant contention. To resolve such disputes, parties shall refer to § 100.13 for mediation procedures. Any experimentation involving high-risk components—specifically those listed in the restricted studies under § 400.11—must be conducted within a designated \"Sanctuary Zone\" as defined by the construction standards of § 1.7. Unauthorized field use of such methodologies, particularly on public lands or in proximity to non-caster populations, shall result in immediate forfeiture of credentials and possible referral for a Paradox Trial. All research materials, including physical reagents and spent focus items, must be surrendered to the Guild for inspection following the conclusion of any experimental cycle to ensure no residual \"taint\" remains as per § 1101.12.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "300.11",
