        {
          "heading": "AUTHORIZATION FOR EXPERIMENTAL ARCANE BRANCHES — Continued",
          "text": "The issuance of an Authorization for Experimental Arcane Branches is governed by the tension between the Conservator mandate for stability and the Innovator drive for advancement. Under § 400.11, all research involving methodologies that deviate from established canonical paths must be submitted to the High Council for review before any practical application occurs. Such experimental branches are defined as magical techniques that have not been integrated into the standard curriculum of the Autumnwood Accords and may pose a risk to local arcane stability. While the Innovator faction, led by Janna Brightspark, advocates for broader access to these methodologies, the Conservators maintain that such advancements must be strictly siloed until their safety is guaranteed by an independent audit.\n\nAny mage seeking to pursue an experimental branch must first secure a specific mandate from Archmage Veyra’s office, who serves as the primary mediator between the conflicting interests of the inner circles. This authorization does not grant a license for unrestricted practice; rather, it permits the practitioner to conduct research within a controlled environment. Any deviation from these conditions constitutes an unauthorized field use and shall be subject to disciplinary action under § 500.11. Furthermore, all experimental components must be documented in a private ledger, as any public declaration of such methods is prohibited under § 300.12 to prevent the spread of potentially unstable arcane signatures before they are fully vetted.\n\nThe oversight of these branches is conducted by the Aegis Magi, who act as the primary enforcement arm for both the Conservators and the Innovators. The Aegis Magi are tasked with ensuring that any experimental branch does not manifest a \"collateral taint\" or breach local reality barriers. If an experimental methodology results in a magical surge or a containment failure, the practitioner shall be subject to immediate investigation under § 200.13. In such instances, the authorization is revoked immediately, and the laboratory site may be sealed by the Guild’s enforcement officers.\n\nAll materials used within an authorized experimental branch must be accounted for in accordance with § 1.9 regarding seals and stamps; any material found to have been smuggled or utilized without a proper seal shall result in the immediate forfeiture of all research privileges. Furthermore, mages engaged in these projects are prohibited from sharing their findings with non-guild entities, including those affiliated with the Regal Empire or other rival factions. Any unauthorized exchange of experimental data is considered a breach of the Accord’s core security protocols and may lead to the initiation of a Paradox Trial under § 1301.12 if the breach results in an uncontrolled arcane event.\n\nFinally, it is noted that while the Innovators may seek to push the boundaries of \"Restricted Research,\" they must do so within the confines of the existing legal framework. No experimental branch shall be permitted to utilize forbidden schools, such as necromancy or blood magic, regardless of its potential for advancement. Any attempt to bypass these restrictions through clandestine means will result in a permanent ban from all guild-sanctioned research facilities and may lead to the seizure of all personal artifacts under § 800.11. All authorized experimental branches must be registered with the central registry at the Autumn Wood headquarters to ensure they remain within the purview of Archmage Veyra’s oversight.",
          "key": "c",
