        {
          "heading": "Authorization for Non-Standard Research Pathways",
          "text": "The issuance of an Experimental Arcane Branch permit serves as the primary legal mechanism for balancing the divergent philosophies of the Conservators and the Innovators under the Autumnwood Accords. While standard research is governed by general oversight protocols, non-standard pathways—defined herein as any magical methodology that deviates from established academic cycles or utilizes high-risk arcane variables—require a specific, time-limited mandate. Such mandates are granted only when the potential for discovery outweighs the risk of ontological instability. Under § 1.6, these deviations must be clearly delineated in the application to ensure they do not constitute \"unauthorized field use\" as defined by broader Accord safety standards.\n\nAny mage seeking to pursue a non-standard pathway must submit a comprehensive petition to the Office of Innovation Oversight. This petition must demonstrate that the proposed methodology has been vetted by a peer committee, ensuring it does not violate the core prohibitions against forbidden schools. While the Innovator faction, led by Janna Brightspark, frequently advocates for broader access to these pathways, the Conservators insist on rigorous containment measures. Therefore, all experimental branches are subject to mandatory observation by the Aegis Magi. The presence of an Aegis officer is a prerequisite for any research involving high-resonance materials or potential rift-point generation. See § 400.12 regarding specific protocols for oversight during these active phases.\n\nShould a researcher be granted permission for a non-standard pathway, they are bound by strict reporting requirements. Any \"unusual\" occurrences—including but not limited to spontaneous mana spikes, localized reality thinning, or the manifestation of unintended spectral echoes—must be reported immediately to Archmage Veyra’s mediation office. Failure to report such events constitutes a breach of the Accord and may result in the immediate revocation of the research permit. In cases where an experiment results in a containment failure, the researcher shall be subject to the disciplinary measures outlined under § 200.13 regarding arcane containment breaches. Furthermore, any equipment or artifacts used during these experimental phases must remain within designated zones to avoid violations of standard safety codes.\n\nThe legal distinction between \"Restricted Research\" and \"Experimental Arcane Branches\" is critical for determining liability. While restricted research involves known quantities with controlled risks, an Experimental Branch is a formal recognition that the outcome is unknown. Consequently, any damage caused by a sanctioned experimental branch is the sole liability of the researcher and their sponsoring house, provided they have adhered to all requirements under § 400.11. If a researcher proceeds without the specific \"Experimental\" designation while engaging in high-risk methodology, they are deemed to be acting outside the protection of the Accord and may face immediate seizure of materials. See § 800.11 for protocols regarding the confiscation of unauthorized arcane tools.\n\nFinally, it is strictly prohibited to use an Experimental Arcane Branch permit as a justification for public demonstrations or unsanctioned communal education. The purpose of these permits is internal advancement and specialized study within the Autumn Wood jurisdiction. Any attempt to market the results of such research to non-casters or external entities without prior mediation by Archmage Veyra shall be considered a violation of § 600.11. All data harvested during an experimental branch must be logged in a private ledger; it may only be entered into the public record upon successful completion and verification by both the Conservators and Innovators. Any researcher found to be circulating \"preliminary\" results outside of sanctioned channels shall have their credentials suspended until a formal audit is completed.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
            "400.12",
            "200.13",
