        {
          "heading": "MANDATED PROTOCOLS FOR NON-CONFORMIST RESEARCH AND INNOVATION",
          "text": "Under the overarching governance of the Autumnwood Accords, certain arcane methodologies are designated as \"Experimental\" rather than \"Standard.\" These protocols apply specifically to research initiatives spearheaded by the Innovator faction under the leadership of Janna Brightspark. While the Conservators maintain that stability is paramount, the Accord recognizes the necessity for advancement in specialized fields. However, such advancements must not bypass the oversight established in § 400.12 regarding Research Integrity and Oversight Protocols. Any research path deviating from the approved curriculum as defined in § 300.11 must be submitted to the High Council of Archmages for a formal variance decree before any practical application occurs.\n\nThe authorization for non-standard research pathways requires a tripartite verification process. First, the petitioner must demonstrate that the proposed methodology does not utilize \"Forbidden Schools,\" which remain strictly prohibited under the primary statutes. Second, the petitioner must prove that the intended outcome does not pose a risk of dimensional instability or collateral contamination as outlined in § 1101.11. Third, if the research involves high-risk arcane fluctuations, it must be conducted within a sanctioned containment zone to prevent an accidental breach of reality. Failure to adhere to these boundaries may result in immediate seizure of materials and a mandatory referral to the Paradox Trial for disciplinary review.\n\nFurthermore, all experimental branches that are granted \"Provisional Status\" must operate under a strict reporting cycle. These projects are subject to monthly audits by the Aegis Magi to ensure that the research remains within the scope of the initial permit. Should an experiment produce unexpected arcane resonance or unintended environmental effects, the researcher is obligated to cease operations immediately and notify the Autumnwood Accords Desk. In cases where unauthorized field usage occurs—specifically in instances involving large-scale transmutation or high-energy output—the researcher shall be subject to the penalties for Unauthorized Field Casting as established in § 500.11.\n\nThe distinction between \"innovation\" and \"recklessness\" is governed by the level of oversight provided during the development phase. Research that proceeds without a signed petition from the Archmage Veyra’s office, or without a designated supervisor from the Innovator leadership, shall be deemed unauthorized. Any research conducted in defiance of these protocols may result in the permanent revocation of the practitioner's credentials and the potential for \"Seal\" actions under § 1.9 regarding the removal of magical capabilities. All non-standard pathways must be documented in a private log; however, no details pertaining to the Quiet List shall ever be disclosed in public forums or common areas, as per the restrictions found in § 300.12.\n\nFinally, any collaboration with outside entities for the purpose of experimental research must be vetted by the Guild’s legal counsel. Specifically, agreements with non-casters are governed by § 600.11, and any involvement with entities from the Silver Flame or other rival factions is strictly prohibited under the terms of the Autumnwood Accords. Any researcher found to be bypassing these oversight mechanisms through clandestine cooperation shall face immediate summary judgment in a trial by peers. All experimental protocols must maintain the integrity of the Accord’s core tenets as defined in § 1.7, ensuring that the pursuit of new knowledge does not compromise the fundamental stability of the Midlands.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "400.12",
