        {
          "heading": "MANDATED PROTOCOLS FOR NON-CONFORMIST RESEARCH AND INNOVATION — Continued",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords recognize that the pursuit of arcane knowledge is inherently volatile, necessitating a structured framework for those seeking to deviate from established magical methodologies. Under § 400.12, all research integrity must be maintained; however, when a practitioner seeks to engage in non-standard research pathways—specifically those championed by the Innovator faction under Janna Brightspark—the scope of oversight expands significantly. Such deviations are not permitted as matters of individual whim but must be codified as specific experimental arcane branches. Any researcher seeking to move beyond standard liturgical forms or traditionalist methodologies must first submit a formal petition for an Innovation Variance. This variance shall only be granted if the proposed methodology can be contained within established safety parameters, ensuring that no breach of the primary magical stability is initiated during the exploratory phase.\n\nPursuant to § 1.6, any \"non-standard\" method involving high-risk components must be explicitly defined in a preliminary petition before practical application begins. The oversight of such research is divided between the Innovators and the Conservators; while the former may advocate for the expansion of arcane boundaries, the latter, led by Archmage Theron, maintains the primary right of refusal regarding any methodology that threatens the structural integrity of the Midlands. If a researcher is granted an Innovation Variance, they are required to maintain a detailed log of all \"deviant\" actions. This log shall serve as the primary evidence in the event of a breach. Should a deviation result in a containment failure or a localized surge, the researcher’s immunity from immediate prosecution under § 200.11 is forfeited, and the site may be subject to seizure by the Aegis Magi for stabilization.\n\nFurthermore, any innovation that involves \"forbidden\" elements—specifically those categorized as high-risk in § 300.11—requires a double-blind verification from both the Innovator and Conservator councils. No researcher shall be permitted to conduct experiments on non-standard pathways without a signed seal of authorization; see § 1.9 regarding the validity of such seals. The use of an unauthorized field site for such experimentation is strictly prohibited under § 500.11, and any deviation from the approved laboratory coordinates will result in the immediate revocation of the researcher's credentials.\n\nIn cases where a research methodology is found to be inherently unstable but possesses significant potential utility, the Research Oversight Committee may grant a \"Limited Scope\" permit. This permits the researcher to proceed with non-conformist methods only within a magically shielded zone, as defined by standard containment protocols under § 200.13. Any breach of these geographical or metaphysical boundaries constitutes an intentional violation of the Accord's safety mandates. All experimental results must be submitted to the Guild archives for peer review; failure to submit findings within thirty days of project completion shall result in a formal inquiry into the researcher’s compliance with § 400.12. No research, regardless of its innovative nature, may be conducted in secret or outside the purview of the Archmage Veyra's mediation.",
