        {
          "heading": "Manifestation of Secondary Resonance and Harmonic Bleed",
          "text": "Any arcane manifestation that produces secondary effects, hereafter referred to as \"Harmonic Bleed,\" must be documented in the primary log of the casting practitioner. This includes but is not limited to: localized temperature fluctuations, atmospheric ionization, minor gravitational shifts, or the unintended transmutation of nearby inanimate matter. Such occurrences are often symptomatic of a caster’s inability to contain the raw energy of their intent within the intended somatic and verbal components. Under § 1.6, any such resonance that persists for more than three minutes beyond the conclusion of the primary spell is deemed an \"Ancillary Effect\" and must be reported to the local Aegis Magi station immediately to ensure it does not compound into a larger breach.\n\nThe distinction between a controlled magical byproduct and an uncontrollable arcane leak is governed by the principles of intent as defined in § 1.7. If a caster knowingly utilizes a technique that they anticipate will produce secondary effects for tactical advantage, such as a \"shockwave\" to deter opponents or a \"lingering aura\" to mask their presence, these must be disclosed during the initial filing of the casting permit. Failure to disclose an intended resonance may result in the revocation of research privileges under § 400.12. Conversely, if the bleed is unintentional and occurs despite the caster's best efforts to contain it, the practitioner shall remain exempt from penalties provided they report the incident within one lunar cycle for monitoring by the Conservators.\n\nFurthermore, any secondary resonance that impacts the structural integrity of non-magical architecture or the physical well-being of non-casters must be flagged as a \"High-Risk Variance.\" Such instances fall under the purview of § 500.12 regarding Arcane Field Operations and Conduct. In such cases, the practitioner is required to provide a detailed transcript of the casting components used, allowing the Innovators and Conservators to determine if the variance was caused by a flaw in the spell's construction or an external interference from unauthorized sources.\n\nThe Guild maintains a strict stance on \"lingering\" effects that manifest in public spaces or common thoroughfares. If a secondary resonance persists for more than one hour, it must be neutralized by a certified Aegis Mage to prevent the accumulation of \"Arcane Grime.\" Such buildup can lead to the degradation of local reality threads, necessitating a formal survey of the area. Practitioners who fail to report persistent bleeds may find their credentials suspended under § 800.12 for negligence in containment. All documentation regarding these reports shall be filed according to the standards set forth in § 900.12, ensuring that the Guild maintains a comprehensive record of all magical discharges within its jurisdiction.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
            "1.7",
            "400.12",
            "500.12",
            "800.12",
            "900.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Recognition of Harmonic Resonance and Residual Echoes",
          "text": "The detection and reporting of secondary magical resonance, hereafter referred to as \"Harmonic Bleed,\" constitute a mandatory duty for all practitioners operating under the jurisdiction of the Autumnwood Accords. While primary spells are governed by standard casting protocols, any subsequent atmospheric disturbances, lingering arcane vibrations, or environmental echoes resulting from such castings must be documented in an addendum to the initial casting log. This requirement ensures that the stability of the local weave is preserved against cumulative degradation. Under § 1.7, these secondary effects are considered part of the \"Aggregation of Conduct,\" and failure to report a lingering resonance may result in the caster being held liable for subsequent environmental instability caused by third-party interactions with said residue.\n\nSpecifically, when an arcane event produces a measurable \"echo\"—defined as a persistent magical signature that remains active after the primary spell has concluded—the practitioner must notify the nearest Aegis Magi station or relevant oversight body. Such echoes are often indicative of sub-layer leakage where the initial casting breached deeper strata of the local reality. If such a breach is suspected, the caster shall follow the procedures for containment as outlined under § 200.13. The presence of these resonances must be cross-referenced with the primary spell’s authorization; if no prior permission was granted for high-variance casting, the occurrence of Harmonic Bleed may trigger an automatic investigation into the practitioner's compliance with the restrictions on \"Unsanctioned Arts\" as noted in § 300.11.\n\nFurthermore, instances where multiple castings in a single geographic area produce overlapping harmonic frequencies must be reported immediately to prevent constructive interference. Such interference can lead to localized reality thinning or involuntary manifestation of arcane phenomena. In cases where the resonance is deemed \"volatile,\" the practitioner may be required to stand down and allow for professional stabilization by the Conservators. The Innovator faction, while advocating for more permissive research boundaries under § 400.13, acknowledges that lingering harmonics pose a structural risk to the Midlands. Consequently, any intentional cultivation of resonance for the purpose of \"research\" must still be filed under the appropriate permit systems in § 400.11.\n\nFinally, it is strictly prohibited for practitioners to utilize \"Harmonic Bleed\" as a means of clandestine communication or hidden signaling. Any such use of residual echoes constitutes a violation of the prohibitions on unauthorized transmission and shall be prosecuted under § 300.12. All reported resonances must be logged with the specific duration of the echo, its perceived intensity, and its proximity to any known sacred sites or public thoroughfares. Failure to provide these details may result in the forfeiture of casting privileges under § 800.11. Practitioners are reminded that while the Accord allows for innovation, the integrity of the realm's core stability remains the paramount concern of the Autumnwood Accords.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1.7",
            "200.13",
            "300.11",
            "400.13",
            "400.11",
            "300.12",
            "800.11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Quantification of Harmonic Bleed and Resonance Decay",
          "text": "The quantification of harmonic bleed refers to the measurable degradation of local weave stability following an arcane event, specifically focusing on the \"echoes\" left behind by high-intensity casting. While primary spell effects are governed under § 900.11 regarding the duty to file before casting, the secondary resonance—often characterized as \"harmonic bleed\"—must be documented even if the primary spell was authorized. This is particularly critical in the Midlands and surrounding territories where the density of magical infrastructure makes the distinction between a clean cast and an echoing one vital for public safety. Any practitioner who observes a lingering harmonic signature exceeding three decibels of spectral variance must file a supplementary report to ensure that subsequent mages do not inadvertently trigger a resonance chain reaction, as prohibited under § 100.13 regarding inter-factional arbitration and containment.\n\nFurthermore, the distinction between \"residual echoes\" and \"sub-layered effects\" is mandatory for legal determination of liability. A residual echo is a passive lingering of energy that fades within one lunar cycle; such instances may be ignored unless they manifest as physical hazards. However, sub-layered effects are active, secondary manifestations caused by the interaction of an intentional spell with the local environment's latent currents. Such interactions must be reported immediately to the Archivists at the Autumnwood Accords Desk. Under § 400.13, these instances may indicate a breach in innovation oversight or a failure of containment protocols. The Aegis Magi are authorized to seize any artifacts found at such sites if the resonance decay is not occurring at a linear rate, as per the standards for evidence established under § 700.12.\n\nIn cases where an Innovator-led project results in harmonic bleed that crosses into public thoroughfares or non-sanctioned zones, the practitioner must submit to a mandatory audit of their methodology. This ensures that the \"innovation\" does not constitute a violation of the core safety tenets. If a mage fails to report a known resonance, they may be subject to a Paradox Trial under § 1301.12 for failure to mitigate potential arcane contamination. All reports regarding harmonic bleed must be filed using the standard seal protocols defined in § 1.9. Failure to provide adequate documentation of these secondary effects shall result in a mandatory review of the individual's casting privileges and may lead to the revocation of their right to perform research under the provisions of § 400.11.\n\nFinally, any resonance that exhibits \"sentient-mimicry\" or displays non-linear patterns suggesting an external influence must be reported as a potential breach. Such instances are not considered standard variance and may trigger immediate containment protocols. These proceedings shall follow the strict evidentiary standards of § 700.12 to ensure that all claims of environmental degradation are substantiated before punitive measures are enacted. Any merchant or non-caster who observes such phenomena is encouraged to contact a licensed mediator, though they must remain outside the primary radius as defined under § 500.12 until the Aegis Magi arrive to secure the site.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "900.11",
            "100.13",
            "400.13",
            "700.12",
            "1301.12",
            "1.9",
            "400.11",
