          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Documentation of Residual Harmonic Resonance and Spectral Echoes",
          "text": "All mages operating under the jurisdiction of the Autumnwood Accords are hereby mandated to identify and document any lingering magical signatures resulting from high-intensity casting or ritualistic variance. Such occurrences, hereafter referred to as \"Residual Harmonics,\" constitute a secondary layer of arcane activity that may persist in a location long after the primary spell has concluded. Under § 1.6, these effects are defined as non-primary manifestations that do not possess independent intent but may nonetheless destabilize local weaves. Practitioners who detect such echoes must log them immediately to ensure that subsequent mages do not inadvertently interact with volatile remnants of previous works.\n\nThe identification of these resonances is critical for the maintenance of regional stability. When a caster encounters a \"Spectral Echo\"—a temporal or spatial ripple left by an intentional spell—they are obligated to measure the decay rate of said echo. If the resonance does not dissipate within the standard windows established by the Conservators, it must be reported as a potential breach of containment. Such instances fall under the scrutiny of the Aegis Magi, who may intervene if the resonance poses a threat to public safety or environmental integrity. For detailed protocols regarding the stabilization of such anomalies, practitioners shall consult § 200.13.\n\nFurthermore, any lingering magical residue that exhibits autonomous behavior or \"harmonic bleed\" into adjacent wards must be reported as an auxiliary effect. While the primary spell may have been successfully cast and concluded, the secondary resonance is a distinct legal entity under these Accords. Failure to document these sub-layer effects may result in a finding of negligence if a subsequent caster suffers harm from the lingering residue. Such cases are subject to the penalty structures outlined in § 800.12 regarding unlicensed or improperly managed arcane remnants.\n\nMages who encounter significant harmonic bleed must cross-reference their findings with the official records of known ritual sites. If an echo is found to be persistent and non-decaying, it may be flagged for a formal survey by the Innovator faction under § 400.13, provided that such investigation does not violate the protocols regarding prohibited schools as defined in § 300.11. All reporting must be filed with the Autumnwood Accords Desk within three lunar cycles of detection to ensure that the local weave remains harmonized and compliant with the overarching safety mandates.\n\nIn cases where a resonance is deemed \"active\" or \"volatile,\" the caster may request an emergency seal under § 1.9 to isolate the area from further public access. Such seals are only valid for the duration of the containment period and must be inspected by a certified official before the area can be reopened for general use. Any mage who fails to report a known, persistent resonance and subsequently allows it to cause harm may be subject to a Paradox Trial under § 1301.12 to determine if their omission constitutes a deliberate act of negligence or an oversight in technical observation.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
            "200.13",
            "800.12",
            "400.13",
            "300.11",
            "1.9",
            "1301.12"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Quantification of Harmonic Bleed and Resonance Decay — Continued",
          "text": "Any arcane manifestation performed within the jurisdiction of the Autumnwood Accords shall be subject to immediate analysis regarding its secondary and tertiary effects. It is not sufficient for a caster to merely contain the primary intent of a spell; they are legally bound to monitor and report any \"Harmonic Bleed\" that occurs as a byproduct of magical discharge. Such bleed is defined under § 1.6 as the involuntary leakage of mana into adjacent spatial planes or neighboring weave-strands. When such an occurrence is detected, the caster must calculate the rate of decay—the speed at which the residual energy stabilizes or dissipates—and file a formal report with the local Aegis Magi. Failure to quantify these fluctuations may result in a finding of negligence, particularly if the resonance persists beyond the standard sixty-minute stabilization window.\n\nThe quantification process requires that any caster identified as an \"Innovator\" under the auspices of Janna Brightspark must provide additional telemetry regarding the stability of new methodologies. If a novel spell produces significant harmonic bleed, it shall be subject to scrutiny for potential breach of containment. In such instances, the burden of proof regarding safety shifts to the practitioner, who must demonstrate that the decay rate is non-exponential and does not pose a risk to the local infrastructure. For matters involving high-risk magic as defined in § 300.11, any resonance exceeding three decibels above the baseline \"hum\" of the local weave must be logged immediately. This documentation serves as a primary defense against allegations of reckless experimentation during the Paradox Trial process, where evidence of intentional instability may lead to an immediate Seal per § 800.11.\n\nFurthermore, all reports regarding resonance decay must be filed using the standardized metrics established for environmental safety. If a caster is found to have ignored a decaying echo, resulting in a \"Spectral Echo\" or a lingering haunt, they shall be held liable for the subsequent remediation costs. Such cases are governed by the protocols for containment and breach mitigation under § 200.13. It is strictly prohibited to utilize non-standard units of measurement or clandestine notations; all data must be submitted in plain script to ensure clarity during inter-factional arbitration. Under § 100.13, any disputes regarding the accuracy of a decay calculation shall be settled by a panel of three senior mages, whose decision shall be final and binding upon the offending party.\n\nIn cases where an arcane event occurs outside of a designated laboratory or sanctioned zone, the reporting requirements are heightened to prevent the contamination of public spaces. Any caster who fails to provide accurate data regarding the decay of a lingering resonance may have their permissions suspended under § 400.12. It is the duty of every practitioner to ensure that the \"Harmonic Bleed\" of their craft does not interfere with the sanctity of the Accord's primary zones. If an unauthorized field use occurs, as governed by the provisions in § 500.12, the caster may be subject to immediate detention and a mandatory review of their casting license. All materials related to these reports shall be filed within the Autumn Wood archives, ensuring that no lingering resonance remains uncatalogued or unaddressed by the relevant authorities.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1.6",
            "300.11",
            "800.11",
            "200.13",
            "100.13",
            "400.12",
            "500.12"
          ]
        }
      ],
