    {
      "cite": "200.14",
      "part": "part_ii",
      "title": "Additional Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Additional Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation",
          "text": "Under § 200.13, protocols for arcane containment and breach mitigation are already established to ensure that rogue or dangerous magic does not escape into the public domain. However, these existing provisions may be insufficient in certain high-risk scenarios. This additional section aims to refine and expand upon those protocols, providing a more nuanced approach to managing breaches of magical containment.\n\nThe Aegis Magi, tasked with enforcing the dominant faction's will, shall have the authority to implement temporary containment measures when faced with an imminent threat of breach. These measures are designed not only to protect the public but also to minimize collateral damage and ensure the integrity of the affected area. The Aegis Magi may deploy containment fields or other mitigation techniques without prior approval from the Accords Desk, provided that immediate action is necessary due to the severity of the breach.\n\nIn cases where a containment breach has occurred, the Archmage Veyra shall convene an emergency council composed of peers and experts in various magical disciplines. This council will assess the situation and determine appropriate remedial measures. The council's recommendations may include sealing the rogue magic or relocating it to a secure location through a process known as \"pocket-prisoning.\" Such actions are governed by the Paradox Trial, § 100.6.\n\nIt is imperative that all mages involved in managing breaches take immediate and decisive action to contain any breach, regardless of their affiliation with the Innovators or Conservators. Failure to do so may result in disciplinary measures under § 200.9, including suspension from the Guild or even permanent removal from magical practice. The Aegis Magi are responsible for ensuring compliance with these protocols.\n\nFor breaches involving constructs holding quills or other magical devices that could pose a threat if unattended, the Aegis Magi shall ensure that such items are secured and monitored until the breach is contained. This may involve temporary confiscation of the construct by the appropriate authorities as per § 200.6. In instances where a breach cannot be contained within the immediate area, broader containment measures may be necessary, extending beyond the boundaries of the affected location.\n\nThe Accords Desk shall maintain a record of all breaches and their subsequent containment efforts for future reference and learning. These records are essential in refining protocols and enhancing the overall safety of magical practice. They also serve as evidence that proper procedures were followed when incidents occur.\n\nIn summary, these additional provisions aim to enhance the effectiveness of arcane containment measures by providing clear guidelines for immediate action during breaches and ensuring that all mages are held accountable for their role in maintaining magical integrity. The protocols outlined here reflect a commitment to both safety and respect for the law, as articulated in the Autumnwood Accords.\n\nUnder § 200.13 Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation, these additional measures shall supplement existing protocols without conflicting with them. The aim is to provide flexibility in response to breaches while maintaining a high standard of magical practice.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "200.13",
            "100.6",
            "200.9",
            "200.6"
