    {
      "cite": "100.15",
      "part": "part_i",
      "title": "Catchline Title: Protocols for Immediate and Expedited Remediation",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Catchline Title: Protocols for Immediate and Expedited Remediation",
          "text": "Under the Autumnwood Accords, the Mages' Guild Accords Desk is entrusted with the responsibility of ensuring that any breach or deviation from established protocols does not linger unaddressed. The immediate and expedited remediation of such breaches is critical to maintaining the integrity of magical practices within the jurisdiction of the Guild. This section sets forth specific protocols designed to ensure that such breaches are addressed swiftly, effectively, and in a manner that restores order without undue delay.\n\nIn accordance with § 100.14 Additional Provisions for Office Boundaries and Jurisdictional Clarity, the Accords Desk has been vested with the authority to implement immediate remediation measures when it is determined that a breach has occurred or when a potential threat arises. These measures are not merely reactive but are designed to preempt any escalation of issues that could compromise the safety and well-being of the community.\n\nThe Desk shall establish an emergency protocol for scenarios where a breach of magic occurs, posing an imminent threat to public safety or the stability of magical practices. Under such circumstances, the Desk may issue a preliminary order for immediate containment under § 200.13 Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation, which allows for the temporary sealing or neutralization of the source of the breach until a more comprehensive investigation can be conducted.\n\nFor breaches that do not pose an imminent threat but are significant enough to warrant prompt attention, the Desk may issue a preliminary directive under § 800.14 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation. This directive shall outline specific steps for the containment or neutralization of the breach until further action can be taken.\n\nUpon receipt of reports from the field or other relevant sources, the Desk must conduct an initial evaluation to determine the nature and extent of the breach. If the breach is found to require immediate attention due to its potential impact on public safety or magical practices, the Desk shall issue a preliminary order for remediation under § 200.14 Additional Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation.\n\nThe Desk must ensure that all parties involved in the breach are notified of the preliminary order and given an opportunity to present their case before any final action is taken. This ensures that all relevant information is considered, thereby facilitating a more comprehensive resolution under § 100.13 Protocols for Mediation and Inter-Factional Arbitration.\n\nOnce a final decision has been made regarding the remediation of the breach, the Desk shall oversee its implementation to ensure compliance with established protocols. If necessary, enforcement measures may be taken against those responsible for the breach under § 800.14 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation. The Desk must also maintain thorough records of all remediation efforts in accordance with § 100.4 Records of Speech.\n\nIn instances where a breach results from unauthorized or excessive use of magic, the Desk shall consult with the relevant factions—such as the Conservators and Innovators—to determine an appropriate course of action under § 400.13 Protocols for Deviant Methodology and Innovation Oversight. This collaborative approach ensures that all perspectives are considered in addressing the breach.\n\nThe Desk must also ensure that any lingering effects of the breach are adequately addressed to prevent recurrence. Under § 500.14 Catchline Title: Remediation and Obligations for Lingering Arcane Effects, the Desk shall oversee the remedial processes until they are completed satisfactorily.\n\nIn summary, the protocols outlined in this section are designed to ensure that any breach of magical practices is addressed immediately and effectively, thereby maintaining the integrity and safety of the Guild's operations. These measures reflect the Accords' commitment to swift and decisive action to uphold the principles of magic as defined by § 100.3 Quorum of the Desk.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "100.14",
            "200.13",
            "800.14",
            "200.14",
            "100.13",
            "100.4",
            "400.13",
            "500.14",
            "100.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Protocols for Immediate and Expedited Remediation in Sealed Magic Cases",
          "text": "Under the Autumnwood Accords, the sealing of magic is a grave measure that can have far-reaching impacts on individuals and communities. The process of sealing magic must be managed with utmost precision to ensure fairness and efficacy. This section outlines protocols designed to expedite and prioritize immediate remediation in cases where mages are found guilty of violations severe enough to warrant the imposition of sealed magic.\n\n### Immediate Notification and Communication Protocols\n\nUpon a finding by the Paradox Trial that a mage has committed a breach of the Accords, it is imperative that the individual be promptly informed of their sentence. The sealing of magic represents a significant alteration in one's life and must not be carried out without clear communication of all implications. The Aegis Magi are responsible for ensuring immediate notification to the sealed mage and any relevant parties, including family members or guild affiliates.\n\n### Priority Assessment and Preliminary Remediation\n\nFor mages whose magic is being sealed, a preliminary assessment should occur immediately post-verdict. This includes a detailed evaluation by trained Aegis Magi to identify the specific spells, artifacts, and practices that have been involved in the violation. The goal here is to ensure that all aspects of the mage’s magical proficiency are accurately cataloged for future reference. This preliminary step ensures that when the magic is eventually restored or if there is a subsequent appeal, the process can proceed without further delays.\n\n### Expedited Seal Removal and Restoration Protocols\n\nIn cases where the sealed individual has successfully completed their sentence under the terms of the Paradox Trial, provisions must be in place for the expedited removal of the seal. The Aegis Magi are tasked with overseeing this process to ensure that it is conducted safely and efficiently. This includes a thorough review by an independent panel to confirm that all conditions have been met before proceeding.\n\n### Contingency Plans for Sealed Mages\n\nFor mages whose magic has been sealed, contingency plans must be in place to address any potential emergencies or urgent needs during the period of sealing. This could include provisions for alternative magical support in critical situations, such as medical emergencies or other life-threatening scenarios. Such arrangements are essential to mitigate risks and ensure that the mage remains safe and secure.\n\n### Review and Appeal Protocols\n\nOnce a mage has been sealed, there must be mechanisms in place for thorough review and appeal processes. These reviews should include input from independent legal experts and peers who can provide an objective assessment of the case. The Accords Desk is responsible for managing these appeals, ensuring that all parties have access to fair and transparent procedures.\n\nIn conclusion, the protocols outlined here aim to ensure that the sealing of magic cases are handled with utmost care and expediency. By prioritizing immediate notification, preliminary remediation, expedited seal removal, contingency plans, and review mechanisms, the Autumnwood Accords can provide a framework for handling these sensitive matters in a manner that is both effective and fair. These protocols reflect the Guild's commitment to maintaining integrity and justice within its ranks while ensuring that all members are treated with respect and dignity.\n\nUnder § 100.15, it is essential to note that these protocols are designed to be flexible and adaptable to the unique circumstances of each case. See § 900.13 for more detailed information on reporting ancillary effects and sub-layered magic, which can impact the overall management of sealed cases. Additionally, the Aegis Magi must ensure compliance with all relevant sections under § 200.14 regarding protocols for arcane containment and breach mitigation to safeguard communities during these processes.\n\nBy adhering to these protocols, the Mages' Guild can uphold its commitment to the Accords and provide a framework that is both just and efficient in dealing with cases involving sealed magic.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "100.15",
            "900.13",
            "200.14"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Protocols for Immediate and Expedited Remediation in Contaminated Environments",
          "text": "In the wake of unprecedented breaches involving arcane residue, the Mages' Guild has been tasked with ensuring that such incidents do not spiral into larger calamities. This section outlines protocols for immediate and expedited remediation aimed at mitigating the risks associated with contaminated environments where magic has been improperly or illegally cast.\n\n### Introduction to Contaminated Environments\n\nContaminated environments arise from breaches of the Accords, particularly when mages fail to adhere to the prescribed containment protocols outlined in § 200.13 Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation. These incidents are not only a threat to the immediate vicinity but also have implications for the wider community. The nature of magic can linger in its environment, creating echoes that may inadvertently affect subsequent castings or even cause unforeseen disruptions.\n\n### Immediate Response\n\nUpon detection of an improperly contained breach, the first protocol is swift containment under § 1401.12 Preservation of Canonical Continuity and Scriptural Integrity. This ensures that any further spreading of the residue is halted immediately. The Aegis Magi are responsible for enforcing this initial containment, as stipulated in § 100.13 Protocols for Mediation and Inter-Factional Arbitration.\n\n### Remediation Protocols\n\nOnce containment is achieved, remediation protocols must be initiated with urgency. These protocols aim to neutralize the residue without causing additional disturbances. The use of specialized artifacts or rituals may be necessary, as described in § 700.13 Liability for Autonomous Construct Malfeasance and § 800.14 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation.\n\n### Environmental Impact Assessment\n\nBefore initiating any remediation efforts, an environmental impact assessment is conducted to evaluate the extent of contamination. This process involves cartography, as outlined in § 1201.13 Additional Provisions for Ancillary Planar Transits, to ensure that all affected areas are accurately surveyed and documented.\n\n### Collaboration with Conservators\n\nThe Conservators play a crucial role in these protocols by providing insights into the nature of magic involved. Their expertise is invaluable in selecting appropriate remediation methods, as detailed under § 400.13 Unauthorized Research Permits and Exceeding Boundaries. The Innovators, on the other hand, may contribute novel solutions to more complex contamination scenarios.\n\n### Monitoring and Aftermath\n\nOnce remediation efforts are complete, a period of monitoring is conducted to ensure that the environment has returned to its stable state. This phase involves regular checks under § 1101.13 Liability for Residue and Lingering Arcane Echoes, ensuring no lingering effects remain. If any issues arise post-remediation, further intervention may be required.\n\n### Cross-Factional Cooperation\n\nThe successful resolution of contaminated environments relies heavily on cooperation between the Conservators and Innovators. This collaboration ensures that both factions contribute their unique expertise to the process. § 100.14 Additional Provisions for Office Boundaries and Jurisdictional Clarity provides a framework for such cooperation, emphasizing the importance of maintaining open lines of communication.\n\n### Conclusion\n\nThe protocols outlined in this section are designed to ensure swift and effective remediation of contaminated environments. By adhering to these guidelines, the Mages' Guild aims to prevent further escalation of incidents involving improper use of magic. This not only safeguards the immediate area but also reinforces the integrity of the Accords as a whole.\n\nSee § 200.13 for protocols on arcane containment and breach mitigation; under § 400.13 for unauthorized research permits and exceeding boundaries; reference § 700.13 for liability for autonomous construct malfeasance, § 800.14 for provisions governing unlawful casting and confiscation; see § 900.13 for reporting of ancillary and sub-layered arcane effects; and § 1201.13 for conditional exemptions for ancillary planar transits.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "200.13",
            "1401.12",
            "100.13",
