    {
      "cite": "200.15",
      "part": "part_ii",
      "title": "Catchline Title: Emergency Protocols for Arcane Breach Mitigation",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Catchline Title: Emergency Protocols for Arcane Breach Mitigation",
          "text": "In the event of an unforeseen breach in arcane containment or a sudden eruption of magical energy, immediate and decisive action is paramount to prevent widespread chaos and harm. The Autumnwood Accords Desk recognizes that such incidents can occur at any time, thus these emergency protocols are designed to ensure a swift and effective response.\n\n§200.15.1 Emergency Protocols\n\nWhen an arcane breach is reported or detected, the immediate responsibility lies with the nearest Aegis Magi. Upon confirmation of a breach, the Aegis Magi shall initiate Protocol Alpha, which includes but is not limited to the following steps:\n\n1. The Aegis Magi must secure the area immediately by redirecting all non-essential personnel from the vicinity.\n2. They are required to coordinate with local authorities and other relevant parties to establish a containment perimeter.\n3. Upon securing the area, they shall proceed to identify the source of the breach. This step is critical for determining the appropriate course of action.\n\n§200.15.2 Containment Measures\n\nOnce the source has been identified, the Aegis Magi must employ containment measures suitable to the nature and severity of the breach:\n\n- If the breach can be attributed to rogue magic or a single caster, the Protocol Beta: Sealed Arcane may be initiated.\n  - Under §100.13 Mediation and Inter-Factional Arbitration, the Paradox Trial is convened to determine guilt and impose appropriate sanctions (see §200.13 Protocols for Arcane Containment).\n\n- For breaches originating from more complex or larger-scale sources, such as ancient artifacts or constructs with autonomous capabilities, Protocol Gamma: Pocket Prison must be enacted.\n  - This protocol allows the magic of the source to be contained within a pocket dimension, thus preventing further spread (see §200.13 Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation).\n\n§200.15.3 Reporting and Documentation\n\nAll incidents of arcane breaches must be meticulously documented by the Aegis Magi for future reference. The report shall include:\n- Date, time, and location of the breach.\n- Description of the nature and extent of the breach.\n- Identification of those involved or responsible.\n- Measures taken to mitigate the situation.\n- Any collateral damage and its assessment.\n\nUnder §900.13 Reporting Ancillary Effects and Sub-Layered Magic, all reports must be submitted to the Autumnwood Accords Desk for thorough review and archiving (see §200.14 Additional Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation).\n\n§200.15.4 Post-Mitigation Actions\n\nUpon successful mitigation of the breach:\n- The Aegis Magi must ensure all affected areas are thoroughly cleansed of any lingering magical residue.\n- They shall coordinate with relevant parties to conduct a post-breach survey, ensuring that no further issues arise from the incident (see §1101.13 Liability for Residue and Lingering Arcane Echoes).\n\n§200.15.5 Enforcement and Oversight\n\nThe enforcement of these emergency protocols is mandatory and shall be strictly adhered to by all members of the Mages' Guild. Failure to comply with any part of this protocol shall result in severe disciplinary measures under §200.9 Prohibited Practices and Disciplinary Measures.\n\nIn summary, the Autumnwood Accords Desk emphasizes that the swift and effective response to an arcane breach is crucial for maintaining the balance of magic within the region. By adhering to these emergency protocols, the Guild ensures a safe environment conducive to magical study and practice (see §100.14 Additional Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation).",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "200.15.1",
            "200.15.2",
            "100.13",
            "200.13",
            "200.15.3",
