      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Catchline Title: Liability for Ancillary Arcane Events and Casualties",
          "text": "Under § 1401.14 Conditional Exemption for Ancillary Planar Transits, the Mages' Guild Accords Desk has established protocols to mitigate the risks associated with ancillary planar transits. These protocols are designed to protect both the Guild members and the general populace from unintended consequences of such activities. This section aims to expand upon those protocols by addressing additional liabilities that may arise from ancillary arcane events and their potential impact on public safety.\n\nAncillary arcane events, while not always planned or anticipated, can have significant repercussions if not properly managed. These events can range from minor disruptions in the fabric of reality to more severe, unpredictable phenomena. The Mages' Guild is responsible for overseeing these occurrences to ensure that they do not cause undue harm or disruption to the community.\n\n### Liability for Ancillary Arcane Events\n\nThe liability for ancillary arcane events extends beyond the immediate casters. All members of the Guild are bound under § 1401.14 to report any potential planar transit or anomaly immediately. Failure to do so can result in severe penalties, as outlined in § 800.13. The responsible party must also undertake remediation efforts to mitigate any damage caused by these events.\n\n### Casualties and Compensation\n\nUnder § 500.10 Compensation and Indemnification, provisions are made for compensation and indemnification of those affected by ancillary arcane events. This includes medical expenses, property damages, and other reasonable costs incurred as a result of such incidents. The Guild is obligated to cover these costs under the auspices of § 500.14 Remediation and Obligations for Lingering Arcane Effects.\n\n### Public Safety Protocols\n\nThe Mages' Guild is committed to ensuring public safety through proactive measures. This includes the implementation of additional protocols aimed at minimizing the risk of ancillary events. These protocols are detailed in § 500.7 Public Safety — Additional Protocols, which mandate regular inspections and reviews of all potential high-risk operations.\n\n### Enforcement and Remediation\n\nEnforcement of these responsibilities is a critical aspect of maintaining Guild integrity. The Aegis Magi play a pivotal role in ensuring compliance with these protocols. Under § 200.15 Emergency Protocols for Arcane Breach Mitigation, the Aegis are empowered to take immediate action should an ancillary event occur, providing timely intervention and minimizing potential harm.\n\n### Reporting Obligations\n\nAll members of the Guild are required to report any knowledge or suspicion of an ancillary arcane event to their local Conservator under § 400.13 Protocols for Deviant Methodology and Innovation Oversight. This ensures that all incidents are documented and managed appropriately, reducing the risk of widespread disruption.\n\n### Conclusion\n\nIn summary, the Mages' Guild is committed to ensuring the safety and well-being of its members and the public through robust protocols designed to mitigate the risks associated with ancillary arcane events. By adhering to these guidelines and cooperating fully with the Aegis Magi, all members can help maintain the integrity of magical practices and promote a safer environment for all.\n\nSee § 500.14 Remediation and Obligations for Lingering Arcane Effects; see § 500.7 Public Safety — Additional Protocols; see § 200.15 Emergency Protocols for Arcane Breach Mitigation.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1401.14",
            "800.13",
            "500.10",
