      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Catchline Title: Oversight Protocols for Construct Labor and Associated Obligati",
          "text": "Under §600.14, Oversight and Compliance Protocols for Construct Labor, there are stringent measures in place to ensure that the use of autonomous constructs adheres strictly to established protocols and regulatory frameworks. These protocols aim to prevent unauthorized or dangerous activities by constructs, ensuring public safety and compliance with arcane law.\n\n§600.15 Additional Provisions §600.15 outlines specific oversight mechanisms for constructing and managing autonomous constructs. This section mandates that all mages utilizing such constructs must adhere to a series of guidelines designed to mitigate risks associated with construct labor.\n\nFirstly, all constructs are required to be registered with the Mages' Guild within three days of their completion or acquisition. This registration process ensures transparency and accountability in the use of autonomous constructs. Failure to register constitutes a violation under §800.14 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation.\n\nSecondly, construct labor must be conducted only in designated areas as approved by the local Aegis Magi. Under §200.15 Emergency Protocols for Arcane Breach Mitigation, any unauthorized use outside these areas is subject to immediate cessation orders and potential confiscation of the construct. The Aegis Magi have the authority to enforce these measures under §400.15 Oversight Protocols for Exceptional Research Permits and Supervised Experiments.\n\nMoreover, mages responsible for construct labor are required to maintain a minimum warding protocol as outlined in §600.4 Construct Labor: Minimum Ward. This ensures that constructs do not stray beyond their intended parameters or become a threat to the public. A breach of these wards could result in liability under §1301.14 Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption.\n\nConstructs are prohibited from engaging in activities that could lead to environmental harm, as detailed in §500.13 Mitigation of Environmental Arcane Decay. Mages failing to adhere to these environmental standards would be subject to penalties under §800.14 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation.\n\nAdditionally, the use of constructs for activities that could lead to collateral contamination is strictly regulated. Under §1101.13 Liability for Collateral Contamination and Remedial Obligations, mages must take immediate steps to mitigate any such contamination. Failure to do so can result in significant penalties under §800.14.\n\nFurthermore, any construct labor involving autonomous constructs that are capable of independent action requires a continuous monitoring system as per §600.13 Liability for Autonomous Construct Malfeasance. This ensures that constructs cannot operate without supervision or accountability. Mages found in violation could face severe repercussions under §500.14 Remediation and Obligations for Lingering Arcane Effects.\n\nIn cases where a construct is involved in an incident leading to casualties, the mage responsible must immediately report the matter according to §900.13 Reporting of Ancillary and Sub-Layered Arcane Effects. Failure to comply with this reporting requirement can result in penalties under §800.14 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation.\n\nLastly, mages engaged in construct labor must adhere strictly to all protocols outlined in §600.15 Additional Provisions §600.15. Any deviation from these protocols could lead to immediate cessation of activities and potential confiscation of the construct. The Aegis Magi are responsible for overseeing compliance with these measures under §400.15 Oversight Protocols for Exceptional Research Permits and Supervised Experiments.\n\nIn summary, §600.15 Additional Provisions §600.15 establishes comprehensive oversight protocols to ensure the safe and legal use of autonomous constructs by mages within the jurisdiction of the Mages' Guild Accords Desk. Compliance with these provisions is crucial for maintaining public safety and upholding the integrity of magical law.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "600.14",
            "600.15",
            "800.14",
            "200.15",
            "400.15",
            "600.4",
            "1301.14",
