      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Collateral Contamination and Remedial Protocols",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords are replete with provisions aimed at mitigating the risks associated with arcane magic. Section 1101.14 already addresses the remedial obligations for collateral contamination; however, a new catchline is needed to encompass the broader issue of collateral contamination and its remediation protocols. This section, §1101.15, shall be titled \"Collateral Contamination and Remedial Protocols,\" providing specific guidelines on how to handle situations where the effects of magical activities extend beyond the intended target.\n\nUnder this section, mages are required to take all necessary precautions to prevent collateral contamination. When such an incident occurs, the mage responsible must immediately cease all operations and secure the area as per §100.14. The mage must then document the extent of the contamination in accordance with §900.15 and report it to the nearest Aegis Magus or Guild representative for evaluation.\n\nIf collateral contamination is determined to be within permissible limits, the mage may proceed with remediation under supervision according to §200.14. If contamination exceeds acceptable thresholds, the mage must seek immediate assistance from the Aegis Magi to contain and neutralize the effects. The Aegis Magi shall have full authority to impose additional measures as deemed necessary by them.\n\nIn cases of significant collateral contamination, a Paradox Trial may be convened under §700.13 to determine appropriate sanctions. The mage responsible for the contamination must cooperate fully during this process. If the mage fails to comply or demonstrates repeated negligence, stricter penalties may be imposed, including potential sealing of their magic.\n\nThe section also emphasizes the importance of preventive measures. Mages are encouraged to engage in advanced training and study as outlined in §400.15 to better understand and mitigate the risks associated with their arcane practices. Continuous education is a critical component of ensuring that all mages operate within safe parameters.\n\nIt is important to note that collateral contamination can have far-reaching effects, not only on immediate surroundings but also on individuals and structures beyond the initial target area. Therefore, mages are advised to be vigilant in their practice and to seek expert guidance when dealing with complex or potentially hazardous magic. By adhering to these protocols, the Autumnwood Accords aim to protect both the magical community and its environment from the unintended consequences of arcane activities.\n\nThe enforcement of these provisions is critical for maintaining the integrity and safety of the magical community. Mages who fail to comply may face severe penalties under §800.14. The goal is not merely to punish but to ensure that all mages are equipped with the knowledge and resources necessary to practice magic responsibly. Under these protocols, mages must take proactive steps to prevent contamination and respond swiftly when it occurs.\n\nIn conclusion, collateral contamination is a serious issue that requires careful attention and immediate action. By implementing these remedial protocols, the Autumnwood Accords seek to minimize risks and ensure the continued safety and stability of the magical community. Mages are encouraged to remain diligent in their practices and to seek assistance when necessary to prevent potential disasters.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1101.15",
            "100.14",
