    {
      "cite": "1201.15",
      "part": "part_xii",
      "title": "Conditional Exemption for Ancillary Planar Transits",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Conditional Exemption for Ancillary Planar Transits",
          "text": "In the governance of planar transit, the Mages' Guild Accords Desk recognizes that certain circumstances necessitate exceptional handling to ensure compliance with both the spirit and letter of the law. This section provides conditional exemptions for ancillary planar transits under specific conditions. The purpose is not merely to mitigate legal obligations but also to provide a framework within which mages can conduct their duties without undue burden, while still adhering to the overarching principles of magical stewardship.\n\nUnder § 1201.15, an exemption may be granted for ancillary planar transits conducted in emergency situations where immediate action is required to prevent harm or loss. This includes instances where a mage must cross into another jurisdiction to contain a breach of arcane law. The exemption is not automatic and requires a formal application under § 400.15, which outlines the protocols for Exceptional Research Permits and Supervised Experiments.\n\nIn such cases, the applicant must demonstrate that no other means are available to achieve the necessary objective without breaching planar sovereignty or causing additional harm. The Archmage Sovereign has the authority to approve or deny these applications. Approval is contingent upon a thorough evaluation of the potential risks and benefits, ensuring compliance with § 100.14 on Office Boundaries and Jurisdictional Clarity.\n\nThe exemptions granted under this section are time-limited and subject to periodic review by the Guild's Oversight Council. This ensures that any ancillary transits conducted remain within acceptable parameters set forth in § 700.15 on Oversight Protocols for Construct Labor and Associated Obligations. Any deviation from these protocols must be reported promptly under § 900.14, which deals with the Reporting Ancillary Effects and Sub-Layered Magic.\n\nIt is important to note that while these exemptions are granted, they do not relieve a mage of their responsibility to adhere to all other relevant sections of this Codex. For instance, § 200.15 on Emergency Protocols for Arcane Breach Mitigation still applies, ensuring that all necessary steps are taken to mitigate any ancillary effects.\n\nFurthermore, the granting of an exemption does not imply endorsement of unauthorized field use. As stated in § 400.14 on Unauthorized Research Permits and Exceeding Boundaries, such actions are strictly prohibited unless explicitly permitted by the Council under exceptional circumstances. The intent behind this section is to balance the need for flexibility with the imperative of maintaining control over magical activities.\n\nIn conclusion, ancillary planar transits conducted in emergencies may be granted conditional exemptions under § 1201.15. These exemptions are designed to facilitate necessary actions while ensuring compliance with broader legal and ethical considerations. Mages seeking such exemptions must apply formally and demonstrate the necessity of their actions. The oversight mechanisms outlined within this section ensure that these allowances do not undermine the fundamental principles governing magical practice in the Guild.\n\nSee § 400.15 for detailed protocols regarding Exceptional Research Permits and Supervised Experiments, § 700.15 on Oversight Protocols for Construct Labor and Associated Obligations, and § 900.14 for reporting ancillary effects and sub-layered magic.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1201.15",
