    {
      "cite": "1301.15",
      "part": "part_xiii",
      "title": "Catchline Title: Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Catchline Title: Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords, under the governance and mediation by Archmage Veyra as Sovereign, recognize that the disruption of arcane phenomena can have unforeseen and sometimes hazardous effects. This section outlines specific protocols designed to mitigate these disruptions and ensure the safety of both mages and non-mages within the jurisdiction of the Guild.\n\nSection 1301.15 mandates that any mage or construct utilizing magic in a manner that inadvertently causes an ancillary arcane disruption must immediately cease their activity, regardless of the nature or scale of the disruption. The mage or construct operator is required to notify the nearest Aegis Magi or other authorized personnel within one minute of detecting the disruption. Failure to comply with this requirement shall be deemed a violation under § 1401.15 and may result in penalties as specified under § 1301.8.\n\nUnder § 1301.12, when an arcane disruption is detected, remediation protocols must commence immediately. The mage or construct operator is responsible for initiating the first phase of remediation, which involves isolating the source of the disruption and preventing further escalation. If isolation efforts fail to contain the disruption, the Aegis Magi shall be contacted for further assistance under § 200.15.\n\nThe Autumnwood Accords emphasize that the primary responsibility for mitigating ancillary arcane disruptions lies with the mage or construct operator. This includes the obligation to provide a detailed report of the incident and its circumstances within twenty-four hours, as outlined in § 900.14. The report must include all relevant data and evidence necessary for a thorough investigation into the cause of the disruption.\n\nSection 1301.15 also specifies that if the disruption is determined to be caused by unauthorized or excessive use of magic (as defined under § 400.14), the mage responsible may face additional sanctions, including those outlined in § 800.15 for unlawful casting and confiscation. In cases where the disruption results from sanctioned but uncontrolled research, the mage involved shall undergo a period of supervised research under the guidance of Aegis Magi to ensure compliance with Guild protocols.\n\nFurthermore, § 1301.15 mandates that mages responsible for ancillary arcane disruptions must adhere to strict remediation protocols established by the Guild. These protocols are designed to minimize potential harm and restore stability within the disrupted environment. The specifics of these protocols shall be determined on a case-by-case basis by the Aegis Magi, taking into account the nature of the disruption and its severity.\n\nIn instances where the disruption results in casualties or significant property damage, § 1301.5 may provide additional obligations for the mage responsible to contribute to remediation efforts. These obligations are designed to ensure that those affected by the disruption receive appropriate compensation and support under the principles laid out in § 1401.8.\n\nFinally, § 1301.15 emphasizes the importance of continuous monitoring and reporting of ancillary arcane disruptions. This is crucial for maintaining the safety and stability within the jurisdiction of the Guild. All mages are required to undergo periodic training on recognizing and managing such disruptions under § 600.15.\n\nIn summary, § 1301.15 provides a comprehensive framework for addressing ancillary arcane disruptions, emphasizing immediate containment, thorough investigation, and effective remediation efforts. This section aims to ensure that any disruption is managed with the utmost care and attention to safety, aligning with the broader goals of the Autumnwood Accords.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1401.15",
            "1301.8",
            "1301.12",
