    {
      "cite": "100.16",
      "part": "part_i",
      "title": "Catchline Title: Speech Protocols and Oversight",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Catchline Title: Speech Protocols and Oversight",
          "text": "Under §1401.13 Preservation of Canonical Continuity and Scriptural Integrity, the Mages' Guild accords strict adherence to maintaining the integrity of its laws and protocols. This section further refines these principles by introducing specific protocols for speech and communication within the guild's halls, ensuring that all expressions are in keeping with the guild’s established norms and traditions.\n\nThe primary objective of this new provision is to safeguard against any potential misuse or misinterpretation of speech during casting or magical communication. All mages, including those of the Conservator and Innovator factions, must adhere to these protocols when engaging in verbal interactions within the halls of Autumn Wood or its branches. This includes but is not limited to discussions involving forbidden schools, restricted research, and any other topics that may be contentious.\n\nUnder §100.16 Additional Provisions for Speech Protocols and Oversight, it shall be required that all mages, upon entering a hall where such protocols apply, must declare their intent to speak in accordance with the guild’s established guidelines. This declaration is not merely a formality but an affirmation of commitment to maintaining the sanctity of magical communication.\n\nFurthermore, any mage found to have violated these protocols will face disciplinary action under §800.15 Oversight Protocols for Exceptional Research Permits and Supervised Experiments. The severity of this action may vary depending on the nature and extent of the violation, ranging from a formal warning to more stringent measures such as temporary suspension or even permanent expulsion from certain halls.\n\nThe speech protocols extend beyond mere verbal declarations; they also encompass the manner in which mages communicate their intentions and results through magical means. Any mage employing speech in a manner that is deemed inappropriate by the hall’s governing body will be subject to immediate review under §1401.13 Preservation of Canonical Continuity and Scriptural Integrity.\n\nUnder these protocols, it is imperative that all speech within the halls remain respectful and constructive, fostering an environment conducive to learning and growth rather than conflict or disruption. This is particularly crucial given the fractious nature of the Mages' Guild, where differing opinions on magical practices are common.\n\nMoreover, any mage who feels their rights have been infringed upon by another’s speech in violation of these protocols may file a complaint under §100.15 Catchline Title: Protocols for Immediate and Expedited Remediation. The hall’s governing body shall then conduct an investigation into the matter, with swift action taken to rectify any breaches.\n\nLastly, it is worth noting that these speech protocols are not static but evolve over time as new challenges arise within the guild. Therefore, amendments may be proposed by any member of the guild and reviewed under §100.13 Protocols for Mediation and Inter-Factional Arbitration. Such proposals must demonstrate a clear need and support from a majority of the guild’s members to be considered.\n\nIn summary, §100.16 Additional Provisions for Speech Protocols and Oversight ensures that all speech within the halls remains respectful, constructive, and in keeping with the Mages' Guild’s established principles. This section serves as a vital tool in maintaining harmony and order within the guild, thereby preserving its integrity and fostering an environment conducive to learning and growth.\n\nUnder §700.14 Catchline Title: Oversight and Compliance Protocols for Construct Labor, this provision complements existing protocols by ensuring that all aspects of speech and communication are consistently aligned with the guild’s core values.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1401.13",
            "100.16",
