        {
          "heading": "Remedial Protocols for Unlawful Merging and Consequential Collateral Damage",
          "text": "In the administration and governance of magic, as outlined by the Autumnwood Accords, unlawful merging presents a significant challenge to the maintenance of order and safety within the Midlands. The process of merging spells or magical entities can have unforeseen consequences, leading to collateral damage that affects not only the mages involved but also the environment and innocent bystanders. This section outlines the remedial protocols necessary for addressing such incidents and minimizing harm.\n\nUnlawful merging typically arises from the unauthorized combination of incompatible or inherently dangerous magic. The process can result in unstable constructs or entities that may pose a threat to nearby magical users, flora, fauna, and built structures. Under § 1101.16, mages must follow strict protocols designed to mitigate these risks.\n\nWhen an unlawful merging is reported or discovered, the first step involves immediate containment of the affected area. This requires the intervention of Aegis Magi, who are responsible for ensuring that no further damage is caused. Under § 400.15 and § 200.16, the Aegis Magi have authority to impose emergency protocols aimed at containing the threat and preventing escalation.\n\nOnce the immediate threat has been neutralized, a formal investigation must be conducted to determine the nature of the merging and its cause. This is crucial for understanding how the magic was misaligned and what safeguards were or were not followed. The Paradox Trial plays a key role in this process by assessing the guilt or innocence of the mage(s) involved (see § 1600.15). If found guilty, appropriate sanctions are imposed under § 800.14.\n\nAfter the cause is identified and the immediate threat contained, remediation begins. This involves several stages:\n\n### Stage One: Damage Assessment\nA team of specialized mages conducts a thorough assessment to determine the extent of the collateral damage caused by the merging. This includes evaluating environmental impacts on flora and fauna, as well as any structural damage to buildings or other structures (see § 700.16). The assessment also considers potential long-term effects that could arise from the merging.\n\n### Stage Two: Containment and Removal\nDuring this stage, containment zones are expanded if necessary, ensuring that no further risk is posed by unstable constructs or entities. Specialized teams then proceed with the safe removal of any dangerous elements. This may involve disintegration spells or other methods to neutralize the threat (see § 1301.14). Under § 500.16, all remediation activities must be conducted in a manner that minimizes further risk to the environment and public.\n\n### Stage Three: Rehabilitation\nRehabilitation efforts aim to restore the affected area to its pre-incident state as much as possible. This involves restoring damaged structures (if feasible), rehabilitating ecosystems, and addressing any long-term environmental concerns identified during the initial assessment. The use of healing spells or other restorative magic is encouraged under § 700.16.\n\n### Stage Four: Prevention Measures\nTo prevent similar incidents in the future, a comprehensive set of protocols for safe merging practices is established (see § 400.16). These protocols may include mandatory training and certification programs for mages who wish to engage in complex spells or magical combinations. Additionally, stricter guidelines on the use of certain types of magic are introduced based on the findings from the investigation.\n\nThe success of these remedial protocols depends heavily on swift and decisive action by all parties involved. Immediate containment ensures that no further harm is caused while the situation is being investigated and addressed. Rigorous assessment and rehabilitation efforts ensure that both the immediate threat and long-term environmental impacts are mitigated as effectively as possible.\n\nFurthermore, under § 100.15 and § 200.16, public safety remains a priority in all remediation activities. The Mages' Guild is committed to ensuring that any unlawful merging incidents are handled with the utmost care for the well-being of all affected parties. By adhering to these protocols, the Guild aims not only to protect its members and the environment but also to foster a culture of responsible magic use within the Midlands.\n\nIn conclusion, the remedial protocols outlined in this section provide a structured approach to addressing unlawful merging incidents and their collateral damage. These measures ensure that the risks associated with such events are minimized while promoting a safer, more regulated magical community.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1101.16",
            "400.15",
