            "400.16",
            "100.15"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Advanced Protocols for Sealing and Pocket-Dimensional Imprisonment — Oversight",
          "text": "Under the authority granted by § 200.13 regarding the mandatory containment of volatile arcane phenomena, the Guild has codified specific procedures for the permanent or temporary sequestration of hazardous entities within extradimensional spaces. When a breach is deemed irreparable through standard dampening fields as outlined in § 200.14, and the threat level necessitates immediate isolation beyond physical barriers, the activation of pocket-dimensional imprisonment becomes the requisite course of action. This process is strictly governed by the principles established in § 1.15 concerning expedited remediation, ensuring that the transition from a breached reality to a contained void occurs without further escalation or collateral damage to the ambient mana flow. The sealing matrix must be calibrated to the specific resonance frequency of the offending entity, a technical requirement that falls under the broader operational standards described in § 1.17 for peer review and mediation when multiple containment teams are involved in the operation.\n\nThe execution of such high-level containment requires a specialized class of wardens trained in the manipulation of spatial geometry, distinct from those who merely manage standard containment fields. Before any dimensional breach is initiated to house a rogue mage or an uncontrolled artifact, a preliminary assessment must be conducted to determine if the entity possesses capabilities that could interact with the pocket dimension itself. If there is evidence that the subject might attempt to communicate with the outside world through the dimensional membrane, additional filtering protocols must be applied, referencing the emergency response frameworks detailed in § 200.16 which dictate swift and effective responses to catastrophic scenarios. The sealing ritual is not merely a mechanical insertion but a legal act of confinement that renders the prisoner subject to the jurisdiction of the Paradox Trial, as defined in the penal codes for rogue mages. This judicial continuity ensures that even while imprisoned in an extradimensional cell, the accused retains their rights until the final adjudication of guilt or innocence, preventing arbitrary detention without due process.\n\nFurthermore, the administration of these sealed compartments requires ongoing monitoring to prevent the degradation of the dimensional walls, a failure mode that would constitute a new breach requiring immediate attention under § 200.13. The maintenance logs for any active pocket dimension must be reviewed quarterly by the High Council to ensure that the containment integrity remains within acceptable safety margins, aligning with the restricted research protocols found in § 500.12 regarding unsanctioned commercial spellcasting and unauthorized field operations. Any deviation from the established sealing sequence constitutes a violation of the Accords and may trigger an emergency protocol under § 200.15 for arcane breach mitigation if the seal begins to fail prematurely. The use of ancient pacts or legendary binding agreements to reinforce the dimensional walls is permissible only with express authorization from the High Council, adhering to the regulatory stance on forbidden schools and dangerous magic research found in the political spectrum of the Guild.\n\nIn instances where a pocket dimension becomes compromised by external forces or internal decay, the evacuation procedure must follow the strict hierarchy outlined in § 1.14 for expedited enforcement and immediate remedies, ensuring that no personnel are left behind during the collapse of the containment field. The transfer of prisoners between sealed dimensions is subject to rigorous verification protocols to prevent the smuggling of illicit artifacts or unauthorized spellcasters, a concern directly related to the provisions governing unlawful casting and confiscation found in § 800.15. Ultimately, the advanced protocols for sealing serve as the final line of defense against the escape of dangerous arcane phenomena, bridging the gap between physical containment and metaphysical incarceration while upholding the fundamental tenets of justice and safety enshrined in the foundational sections of the Accords.",
