          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Allocation and Redistribution of Sealed Mana Following Unauthorized Breach — Adm",
          "text": "In the event that an unauthorized arcane breach occurs, resulting in the spontaneous or forced sealing of volatile mana within the surrounding environment or the physical forms of affected individuals, the immediate responsibility for its management falls upon the designated Remediation Council established under § 200.16 Emergency Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation. The provisions set forth within this section establish the mandatory protocols regarding the containment of volatile arcane phenomena and the subsequent mitigation of environmental breaches, a mandate that extends logically to the redistribution of the sealed substance once the acute danger has passed. It is imperative that no sealed mana be treated as public property or discarded without explicit authorization from the High Council, for such actions would constitute a violation of the Mana Reverence principle outlined in § 1001.16 Confidentiality and Reporting Obligations for Mages' Guild Memb, which dictates that all arcane matters remain under strict regulatory purview until formally adjudicated. The process of allocation is not merely logistical but deeply legalistic, requiring an assessment of the source of the breach to determine whether the sealed mana constitutes a hazardous byproduct or a recoverable resource. Under § 200.13 Protocols for Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation, the initial phase focuses on stabilization; however, the transition from containment to redistribution requires a separate layer of administrative oversight to ensure that the reallocation does not inadvertently trigger secondary breaches or violate the sanctity of ancient pacts referenced in § 800.2 Paradox Trial Procedure.\n\nThe primary mechanism for redistribution involves the formation of a temporary custodial committee comprised of senior mages and legal clerks, whose sole function is to evaluate the integrity of the sealed mana and identify suitable recipients for its integration into sanctioned fields of study or remedial operations. This evaluation must adhere strictly to the standards of evidence and admissibility outlined in § 700.14 Admissibility Standards for Arcane Testimony and Artifacts, ensuring that the provenance and condition of the sealed energy are fully documented before any transfer is authorized. The committee shall possess no authority to redistribute mana that exhibits signs of corruption, instability, or connection to forbidden schools of magic, as defined in § 300.12 Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission regarding the handling of unsanctioned arts. Furthermore, any attempt to utilize sealed mana for commercial purposes without express authorization from the Guild's High Council is strictly prohibited under § 500.12 Additional Provisions Regarding Arcane Field Operations and Conduct, which forbids unsanctioned commercial spellcasting activities outside the bounds of licensed practice. The redistribution process must also account for the burden of proof resting upon the party asserting a particular fact regarding the safety or legality of the proposed allocation, as reinforced by § 700.6 Burden of Proof and Standard of Evidence in Arcan.\n\nWhen the sealed mana is deemed stable and suitable for reintroduction into the arcane ecosystem, it shall be allocated according to a priority matrix that weighs the severity of the original breach against the potential utility of the recovered energy. Priority shall be given to remediation efforts aimed at healing collateral contamination, as described in § 1101.14 Collateral Contamination and Remedial Obligations, where unintended consequences resulting from proximity or interaction between magical artifacts require immediate attention. In cases where the sealed mana originated from a breach caused by a rogue mage who is subsequently subject to penal sanctions, such as Sanction and Seal under the Paradox Trial system detailed in § 800.2 Paradox Trial Procedure, the redistribution must be conducted with heightened secrecy to prevent public panic or the misuse of the offender's residual power. The custodial committee shall draft a formal report detailing the composition of the sealed mana, the methods of its stabilization, and the specific recipients approved for its use, ensuring full compliance with the confidentiality requirements set forth in § 1001.16 Confidentiality and Reporting Obligations for Mages' Guild Memb. Failure to adhere to these protocols regarding the allocation and redistribution of sealed mana shall be treated as a severe violation of the Accords, potentially triggering further proceedings under the Paradox Trial or resulting in the permanent sealing of the mana itself to prevent any risk of paradoxical collapse.",
