      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Specimen Custody and Chain of Evidence Mandates for Arcane Research",
          "text": "Whereas the integrity of all magical research must be preserved to ensure public safety and maintain the balance of natural forces, it is hereby mandated that all studies conducted under permit shall adhere to strict ethical standards regarding the custody of living specimens, unstable artifacts, and volatile energy signatures. Under § 400.12 Research Integrity and Oversight Protocols, the primary objective of any research facility is to prevent contamination between distinct magical schools and to ensure that no forbidden school of magic, such as necromancy or blood magic, inadvertently influences the experimental outcome without express authorization. Consequently, every researcher holding a valid permit issued pursuant to § 400.6 Conditions for Valid Research Permits shall maintain an unbroken chain of custody for all materials introduced into the field or laboratory environment. This requirement applies with particular force where specimens are subject to Unauthorized Titan Growth Penalties and Remedies under § 400.11, as the physical manifestation of a growing anomaly demands immediate and continuous observation by a certified Arcane Artisan.\n\nThe custodial obligation extends beyond mere possession; it requires active monitoring of the specimen's magical signature against the baseline established in the original research proposal filed with the Autumnwood Accords Desk. Where a specimen exhibits signs of deviant methodology or innovation that falls outside the scope of the approved permit, such as unauthorized planar transits or conditional exemptions not covered under § 400.16 Conditional Exemption for Ancillary Planar Transits, the researcher must immediately cease interaction and notify the Oversight Committee. Failure to report such deviations constitutes a breach of § 400.8 Research Integrity and Oversight, which further mandates that all studies be subject to rigorous peer review under § 400.9 Research Integrity and Peer Review. It is not sufficient for a researcher to claim ignorance of a specimen's behavior when the research protocol explicitly calls for containment standards detailed in § 400.7 Specimen Containment Standards and Disposal Protocols; such negligence shifts the burden of proof entirely onto the accused party in any subsequent adjudication.\n\nFurthermore, the chain of evidence procedures must be meticulously documented to withstand scrutiny during an audit conducted under § 400.10 Research Oversight and Audit Procedures. Any break in this chain, whether caused by accidental leakage from a pocket dimension lab or intentional tampering to hide the true nature of a specimen, renders the research data inadmissible and subjects the researcher to sanctions ranging from seal removal to exile into a pocket dimension. In matters of arcane adjudication regarding custody breaches, the default allocation of proof remains with the accuser, yet the presumption under § 700.11 Burden Shifting and Presumptions in Arcane Litigation may warrant a shift where the defendant possesses exclusive access to the evidence and has failed to produce a log consistent with § 400.12 mandates. This strict liability approach ensures that the safety of the public space is never compromised by the whims of radical Innovators who might push boundaries too far, as warned against in the political debates surrounding The Unsanctioned Arts.\n\nThe prohibition on using magical means to convey information pertaining to the custody status of a specimen without written authorization from the Office of Archmage Sovereign, as stipulated in § 300.12 Prohibition on Magical Correspondence and Transmission, applies equally to internal reports between researchers and oversight bodies. Unauthorized transmission of data regarding a volatile specimen could itself constitute an act of unlicensed artisanry under § 500.12 Additional Provisions Regarding Arcane Field Operations and Conduct if performed outside the bounds of one's license. Additionally, where commercial spellcasting activities are attempted in connection with the sale or disposal of such specimens without express authorization from the Guild's High Council, as prohibited in § 500.12, the researcher faces enhanced penalties under § 800.11 Additional Provisions Regarding Penalties for Unauthorized Arcane Activity. The casting of spells without prior clearance by the Autumnwood Accords Desk to manipulate or transport these specimens constitutes an act of unlicensed artisanry that jeopardizes the sanctity of the mana reserve, violating the principles of Mana Reverence and risking the breaking of ancient pacts with legendary beings.\n\nFinally, it must be noted that any specimen exhibiting Unauthorized Titan Growth must be treated as a high-priority containment breach until remediation is complete under § 400.11. The research integrity protocols demand that no exception be made for specimens that have exceeded their designated growth parameters or boundary conditions set forth in § 400.14 Unauthorized Research Permits and Exceeding Boundaries. By adhering to these stringent custody and evidence requirements, the Autumnwood Accords Desk ensures that the pursuit of knowledge does not come at the cost of safety, balance, or the stability of the realm against the forces of chaos and the Unsanctioned Arts.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "400.12",
