          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Protocol for the Stratigraphic Excavation of Composite Thaumaturgical Layers",
          "text": "The certification process mandated under § 900.17 regarding sub-layered and latent arcane signatures demands a rigorous adherence to procedural standards that distinguish mere superficial observation from true stratigraphic excavation of composite thaumaturgy. When an initiate or certified analyst submits a petition for the stratification of a magical signature, the initial assessment must determine if the signature exhibits characteristics of layering, where distinct arcs of power have been superimposed upon one another without full dissolution of the underlying strata. This determination is critical because, as noted in § 900.14 concerning reporting ancillary effects and sub-layered magic, the presence of such complexity often indicates that the practitioner has engaged in advanced synthesis or concealment techniques that bypass standard regulatory scans. Therefore, the analyst must employ high-fidelity thaumaturgical resonance imaging to map the depth of the signature, ensuring that no latent component remains hidden from the certification board. Failure to penetrate the outer shell of a magic construct and identify the foundational ley-line manipulations may result in a false negative certification, which carries severe liability implications under the general provisions regarding persons bound by the Accords found in § 1.4.\n\nFurthermore, the temporal integrity of the signature must be preserved throughout the excavation process, as the act of analysis itself can inadvertently alter the latent properties if the resonance frequency is not precisely calibrated to the specific school of magic being examined. The analyst shall maintain a log of all resonance frequencies applied during the procedure, cross-referencing these against the established safety protocols outlined in § 500.12 regarding additional provisions for arcane field operations and conduct. This record-keeping serves not only as a testament to the analyst's competence but also as a necessary step in preventing accidental destabilization of the composite signature, which could lead to catastrophic releases of stored thaumaturgical energy. Any deviation from the prescribed frequency calibration must be immediately reported to the oversight council, as unchecked interference with latent signatures is tantamount to unauthorized modification of the magical landscape. Such actions violate the core principle that all magic, whether singular or layered, remains subject to the jurisdictional authority retained by the Autumnwood Accords Desk, as reaffirmed in § 1201.7 regarding portal and planar regulations which extend to all persons within the jurisdiction.\n\nIn cases where the stratigraphic analysis reveals a signature composed of conflicting or opposing magical schools, the certification board shall invoke the burden-shifting presumptions detailed in § 700.11 to determine the intent behind such composite construction. If the outer layers appear benign while the inner strata contain forbidden elements, the presumption shall shift to the practitioner requiring them to provide a comprehensive justification for the synthesis of these opposing forces. This is particularly relevant when considering the political tensions between the Conservators and Innovators regarding the study of dangerous or restricted schools of magic, as detailed in the political spectrum concerning the unsanctioned arts. The board must weigh the potential benefits of such composite magic against the inherent risks it poses to the stability of the Weave, ensuring that no practitioner can claim ignorance of the latent dangers embedded within their own signature. Consequently, the certification granted for any multi-layered signature is contingent upon a complete and transparent disclosure of all constituent elements, aligning with the overarching mandate of § 900.6 which requires full disclosure and certification of ancillary magic to ensure regulatory oversight is not exhausted by mere technicalities.\n\nFinally, the physical or digital medium upon which the certified stratigraphy is recorded must be sealed with an indelible thaumaturgical sigil that cannot be altered without triggering a paradox alarm linked directly to the Paradox Trial mechanism described in § 800.2. This seal ensures that the certification remains immutable and serves as the definitive legal record of the signature's composition at the time of analysis. Should any attempt be made to obscure or modify this certified record, the alteration itself shall constitute a violation of the Accords, subjecting the perpetrator to immediate review by the Paradox Trial where the severity of the violation may warrant a Seal of Silence under § 800.3 if the intent was malicious concealment of latent dangers. Thus, the certification of sub-layered and latent arcane signatures is not merely a technical validation but a profound legal act that binds the practitioner to a standard of transparency and accountability, ensuring that the complex architecture of modern thaumaturgy remains visible, auditable, and safely integrated within the broader framework of the Autumnwood Accords.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "900.17",
            "900.14",
            "1.4",
            "500.12",
            "1201.7",
