      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "§ 800.17 Allocation and Reclamation of Sealed Capacities",
          "text": "Under the authority granted by § 800.7 Related Requirements and in strict adherence to the principles outlined in § 800.1 Discipline; Range of Sanctions, this section establishes the definitive protocol for the reclamation of magical potential following the imposition of a Sanction and Seal. It is the settled interpretation of the Accords that when an individual mage or rogue entity is subjected to the penal sanction of capacity sealing under the Paradox Trial provisions described in § 800.5 Pocket-Prison Procedure, the resulting void within their metaphysical constitution does not merely cease to exist but becomes a state-managed asset subject to immediate reclamation protocols. The Guild Accords Desk, acting pursuant to its mandate in § 1.4–1.9 regarding persons and seals, hereby declares that any unclaimed or improperly disposed of sealed capacity constitutes a hazard to the ambient mana flow and must be retrieved by certified Arcane Recovery Teams no later than three standard cycles following the finalization of the verdict. This requirement aligns with the environmental safeguards detailed in § 800.16 Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption and Environmental Impact, ensuring that the extraction process does not inadvertently trigger residual paradoxes or destabilize local ley lines.\n\nThe procedure for reclamation shall be executed only after the completion of any mandatory reporting requirements under § 800.13 Mandatory Reporting of Arcane Artifact Malfunction and Degradation, which serves as a prerequisite for determining the stability of the sealed individual. Furthermore, the allocation of these reclaimed capacities is strictly governed by the prohibitions against commercial exploitation found in § 500.12 Additional Provisions Regarding Arcane Field Operations and Conduct; specifically, no entity shall engage in the trafficking or unauthorized redistribution of sealed magical potential without express authorization from the High Council. Any attempt to bypass this chain of custody, including efforts to siphon energy directly from a penalized individual or their containment vessel, shall be classified as an act of unlawful casting under § 800.9 Penalties for Unlawful Casting and Use of Arcane Artifacts. The severity of such infractions is amplified when they involve the use of confiscated items that have been subjected to the specific disposal mechanisms outlined in § 800.10 Disposition of Confiscated Items, as tampering with these designated objects constitutes a dual violation of both property law and magical ethics.\n\nIn instances where the reclamation process reveals anomalies suggesting that the original sanctioning was insufficient to fully contain the mage's paradox signature, the case shall be referred immediately for review under § 800.12 Additional Provisions Regarding Unlawful Casting and Confiscation. This referral mechanism ensures that the foundational prohibitions regarding retroactive application of sanctions remain intact; no new penalties or extended confinement terms may be imposed based solely on post-reclamation findings without a fresh adjudication, thereby preserving the integrity of the Ex Post Facto Prohibition referenced in § 800.9 Ex Post Facto Prohibition and Retroactive Sanctions. The Desk further notes that any disputes arising from the valuation of reclaimed capacity or the liability of recovery teams must be litigated in accordance with the evidentiary standards set forth in § 700.12 Additional Provisions Regarding Arcane Litigation and Evidence, where magical residue serves as admissible proof of successful reclamation or procedural error.\n\nIt is imperative that all personnel involved in the reclamation process acknowledge the supplementary obligations detailed in § 800.6 Ancillary Obligations, which mandate rigorous documentation of every step taken during the extraction of sealed power. Failure to maintain these records shall result in disciplinary action under the same range of sanctions applicable to the original offender, reinforcing the principle that negligence in post-penalty administration is as dangerous as the initial transgression. The Desk also cites § 1301.2 Penalties for additional context regarding the cascading consequences of ignoring reclamation windows, noting that uncollected capacities may eventually attract unwanted attention from entities opposed to the Accords, including factions such as the Silver Flame who view all unnatural phenomena as abominations requiring purging. Consequently, the timely and lawful retrieval of sealed potential is not merely an administrative task but a critical defense mechanism against broader metaphysical threats.\n\nFinally, this section operates in concert with the transitional arrangements established in § 1301.11 Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements to ensure that no individual or entity knowingly facilitates the unauthorized retention of sealed capacities. The Accords Desk reserves the right to invoke the residual clauses of § 100.12 Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements should any gap emerge in the current reclamation framework, ensuring that the operational continuity of the penal system remains unbroken despite evolving magical technologies or shifting political landscapes within the Conservator and Innovator factions. By integrating these specific procedural mandates into the broader disciplinary measures of Part 800, this provision completes the regulatory loop from sanction to disposal, ensuring that the magic removed from society is neither lost nor misused, but rather restored to a state of safe, controlled potential under the watchful eye of the Guild's highest authorities.",
          "key": "a",
