        {
          "heading": "The Mechanics of Resonant Unsealing in Transit",
          "text": "Under the provisions established for the management of sealed capacities, the physical transport of an artifact containing repressed or dormant magic presents a unique set of legal and logistical challenges that must be addressed distinct from standard containment protocols. When a vessel designated under § 800.17 is moved across dimensional thresholds or traverses zones of high arcane flux, the seal itself becomes subject to what is termed \"resonant drift,\" a phenomenon wherein the frequency of the binding lattice slowly desynchronizes with the ambient magical environment. This section mandates that any transport convoy carrying sealed capacities must be accompanied by a licensed conservator whose primary duty is to monitor the integrity of the seal against external interference, ensuring that the potential within does not accidentally manifest before reaching its destination or a designated reclamation site. The failure to maintain this constant surveillance constitutes a breach under § 800.15, as the unintended release of even minor amounts of stored potential can trigger ancillary arcane disruption in surrounding settlements.\n\nThe legal framework governing these transports requires that all vessels carrying sealed capacities be marked with the official insignia of the Archmage Sovereign and equipped with dampening fields calibrated to the specific frequency of the seal being transported. It is hereby forbidden, under any circumstance permitted by § 100.15, for a practitioner to attempt to accelerate the reclamation process through unauthorized catalytic rituals while the vessel is in transit; such actions are reserved exclusively for the High Council of the Autumnwood Accords upon arrival at the receiving jurisdiction. The burden of proof regarding the stability of a sealed capacity during transport rests entirely with the carrier, who must maintain a continuous log detailing any fluctuations in ambient mana density or seal tension. If a vessel is forced to halt due to an emergency breach of containment protocols, as defined in § 200.16, the immediate response must be to initiate emergency sealing procedures rather than attempting to evacuate the contents, unless the threat of catastrophic release outweighs the risk of retention, a judgment call explicitly reserved for senior practitioners under § 800.5 Pocket-Prison Procedure guidelines.\n\nFurthermore, the transfer of custody between jurisdictions carrying sealed capacities is governed by strict protocols regarding the documentation of the seal's current state and its remaining temporal lifespan. Any discrepancy found during the handover process, such as a seal that has degraded beyond the safety threshold established in § 400.7 Specimen Containment Standards and Disposal Proto, must be reported immediately to the Accords Desk for re-evaluation. The carrier of a compromised vessel shall not be permitted to proceed until the artifact is either safely returned to its original sealing matrix or transferred to a secure facility capable of handling unstable contents under the supervision of an independent auditor. This provision ensures that the integrity of the arcane lattice remains uncompromised by negligence in transit, reinforcing the principle that the safety of the natural world takes precedence over the convenience of logistical efficiency.\n\nIn instances where the seal is damaged or compromised during transit, the carrier must adhere to the remediation protocols outlined in § 800.15, which dictate the immediate isolation of the affected area and the summoning of emergency response teams trained in arcane containment. The failure to comply with these emergency protocols can result in severe penalties, including the invocation of the Paradox Trial under the penal system of the Mages' Guild, where guilt may be determined by a formal, magically-regulated duel or through the application of Sanction and Seal depending on the severity of the breach. Ultimately, the safe transport of sealed capacities is not merely a logistical exercise but a critical component of maintaining the delicate balance between stored potential and the stability of the world, requiring vigilance, discipline, and strict adherence to the laws set forth in these Accords.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "800.17",
            "800.15",
