    {
      "cite": "900.18",
      "part": "part_ix",
      "title": "Ancillary Arcane Disruption Protocol Enhancements",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Ancillary Arcane Disruption Protocol Enhancements",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords recognize that the reporting and handling of ancillary arcane effects require additional provisions to ensure safety and compliance with the Accords. Section 900.18 introduces enhanced protocols designed to mitigate risks associated with unintended disruptions caused by ancillary magic. These protocols are intended not only for the casters themselves but also for those who may be affected by such disturbances.\n\nUnder § 900.18, casters must immediately report any disruption of an arcane field or effect that has caused significant interference with public safety, property, or other magical constructs. This includes disruptions that arise from sub-layered magic and latent signatures, as addressed in § 900.17. Failure to comply with this obligation may result in penalties under § 800.11 for unlawful casting and confiscation of materials.\n\nFurthermore, casters must maintain a detailed log of all such reported incidents, including the nature of the disruption, its duration, and any measures taken to mitigate or remediate it. These logs shall be made available upon request from the Mages' Guild Accords Desk or any authorized body under these Accords. Failure to keep adequate records may result in additional penalties as outlined in § 900.12.\n\nThe Accords also mandate that all casters take reasonable steps to prevent further disruption, which includes but is not limited to identifying and addressing the root cause of the disturbance. This requirement extends particularly to those involved in exceptional research permits or supervised experiments under § 900.15, where additional oversight may be necessary.\n\nIn cases where a caster's actions have resulted in significant disruptions, the Accords provide for remediation protocols outlined in § 900.16. These protocols are designed to restore balance and stability to the affected area or construct. The responsible party must adhere strictly to these protocols to avoid further complications. In instances of severe disruption, the Accords may call upon specialized teams to assist with the remediation process.\n\nAdditionally, any caster who knowingly engages in activities that create significant disruptions without appropriate safeguards is subject to stricter penalties under § 800.12. Such activities include but are not limited to casting in densely populated areas or near critical infrastructure without prior approval from the Mages' Guild Accords Desk.\n\nThe Autumnwood Accords emphasize the importance of transparency and cooperation between casters and regulatory bodies. Casters are encouraged to work closely with the Mages' Guild Accords Desk when planning and executing potentially disruptive spells, especially those involving sub-layered magic or latent signatures. This cooperative approach ensures that all parties involved have a clear understanding of potential risks and can take necessary precautions.\n\nIn conclusion, § 900.18 introduces enhanced protocols aimed at mitigating the risks associated with ancillary arcane disruptions. These protocols are essential for maintaining public safety and ensuring compliance with the Accords. Casters are encouraged to comply fully with these requirements to avoid penalties and contribute to a safer magical environment. For more detailed information on reporting and remediation procedures, see § 900.13 and § 900.16 respectively.\n\nUnder § 900.6 Disclosure and Certification of Ancillary Magic, casters are also required to disclose any known ancillary effects that might arise from their spells. This ensures that all parties involved in a spell's casting understand the potential risks and can take appropriate measures. For more information on disclosure requirements, see § 900.6.\n\nAdditionally, under § 900.12 Additional Provisions, nothing in this Part shall be construed to limit or impair the full force and effect of any other provision contained herein or in the Autumnwood Accords generally. Any act, omission, or practice in violation of these provisions may result in penalties as outlined in § 800.11. For more information on sanctions for unauthorized casting, see § 800.11.\n\nLastly, under § 900.15 Oversight Protocols for Exceptional Research Permits and Supervised Experiments, casters conducting research or experiments that involve significant disruption potential are required to adhere to strict oversight protocols. These protocols ensure that all parties involved have a clear understanding of the risks and can take necessary precautions. For more information on these protocols, see § 900.15.\n\nIn summary, § 900.18 provides essential guidelines for handling ancillary arcane disruptions, ensuring safety and compliance with the Accords. Casters are urged to comply fully with these requirements to avoid penalties and contribute to a safer magical environment.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "900.18",
