    {
      "cite": "1101.18",
      "part": "part_xi",
      "title": "Remedial Protocols for Unlawful Casting and Contamination",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Remedial Protocols for Unlawful Casting and Contamination",
          "text": "In the administration of justice and the regulation of magical practice, the Autumnwood Accords have long sought to balance the freedom to innovate with the responsibility to uphold public safety. Section §1101.18 Additional Provisions aims to address a critical gap in remedial protocols when collateral contamination arises from unlawful casting or negligence. This section shall provide clarity on the obligations of mages and their clients following such incidents, ensuring that any magical item or construct damaged by unauthorized or negligent spellcasting is promptly addressed.\n\nUnder §500.11 Unsanctioned Field Operations and Liability, it has been established that the casting of spells without prior clearance from the Autumnwood Accords Desk constitutes an act of unlicensed artisanry. Such acts not only jeopardize public safety but also introduce risks of collateral contamination. Section §1101.18 seeks to mitigate these risks by imposing specific remedial obligations on those who engage in such unauthorized activities.\n\nWhen a magical item or construct suffers damage, corruption, or destabilization due to unauthorized alteration, negligent maintenance, or exposure to prohibited energies, such defect shall be deemed a collateral contamination under §1101.7 Collateral Taints and Magical Contagion. The mage responsible for the casting is required to bear the primary burden of proof regarding the extent of the contamination and any necessary remedial actions (see §1101.8 Burden of Proof and Presumptions).\n\nUnder §1101.14 Collateral Contamination and Remedial Obligations, the mage must first ensure that all affected items are removed from public use until such time as they may be deemed safe for continued existence or disposal (see §1101.15 Collateral Contamination and Remedial Protocols). The mage shall then submit a report to the Autumnwood Accords Desk detailing any observed collateral contamination, including descriptions of magical residue, lingering arcane echoes, and potential risks to the integrity of the item.\n\nIf the item is found to be irreparably contaminated or potentially dangerous, it must be rendered harmless through appropriate measures. These may include the use of neutralization protocols (see §1101.17 Remedial Protocols for Unlawful Casting and Contamination), which are designed to mitigate any lingering magical effects without causing further harm.\n\nThe mage shall also bear responsibility for notifying all parties who have interacted with or possessed the affected item since its last known state of integrity. Such notifications must be made within a reasonable time frame, allowing individuals to take necessary precautions against potential risks (see §1101.3 Notification Requirements).\n\nIn cases where the collateral contamination is deemed minor and can be remedied without rendering the item harmless, the mage may opt to undertake such measures themselves. However, if the contamination persists or worsens despite efforts to address it, further action shall be required under §1101.4 Emergency Protocols.\n\nThe Autumnwood Accords acknowledge that collateral contamination is an unintended consequence of magical practice and seeks to ensure that appropriate protocols are in place for its mitigation. By imposing these obligations on mages who engage in unauthorized casting or negligence, the Accords aim not only to protect public safety but also to maintain the integrity of arcane practices.\n\nIt is further noted that under §1101.6 Unintended Consequences, mages are required to act reasonably and prudently when engaging in any form of magical work. The failure to do so can lead to liability for collateral contamination (see §1101.3 Liability for Residue and Lingering Arcane Echoes). Therefore, the provisions set forth in this section serve as a reminder that all mages must act with due diligence and care when performing any form of arcane magic.\n\nFinally, it is emphasized that compliance with these remedial protocols shall be subject to periodic review by the Autumnwood Accords Desk. Failure to adhere to these obligations may result in sanctions under §500.11 Unsanctioned Field Operations and Liability or other penal measures as deemed necessary (see §1101.4 Sanctions for Breach of Protocols).\n\nIn conclusion, §1101.18 Additional Provisions seeks to establish a clear framework for addressing collateral contamination resulting from unauthorized or negligent casting. By imposing specific obligations on mages and their clients, the section aims to ensure that any such incidents are promptly addressed, thereby safeguarding public safety and maintaining the integrity of arcane practices.",
          "key": "a",
