        {
          "heading": "Remediation Protocols for Collateral Merging Events",
          "text": "In the event that an act of unlawful casting has resulted in unintended merging events, remedial protocols must be followed to ensure the safety and integrity of magical constructs, items, or environments involved. Under § 1101.18, these protocols are designed not only to mitigate immediate risks but also to prevent further contamination or destabilization that could have broader implications.\n\nCollateral Merging Events (CMEs) refer to situations where unlawful casting has inadvertently brought together magical entities, items, or constructs in ways they were not intended for. These events can result from a variety of causes, including unauthorized modifications, negligent maintenance, exposure to prohibited energies, or the casting of spells that exceed their intended parameters. § 1101.18 mandates that when such merging occurs, immediate action must be taken to separate and stabilize the affected entities.\n\nThe first step in addressing CMEs is a thorough inspection conducted by authorized Mages' Guild personnel. This includes assessing the nature and extent of the merge, identifying any potentially harmful or unstable elements, and determining the most effective means to isolate them. Under § 1101.14, these personnel are required to document their findings comprehensively, ensuring that all relevant data is accurately recorded for future reference.\n\nOnce a CME has been identified, remediation efforts focus on separation and stabilization. Depending on the nature of the merge, this may involve physical disassembly or magical disruption techniques. § 1101.17 provides guidelines on the use of various remedial protocols, including the application of containment fields to prevent further spread of contamination. In cases where a stable separation is not possible without causing additional damage, alternative solutions such as reprogramming or reintegration under controlled conditions may be considered.\n\nThe Mages' Guild reserves the right to impose additional obligations on those responsible for CMEs. These may include reparations for any damage caused, mandatory training programs to improve casting techniques and safety measures, and periodic monitoring by guild officials to ensure compliance with all remedial protocols. Under § 800.11 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation, there are also potential penalties that could be imposed, ranging from fines to suspension of magical privileges.\n\nFurthermore, the Mages' Guild encourages reporting mechanisms for CMEs. Any individual or entity responsible for an act leading to a merging event must report it immediately to the appropriate authorities. § 800.12 further outlines the obligations on those involved in such incidents, emphasizing the importance of transparency and accountability. Failure to comply with these reporting requirements can result in severe penalties under the Guild's disciplinary measures.\n\nIn instances where a CME results in significant collateral contamination or destabilization, the Mages' Guild may elect to engage in more extensive remediation efforts. This could include the destruction of contaminated items or constructs, relocation of affected areas, and implementation of long-term monitoring protocols. The aim is not only to address immediate issues but also to prevent recurrence through education and stricter enforcement of safety measures.\n\nIt is important to note that each case of CME will be handled on a case-by-case basis, taking into account the specific circumstances involved. § 1101.16 emphasizes the importance of flexibility in applying remedial protocols to ensure they are effective and appropriate for each unique situation.\n\nIn conclusion, the Mages' Guild's approach to dealing with Collateral Merging Events underscores its commitment to maintaining order and safety within the magical community. By adhering to these protocols, the Guild aims to protect both individuals and the broader environment from the potential dangers of unlawful casting. This comprehensive framework ensures that any merging event is addressed promptly and effectively, thereby fostering a safer and more regulated magical world.",
          "key": "b",
