        {
          "heading": "Remediation Protocols for Unlawful Merging Events Involving Conjured Constructs",
          "text": "Under the auspices of these Accords, when mages engage in unlawful casting or negligent practices that lead to the unintended merging of conjured constructs, it becomes imperative to establish clear protocols for remediation. Conjuring is a complex and potent form of magic that, if misused or mishandled, can result in dangerous and unpredictable outcomes. This section outlines the necessary procedures for addressing such events, ensuring both safety and accountability.\n\n### Legal Framework\n\nIn cases where conjured constructs have been merged unlawfully or inadvertently, the mage responsible must immediately report the incident to the Autumnwood Accords Desk (§ 1101.18). Upon receipt of notification, the Desk shall conduct a thorough investigation into the circumstances surrounding the merging event. The mage is required to provide all relevant documentation, including spell components and any other artifacts involved in the casting (§ 700.12).\n\n### Assessment and Risk Evaluation\n\nThe Accords Desk will assess the risk posed by the merged constructs based on their nature and potential effects. If the merged construct poses a significant threat to public safety or stability, immediate containment measures shall be initiated under § 800.9 Penalties for Unlawful Casting and Use of Arcane Artifacts (see also § 1101.14). The mage responsible will be held accountable for ensuring that any necessary containment is carried out promptly.\n\n### Remedial Measures\n\nThe remediation protocols outlined in this section are designed to mitigate the risks associated with merged conjured constructs. These measures include, but are not limited to:\n\n- **Containment and Sealing**: In instances where the merged construct presents an immediate danger, it must be contained and sealed away until further investigation is complete (§ 1101.17). The mage responsible for the casting will bear the costs associated with containment and storage.\n\n- **Reversion Spells**: If possible, reversion spells may be employed to attempt to reverse the merging process. However, these spells are highly unpredictable and can themselves pose risks. Therefore, their use must be authorized by the Accords Desk (§ 800.12).\n\n- **Disassembly of Constructs**: In some cases, the only viable option may be the disassembly of the merged construct to separate its components. This procedure is fraught with danger due to the potential for further destabilization or recombination. The mage responsible will need to work closely with experienced mages and adherents to the Accords Desk (§ 1101.16).\n\n### Accountability and Reporting Obligations\n\nThe mage responsible for the unlawful casting that led to the merging of conjured constructs shall face disciplinary action under § 800.15 Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption. Additionally, they must provide a detailed report on the events leading up to the merging, including any spells used and their intended purposes (§ 700.12). This report will be reviewed by the Accords Desk, which may impose further sanctions as deemed necessary.\n\n### Post-Merge Evaluation\n\nAfter containment or disassembly has been completed, a post-merge evaluation shall take place. This evaluation will assess whether any lessons were learned from the incident that could prevent future occurrences. The mage responsible for the casting will be required to attend this evaluation and provide insights into potential improvements in their practices (§ 800.12). Failure to comply with these requirements may result in additional penalties under § 800.9.\n\n### Cross-Reference\n\nThis section builds upon the foundational principles laid out in § 800.15 Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption, which provides a broader framework for addressing collateral damage and unintended effects of magical actions (see also § 1101.14). The protocols established herein are designed to complement these overarching guidelines, ensuring that all aspects of conjured construct merging events are handled in accordance with the Accords.\n\nIn conclusion, the remediation protocols outlined here aim to ensure that any unlawful or negligent acts leading to the merging of conjured constructs are addressed swiftly and effectively. By adhering to these procedures, mages can help maintain the integrity and safety of magical practices within the jurisdiction of the Autumnwood Accords Desk.",
          "key": "d",
