        {
          "heading": "Remediation Protocols for Unlawful Casting and Construct Interference",
          "text": "Under § 1101.18, the Mages' Guild Accords Desk has established comprehensive protocols to address scenarios where unlawful casting has inadvertently caused interference with or manipulation of magical constructs. The term \"construct interference\" encompasses situations in which a mage's unauthorized spell or arcane manipulation has altered, damaged, or otherwise adversely affected an existing construct not under their control. This interference may lead to unintended consequences that can range from minor inconveniences to catastrophic failures.\n\nThe primary objective of these protocols is to mitigate the damage caused by such interference and ensure that the construct in question remains functional and safe for its intended purpose. The mage responsible for the unlawful casting will be held accountable under § 800.11 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation, and shall be required to comply with the remedial measures prescribed herein.\n\nConstructs affected by such interference may include automated machinery, magical wards, protective enchantments, or even more complex constructs like golems and animated objects. The mage who performed the unlawful casting must first report the incident in accordance with § 1101.12 Collateral Contamination and Remedial Obligations. Failure to do so will result in additional penalties under § 800.1 Discipline; Range of Sanctions.\n\nUpon receiving notification, the Accords Desk shall conduct an immediate investigation pursuant to § 700.12 Additional Provisions Regarding Arcane Litigation and Evidence. The mage responsible for the unlawful casting must provide all relevant information regarding their actions, including the spell cast, the location where it was performed, and any witnesses present at the time of the incident.\n\nOnce the Accords Desk has determined that interference with a construct has occurred, remedial protocols will be implemented based on the nature and extent of the damage. These protocols may include but are not limited to:\n\n1. Immediate cessation of all operations involving the affected construct until it can be fully evaluated.\n2. Isolation of the area where the interference took place to prevent further escalation or collateral damage.\n3. Restoration of the construct to its original state, if possible. This process shall follow the guidelines set forth in § 800.12 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation.\n4. In cases where restoration is not feasible, the mage responsible for the interference will be required to compensate the owner or operator of the construct according to the standards outlined in § 300.5 Damage Compensation.\n\nIn instances where the unlawful casting has resulted in significant damage to a critical construct, emergency protocols may be invoked as per § 800.18 Remediation Protocols and Reporting Obligations for Arcane Malfunctions. Such cases may include scenarios where the interference has endangered public safety or disrupted essential services.\n\nFurthermore, under § 1101.17 Remedial Protocols for Unlawful Casting and Contamination, the mage responsible for the unlawful casting must undergo a peer review process to assess their understanding of the potential consequences of their actions. This review shall be conducted by a panel of experienced mages selected from both the Conservator and Innovator factions within the Mages' Guild. The findings of this review will inform any disciplinary action taken against the mage in question.\n\nIt is important to note that the Accords Desk reserves the right to modify these protocols on an ad-hoc basis to address newly identified risks or challenges. Any such modifications shall be communicated promptly to all affected parties, including the mage responsible for the unlawful casting and the owners of the affected constructs.\n\nThe Mages' Guild Accords Desk emphasizes the paramount importance of adhering to the established guidelines governing lawful magical practice. The protocols outlined herein are designed not only to protect the integrity of magical constructs but also to safeguard the broader community from potential hazards arising from irresponsible or unregulated use of magic. By strictly enforcing these remedial measures, the Mages' Guild seeks to promote a culture of responsible magic-wielding and uphold the highest standards of professional conduct among its members.\n\nUnder § 1101.14 Collateral Contamination and Remedial Obligations, it is emphasized that collateral contamination extends beyond mere physical damage; it encompasses any alteration or disruption caused by unlawful casting. Therefore, when a mage's actions inadvertently interfere with existing constructs, they are subject to the same remediation protocols as those dealing with direct contamination events. See § 1101.14 for additional details on this topic.\n\nThe Accords Desk encourages all mages to exercise vigilance and caution in their magical practice, recognizing that even the slightest deviation from proper protocol can have far-reaching implications. By adhering to these protocols, mages not only uphold the integrity of the guild but also contribute to a safer, more harmonious environment for all those who wield magic.",
