      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Additional Provisions for Unlicensed Arcane Containment and Breach Mitigation",
          "text": "In recognition of the increasing complexity of magical applications and the necessity to safeguard against rogue or dangerous magic that could breach containment protocols, additional provisions are hereby established under Part 200. The purpose of these supplementary protocols is to ensure that unlicensed individuals who engage in arcane activities outside their formal training and licensing do not compromise public safety or violate the fundamental principles of magical ethics.\n\nUnder § 200.19, it is made clear that any individual without a valid license from the Mages' Guild shall be subject to stringent containment protocols should they breach containment measures. This includes the immediate confiscation of all materials and tools used in such activities, along with the mandatory reporting to the Autumnwood Accords Desk for evaluation and potential disciplinary action. The desk retains the authority to impose sanctions as outlined in § 200.9.\n\nThe provisions under § 200.19 mandate that unlicensed individuals found responsible for breaches must participate in a comprehensive assessment process overseen by a panel of licensed mages. This assessment ensures that any potential risks associated with their activities are mitigated and provides guidance on how to proceed lawfully should they choose to engage in further magical practice.\n\nFurthermore, § 200.19 stipulates that unlicensed individuals who breach containment or commit acts of coercion or degradation (see § 200.12 for specific prohibitions) shall face enhanced penalties as outlined in § 800.11. The desk is empowered to order the cessation of all activities, the sealing of any magical artifacts involved, and the initiation of a trial process similar to those described in the Paradox Trial policy (see mage_guild.penal.sanction_and_seal).\n\nIn cases where containment breaches are severe or result in direct harm to others, § 200.19 allows for immediate action by authorized personnel, including the use of emergency protocols as defined in § 200.15 and the deployment of specialized containment teams trained for such situations.\n\nThe desk shall maintain a record of all incidents involving unlicensed individuals who breach arcane containment measures or engage in coercive activities (see also § 700.12). These records are critical to the ongoing evaluation and enforcement of the protocols and ensure transparency in adherence to these additional provisions.\n\nLastly, it is emphasized that the Autumnwood Accords Desk shall work closely with local law enforcement and other relevant authorities to coordinate efforts and ensure compliance with these provisions (see § 500.12 for related requirements regarding field operations). The desk retains discretion over the interpretation of these rules in light of evolving circumstances but must adhere strictly to the foundational principles set forth in § 700.1 Evidence Generally.\n\nIn conclusion, § 200.19 serves to protect public safety and uphold ethical standards by providing clear guidelines for addressing breaches by unlicensed individuals. This section underscores the Guild's commitment to ensuring that all magical practices are conducted responsibly and in accordance with the Accords' principles.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "200.19",
            "200.9",
            "200.12",
            "800.11",
            "200.15",
            "700.12",
