    {
      "cite": "300.19",
      "part": "part_iii",
      "title": "Additional Provisions for Magical Correspondence and Transmission Oversight",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Additional Provisions for Magical Correspondence and Transmission Oversight",
          "text": "In the administration of the laws governing the use of magic, it is imperative to ensure that all forms of magical correspondence and transmission are subject to strict oversight and control. § 300.19 seeks to supplement existing regulations by providing additional safeguards against the misuse of these potent tools, particularly in relation to the Unsanctioned Arts and the Quiet List.\n\nUnder § 300.12, it is already prohibited for any caster to utilize magical means to convey information pertaining to the Unsanctioned Arts without express authorization from the Office of Archmage Sovereign. However, this prohibition does not cover all forms of magical transmission or correspondence. § 300.19 aims to fill this gap by imposing additional restrictions and oversight mechanisms.\n\nAll casters are required to report any instances of unauthorized magical transmission or correspondence involving the Unsanctioned Arts immediately to the Office of Archmage Sovereign for review and potential action under § 800.12. This includes, but is not limited to, the use of telepathic spells, astral projection, or any other form of arcane communication that bypasses conventional means.\n\nFurthermore, under § 300.19, any caster engaging in magical correspondence or transmission shall adhere to a set of Transmission Protocols outlined in § 300.14. These protocols are designed to ensure the security and integrity of all transmissions, preventing unauthorized access and misuse. Violations of these protocols may result in disciplinary action under § 500.12.\n\nThe Quiet List, as defined in § 300.10, is a list maintained by the Office of Archmage Sovereign that includes names of those who have committed acts or transgressions deemed serious enough to warrant a prohibition on magical correspondence and transmission. Under § 300.19, any caster attempting to communicate with individuals listed on the Quiet List without express permission from the Office will be subject to severe penalties under § 500.12.\n\nAdditionally, § 300.19 imposes stringent requirements for the use of magical correspondences and transmissions in research contexts. Researchers must adhere strictly to protocols laid out in § 400.12 Research Integrity and Oversight Protocols. Violations of these protocols could lead to the suspension or revocation of research permits under § 500.11 Unsanctioned Field Operations and Liability.\n\nThe Office of Archmage Sovereign retains full discretion over all matters relating to magical correspondence and transmission, including the imposition of additional conditions or restrictions as necessary. This includes the power to issue emergency orders banning specific forms of magical communication in times of crisis, under § 300.17 Contingencies for Unauthorized Arcane Breaches.\n\nIn summary, § 300.19 seeks to enhance the existing framework by providing clear guidelines and oversight mechanisms for all forms of magical correspondence and transmission. It ensures that these potent tools are used responsibly and in accordance with the laws governing the Autumnwood Accords. Any caster found to be violating the provisions set forth herein shall face severe consequences, including potential legal action under § 800.12 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation.\n\nIt is incumbent upon all casters to familiarize themselves with these regulations and ensure compliance. Failure to do so will not only result in personal liability but may also have broader implications for the profession of magic as a whole. The integrity of magical practice depends on the adherence to these standards, ensuring that the balance of natural forces remains undisturbed.\n\nUnder § 300.19, any caster attempting to communicate with individuals listed on the Quiet List without express permission from the Office shall be subject to severe penalties under § 500.12.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "300.19",
            "300.12",
            "800.12",
            "300.14",
            "500.12",
