            "1201.15",
            "1301.15"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Ancillary Arcane Effects Reporting Protocols: Protocol Compliance and Enforcemen",
          "text": "The Mages' Guild Accords Desk recognizes that the proper enforcement and adherence to § 900.19 Ancillary Arcane Effects Reporting Protocols are paramount in ensuring the safety and well-being of all practitioners, residents, and observers within the jurisdiction of the Autumnwood Accords. The protocols outlined herein not only seek to identify and document ancillary arcane effects but also provide clear guidelines for their reporting and subsequent remediation.\n\nCompliance with these protocols is mandatory for all licensed mages operating under the auspices of the Mages' Guild Accords Desk. Under § 1401.14 Conditional Exemption for Ancillary Planar Transits, it has been recognized that certain transitory applications of planar transit are ancillary to primary magical acts and require specific handling to ensure compliance with both the spirit and letter of the law. Therefore, any deviation from these protocols shall be met with stringent enforcement measures.\n\nUnder § 500.15 Catchline Title: Liability for Ancillary Arcane Events and Casualties, mages failing to report ancillary arcane effects in a timely manner may be held liable for any resulting harm or damage caused by such effects. The Accords Desk will rigorously enforce compliance with these protocols through periodic audits and inspections. Any mage found non-compliant shall face sanctions under § 1401.16 Conditional Exemption and Ancillary Arcane Disruption Protocols, including potential sealing of their magic.\n\nThe enforcement mechanism for protocol compliance includes a two-tiered system: formal notifications followed by escalating penalties upon repeated infractions. A mage first notified of non-compliance will be required to undergo additional training under § 900.14 Reporting Ancillary Effects and Sub-Layered Magic, emphasizing the importance of real-time monitoring and immediate reporting. Repeated failures may result in more severe measures such as the imposition of fines or, in egregious cases, the loss of magical privileges.\n\nIn instances where a mage is found to have knowingly neglected their duty under these protocols, the Accords Desk will conduct a comprehensive review pursuant to § 800.15 Catchline Title: Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption in Non-Acceptable Circumstances. This includes an evaluation of any ancillary effects that may have occurred as a result of such neglect and the provision of necessary remedial actions.\n\nMoreover, the Accords Desk will ensure transparency through public reporting mechanisms. Violations and their resolutions will be documented and made available to the public for scrutiny under § 1301.16 Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption. This not only serves as a deterrent but also fosters trust between practitioners and the wider community.\n\nThe enforcement of these protocols is further bolstered by the establishment of a dedicated compliance officer whose role it is to oversee adherence, provide guidance, and ensure that all mages are equipped with the necessary knowledge and tools to comply fully. This officer will collaborate closely with § 900.18 Ancillary Arcane Disruption Protocol Enhancements to refine and enhance reporting protocols as needed.\n\nIn conclusion, compliance with these ancillary arcane effects reporting protocols is not merely a matter of adherence to legal requirements but also a commitment to the safety and harmony within our magical community. The Accords Desk remains steadfast in its duty to ensure that all practitioners uphold their responsibilities under these protocols, thereby safeguarding the integrity and well-being of all involved.\n\nUnder § 1201.15 Conditional Exemption for Ancillary Planar Transits, the Mages' Guild Accords Desk recognizes that certain circumstances necessitate exceptional handling to ensure compliance with both the spirit and letter of the law. This section provides a framework for such exceptional handling, ensuring that all mages are guided in their application of planar transit, which is often ancillary or secondary to primary magical acts.\n\nThe enforcement mechanisms mentioned earlier are part of a broader strategy to ensure that all practitioners understand the importance of reporting ancillary effects and comply with these protocols. § 1301.17 Additional Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption further supports this effort by providing supplementary measures to address disruptions caused by such effects.\n\nThrough diligent enforcement, transparency, and continuous improvement, the Mages' Guild Accords Desk aims to maintain a safe and harmonious environment for all practitioners of magic within its jurisdiction.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "900.19",
            "1401.14",
            "500.15",
