    {
      "cite": "100.20",
      "part": "part_i",
      "title": "Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords Desk recognizes that exigent circumstances may arise necessitating the temporary dismissal or reconstitution of the Guild's offices. These provisions are intended to govern such situations in an orderly manner, ensuring continuity of operation during times of crisis.\n\nUnder § 100.20, when the necessity for a temporary dismissal arises, it shall be conducted by the Archmage Sovereign with the concurrence of at least three members of the Desk. The decision must be made public and recorded in the Accords Log for future reference. Upon such a dismissal, all personnel are to continue their duties under the supervision of the remaining officers until reconstitution occurs.\n\nReconstitutions shall follow similar protocols. A request for reconstitution may be initiated by the Archmage Sovereign or any member holding a seat on the Desk. The reconstitution process requires the presence and agreement of at least three members of the Guild's Council, excluding any individuals involved in the initial dismissal. Reconstitution must be publicly announced and logged.\n\nIn cases where the Guild offices are temporarily dismissed, all ongoing matters shall be placed into a state of limbo pending reconstitution. This includes unresolved disputes, ongoing mediation processes, and uncompleted peer reviews. Under § 100.20, such matters may not proceed further until the Desk is reconstituted, but they must remain preserved in their current state.\n\nThe Desk shall provide detailed protocols for transitioning between the dismissed and reconstituted states to ensure continuity of operations. These protocols are designed to minimize disruption and maintain the Guild's operational integrity during periods of transition. All personnel involved in these processes shall adhere strictly to these guidelines, ensuring that no actions taken during a temporary dismissal are considered valid or binding without reconstitution.\n\nUnder § 100.20, all temporary dismissals and subsequent reconstitutions must be reported to the High Council for review and approval. The Desk is responsible for maintaining records of such events, which shall include the reasons for the dismissal, the duration of any disruption, and a summary of actions taken during this period. These records are subject to audit by the High Council.\n\nFurthermore, § 100.20 mandates that in situations where a temporary dismissal is necessary due to exigent circumstances, the Desk must provide alternative means of addressing immediate concerns or disputes that would otherwise be compromised. This may include the appointment of interim officers or the establishment of ad hoc committees to manage critical matters until full reconstitution occurs.\n\nThe Desk shall maintain a reserve of resources and personnel capable of responding to emergencies requiring temporary dismissals. These reserves are intended to mitigate risks associated with disruptions in governance and ensure that critical functions can continue without significant delay.\n\nUnder § 100.20, the Desk is required to develop contingency plans for potential scenarios where reconstitution may take longer than anticipated due to unforeseen circumstances. Such plans must include procedures for maintaining operational continuity during prolonged periods of disruption. These plans shall be reviewed and updated regularly by the High Council and made available to all relevant officers.\n\nIn instances where a temporary dismissal has occurred, the Desk is responsible for ensuring that no actions taken in limbo are deemed valid or binding without reconstitution. This includes any decisions, agreements, or communications that occur during the period of limbo. Under § 100.20, all such matters must be reviewed and potentially reopened upon full reconstitution to ensure compliance with these protocols.\n\nThe Desk shall also provide guidance on how to manage personnel in the event of a temporary dismissal. This includes procedures for maintaining discipline and ensuring that officers continue to perform their duties under supervision until reconstitution occurs. Under § 100.20, all personnel involved in such situations must adhere strictly to these guidelines to maintain the Guild's operational integrity.\n\nFor matters directly related to the operation and governance of the Guild offices during a temporary dismissal or reconstitution, see § 100.14 for Additional Provisions for Office Boundaries and Jurisdictional Clarity. The Desk is responsible for ensuring that all personnel are aware of these provisions and are prepared to act accordingly.\n\nUnder § 100.20, the Desk shall provide clear guidance on how to manage critical issues that may arise during a temporary dismissal or reconstitution. This includes procedures for addressing urgent matters, maintaining operational continuity, and ensuring that no actions taken in limbo are considered valid without full reconstitution. The Desk is responsible for developing these protocols and ensuring they are followed rigorously.\n\nIn conclusion, the provisions outlined under § 100.20 aim to provide a structured approach for managing temporary dismissals and reconstitutions of the Guild offices. These protocols ensure continuity of operations during critical periods, maintain the integrity of governance processes, and uphold the standards set forth by the Autumnwood Accords. The Desk is responsible for ensuring that all personnel are aware of these provisions and prepared to act in accordance with them.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "100.20",
            "100.14"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Emergency Reconstitution Protocols",
          "text": "The protocols outlined in § 100.20 concerning the temporary dismissals and reconstitutions of the Mages' Guild are designed to ensure orderly management during periods of crisis or when extraordinary circumstances necessitate immediate action. This page focuses on a critical component: emergency reconstitution protocols, which provide a framework for restoring full operational capacity swiftly following an interruption that affects the Guild's core functions.\n\nUnder § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild, it is established that only those explicitly vested with the right of speech by Archmage Veyra or the presiding body may represent the Guild. This principle extends to the reconstitution process where the leadership must be able to act decisively and effectively in emergencies.\n\nIn instances where an emergency necessitates a temporary cessation of Guild operations, the protocols outlined in § 1001.16 on Confidentiality and Reporting Obligations for Mages' Guild Members come into play. These protocols ensure that critical information is handled securely and transparently during reconstitution efforts.\n\nThe process begins with the identification of a significant disruption to Guild operations, such as an internal crisis or external threat. Upon detection, the leadership must initiate § 100.20's temporary dismissal procedures immediately. This includes notifying key stakeholders and ensuring that critical functions are managed by designated interim personnel in accordance with § 400.9 Research Integrity and Peer Review.\n\nOnce the immediate danger has been mitigated or resolved, a plan for reconstitution is necessary. Under § 100.20 Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions, the Guild leadership must convene within forty-eight hours to assess the extent of the disruption and outline steps for restoration. This includes reviewing current operational challenges and ensuring all members are aware of their roles in the recovery process.\n\nA critical component of emergency reconstitution is maintaining communication channels as outlined under § 1001.21 Protocols for Continuous Communication. The Guild must ensure that all relevant parties, including external stakeholders and members, are promptly informed of any changes to operations or procedures. This ensures continuity and avoids confusion during the reconstitution phase.\n\nIn cases where a significant disruption affects multiple factions within the Guild, § 100.17 Protocols for Exclusionary Hearings and Peer Review plays a crucial role. These protocols provide a structured approach to addressing grievances and ensuring that all parties involved in the disruption are treated fairly and justly. This helps foster trust and cooperation during the reconstitution process.\n\nAdditionally, under § 500.7 Public Safety — Additional Protocols, special attention is given to maintaining public safety during reconstitution efforts. This includes safeguarding the integrity of thaumaturgical operations and ensuring that no unauthorized activities occur. The Guild must adhere to all applicable regulations as outlined in § 1401.13 Preservation of Canonical Continuity and Scriptural Integrity to ensure that any changes or adjustments do not disrupt established foundational principles.\n\nFinally, the reconstitution process must be transparent and inclusive, reflecting the Guild's commitment to fair governance as stated in § 100.2 Protocols for Representation. All members have the right to participate in discussions regarding recovery efforts and to voice concerns about potential risks or inefficiencies. This ensures that all parties are aligned with the Guild’s mission and objectives.\n\nIn summary, emergency reconstitution protocols serve as a vital component of § 100.20 Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions. They provide a structured approach to ensuring rapid recovery in times of crisis while maintaining transparency, inclusivity, and adherence to regulatory standards. By following these protocols, the Mages' Guild can navigate disruptions with efficiency and resilience, preserving its integrity and operational continuity.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "100.20",
            "100.2",
            "1001.16",
            "400.9",
            "1001.21",
            "100.17",
            "500.7",
            "1401.13"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Protocols for Emergency Reconstitution Following Natural Disaster",
          "text": "In the event that a Guild office is rendered incapacitated or temporarily inactive due to an unforeseen natural disaster, it is incumbent upon the Mages' Guild to maintain operational continuity and ensure the uninterrupted delivery of services. The protocols outlined herein are designed to address such emergencies, ensuring that critical functions can be resumed as swiftly as possible without compromising the integrity of the Autumnwood Accords.\n\nUnder § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild, it is established that the authority to represent the Mages' Guild lies with those explicitly vested by Archmage Veyra or the presiding officers. In circumstances where a natural disaster impacts an office’s operational capacity, the immediate reconstitution of critical functions becomes paramount. § 1001.16 Confidentiality and Reporting Obligations for Mages’ Guild Members further emphasizes that all communications related to such emergencies must be conducted with strict confidentiality, ensuring that sensitive information is not exposed to unauthorized parties.\n\nThe first step in responding to a natural disaster affecting an office is the assessment of the extent of damage and disruption. § 100.20 Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions provides guidance on how to temporarily dismiss operations while ensuring continuity through remote or alternative means. This involves the immediate activation of emergency protocols, including the reassignment of responsibilities to unaffected offices or personnel located in other Guild seats.\n\nUpon assessment, the affected office must promptly report the nature and scope of the disaster to the Autumnwood Accords Desk for review under § 100.20 Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions. The desk will then coordinate with relevant factions, including the Conservators and Innovators, to determine the best course of action. If necessary, a temporary reconstitution may be required to ensure that critical functions continue uninterrupted.\n\nDuring the reconstitution period, § 100.20 Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions mandate that all personnel involved in emergency operations adhere strictly to established protocols. This includes the use of alternative facilities, remote access technologies, and other measures designed to mitigate operational disruption. The desk will also facilitate the necessary logistical support to ensure that critical functions can be resumed as swiftly as possible.\n\nThe duration of any temporary reconstitution is subject to periodic review under § 100.20 Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions, which allows for adjustments based on evolving conditions. Upon the resumption of full operational capacity, a thorough evaluation of the emergency response measures will be conducted to identify areas for improvement. This evaluation should consider both immediate actions taken during the crisis as well as long-term strategies to enhance resilience against future natural disasters.\n\nMoreover, § 1001.16 Confidentiality and Reporting Obligations for Mages’ Guild Members underscores the importance of maintaining confidentiality throughout emergency response efforts. Any breaches in this regard could undermine trust and operational efficiency. The desk will ensure that all communications are conducted with utmost discretion to safeguard sensitive information from unauthorized exposure.\n\nIn summary, the protocols outlined herein provide a structured framework for responding to natural disasters affecting Guild offices. By adhering strictly to established procedures, the Mages' Guild can ensure that critical functions are maintained during emergencies, thereby upholding the integrity of the Autumnwood Accords and providing continuity in service delivery. This approach not only mitigates operational disruptions but also enhances the Guild's resilience against future challenges.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "100.2",
            "1001.16",
            "100.20"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Protocols for Interim Leadership Transfers",
          "text": "In instances where the Mages' Guild, as an institution, requires temporary reconstitution or disassembly, protocols must ensure that leadership continuity is maintained and that the integrity of the Guild's operations remains unimpaired. These protocols are designed to address situations in which a critical mage within a factional seat has become incapacitated or has been otherwise temporarily removed from active duty, necessitating an interim transfer of responsibilities.\n\nUnder § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild, it is established that only those explicitly vested with the right of speech by Archmage Veyra or the presiding officers may represent the Mages' Guild. This principle holds true even in cases where a seat within one of the factional offices becomes temporarily vacant. Therefore, when such a vacancy arises, an interim leader must be appointed to fill the gap until a permanent replacement can be named and sworn into their role.\n\nThe process for appointing an interim leader is outlined under § 1001.16 Confidentiality and Reporting Obligations for Mages' Guild Members. Interim leaders are bound by strict confidentiality requirements, ensuring that sensitive information regarding ongoing investigations or matters of public safety remains protected during the temporary leadership period. This ensures that any actions taken in their capacity as interim leader do not compromise the integrity of the Guild's proceedings.\n\nInterim leadership transfers are initiated under § 100.20 Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions, which sets forth the steps required to ensure a smooth transition of power. Upon an event necessitating an interim transfer, the presiding officers of the Mages' Guild must convene to evaluate the situation and determine the appropriate course of action. They are instructed to consider the nature and duration of the vacancy, as well as any potential impact on the Guild's operations.\n\nUnder § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild, the presiding officers have discretion in determining who is qualified to serve as an interim leader. This decision must be made based on the qualifications of candidates within the Mages' Guild, ensuring that the individual appointed possesses the necessary expertise and experience to manage the factional seat effectively during their tenure.\n\nThe responsibilities of an interim leader are extensive and encompass all matters typically handled by the vacated position. These responsibilities include, but are not limited to, oversight of operations, communication with relevant parties, and participation in guild-wide decisions. It is imperative that the interim leader maintains transparency and adheres to the Guild's protocols for confidentiality and reporting.\n\nUpon conclusion of their term as an interim leader, the individual must submit a detailed report of their actions and decisions during the temporary leadership period. This report serves as a record of the actions taken and provides insights into any challenges faced and how they were addressed. The report is subject to review by the presiding officers, who will evaluate its compliance with Guild protocols and consider it in determining the suitability of the individual for permanent appointment.\n\nIn cases where an interim leader's tenure exceeds a specified period, or if their performance during this time does not meet the expected standards, the Guild may elect to appoint a new interim leader. Such decisions are made following a thorough evaluation process that considers both the immediate needs of the factional seat and the broader implications for the Guild.\n\nThe protocols established under § 100.20 Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions ensure that the Mages' Guild can effectively manage its operations during periods of temporary leadership transfers, maintaining the integrity and continuity of its activities. By adhering to these protocols, the Guild ensures that any disruptions to its operations are minimized, and the best possible candidates are identified for permanent roles in factional seats.\n\nIn summary, the protocols for interim leadership transfers serve as a critical mechanism within the Mages' Guild's administrative structure, ensuring that the Guild remains operational and effective even during times of temporary disruption. These protocols reflect the Guild's commitment to maintaining its core values of integrity, confidentiality, and procedural adherence, all of which are essential to upholding the trust placed in the Mages' Guild by the wider community.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "100.2",
            "1001.16",
            "100.20"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Protocols for Emergency Reconstitution Following Severe Thaumaturgical Incident",
          "text": "In the event that severe thaumaturgical incidents necessitate the temporary or permanent cessation of operations by an office within the Mages' Guild, protocols must be followed to ensure continuity and stability. Under these protocols, the Autumnwood Accords Desk shall facilitate a swift reconstitution of the affected office, thereby restoring its full operational capacity. This section is integral to maintaining the integrity and efficacy of the Guild's administrative structure in times of crisis.\n\nThe process of emergency reconstitution begins with an immediate assessment by the Autumnwood Accords Desk upon notification or observation of a severe thaumaturgical incident that jeopardizes an office's ability to function effectively. Such incidents may include, but are not limited to, widespread magic failures, thaumaturgical breaches, and natural disasters that directly impact the Guild’s infrastructure. Upon such determination, the desk shall notify the High Council, which has the authority to convene a special session for the purpose of reconstituting the office in question.\n\nThe High Council may choose to appoint an interim leadership team from within the affected office or select individuals from other offices with relevant experience and expertise. This team shall have the immediate responsibility of overseeing the emergency operations and ensuring that all necessary actions are taken to mitigate risks and restore full functionality. Under § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild, only those individuals explicitly vested with the right of speech by Archmage Veyra or the presiding High Council may speak on behalf of the Mages' Guild during this period.\n\nIn cases where the incident results in the permanent cessation of an office’s operations, a formal reconstitution process is initiated. This involves the reappointment of officers and the re-establishment of the office's protocols and responsibilities. The High Council shall issue a decree outlining the terms and conditions under which the office will operate post-reconstitution. Under § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild, this decree must be ratified by Archmage Veyra or another designated representative to ensure its legitimacy.\n\nDuring the reconstitution process, the Autumnwood Accords Desk shall collaborate with the affected office and the High Council to identify any additional resources required to support the transition. This may include personnel reallocation from other offices, technological assistance, and financial support. The desk is responsible for ensuring that these resources are made available in a timely manner under § 100.20 Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions.\n\nFurthermore, the reconstitution process must be transparent and inclusive of all stakeholders. Under § 1.4 Persons Bound, this includes ensuring that affected mages and offices have access to adequate representation during the reconstitution proceedings. The desk shall facilitate mediation where necessary under § 100.13 Protocols for Mediation and Inter-Factional Arbitration to ensure that all parties involved in the reconstitution process are heard.\n\nUpon completion of the reconstitution, the Autumnwood Accords Desk shall issue a final report detailing the steps taken during the emergency period, including any challenges faced and solutions implemented. This report shall be made available for review by the High Council and other relevant bodies under § 1001.16 Confidentiality and Reporting Obligations for Mages' Guild Members.\n\nIn summary, these protocols ensure that the Mages' Guild can swiftly respond to severe thaumaturgical incidents without compromising its operational integrity. By following these procedures, the Guild maintains stability and continuity in its governance structures, thereby upholding the foundational principles of the Autumnwood Accords as set forth in § 1.2 Enacting Authority; Autumnwood Accords Desk.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "100.2",
            "100.20",
            "1.4",
            "100.13",
            "1001.16",
            "1.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions: Protocol for Suspension ",
          "text": "In the administration of magic within the Midlands, the Mages' Guild is charged with maintaining the balance between order and liberty, ensuring that the use of magic remains a beacon of civilization rather than a source of chaos. The Protocols for Temporary Dismissals and Reconstitutions are designed to provide a structured framework for addressing extraordinary circumstances necessitating the temporary suspension or revival of certain factions within the Guild. This protocol specifically concerns the process by which factions may be temporarily dismissed from their roles, with the option for swift reconstitution in cases that require immediate action.\n\nUnder § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild (see § 100.2), it is incumbent upon those authorized to represent the Mages' Guild to ensure that any actions taken under this protocol are consistent with the Guild’s mandate and the Autumnwood Accords. The authority to initiate a suspension or revocation of factional roles must be exercised judiciously, ensuring that such actions do not impede the Guild's capacity to fulfill its core functions.\n\n### Protocol for Suspension and Revival\n\nThe process for suspending a faction begins with an official request from either the presiding Archmage Veyra or any duly authorized representative. This request is made in writing and must specify the reasons for suspension, ensuring that they align with the Guild’s mandate as outlined in § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild (see § 1.4 Persons Bound). The requesting party shall provide a detailed account of the faction's transgressions or the exigent circumstances necessitating its temporary removal from active duties.\n\nUpon receipt of such a request, the presiding Archmage convenes an emergency council meeting, drawing together members with expertise relevant to the matter at hand (see § 100.13 Protocols for Mediation and Inter-Factional Arbitration). This council is tasked with reviewing the circumstances and determining whether suspension is warranted. The council's decision must be unanimous or reach a two-thirds majority vote, reflecting the serious nature of such actions.\n\nIn cases where it is deemed necessary to immediately revive a faction following an official suspension, the process for reconstitution begins with an equally formal request from the presiding Archmage or authorized representative (see § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild). This request must outline the reasons for immediate reconstitution and include a detailed plan for addressing any issues that led to the initial suspension.\n\n### Emergency Revival Protocols\n\nThe emergency revival protocol is particularly critical in circumstances where a faction's absence could lead to significant disruption within the Guild or broader thaumaturgical community. For example, this might occur following a severe thaumaturgical incident (see § 100.17 Protocols for Exclusionary Hearings and Peer Review) that necessitates immediate action to restore order.\n\nIn such cases, the emergency revival protocol allows for swift reconstitution by bypassing certain procedural requirements typically associated with formal reinstatement. The council may authorize an expedited process under § 100.15 Catchline Title: Protocols for Immediate and Expedited Remediation (see § 1.15 Additional Provisions for Expedited Remediation and Immediate Response Protocols), ensuring that factions can resume their duties as soon as possible.\n\n### Confidentiality and Reporting Obligations\n\nUnder § 1401.13 Preservation of Canonical Continuity and Scriptural Integrity, it is crucial to maintain the integrity of the canonical laws governing the Guild (see § 1.2 Enacting Authority; Autumnwood Accords Desk). Therefore, all communications regarding the suspension or revival of factions must adhere strictly to this principle. Any sensitive information disclosed during these protocols must be handled with utmost confidentiality and reported only on a need-to-know basis.\n\n### Conclusion\n\nThe Protocol for Suspension and Revival of Factions is a critical component in maintaining the operational integrity of the Mages' Guild. By providing clear guidelines for both suspending and reviving factions, this protocol ensures that the Guild can respond effectively to extraordinary circumstances without compromising its foundational principles or procedures. Through careful adherence to these protocols, the Mages' Guild can uphold its mandate as a bastion of thaumaturgical order and innovation within the Midlands.\n\nUnder § 100.2 Who May Speak for the Guild (see § 1.4 Persons Bound), this protocol reinforces the importance of accountability in decision-making processes. By ensuring that only authorized representatives may invoke these protocols, the Guild upholds its commitment to responsible governance and the rule of law.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "100.2",
            "1.4",
            "100.13",
            "100.17",
            "100.15",
            "1.15",
            "1401.13",
            "1.2"
          ]
        }
