        {
          "heading": "Prohibitions on Coercive and Degradational Magic",
          "text": "In furtherance of the objectives set forth in these Accords, it is hereby declared that the use of magic designed to dominate, debase, or psychologically scar individuals beyond their immediate pain constitutes a fundamental violation of magical ethics and societal norms. Such acts are prohibited under all circumstances unless explicitly authorized by the High Council for exceptional reasons.\n\nThe Autumnwood Accords recognizes the inherent dignity and autonomy of every individual and mandates that all magical practices must uphold these principles. The Guild's mandate is to ensure that all magical activities adhere to the highest ethical standards, reflecting respect for all persons involved in any arcane transactions. Any casting or incantation aimed at coercing, humiliating, or otherwise degrading a person in ways that exceed mere pain is strictly forbidden.\n\nUnder § 200.9, the Guild strictly forbids the use of magic designed to dominate, debase, or psychologically scar individuals beyond their immediate pain. Such acts constitute a fundamental violation of magical ethics and are anathema to the values espoused by the Accords. The Autumnwood Accords recognize that the integrity and well-being of every individual must be preserved at all times.\n\nThe Guild's stance on this matter is unequivocal: no magical practice shall be employed to manipulate, exploit, or degrade another person. This prohibition extends not only to direct spells but also to any form of coercive behavior or psychological manipulation facilitated through magic. The High Council reserves the right to review and adjudicate such cases to ensure compliance with these standards.\n\nFurthermore, under § 500.12, unsanctioned commercial spellcasting is prohibited without express authorization from the Guild's High Council. Any caster engaging in such activities outside their licensed practice risks disciplinary action. This principle also applies to coercive or degradational magic, which must be conducted within the bounds of legitimate and ethical practices.\n\nThe Autumnwood Accords emphasize that all magical practices shall respect the individual’s autonomy and dignity. The Guild's mandate is to ensure that all magical activities adhere to these principles. Any breach of this prohibition will result in severe disciplinary measures, including but not limited to having one's magic sealed or being cast into a pocket dimension.\n\nThe High Council reserves the right to review cases involving coercive or degradational magic and to impose appropriate sanctions. Under § 800.12, additional provisions regarding unlawful casting and confiscation are applicable in such cases. The Guild will not tolerate any actions that violate the ethical principles outlined by these Accords.\n\nUnder § 700.12, provisions governing arcane litigation and evidence are designed to ensure that magical activities do not compromise individual dignity or autonomy. Any case involving coercive or degradational magic shall be handled with utmost sensitivity and respect for all parties involved. The Guild's commitment to ethical standards is paramount in these matters.\n\nIn conclusion, the Autumnwood Accords underscore the importance of maintaining a balance between the power of magic and the protection of individual rights and dignity. The use of coercive or degradational magic is strictly prohibited unless explicitly authorized by the High Council for exceptional reasons. This prohibition extends to all forms of magical practice and ensures that the Guild's mandate remains true to its ethical principles.",
          "key": "c",
