        {
          "heading": "Protocol for Immediate Reporting and Suspension of Mages Engaged in Coercive or ",
          "text": "The Autumnwood Accords, recognizing the paramount importance of magical practices that adhere to ethical standards, mandates the immediate reporting and suspension protocol for mages engaging in coercive or degrading magic. Such actions not only violate the fundamental principles of respect for autonomy but also undermine the trust necessary between mages and their clients, as well as among the members of the Mages' Guild itself.\n\nUnder § 200.9, it is clearly stated that all magical practices must align with ethical standards, which include respect for individuals’ autonomy and dignity. The present protocol seeks to ensure that any mage suspected or found to be engaging in coercive or degrading magic can be swiftly addressed through a structured process that balances immediate response with due process.\n\n### Protocol Initiation\n\nUpon receiving credible reports of coercive or degrading magical practices, the Mages' Guild shall initiate an investigation. This protocol applies equally to all members and associates of the Guild, including apprentices and those who have not yet obtained full membership (see § 1.4 Persons Bound for details on jurisdiction). The immediate response team, comprising experienced mages and mediators from the Guild, is tasked with verifying these reports.\n\n### Immediate Suspension\n\nUpon verification that coercive or degrading magic has been employed, the offending mage shall be immediately suspended from practice until a formal investigation concludes (see § 200.18 for prohibitions on such practices). This suspension ensures that the accused mage cannot continue to exploit their position of trust and influence over clients. The decision to suspend is made by the Guild's Immediate Response Protocol Committee, which operates under the authority of § 1.18 Additional Provisions for Mages' Guild Mediation and Immediate Response Protocol.\n\n### Confidentiality and Reporting Obligations\n\nAll members of the immediate response team are bound by confidentiality agreements (see § 1001.19 Confidentiality and Non-Disclosure Agreements for Magical Transactions). These agreements ensure that sensitive information regarding the accused mage is not disclosed without due process, protecting the individual’s reputation until a formal investigation is complete.\n\n### Formal Investigation\n\nThe accused mage shall undergo a formal investigation conducted by the Guild's Mediation and Peer Review Protocols Committee (see § 1.17 Additional Provisions for Mages' Guild Mediation and Peer Review Protocols). This committee ensures that all allegations are thoroughly investigated, providing a fair process for both the accuser and the accused. During this time, the accused mage shall not engage in any form of magical practice without explicit permission from the Guild (see § 200.12 Prohibitions on Coercive and Degradational Magic).\n\n### Reporting Obligations\n\nIn addition to immediate suspension, the accused mage is required to report all ongoing or planned coercive or degrading practices within their sphere of influence immediately upon receiving a notice from the Guild. Failure to comply with this requirement shall be treated as an independent violation (see § 1001.6 Endowments and Gifts of Magical Assets for further details on asset management). The accused mage must also provide full cooperation during the investigation process, including but not limited to submitting to voluntary audits and providing any relevant documentation.\n\n### Remediation and Reintegration\n\nUpon completion of the formal investigation, the accused mage may be subject to a range of remedial measures. These could include mandatory training in ethical conduct (see § 500.8 Compensation and Debt Settlement for ancillary provisions), community service within the Guild or its affiliated institutions, or other forms of reparation as deemed necessary by the Mediation and Peer Review Protocols Committee.\n\n### Reintegration Process\n\nIf the accused mage successfully completes the remedial measures and is cleared through a peer review process, they may be allowed to return to practice under supervision. Supervision ensures that the accused mage adheres to ethical standards and does not repeat past transgressions (see § 200.18 Prohibitions on Coercive and Degradational Magic for prohibitions and protocols).\n\n### Cross-Referencing\n\nThis protocol is designed to be in harmony with other sections of the Autumnwood Accords, particularly § 200.9, which emphasizes ethical conduct, and § 1001.6, which deals with asset management and reporting obligations. The immediate response protocol ensures that any mage accused or found guilty of coercive or degrading practices can be swiftly addressed, maintaining the integrity and reputation of the Mages' Guild.\n\nThe swift implementation of this protocol is crucial in upholding the Guild's mandate to ensure that all magical practices adhere to ethical principles. By providing a clear framework for immediate response, investigation, and remediation, the Guild maintains its commitment to fostering an environment where respect and dignity are paramount.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "200.9",
            "1.4",
            "200.18",
            "1.18",
            "1001.19",
            "1.17",
