        {
          "heading": "Protocol for Immediate Suspension and Support for Victims of Coercive and Degrad",
          "text": "Under § 200.9, the Guild strictly forbids the use of magic designed to dominate, debase, or psychologically scar individuals beyond their immediate pain. Such acts not only violate the fundamental ethical principles that underpin the use of magic but also contravene the rights and dignity of all persons within the jurisdiction of the Mages' Guild (see § 1.4). The Autumnwood Accords mandate that the Guild must ensure that magical practices adhere to these principles, which include respect for individual autonomy and integrity.\n\nIn instances where a mage is suspected or confirmed to have engaged in coercive or degradational magic, it is imperative that immediate action be taken to suspend such mages from further practice until they can demonstrate their commitment to ethical conduct (see § 200.18). The Protocol for Immediate Suspension and Support for Victims of Coercive and Degradational Magic seeks to provide a framework for swift and effective intervention, ensuring the safety and well-being of all parties involved.\n\nUpon receiving credible reports or evidence suggesting that a mage has engaged in coercive or degradational magic (see § 1001.6 regarding endowments and gifts), the Guild shall immediately suspend the accused mage's magical abilities, pending an investigation (§ 200.9). This suspension shall be communicated to all relevant parties, including the accused mage, their peers, and any victims or witnesses of the alleged acts.\n\nThe Protocol mandates that the Guild provide immediate support services for any victims of coercive and degradational magic (see § 1001.16 on confidentiality and reporting obligations). This includes counseling services, psychological support, and medical care if required. The Guild shall ensure that these services are available to all victims, regardless of their status or background within the magical community.\n\nFurthermore, the Protocol emphasizes the importance of confidentiality in such matters (see § 1001.6 on endowments and gifts). All information pertaining to the accused mage and the victim(s) must be handled with utmost discretion and care to protect all parties involved from further harm. The Guild shall establish a secure channel for reporting incidents, ensuring that victims feel safe in coming forward without fear of reprisal or public exposure.\n\nThe Protocol also mandates that the accused mage undergoes a thorough peer review process (see § 1.17 on additional provisions for mediation and peer review protocols) to determine their fitness to practice magic again. During this process, the accused shall have the opportunity to present evidence of their rehabilitation and commitment to ethical conduct. The Guild may impose further sanctions or conditions upon the accused mage as deemed necessary by the reviewing body (see § 200.18).\n\nIn cases where immediate action is required but a full investigation has not yet been completed, the Protocol for Immediate Suspension and Support for Victims of Coercive and Degradational Magic aims to provide temporary relief. This includes issuing restraining orders against the accused mage, ensuring they do not come into contact with their victims or witnesses (see § 1001.6 on endowments and gifts). Additionally, the Protocol encourages the accused mage to participate in rehabilitation programs focused on addressing underlying issues that may have led to their misconduct.\n\nThe Protocol also ensures that any records of incidents involving coercive and degradational magic are thoroughly documented and stored securely (see § 100.4 on records of speech). These records shall be accessible only to authorized personnel for the purpose of ensuring compliance with the Protocol and for future reference in case similar incidents arise.\n\nIn conclusion, the Protocol for Immediate Suspension and Support for Victims of Coercive and Degradational Magic is a critical component of the Guild's mandate under § 200.9. By providing immediate suspension, support services, confidentiality measures, peer review processes, and documentation protocols, the Guild aims to uphold the highest standards of ethical conduct within the magical community. This Protocol not only protects victims but also serves as a deterrent against future acts of coercion and degradation. The Autumnwood Accords emphasize that all members of the magical community are bound by these principles, and any violation is met with swift and decisive action (see § 1.4 on persons bound).",
