        {
          "heading": "Remediation and Compensation for Ancillary Casualties Involving Non-Consensual E — Continued",
          "text": "In the conduct of arcane operations, mages and their apprentices are entrusted with the solemn duty to ensure that their activities do not inadvertently expose individuals or populations to harmful arcane energies without prior consent. Under § 500.19 Remediation and Compensation for Ancillary Casualties Resulting from Arcane Operations, it is incumbent upon those conducting such operations to mitigate any ancillary casualties that arise. This page specifically addresses the remediation and compensation protocols applicable when non-consensual exposure to arcane energies occurs.\n\nNon-Consensual Exposure can be defined as a situation where individuals or communities are exposed to potentially harmful or destabilizing arcane effects without their explicit consent, often due to unforeseen circumstances such as unexpected fluctuations in magical fields or unanticipated side effects. § 1401.15 Conditional Exemption for Ancillary Planar Transits provides that mages operating within the jurisdiction of the Mages' Guild Accords Desk are required to adhere to strict protocols designed to minimize risks associated with ancillary planar transits, but these protocols do not cover all potential scenarios where non-consensual exposure might occur.\n\nUnder § 500.19 Remediation and Compensation for Ancillary Casualties Resulting from Arcane Operations, remediation efforts are directed toward addressing the immediate health and safety concerns of those affected by such exposures. The mage responsible for the operation must undertake a thorough assessment of the extent of the exposure and the potential long-term effects on individuals or communities. This includes but is not limited to conducting medical examinations, providing necessary treatments, and ensuring that all exposed parties have access to ongoing support services.\n\nCompensation for ancillary casualties involving non-consensual exposure extends beyond immediate health care. Mages are required under § 1301.15 Catchline Title: Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption to provide adequate financial compensation for any losses or damages sustained as a result of the exposure. This includes not only medical expenses but also emotional distress, loss of income, and any other direct consequences that can be attributed to the non-consensual exposure.\n\nThe mage responsible for the operation must establish a comprehensive remediation fund to cover all necessary costs related to both immediate and long-term care. § 100.12 Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements mandate that these funds should be managed under strict oversight by an independent committee, ensuring transparency and accountability in the distribution of resources.\n\nFurthermore, mages must adhere to § 500.14 Remediation and Obligations for Lingering Arcane Effects when dealing with long-term effects of non-consensual exposure. This includes ongoing monitoring of exposed individuals or communities to detect and treat any lingering effects that may not manifest immediately after the initial exposure.\n\nIn instances where the mage responsible for the operation is found negligent, § 500.18 Liability for Ancillary Arcane Disruptions and Casualties imposes strict liability on the mage and their apprentices, mandating full compensation for all damages incurred by those affected. Negligence can include failure to adhere to established protocols designed to prevent non-consensual exposure, inadequate remediation efforts, or any other actions that demonstrate a lack of due diligence.\n\nThe Accords Desk shall convene under § 1.20 Protocols for Ancillary Dispute Resolution and Remediation in cases where disputes arise regarding the adequacy of remediation efforts or compensation provided. The Desk may impose additional remedies beyond those already outlined, including public apologies, temporary suspension of arcane privileges, or even more severe sanctions as deemed necessary to ensure that such incidents are not repeated.\n\nIn conclusion, the Mages' Guild Accords Desk emphasizes the paramount importance of ensuring that all parties involved in arcane operations understand and comply with their obligations regarding non-consensual exposure. By adhering to these protocols, mages can help prevent ancillary casualties while also providing appropriate compensation for any damages sustained. This approach not only upholds the integrity of the magical community but also fosters trust between mages and the broader population they serve.",
