    {
      "cite": "1201.20",
      "part": "part_xii",
      "title": "Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Tolls",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Tolls",
          "text": "The Mages' Guild Accords Desk recognizes that the use of planar transit extends beyond the immediate jurisdiction of any single magical hall or guild. While Autumnwood Hall holds primary authority over all magical activities within its purview, certain ancillary transits may occur outside this control. These transits are subject to specific tolls and regulatory protocols designed to ensure compliance with the Accords while maintaining the integrity of planar transit operations.\n\nUnder § 1201.11 Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Tolls, it is established that no jurisdiction shall be construed as limiting the authority of Autumnwood Hall over all lawful magical activities conducted within its purview, regardless of physical location. This section further clarifies that planar tolls are applicable not only to transits initiated from or terminating in Autumnwood Hall but also extend extraterritorially where necessary.\n\nPlanar tolls serve multiple purposes: they fund the maintenance and security of the planar transit network, ensure compliance with Accords, and provide compensation for any potential damages incurred during transit. The amount of these tolls is determined based on a variety of factors including distance traversed, duration of transit, and nature of the operation being conducted.\n\nCasters intending to utilize portals or planar gates must obtain prior transit clearance from the Office of Archmage Sovereign. Such clearance shall be granted only upon presentation of valid identification. This requirement is designed to prevent unauthorized use of planar transit that could destabilize the network or cause harm. Under § 1201.12 Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations, all casters must comply with this protocol.\n\nTolls are collected at points of entry into planar transit zones designated by Autumnwood Hall. Collection is mandatory for all users, including those from foreign jurisdictions. Revenue generated through tolls is allocated to various funds managed by the Office of Archmage Sovereign, which include maintenance, research, and emergency response. These funds ensure that the network remains functional and secure.\n\nIn instances where a caster operates under an extraterritorial jurisdiction, compliance with planar transit protocols may be subject to additional scrutiny. § 1201.8 Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty outlines specific requirements for such operations, ensuring alignment with the Accords regardless of location. This includes the necessity for foreign jurisdictions to enter into agreements that recognize Autumnwood Hall's authority.\n\nThe Mages' Guild Accords Desk also recognizes that certain ancillary planar transits may be necessary for the conduct of primary magical operations. § 1201.14 Catchline Title: Conditional Exemption for Ancillary Planar Transits provides exemptions from some transit and stamping obligations in these cases, allowing for a balance between regulation and operational necessity.\n\nTo ensure compliance with all extraterritorial requirements, the Desk maintains a system of audits and inspections. These measures are designed to verify that all transits adhere to established protocols and contribute appropriately to toll funds. Violations of these rules may result in sanctions under § 1401.15 Conditional Exemption for Ancillary Planar Transits.\n\nUnder § 1201.19 Additional Provisions for Ancillary Planar Transits and Associated Protocols, the Desk has established additional measures to address complex situations involving extraterritorial jurisdiction. These include protocols for dealing with emergency transits that may cross multiple jurisdictions simultaneously.\n\nIn conclusion, § 1201.20 Additional Provisions aims to provide comprehensive oversight of planar transit operations within and beyond Autumnwood Hall's immediate control. By implementing clear toll structures and compliance measures, the Desk ensures that all users contribute fairly to maintaining a secure and functional network while respecting extraterritorial jurisdictions. This section reinforces the authority of Autumnwood Hall in managing these complex interactions, ensuring that the Accords are upheld across all relevant territories.\n\nSee § 1201.12 for further details on transit clearance obligations; see § 1401.15 for sanctions applicable to violations of planar protocols; and under § 1201.8 for extraterritorial considerations that influence this regulation.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1201.11",
            "1201.12",
            "1201.8",
            "1201.14",
            "1401.15",
            "1201.19",
            "1201.20"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Ancillary Protocols for Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations",
          "text": "Under the regime established by the Autumnwood Accords, all mages who facilitate the transit of sentient beings, goods, or essence across planar borders are bound by certain ancillary protocols designed to ensure that such transits are conducted safely and in compliance with legal requirements. These protocols are essential for maintaining order within the jurisdictional boundaries set forth by the Hall, particularly those that extend beyond the immediate reach of local governance.\n\nThe Ancillary Protocols for Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations are detailed further under § 1201.12, which mandates that all casters intending to utilize portals or planar gates must obtain prior transit clearance from the Office of Archmage Sovereign. This clearance is granted only upon presentation of valid identification and a formal application demonstrating compliance with all relevant laws and regulations. The purpose of this requirement is to ensure that only those who are properly authorized can engage in such activities, thereby reducing the risk of unauthorized or harmful transits.\n\nThe Ancillary Protocols also include the obligation for casters to secure Transit Stamps as required under § 1201.1. These stamps serve not only as a record of the transit but also as an acknowledgment that the caster has adhered to all necessary legal and regulatory requirements. The Office of Archmage Sovereign is responsible for issuing these stamps, ensuring that they are applied accurately and consistently across all jurisdictions.\n\nUnder § 1201.6, it is emphasized that the authority of the Hall extends extraterritorially to ensure that transits conducted within its purview adhere strictly to established guidelines. This means that even when a caster operates from outside the immediate jurisdiction of Autumnwood Hall, they are still subject to the laws and regulations set forth by this body. The Office of Archmage Sovereign plays a crucial role in enforcing these extraterritorial jurisdictions, ensuring compliance through periodic audits and inspections.\n\nFurthermore, § 1201.18 outlines specific conditions under which ancillary transits may be exempt from certain protocols, particularly when the transit is deemed inherently ancillary to primary operations within the Hall’s jurisdiction. These exemptions are granted in recognition of the practical necessity for such activities but do not absolve casters of their broader responsibilities regarding safety and legal compliance.\n\nThe Ancillary Protocols also encompass measures aimed at ensuring that transits are conducted with due consideration for environmental impact, a principle enshrined under § 1201.3. This ensures that magical activities across planar borders do not inadvertently disrupt the natural balance of the regions involved. The Office of Archmage Sovereign works closely with local authorities and environmental organizations to ensure that such considerations are properly addressed.\n\nIn instances where transits are conducted in conjunction with other jurisdictions, § 1201.16 provides for conditional exemptions that allow for a more collaborative approach between different governing bodies. This ensures that transits can proceed smoothly while respecting the sovereignty of all involved parties. The Office of Archmage Sovereign coordinates these efforts, ensuring that all relevant protocols are followed and that any necessary adjustments to ensure compliance are made.\n\nIn summary, the Ancillary Protocols for Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations are integral to maintaining order within the jurisdictional boundaries set by Autumnwood Hall. These protocols encompass a range of measures designed to ensure safe, compliant, and environmentally responsible transits across planar borders. By adhering to these protocols, casters help uphold the integrity of magical governance and contribute to the stability of the regions involved in such activities.",
          "key": "b",
          "refs": [
            "1201.12",
            "1201.1",
            "1201.6",
            "1201.18",
            "1201.3",
            "1201.16"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Ancillary Protocols for Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations — Continued",
          "text": "Under the regime of this Part, all magical transit across planar borders shall comply with established protocols designed to ensure that ancillary activities are conducted in a manner consistent with the jurisdictional oversight of Autumnwood Hall. These ancillary protocols aim not only to maintain the integrity of the Accords but also to prevent any potential abuse or circumvention of established rules. Ancillary activities, such as secondary transits or auxiliary operations, often serve an essential purpose related to the primary magical operation being conducted. However, they are subject to strict guidelines and oversight.\n\nAncillary Protocols for Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations encompass a wide range of scenarios where planar transits extend beyond the immediate destination to include additional points within the jurisdictional boundaries of Autumnwood Hall. These protocols are designed to ensure that any such transit is conducted with proper authorization and under strict supervision. This includes, but is not limited to, secondary stops for the purpose of inspection, restocking, or reconfiguration of magical equipment.\n\nThe Office of Archmage Sovereign shall issue a clearance document prior to any ancillary planar transit being executed. This clearance must be obtained from the Mages' Guild Accords Desk and is valid only if all parties involved can demonstrate compliance with § 1201.12 Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations. Under these protocols, casters are required to provide detailed itineraries for any planned ancillary transits, including specific points of transit, duration of stay at each point, and the nature of activities conducted.\n\nAny deviation from the approved itinerary must be reported immediately to the Office of Archmage Sovereign. Violation of these protocols may result in penalties under § 1201.6 Transit Stamps; Planar Tolls; Extraterritorial Casting into Diet Chambers; Cartography as Raid License; Miscellaneous Provisions, which includes potential revocation of the caster's planar transit privileges.\n\nThe rationale behind these ancillary protocols is to ensure that all transits within the jurisdiction are conducted in a manner consistent with the Accords. It also seeks to prevent any exploitation of the system for unauthorized activities or evasion of tolls and stamps. The protocols are designed to maintain transparency and accountability, ensuring that all magical operations are subject to the same level of scrutiny as primary planar transits.\n\nFurthermore, these protocols apply not only to the casters but also to those who assist in facilitating ancillary transits. This includes apprentices, assistants, and any other individuals involved in the process. All such parties must be identified and approved by the Office of Archmage Sovereign prior to the commencement of any ancillary transit activities.\n\nIt is important to note that these protocols are not limited to planar transits but also extend to any ancillary operations conducted within the jurisdictional boundaries. This includes, but is not limited to, the use of portals, gates, and other forms of magical transportation. The Accords Desk shall review all such operations on a case-by-case basis to ensure compliance with established protocols.\n\nUnder § 1201.8 Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty, it is emphasized that these ancillary protocols do not supersede any applicable laws governing the transport of hazardous materials or the taxation thereof at designated transit points. This provision ensures that all ancillary transits are conducted in a manner consistent with the broader legal framework established by the Accords.\n\nIn conclusion, Ancillary Protocols for Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations serve to enhance the overall effectiveness of the Accords by ensuring that all planar transits are conducted in a transparent and accountable manner. These protocols are designed to prevent any potential abuse or circumvention of established rules while maintaining the integrity of the jurisdictional oversight provided by Autumnwood Hall.",
          "key": "c",
          "refs": [
            "1201.12",
            "1201.6",
            "1201.8"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Ancillary Protocols for Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations: Compliance and ",
          "text": "Under the regime established by the Autumnwood Accords, all mages who facilitate the transit of sentient beings, goods, or essence across planar borders are bound by strict protocols concerning extraterritorial jurisdiction and planar tolls. These obligations extend beyond mere compliance with the initial clearance requirements (§ 1201.12) to encompass a framework for continuous verification and adherence to the stipulated conditions (see § 1201.6). This section outlines the specific protocols that ensure mages maintain compliance throughout the duration of their planar transits.\n\nThe Office of Archmage Sovereign is responsible for overseeing these ancillary protocols, which are designed to prevent any unauthorized activities or potential abuses within the jurisdictional boundaries (§ 1201.8). Compliance with these protocols is mandatory and enforced rigorously by the Mages' Guild Accords Desk (§ 1201.6).\n\n### Verification Mechanisms\n\nThe first step in ensuring compliance involves regular verification checks conducted by the Office of Archmage Sovereign. These checks are designed to monitor all planar transits and ensure that the casters are adhering to the stipulated terms laid out in their initial clearance (§ 1201.12). The Office employs a variety of methods, including:\n\n- **On-Site Inspections:** Periodic visits by trained mages who verify the conditions on the ground. These inspections ensure that the caster is not engaging in any activities beyond those permitted under the original clearance (§ 1201.6).\n\n- **Remote Monitoring Systems:** Utilization of advanced magical sensors and tracking devices to monitor planar transit activity in real-time. This allows for immediate intervention if any deviation from the agreed-upon terms is detected (see § 1201.8).\n\n### Reporting Requirements\n\nCasters are required to maintain detailed logs of all planar transits, including the nature of goods or beings transported and the duration of the transit. These logs must be submitted periodically to the Office of Archmage Sovereign for review. Failure to comply with these reporting requirements can result in penalties (§ 1201.6).\n\nAdditionally, casters are required to provide updates on any changes in their planar transit plans that could impact jurisdictional boundaries or toll obligations (§ 1201.18). Any deviations from the initial clearance must be reported and approved by the Office of Archmage Sovereign before proceeding.\n\n### Penalties for Non-Compliance\n\nNon-compliance with ancillary protocols can lead to severe penalties, including the imposition of higher planar tolls or the revocation of clearance privileges (§ 1201.6). In cases where non-compliance is found to be deliberate, mages may face additional sanctions, such as having their magic sealed or being cast into a pocket dimension for further investigation.\n\nThe Office of Archmage Sovereign has the authority to impose these penalties and ensure that all mages adhere to the rules set forth by the Autumnwood Accords. This includes the power to suspend clearance privileges indefinitely in severe cases (§ 1201.8).\n\n### Community Responsibility\n\nMages are also encouraged to report any violations or suspicious activities they observe during their own planar transits. Such reports can be submitted through a secure channel provided by the Mages' Guild Accords Desk, which ensures that all information is handled confidentially (§ 1201.6). Reports of this nature may lead to additional verification checks and potential legal action against the offending mage.\n\nIn conclusion, compliance with ancillary protocols for planar transit and stamping obligations is not merely a formality but a critical component of maintaining order within the jurisdictional boundaries established by the Autumnwood Accords. By adhering to these protocols, mages can ensure that their activities are conducted lawfully and responsibly, thereby fostering trust and cooperation among all members of the magical community (see § 1201.6). Any deviation from these standards is not only a breach of the Accords but also an affront to the integrity of the magical community as a whole.",
          "key": "d",
          "refs": [
            "1201.12",
            "1201.6",
            "1201.8",
            "1201.18"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Ancillary Protocols for Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations: Ancillary Activ",
          "text": "Under the regime of this Part, all magical transit across planar borders shall comply with the established protocols designed to ensure both the safety and regulatory compliance of all involved parties. These ancillary activities are inherently bound by the jurisdictional oversight of Autumnwood Hall, regardless of their primary purpose or intent. § 1201.8 Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty provides that certain planar transits are ancillary to primary magical operations, yet these ancillary activities still require careful scrutiny.\n\nThe Office of Archmage Sovereign is responsible for overseeing all transit clearance requests, ensuring compliance with the established protocols and ensuring that any ancillary activities conducted within jurisdictional boundaries are in keeping with the law. § 1201.12 Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations mandates that all casters intending to utilize portals or planar gates must obtain prior transit clearance from this Office. Such clearance shall be granted only upon presentation of valid identification and proof of compliance with all applicable regulations.\n\n### Ancillary Protocols for Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations: Ancillary Activities\n\nAncillary activities are those that support the primary magical operations conducted within the jurisdiction of Autumnwood Hall. These may include, but are not limited to, the maintenance of planar transit infrastructure, the provision of logistical support services, or the facilitation of ceremonial rituals. Such activities, while ancillary in nature, cannot be exempted from compliance with established protocols and laws.\n\nThe Mages' Guild Accords Desk recognizes that certain planar transits are inherently ancillary to the primary magical operations conducted within the jurisdiction of Autumnwood Hall. These ancillary activities, while supporting the main operation, must still adhere to strict regulatory guidelines. § 1201.18 Conditional Exemption and Ancillary Protocols for Extraterritorial Jurisdiction acknowledges that certain planar transits are necessary for the smooth functioning of primary operations and may be exempted from specific regulations under defined circumstances.\n\nUnder § 1201.6 Transit Stamps; Planar Tolls; Extraterritorial C, all transit across jurisdictional boundaries is subject to the Office of Archmage Sovereign's oversight. Ancillary activities conducted within these borders are no exception. The Mages' Guild Accords Desk further clarifies that ancillary activities must be documented and reported through the appropriate channels. § 1201.13 Additional Provisions for Planar Transit and Stamping Obligations mandates that all such activities must be reviewed by the Office of Archmage Sovereign to ensure compliance with established protocols.\n\nThe purpose of these protocols is not merely regulatory but also serves to promote a seamless flow of magical energies across borders, ensuring that no ancillary activity disrupts the stability or integrity of the planar transit system. Ancillary activities may include the provision of services such as the maintenance and repair of portals, the facilitation of ceremonial rituals, or the transport of goods essential for the primary operations.\n\nThe Office of Archmage Sovereign is responsible for reviewing each request for ancillary activities to ensure that they do not pose any risk to the stability or security of the planar transit system. § 1201.6 Transit Stamps; Planar Tolls; Extraterritorial C further stipulates that the Office shall maintain a record of all ancillary activities conducted within jurisdictional boundaries, ensuring transparency and accountability.\n\nIn cases where an ancillary activity is deemed to be in direct support of primary operations, it may qualify for conditional exemption under § 1201.16 Conditional Exemption for Ancillary Planar Transits and Associated Protocols. This exemption shall only apply if the activity directly supports the primary operation without introducing any additional risks or disruptions.\n\nThe Mages' Guild Accords Desk emphasizes that all ancillary activities must be conducted in a manner that respects the jurisdictional boundaries of Autumnwood Hall. Any deviation from these protocols may result in sanctions under § 1201.8 Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty, which stipulates that extraterritorial jurisdiction extends to all activities conducted within its purview.\n\nIn summary, ancillary activities are an integral part of the planar transit system, and their regulation is as critical as the primary operations they support. The Mages' Guild Accords Desk ensures that these activities are conducted in a manner consistent with established protocols, thereby maintaining the integrity and stability of the planar transit system. § 1201.8 Extraterritorial Jurisdiction and Planar Sovereignty provides that extraterritorial jurisdiction extends to all activities conducted within its purview, including ancillary activities.\n\nUnder § 1201.6 Transit Stamps; Planar Tolls; Extraterritorial C, compliance with these protocols is mandatory. Failure to comply may result in penalties under the jurisdictional oversight of Autumnwood Hall. Ancillary activities must be reported and reviewed by the Office of Archmage Sovereign to ensure that they do not pose any risks to the planar transit system or its stability.\n\nThus, ancillary activities are subject to strict regulatory scrutiny, ensuring that they contribute positively to the overall operation without introducing any risks or disruptions. The Mages' Guild Accords Desk remains vigilant in its oversight of these activities, maintaining a balance between support and regulation for the benefit of all participants in the planar transit system.",
          "key": "e",
          "refs": [
            "1201.8",
            "1201.12",
            "1201.18",
            "1201.6",
            "1201.13",
            "1201.16"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Ancillary Protocols for Extradimensional Transits",
          "text": "Under the regime established in this Part, all mages who facilitate or participate in extradimensional transits must comply with ancillary protocols designed to ensure the safety and proper conduct of such magical activities. This section outlines specific requirements that apply to those utilizing portals, planar gates, or any other means of extradimensional travel.\n\nExtradimensional transits, defined herein as any form of planar travel that crosses into non-Euclidean space, present unique challenges for jurisdictional oversight and safety management. The Mages' Guild Accords Desk recognizes the potential risks associated with such activities and has established protocols to mitigate these hazards. These protocols are designed not only to protect mages but also to ensure the integrity of the planar structure itself.\n\nOne critical aspect of these ancillary protocols is the requirement for a detailed transit plan. All mages intending to engage in extradimensional transits must provide a comprehensive plan to the Office of Archmage Sovereign, including the intended destination, duration of stay, and any materials or personnel that will be transported through the portal. This information shall be reviewed by the relevant authorities who may request additional data if deemed necessary.\n\nAnother key requirement involves the notification procedure for unexpected events during transit. Mages are obligated to report any unforeseen occurrences promptly upon their return to the Midlands. Such reports must include detailed accounts of what transpired, including but not limited to any damage caused to planar structures or the presence of unauthorized entities in the extradimensional space.\n\nFurthermore, mages participating in extradimensional transits must maintain a log book that records all aspects of the journey, including timestamps for entry and exit from non-Euclidean planes. These logs shall be made available upon request by authorized officials. Failure to comply with this requirement may lead to sanctions under § 1201.6.\n\nIn cases where extradimensional transits are deemed ancillary to primary magical operations conducted within the jurisdiction of Autumnwood Hall, certain exemptions may apply. Under § 18.3.4, such activities may be exempt from some regulatory requirements provided they do not pose a significant risk to planar stability or safety. However, mages availing themselves of these exemptions must still adhere to any additional conditions specified by the Mages' Guild Accords Desk.\n\nAdditionally, all extradimensional transits require prior clearance from the Office of Archmage Sovereign. This clearance ensures that the proposed transit aligns with existing regulatory frameworks and does not conflict with ongoing operations or plans within other jurisdictions. Failure to obtain such clearance may result in penalties under § 1201.12.\n\nThe Mages' Guild Accords Desk has also implemented measures aimed at preventing unauthorized use of extradimensional transits. These measures include stringent identification checks upon entry into and exit from non-Euclidean planes, as well as the imposition of planar tolls to discourage frivolous or unregulated use. The amount of these tolls is determined based on the complexity and duration of the planned transit.\n\nFinally, it must be noted that any violations of these ancillary protocols may subject mages to severe penalties under § 1201.6. These penalties include but are not limited to fines, suspension from practice, or even confiscation of magical artifacts used in the transits. The Mages' Guild Accords Desk reserves the right to take further action as deemed necessary by the Hall Council.\n\nIn summary, these ancillary protocols for extradimensional transits serve multiple purposes: they ensure safe and regulated use of planar gates; they protect the integrity of the Midlands' jurisdictional boundaries; and they maintain a harmonious relationship between mages engaged in such activities and those who regulate them. Compliance with these protocols is mandatory for all involved parties, reflecting the Mages' Guild Accords Desk's commitment to maintaining order within the magical community.\n\nUnder § 1201.6, see the detailed provisions regarding extraterritorial jurisdiction and planar tolls; see also § 18.3.4 for conditional exemptions applicable to certain ancillary activities. The Mages' Guild Accords Desk encourages all mages to familiarize themselves with these protocols to ensure smooth and compliant extradimensional transits.",
          "key": "f",
          "refs": [
            "1201.6",
            "18.3.4",
            "1201.12"
          ]
        }
      ],
