    {
      "cite": "1301.20",
      "part": "part_xiii",
      "title": "Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption and Liability",
      "kind": "related",
      "status": "filed",
      "body": [
        {
          "heading": "Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption and Liability",
          "text": "Under §1301.14 and §1301.15, the Autumnwood Accords have established protocols for the remediation of ancillary arcane disruptions. These protocols are designed to ensure that any unintended or ancillary effects of magic use are mitigated swiftly and effectively. The provisions in these sections cover a range of scenarios from minor spells gone awry to more significant disruptions requiring immediate action.\n\n§1301.20 Additional Provisions §1301.20 introduces supplementary protocols for ancillary arcane disruption that go beyond the foundational remediation protocols laid out in §§ 1301.14 and 1301.15. This section aims to address scenarios where immediate action is required, but the standard protocols may not be sufficient due to the nature of the disruption or the environment involved.\n\n### Liability for Ancillary Arcane Disruptions\n\nThe liability for ancillary arcane disruptions under §1301.20 is a critical component in ensuring that those responsible for such disruptions are held accountable. Under this section, it shall be unlawful for any individual or entity to knowingly facilitate, promote, or enable the unauthorized casting of spells prohibited under these Accords. This provision directly aligns with § 1301.11, which explicitly prohibits such enabling activities.\n\nIn cases where a disruption arises from an authorized spell, the caster may still bear liability if it can be proven that they were negligent in their actions or failed to follow established protocols. The desk shall review all evidence of negligence and determine appropriate remediation measures under § 1301.16 Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption.\n\n### Liability for Residue and Lingering Arcane Echoes\n\nUnder §1301.13 Liability for Residue and Lingering Arcane Echoes, liability extends beyond immediate disruptions to include the lingering effects of a spell or magical activity. This section emphasizes that any caster who causes an ancillary arcane disruption is also responsible for ensuring that all residue and lingering echoes are fully remediated.\n\nIf residue or echoes persist after initial remediation efforts, the desk shall convene under §1301.17 Additional Remediation Protocols for Ancillary Arcane Disruption to determine further steps necessary to contain or eliminate these effects. Liability for any resulting additional disruptions may be attributed back to the original caster who failed to properly address the residual effects.\n\n### Penalties and Enforcement\n\nThe provisions in §1301.20 are not only focused on remediation but also ensure strict enforcement of liability through penalties under §1301.12 Additional Provisions for Penalty Assessment and Enforcement §1301.12. This section allows the desk to impose fines, sanctions, or other measures as deemed appropriate by the council.\n\nIf a caster is found responsible for an ancillary arcane disruption, they may face additional penalties under §800.11 Provisions Governing Unlawful Casting and Confiscation if it can be shown that their actions were in violation of these Accords. In severe cases, a trial by arcane duel as outlined in the penal system policy of the desk (§mages_guild.penal[0].spectrum) may be necessary to determine guilt.\n\n### Transitional Arrangements\n\nFinally, §1301.20 also includes transitional arrangements designed to facilitate a smooth transition from existing protocols to those established under this section. These arrangements ensure that all parties involved in managing or witnessing an ancillary arcane disruption are aware of their obligations and the procedures they must follow. This is consistent with the broader goal of ensuring clear pathways for compliance set forth in §1301.11 Supplementary Provisions and Transitional Arrangements.\n\nIn summary, §1301.20 Additional Provisions §1301.20 ensures that all ancillary arcane disruptions are addressed promptly and thoroughly through a combination of remediation protocols, liability measures, and enforcement mechanisms. These provisions build on the foundational rules established in §§ 1301.14 and 1301.15 while providing additional safeguards to protect against unintended consequences of magic use.\n\nBy adhering to these provisions, all individuals and entities involved in magical activities can contribute to maintaining the balance and order that is essential for the continued safety and harmony within the realm governed by the Autumnwood Accords.",
          "key": "a",
          "refs": [
            "1301.14",
            "1301.15",
            "1301.20",
            "1301.11",
            "1301.16",
